{"katas":[{"checks":[{"id":"report-text","kind":"behaviour","title":"The report text is unchanged"},{"id":"report-is-sent","kind":"behaviour","title":"The report is delivered once"},{"id":"bad-rows-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"Bad input is rejected and nothing is sent"},{"id":"parser-role","kind":"design","title":"InvoiceParser only parses"},{"id":"formatter-role","kind":"design","title":"InvoiceFormatter only formats"},{"id":"sender-role","kind":"design","title":"Sender is a one-method interface"},{"id":"service-only-coordinates","kind":"design","title":"ReportService neither parses, formats nor stores"},{"id":"parts-are-swappable","kind":"design","title":"ReportService accepts any Sender"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Ask who asks for each change: the CSV owner, whoever designs the text, whoever runs delivery. Each of those is a reason to change, so each wants its own home.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Move the row loop into `InvoiceParser.parse` and the `StringBuilder` work into `InvoiceFormatter.format`. Delivery becomes the `Sender` interface, injected into `ReportService`, which just calls the three in order.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Wire the old entry point to a method reference:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["String run(String csv) {","    String text = formatter.format(parser.parse(csv));","    sender.send(text);","    return text;","}","// Reports.run: new ReportService(..., outbox::add)"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"srp","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"ReportService.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Objects;\n\nfinal class ReportService {\n    private final InvoiceParser parser;\n    private final InvoiceFormatter formatter;\n    private final Sender sender;\n\n    ReportService(InvoiceParser parser, InvoiceFormatter formatter,\n                  Sender sender) {\n        this.parser = Objects.requireNonNull(parser, \"parser\");\n        this.formatter = Objects.requireNonNull(formatter, \"formatter\");\n        this.sender = Objects.requireNonNull(sender, \"sender\");\n    }\n\n    String run(String csv) {\n        String text = formatter.format(parser.parse(csv));\n        sender.send(text);\n        return text;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Reports {\n    private Reports() { }\n\n    static String run(String csv, List<String> outbox) {\n        return new ReportService(new InvoiceParser(), new InvoiceFormatter(),\n            outbox::add).run(csv);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Parts.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord Line(String sku, int qty, long cents) { }\n\n@FunctionalInterface\ninterface Sender {\n    void send(String text);\n}\n\nfinal class InvoiceParser {\n    List<Line> parse(String csv) {\n        List<Line> lines = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (String row : csv.split(\"\\n\")) {\n            if (row.isBlank()) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            String[] p = row.split(\",\");\n            if (p.length != 3) {\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"bad row: \" + row);\n            }\n            lines.add(new Line(p[0].trim(),\n                Integer.parseInt(p[1].trim()), Long.parseLong(p[2].trim())));\n        }\n        return lines;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class InvoiceFormatter {\n    String format(List<Line> lines) {\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        long total = 0;\n        for (Line l : lines) {\n            sb.append(l.sku()).append(\" x\").append(l.qty()).append('\\n');\n            total += l.qty() * l.cents();\n        }\n        sb.append(String.format(\"TOTAL %d.%02d\", total / 100, total % 100));\n        return sb.toString();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"ReportService.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord Line(String sku, int qty, long cents) { }\n\n// Finance changes the CSV, design changes the text, ops changes delivery.\n// All three edit this one class.\nfinal class ReportService {\n    private final List<String> outbox;\n\n    ReportService(List<String> outbox) { this.outbox = outbox; }\n\n    String run(String csv) {\n        List<Line> lines = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (String row : csv.split(\"\\n\")) {\n            if (row.isBlank()) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            String[] p = row.split(\",\");\n            if (p.length != 3) {\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"bad row: \" + row);\n            }\n            lines.add(new Line(p[0].trim(),\n                Integer.parseInt(p[1].trim()), Long.parseLong(p[2].trim())));\n        }\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        long total = 0;\n        for (Line l : lines) {\n            sb.append(l.sku()).append(\" x\").append(l.qty()).append('\\n');\n            total += l.qty() * l.cents();\n        }\n        sb.append(String.format(\"TOTAL %d.%02d\", total / 100, total % 100));\n        String text = sb.toString();\n        outbox.add(text);\n        return text;\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use this entry point. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Reports {\n    private Reports() { }\n\n    static String run(String csv, List<String> outbox) {\n        return new ReportService(outbox).run(csv);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`ReportService` parses CSV, builds text and delivers it, for three different teams.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Give each job its own type, and leave `ReportService` to coordinate them. `Reports.run(csv, outbox)` must keep returning and sending exactly what it does now.","type":"p"},{"items":["`InvoiceParser` (no-arg constructor) with `List<Line> parse(String csv)`.","`InvoiceFormatter` (no-arg constructor) with `String format(List<Line> lines)`.","`interface Sender` with `void send(String text)`.","`ReportService(InvoiceParser, InvoiceFormatter, Sender)` keeps `String run(String csv)`.","`Line` and the `Reports` entry point stay."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"SrpKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass SrpKataTest {\n    static final String CSV = \"pen,2,150\\n\\n book , 1 ,1299\\n\";\n\n    @Check(id = \"report-text\")\n    void reportText() {\n        List<String> outbox = new ArrayList<>();\n        String text = Reports.run(CSV, outbox);\n        Expect.equal(\"pen x2\\nbook x1\\nTOTAL 15.99\", text, \"the report text\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"report-is-sent\")\n    void reportIsSent() {\n        List<String> outbox = new ArrayList<>();\n        String text = Reports.run(\"a,1,5\", outbox);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(text), outbox, \"the messages sent\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bad-rows-rejected\")\n    void badRowsRejected() {\n        List<String> outbox = new ArrayList<>();\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> Reports.run(\"a,1\", outbox), \"a row with two fields\");\n        Expect.raises(NumberFormatException.class,\n            () -> Reports.run(\"a,x,5\", outbox), \"a quantity that is not a number\");\n        Expect.isTrue(outbox.isEmpty(), \"nothing should be sent for a bad file\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"parser-role\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void parserRole() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> parser = Types.named(\"InvoiceParser\");\n        Object p = Types.create(Types.constructor(parser));\n        Method parse = Types.method(parser, \"parse\", String.class);\n        Object lines = Types.call(parse, p, CSV);\n        Expect.isTrue(lines instanceof List<?> l && l.size() == 2,\n            \"InvoiceParser.parse should return the two lines of the CSV\");\n        var src = Source.type(\"InvoiceParser\");\n        Expect.none(src.calls(\"append\"), \"InvoiceParser also builds text\");\n        Expect.none(src.news(\"StringBuilder\"), \"InvoiceParser also builds text\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"formatter-role\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void formatterRole() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> parser = Types.named(\"InvoiceParser\");\n        Class<?> formatter = Types.named(\"InvoiceFormatter\");\n        Object lines = Types.call(Types.method(parser, \"parse\", String.class),\n            Types.create(Types.constructor(parser)), CSV);\n        Object f = Types.create(Types.constructor(formatter));\n        Object text = Types.call(Types.method(formatter, \"format\", List.class), f, lines);\n        Expect.equal(\"pen x2\\nbook x1\\nTOTAL 15.99\", text, \"InvoiceFormatter.format\");\n        var src = Source.type(\"InvoiceFormatter\");\n        Expect.none(src.calls(\"split\"), \"InvoiceFormatter also parses\");\n        Expect.none(src.calls(\"parseLong\"), \"InvoiceFormatter also parses\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sender-role\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void senderRole() {\n        Class<?> sender = Types.named(\"Sender\");\n        Expect.isTrue(sender.isInterface(), \"Sender should be an interface\");\n        var m = Types.singleAbstractMethod(sender);\n        Expect.equal(\"send\", m.getName(), \"the method name\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(String.class), List.of(m.getParameterTypes()), \"send's parameters\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-only-coordinates\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void serviceOnlyCoordinates() {\n        var service = Source.type(\"ReportService\");\n        Expect.none(service.calls(\"split\"), \"ReportService still parses the CSV\");\n        Expect.none(service.calls(\"parseInt\"), \"ReportService still parses the CSV\");\n        Expect.none(service.calls(\"parseLong\"), \"ReportService still parses the CSV\");\n        Expect.none(service.news(\"StringBuilder\"), \"ReportService still builds the text\");\n        Expect.none(service.calls(\"append\"), \"ReportService still builds the text\");\n        Expect.none(service.calls(\"add\"), \"ReportService still delivers into a list itself\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"parts-are-swappable\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void partsAreSwappable() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> parser = Types.named(\"InvoiceParser\");\n        Class<?> formatter = Types.named(\"InvoiceFormatter\");\n        Class<?> sender = Types.named(\"Sender\");\n        List<Object> got = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object spy = Types.implement(sender, args -> { got.add(args[0]); return null; });\n        Constructor<?> c = Types.constructor(Types.named(\"ReportService\"), parser, formatter, sender);\n        Object service = Types.create(c, Types.create(Types.constructor(parser)),\n            Types.create(Types.constructor(formatter)), spy);\n        Object text = Types.call(Types.method(service.getClass(), \"run\", String.class), service, \"z,3,100\");\n        Expect.equal(\"z x3\\nTOTAL 3.00\", text, \"the returned report\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"z x3\\nTOTAL 3.00\"), got, \"what the injected Sender received\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Split the invoice report into its three jobs"},{"checks":[{"id":"percent-tiers","kind":"behaviour","title":"VIP and STAFF prices are unchanged"},{"id":"clearance-floor","kind":"behaviour","title":"CLEARANCE never goes below zero"},{"id":"unknown-tier-pays-full","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unknown tiers pay full price"},{"id":"rule-interface","kind":"design","title":"PriceRule is a one-method interface"},{"id":"pricer-does-not-branch","kind":"design","title":"Pricer has no tier branches"},{"id":"new-tier-needs-no-edit","kind":"design","title":"Pricer accepts a tier it has never seen"},{"id":"tiers-defined-outside-pricer","kind":"design","title":"Tier rules live outside Pricer"}],"hints":[[{"text":"What changes monthly is the set of tiers, and what stays is \"look up a rule, apply it\". Name the rule, then make `Pricer` know only that name.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Give `Pricer` a `Map<String, PriceRule>` through its constructor. `Pricer.price` finds the rule and applies it. The three tiers move to `Tiers.standard()`, and `Pricing` wires them together.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The whole of `Pricer.price` becomes:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["long price(String tier, long cents) {","    return rules.getOrDefault(tier, c -> c).apply(cents);","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"ocp","kind":"refactor","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Pricer.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\n\nfinal class Pricer {\n    private final Map<String, PriceRule> rules;\n\n    Pricer(Map<String, PriceRule> rules) {\n        this.rules = Map.copyOf(rules);\n    }\n\n    long price(String tier, long cents) {\n        return rules.getOrDefault(tier, c -> c).apply(cents);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Pricing {\n    private Pricing() { }\n\n    static long price(String tier, long cents) {\n        return new Pricer(Tiers.standard()).price(tier, cents);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Tiers.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\n\n@FunctionalInterface\ninterface PriceRule {\n    long apply(long cents);\n}\n\nfinal class Tiers {\n    private Tiers() { }\n\n    static Map<String, PriceRule> standard() {\n        return Map.of(\n            \"VIP\", cents -> cents * 90 / 100,\n            \"STAFF\", cents -> cents * 70 / 100,\n            \"CLEARANCE\", cents -> Math.max(cents - 500, 0));\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Pricer.java","source":"// Every new customer tier is another case in this switch.\nfinal class Pricer {\n    long price(String tier, long cents) {\n        return switch (tier) {\n            case \"VIP\" -> cents * 90 / 100;\n            case \"STAFF\" -> cents * 70 / 100;\n            case \"CLEARANCE\" -> Math.max(cents - 500, 0);\n            default -> cents;\n        };\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use this entry point. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Pricing {\n    private Pricing() { }\n\n    static long price(String tier, long cents) {\n        return new Pricer().price(tier, cents);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Each new customer tier means editing the `switch` in `Pricer`.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Make `Pricer` closed for modification: a new tier must be a new rule that is registered, not a new `case`. `Pricing.price(tier, cents)` must keep returning exactly what it returns now, including full price for unknown tiers.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `interface PriceRule` with one method, `long apply(long cents)`.","`Pricer(Map<String, PriceRule>)` keeps `long price(String tier, long cents)`.","Define VIP, STAFF and CLEARANCE as rules outside `Pricer`, in `Tiers.standard()`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"OcpKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass OcpKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"percent-tiers\")\n    void percentTiers() {\n        Expect.equal(900L, Pricing.price(\"VIP\", 1000), \"VIP\");\n        Expect.equal(700L, Pricing.price(\"STAFF\", 1000), \"STAFF\");\n        Expect.equal(279L, Pricing.price(\"STAFF\", 399), \"STAFF rounds down\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"clearance-floor\")\n    void clearanceFloor() {\n        Expect.equal(1500L, Pricing.price(\"CLEARANCE\", 2000), \"CLEARANCE on 20.00\");\n        Expect.equal(0L, Pricing.price(\"CLEARANCE\", 300), \"CLEARANCE never below zero\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-tier-pays-full\")\n    void unknownTierPaysFull() {\n        Expect.equal(1000L, Pricing.price(\"GUEST\", 1000), \"an unknown tier\");\n        Expect.equal(1000L, Pricing.price(\"vip\", 1000), \"tiers are case sensitive\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rule-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void ruleInterface() {\n        Class<?> rule = Types.named(\"PriceRule\");\n        Expect.isTrue(rule.isInterface(), \"PriceRule should be an interface\");\n        Method m = Types.singleAbstractMethod(rule);\n        Expect.equal(\"apply\", m.getName(), \"the method name\");\n        Expect.equal(long.class, m.getReturnType(), \"apply's return type\");\n        Expect.equal(java.util.List.of(long.class), java.util.List.of(m.getParameterTypes()), \"apply's parameters\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"pricer-does-not-branch\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void pricerDoesNotBranch() {\n        var pricer = Source.type(\"Pricer\");\n        Expect.none(pricer.comparedStrings(), \"Pricer still compares tier names\");\n        Expect.none(pricer.switches(), \"Pricer still switches on the tier\");\n        Expect.none(pricer.instanceofs(), \"Pricer inspects the concrete rule type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"new-tier-needs-no-edit\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void newTierNeedsNoEdit() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> rule = Types.named(\"PriceRule\");\n        Object half = Types.implement(rule, args -> (Long) args[0] / 2);\n        var ctor = Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Pricer\"), Map.class);\n        Object pricer = Types.create(ctor, Map.of(\"GOLD\", half));\n        Method price = Types.method(pricer.getClass(), \"price\", String.class, long.class);\n        Expect.equal(500L, Types.call(price, pricer, \"GOLD\", 1000L), \"a tier Pricer has never seen\");\n        Expect.equal(1000L, Types.call(price, pricer, \"VIP\", 1000L), \"a tier missing from the map\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"tiers-defined-outside-pricer\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void tiersDefinedOutsidePricer() {\n        var pricer = Source.type(\"Pricer\");\n        Expect.none(pricer.mentions(\"VIP\"), \"Pricer still knows the VIP tier\");\n        Expect.none(pricer.mentions(\"STAFF\"), \"Pricer still knows the STAFF tier\");\n        Expect.none(pricer.mentions(\"CLEARANCE\"), \"Pricer still knows the CLEARANCE tier\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Add a pricing tier without editing Pricer"},{"checks":[{"id":"rect-stretch","kind":"behaviour","title":"A Rect stretches to 20"},{"id":"square-area","kind":"behaviour","title":"A Square still reports its area"},{"id":"square-honours-rect-contract","kind":"behaviour","title":"A Square never breaks the Rect contract"},{"id":"shape-interface","kind":"design","title":"Shape is a one-method interface"},{"id":"both-are-shapes","kind":"design","title":"Rect and Square are both Shapes"}],"hints":[[{"text":"`stretch` relies on a promise made by `Rect`: setting the width leaves the height alone. `Square` cannot keep it, so the problem is the `extends`, not the setters.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Break the subtype link. Put what both really share, `area()`, into `Shape`, and let `Rect` and `Square` each implement it. `Square` keeps its own state and no longer inherits `setW` or `setH`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The shape of the fix:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["interface Shape { int area(); }","class Rect implements Shape { /* as before */ }","final class Square implements Shape {","    private int side;","    Square(int side) { this.side = side; }","    public int area() { return side * side; }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"lsp","kind":"fix","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Shapes.java","source":"interface Shape {\n    int area();\n}\n\nclass Rect implements Shape {\n    protected int w, h;\n\n    Rect(int w, int h) { this.w = w; this.h = h; }\n\n    void setW(int w) { this.w = w; }\n    void setH(int h) { this.h = h; }\n    public int area() { return w * h; }\n}\n\nfinal class Square implements Shape {\n    private int side;\n\n    Square(int side) { this.side = side; }\n\n    void setSide(int side) { this.side = side; }\n    public int area() { return side * side; }\n}\n\nfinal class Geometry {\n    private Geometry() { }\n\n    static int stretch(Rect r) {\n        r.setW(5);\n        r.setH(4);\n        return r.area();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Shapes.java","source":"class Rect {\n    protected int w, h;\n\n    Rect(int w, int h) { this.w = w; this.h = h; }\n\n    void setW(int w) { this.w = w; }\n    void setH(int h) { this.h = h; }\n    int area() { return w * h; }\n}\n\n// \"A square is a rectangle\", mathematically.\nfinal class Square extends Rect {\n    Square(int side) { super(side, side); }\n\n    @Override void setW(int w) { this.w = w; this.h = w; }\n    @Override void setH(int h) { this.w = h; this.h = h; }\n}\n\nfinal class Geometry {\n    private Geometry() { }\n\n    // Written against Rect's contract: width and height change independently.\n    static int stretch(Rect r) {\n        r.setW(5);\n        r.setH(4);\n        return r.area();\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Geometry.stretch(Rect)` sets a width of 5 and a height of 4 and expects 20. Pass it a `Square` and it returns 16.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Square` must stop being usable where a `Rect` is promised. Do not weaken `Rect`: its `setW` and `setH` stay independent. Keep what clients already rely on.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Rect(int, int)`, `setW`, `setH`, `area()` and `Geometry.stretch(Rect)` keep their behaviour.","`Square(int side)` keeps `area()`.","Add `interface Shape` with `int area()`, implemented by both `Rect` and `Square`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"LspKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass LspKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"rect-stretch\")\n    void rectStretch() {\n        Expect.equal(20, Geometry.stretch(new Rect(2, 3)), \"stretching a Rect to 5 by 4\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"square-area\")\n    void squareArea() {\n        Expect.equal(9, new Square(3).area(), \"a Square of side 3\");\n        Expect.equal(1, new Square(1).area(), \"a Square of side 1\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"square-honours-rect-contract\")\n    void squareHonoursRectContract() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> rect = Types.named(\"Rect\");\n        Class<?> square = Types.named(\"Square\");\n        if (!rect.isAssignableFrom(square)) {\n            return;   // not a Rect, so the Rect contract cannot be broken\n        }\n        Object s = Types.create(Types.constructor(square, int.class), 3);\n        Types.call(Types.method(rect, \"setW\", int.class), s, 5);\n        Types.call(Types.method(rect, \"setH\", int.class), s, 4);\n        Object area = Types.call(Types.method(rect, \"area\"), s);\n        Expect.equal(20, area, \"a Square used as a Rect, after setW(5) and setH(4)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shape-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void shapeInterface() {\n        Class<?> shape = Types.named(\"Shape\");\n        Expect.isTrue(shape.isInterface(), \"Shape should be an interface\");\n        Method m = Types.singleAbstractMethod(shape);\n        Expect.equal(\"area\", m.getName(), \"the method name\");\n        Expect.equal(int.class, m.getReturnType(), \"area's return type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"both-are-shapes\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void bothAreShapes() {\n        Class<?> shape = Types.named(\"Shape\");\n        Expect.isTrue(shape.isAssignableFrom(Types.named(\"Rect\")), \"Rect should be a Shape\");\n        Expect.isTrue(shape.isAssignableFrom(Types.named(\"Square\")), \"Square should be a Shape\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Stop Square from breaking Rect's contract"},{"checks":[{"id":"printer-prints","kind":"behaviour","title":"BasicPrinter still prints"},{"id":"multifunction-roles","kind":"behaviour","title":"MultiFunction prints, scans and faxes as before"},{"id":"role-interfaces","kind":"design","title":"Printer, DocScanner and Fax are one-method roles"},{"id":"basic-printer-only-prints","kind":"design","title":"BasicPrinter promises only printing"},{"id":"multifunction-plays-all-roles","kind":"design","title":"MultiFunction plays all three roles"},{"id":"office-asks-for-roles","kind":"design","title":"Office depends on roles, not on Machine"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A method that throws `UnsupportedOperationException` is a promise the type cannot keep. Look at which clients use which of the three methods.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"One interface per capability: `Printer`, `DocScanner`, `Fax`. Each class implements exactly the ones it can do. Change each `Office` method to take only the role it calls.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The new signatures:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["interface Printer { void print(String doc); }","final class BasicPrinter implements Printer { ... }","final class MultiFunction implements Printer, DocScanner, Fax { ... }","static int printAll(Printer p, List<String> docs)","static String digitise(DocScanner s)"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"isp","kind":"refactor","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Machines.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\ninterface Printer { void print(String doc); }\ninterface DocScanner { String scan(); }\ninterface Fax { void fax(String doc, String number); }\n\nfinal class BasicPrinter implements Printer {\n    final List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public void print(String doc) { out.add(doc); }\n}\n\nfinal class MultiFunction implements Printer, DocScanner, Fax {\n    final List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public void print(String doc) { out.add(doc); }\n    public String scan() { return \"scan:\" + out.size(); }\n    public void fax(String doc, String number) {\n        out.add(\"fax \" + number + \": \" + doc);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Office {\n    private Office() { }\n\n    static int printAll(Printer p, List<String> docs) {\n        for (String d : docs) {\n            p.print(d);\n        }\n        return docs.size();\n    }\n\n    static String digitise(DocScanner s) { return s.scan().toUpperCase(); }\n\n    static void send(Fax f, String doc, String number) {\n        f.fax(doc, number);\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Machines.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// One fat interface: every machine must offer all three jobs.\ninterface Machine {\n    void print(String doc);\n    String scan();\n    void fax(String doc, String number);\n}\n\nfinal class BasicPrinter implements Machine {\n    final List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public void print(String doc) { out.add(doc); }\n    public String scan() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(); }\n    public void fax(String doc, String number) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException();\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class MultiFunction implements Machine {\n    final List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public void print(String doc) { out.add(doc); }\n    public String scan() { return \"scan:\" + out.size(); }\n    public void fax(String doc, String number) {\n        out.add(\"fax \" + number + \": \" + doc);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Office {\n    private Office() { }\n\n    static int printAll(Machine m, List<String> docs) {\n        for (String d : docs) {\n            m.print(d);\n        }\n        return docs.size();\n    }\n\n    static String digitise(Machine m) { return m.scan().toUpperCase(); }\n\n    static void send(Machine m, String doc, String number) {\n        m.fax(doc, number);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`BasicPrinter` implements `Machine` but throws on `scan` and `fax`.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Split `Machine` into role interfaces so that every implementation honours everything it promises, and every client asks only for the role it uses. What `BasicPrinter` and `MultiFunction` print, scan and fax must not change.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Printer.print(String)`, `DocScanner.scan()` and `Fax.fax(String, String)`.","`BasicPrinter` is only a `Printer`; `MultiFunction` plays all three.","`Office.printAll`, `digitise` and `send` take the narrowest role they need.","You may keep `Machine` as a combination of the roles, or remove it."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"IspKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass IspKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"printer-prints\")\n    void printerPrints() {\n        BasicPrinter p = new BasicPrinter();\n        int n = Office.printAll(new MultiFunction(), List.of(\"x\"));\n        p.print(\"a\");\n        p.print(\"b\");\n        Expect.equal(1, n, \"documents printed\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a\", \"b\"), p.out, \"what BasicPrinter printed\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"multifunction-roles\")\n    void multifunctionRoles() {\n        MultiFunction m = new MultiFunction();\n        Office.printAll(m, List.of(\"a\", \"b\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"SCAN:2\", Office.digitise(m), \"digitise after two prints\");\n        Office.send(m, \"memo\", \"555\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a\", \"b\", \"fax 555: memo\"), m.out, \"the machine's log\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"role-interfaces\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void roleInterfaces() {\n        for (String role : List.of(\"Printer\", \"DocScanner\", \"Fax\")) {\n            Class<?> type = Types.named(role);\n            Expect.isTrue(type.isInterface(), role + \" should be an interface\");\n            Types.singleAbstractMethod(type);\n        }\n        Expect.equal(\"print\", Types.singleAbstractMethod(Types.named(\"Printer\")).getName(), \"Printer's method\");\n        Expect.equal(\"scan\", Types.singleAbstractMethod(Types.named(\"DocScanner\")).getName(), \"DocScanner's method\");\n        Expect.equal(\"fax\", Types.singleAbstractMethod(Types.named(\"Fax\")).getName(), \"Fax's method\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"basic-printer-only-prints\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void basicPrinterOnlyPrints() {\n        Class<?> basic = Types.named(\"BasicPrinter\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.named(\"Printer\").isAssignableFrom(basic), \"BasicPrinter should be a Printer\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!Types.named(\"DocScanner\").isAssignableFrom(basic),\n            \"BasicPrinter cannot scan, so it should not be a DocScanner\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!Types.named(\"Fax\").isAssignableFrom(basic),\n            \"BasicPrinter cannot fax, so it should not be a Fax\");\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"BasicPrinter\").mentions(\"UnsupportedOperationException\"),\n            \"BasicPrinter still has methods it cannot honour\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"multifunction-plays-all-roles\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void multifunctionPlaysAllRoles() {\n        Class<?> m = Types.named(\"MultiFunction\");\n        for (String role : List.of(\"Printer\", \"DocScanner\", \"Fax\")) {\n            Expect.isTrue(Types.named(role).isAssignableFrom(m), \"MultiFunction should be a \" + role);\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"office-asks-for-roles\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void officeAsksForRoles() {\n        Class<?> office = Types.named(\"Office\");\n        Method print = Types.staticMethod(office, \"printAll\", Types.named(\"Printer\"), List.class);\n        Method scan = Types.staticMethod(office, \"digitise\", Types.named(\"DocScanner\"));\n        Method fax = Types.staticMethod(office, \"send\", Types.named(\"Fax\"), String.class, String.class);\n        Expect.equal(int.class, print.getReturnType(), \"printAll's return type\");\n        Expect.equal(String.class, scan.getReturnType(), \"digitise's return type\");\n        Expect.equal(void.class, fax.getReturnType(), \"send's return type\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Split the fat Machine into roles"},{"checks":[{"id":"place-returns-receipt","kind":"behaviour","title":"The receipt is unchanged"},{"id":"confirmation-goes-over-smtp","kind":"behaviour","title":"Confirmations still reach SMTP"},{"id":"port-interface","kind":"design","title":"Notifier is a one-method interface"},{"id":"service-does-not-know-smtp","kind":"design","title":"OrderService does not mention SmtpClient"},{"id":"service-takes-its-port","kind":"design","title":"OrderService receives a final Notifier"},{"id":"any-notifier-works","kind":"design","title":"OrderService accepts a Notifier it has never seen"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The business rule (\"confirm the order\") should not depend on how the mail goes out. Invert it: the rule states what it needs, and the mail library adapts to that.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Declare `Notifier` next to `OrderService`. Pass it through the constructor. Write `SmtpNotifier implements Notifier` that wraps an `SmtpClient`, and build the pair inside `Orders.place`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The adapter and the wiring:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["final class SmtpNotifier implements Notifier {","    private final SmtpClient smtp;","    SmtpNotifier(SmtpClient smtp) { this.smtp = smtp; }","    public void notify(String c, String m) { smtp.send(c, m); }","}","// Orders.place: new OrderService(new SmtpNotifier(new SmtpClient()))"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"dip","kind":"refactor","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Orders.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nfinal class SmtpClient {\n    static final List<String> WIRE = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    void send(String to, String body) { WIRE.add(to + \": \" + body); }\n}\n\ninterface Notifier {\n    void notify(String customer, String message);\n}\n\nfinal class SmtpNotifier implements Notifier {\n    private final SmtpClient smtp;\n\n    SmtpNotifier(SmtpClient smtp) { this.smtp = smtp; }\n\n    public void notify(String customer, String message) {\n        smtp.send(customer, message);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class OrderService {\n    private final Notifier notifier;\n\n    OrderService(Notifier notifier) { this.notifier = notifier; }\n\n    String place(String customer) {\n        notifier.notify(customer, \"Order confirmed\");\n        return \"placed for \" + customer;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Orders {\n    private Orders() { }\n\n    static String place(String customer) {\n        return new OrderService(new SmtpNotifier(new SmtpClient()))\n            .place(customer);\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Orders.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// Stands in for a real mail library: \"sending\" appends to WIRE.\nfinal class SmtpClient {\n    static final List<String> WIRE = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    void send(String to, String body) { WIRE.add(to + \": \" + body); }\n}\n\n// The policy class is welded to one delivery mechanism.\nfinal class OrderService {\n    private final SmtpClient smtp = new SmtpClient();\n\n    String place(String customer) {\n        smtp.send(customer, \"Order confirmed\");\n        return \"placed for \" + customer;\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use this entry point. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Orders {\n    private Orders() { }\n\n    static String place(String customer) {\n        return new OrderService().place(customer);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`OrderService` does `new SmtpClient()`, so it cannot run without the mail library.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Let the policy own an abstraction and let the detail implement it. `Orders.place(customer)` must still return the same receipt and still put the same confirmation on `SmtpClient.WIRE`.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `interface Notifier` with `void notify(String customer, String message)`.","`OrderService(Notifier)` keeps `String place(String customer)` and never mentions `SmtpClient`.","Add an adapter that implements `Notifier` over `SmtpClient`; wire it in `Orders.place`.","`SmtpClient` itself stays as it is."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"DipKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass DipKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"place-returns-receipt\")\n    void placeReturnsReceipt() {\n        SmtpClient.WIRE.clear();\n        Expect.equal(\"placed for ann@x.io\", Orders.place(\"ann@x.io\"), \"Orders.place\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"confirmation-goes-over-smtp\")\n    void confirmationGoesOverSmtp() {\n        SmtpClient.WIRE.clear();\n        Orders.place(\"ann@x.io\");\n        Orders.place(\"bob@x.io\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ann@x.io: Order confirmed\", \"bob@x.io: Order confirmed\"),\n            SmtpClient.WIRE, \"what reached the SMTP client\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"port-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void portInterface() {\n        Class<?> port = Types.named(\"Notifier\");\n        Expect.isTrue(port.isInterface(), \"Notifier should be an interface\");\n        Method m = Types.singleAbstractMethod(port);\n        Expect.equal(\"notify\", m.getName(), \"the method name\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(String.class, String.class), List.of(m.getParameterTypes()), \"notify's parameters\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-does-not-know-smtp\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void serviceDoesNotKnowSmtp() {\n        var service = Source.type(\"OrderService\");\n        Expect.none(service.mentions(\"SmtpClient\"), \"OrderService still refers to SmtpClient\");\n        Expect.none(service.news(\"SmtpNotifier\"), \"OrderService still builds its own notifier\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-takes-its-port\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void serviceTakesItsPort() {\n        Class<?> notifier = Types.named(\"Notifier\");\n        Class<?> service = Types.named(\"OrderService\");\n        var field = Types.onlyFieldOfType(service, notifier);\n        Expect.isTrue(java.lang.reflect.Modifier.isFinal(field.getModifiers()),\n            \"OrderService.\" + field.getName() + \" should be final\");\n        Types.constructor(service, notifier);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"any-notifier-works\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void anyNotifierWorks() throws Throwable {\n        SmtpClient.WIRE.clear();\n        Class<?> notifier = Types.named(\"Notifier\");\n        List<List<Object>> calls = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object spy = Types.implement(notifier, args -> { calls.add(List.of(args)); return null; });\n        Object service = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"OrderService\"), notifier), spy);\n        Object receipt = Types.call(Types.method(service.getClass(), \"place\", String.class), service, \"cy@x.io\");\n        Expect.equal(\"placed for cy@x.io\", receipt, \"the receipt\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(List.of(\"cy@x.io\", \"Order confirmed\")), calls, \"what the injected Notifier received\");\n        Expect.isTrue(SmtpClient.WIRE.isEmpty(), \"the service still reached SMTP behind the Notifier's back\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Make OrderService depend on a port, not SMTP"},{"checks":[{"id":"add-counts-each-offer","kind":"behaviour","title":"add counts every offer"},{"id":"add-all-counts-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"addAll counts each element once"},{"id":"still-a-set","kind":"behaviour","title":"It still behaves as a Set"},{"id":"no-hashset-inheritance","kind":"design","title":"CountingSet does not extend HashSet"},{"id":"wraps-any-set","kind":"design","title":"CountingSet wraps any Set it is given"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The bug lives in `HashSet`, which calls `add` from `addAll`. A subclass depends on that private detail. Hold a set instead of being one.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep a `private final Set<E> inner`. Count in `add`, make `addAll` loop over its argument calling your own `add`, and forward everything else. Extending `AbstractSet` saves most of the boilerplate.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The core of it:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["final class CountingSet<E> extends AbstractSet<E> {","    private final Set<E> inner;","    CountingSet() { this(new HashSet<>()); }","    @Override public boolean add(E e) { added++; return inner.add(e); }","    @Override public int size() { return inner.size(); }","    @Override public Iterator<E> iterator() { return inner.iterator(); }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"composition-over-inheritance","kind":"fix","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"CountingSet.java","source":"import java.util.AbstractSet;\nimport java.util.Collection;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.Iterator;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\nfinal class CountingSet<E> extends AbstractSet<E> {\n    private final Set<E> inner;\n    private int added;\n\n    CountingSet() { this(new HashSet<>()); }\n\n    CountingSet(Set<E> inner) { this.inner = inner; }\n\n    @Override public boolean add(E e) {\n        added++;\n        return inner.add(e);\n    }\n\n    @Override public boolean addAll(Collection<? extends E> c) {\n        boolean changed = false;\n        for (E e : c) {\n            changed |= add(e);\n        }\n        return changed;\n    }\n\n    @Override public boolean remove(Object o) { return inner.remove(o); }\n    @Override public boolean contains(Object o) { return inner.contains(o); }\n    @Override public void clear() { inner.clear(); }\n    @Override public int size() { return inner.size(); }\n    @Override public Iterator<E> iterator() { return inner.iterator(); }\n\n    int added() { return added; }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"CountingSet.java","source":"import java.util.Collection;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\n\n// Counts every element offered to the set, so the metrics can chart traffic.\n// Bug: addAll(List.of(\"a\", \"b\")) reports 4.\n@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nclass CountingSet<E> extends HashSet<E> {\n    private int added;\n\n    @Override public boolean add(E e) {\n        added++;\n        return super.add(e);\n    }\n\n    @Override public boolean addAll(Collection<? extends E> c) {\n        added += c.size();\n        return super.addAll(c);\n    }\n\n    int added() { return added; }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`CountingSet.addAll(List.of(\"a\", \"b\"))` reports 4 additions, not 2.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`HashSet.addAll` calls `add` internally, so the subclass counts twice, and patching the arithmetic would break on the next JDK. Stop inheriting the implementation: wrap a `Set` and forward to it.","type":"p"},{"items":["`added()` counts every element offered through `add` or `addAll`, duplicates included.","`CountingSet<E>` is still a `Set<E>` with a no-arg constructor, and no longer extends `HashSet`.","Add `CountingSet(Set<E> inner)`; all storage, ordering and equality come from `inner`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"CompositionKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.TreeSet;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass CompositionKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"add-counts-each-offer\")\n    void addCountsEachOffer() {\n        CountingSet<String> s = new CountingSet<>();\n        s.add(\"a\");\n        s.add(\"a\");\n        s.add(\"b\");\n        Expect.equal(3, s.added(), \"added() after three adds, one of them a duplicate\");\n        Expect.equal(2, s.size(), \"size after the same adds\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"add-all-counts-once\")\n    void addAllCountsOnce() {\n        CountingSet<String> s = new CountingSet<>();\n        s.addAll(List.of(\"a\", \"b\"));\n        Expect.equal(2, s.added(), \"added() after addAll of two elements\");\n        s.addAll(List.of(\"b\", \"c\", \"d\"));\n        Expect.equal(5, s.added(), \"added() after a second addAll of three, one a duplicate\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"still-a-set\")\n    void stillASet() {\n        Set<String> s = new CountingSet<>();\n        s.addAll(List.of(\"a\", \"b\"));\n        Expect.isTrue(s.contains(\"a\") && !s.contains(\"z\"), \"contains\");\n        Expect.isTrue(s.remove(\"a\") && s.size() == 1, \"remove\");\n        s.clear();\n        Expect.isTrue(s.isEmpty(), \"clear\");\n        Expect.equal(Set.of(), s, \"equality with an empty set\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-hashset-inheritance\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noHashsetInheritance() {\n        Class<?> c = Types.named(\"CountingSet\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!java.util.HashSet.class.isAssignableFrom(c),\n            \"CountingSet still extends HashSet, so it inherits how HashSet implements addAll\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"wraps-any-set\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void wrapsAnySet() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> c = Types.named(\"CountingSet\");\n        Set<String> tree = new TreeSet<>();\n        Object wrapper = Types.create(Types.constructor(c, Set.class), tree);\n        @SuppressWarnings(\"unchecked\")\n        Set<String> s = (Set<String>) wrapper;\n        s.addAll(List.of(\"b\", \"a\"));\n        Expect.equal(Set.of(\"a\", \"b\"), tree, \"the wrapped set should receive the elements\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a\", \"b\"), List.copyOf(s), \"iteration should follow the wrapped TreeSet\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Fix the double-counting set by wrapping it"},{"checks":[{"id":"total-sums","kind":"behaviour","title":"total still sums"},{"id":"lengths-maps-words","kind":"behaviour","title":"lengths still maps words to sizes"},{"id":"tally-records","kind":"behaviour","title":"Tally still records in order"},{"id":"total-accepts-any-collection","kind":"design","title":"total accepts a List, a Set and a Deque"},{"id":"lengths-accepts-any-collection","kind":"design","title":"lengths accepts a Set"},{"id":"signatures-name-no-concrete-class","kind":"design","title":"No signature names a concrete collection"},{"id":"lengths-returns-an-interface","kind":"design","title":"lengths returns Map"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Ask of each method: what does it actually do with the argument? Both only loop over it. That loop is the capability to ask for.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Parameters that are only iterated become `Collection` (or `Iterable`). Return types and fields become `Map` and `List`. The `new ArrayList<>()` and `new HashMap<>()` calls stay, because something must choose a class.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Only the left-hand types change:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["static int total(Collection<Integer> xs) { ... }","static Map<String, Integer> lengths(Collection<String> words) {","    Map<String, Integer> out = new HashMap<>();","    ...","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"program-to-interface","kind":"refactor","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Stats.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Collection;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nfinal class Stats {\n    private Stats() { }\n\n    static int total(Collection<Integer> xs) {\n        int sum = 0;\n        for (int x : xs) {\n            sum += x;\n        }\n        return sum;\n    }\n\n    static Map<String, Integer> lengths(Collection<String> words) {\n        Map<String, Integer> out = new HashMap<>();\n        for (String w : words) {\n            out.put(w, w.length());\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Tally {\n    private final List<Integer> history = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    void record(int x) { history.add(x); }\n\n    List<Integer> history() { return history; }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Stats.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\n\n// Every signature names a concrete collection class, so callers must too.\nfinal class Stats {\n    private Stats() { }\n\n    static int total(ArrayList<Integer> xs) {\n        int sum = 0;\n        for (int x : xs) {\n            sum += x;\n        }\n        return sum;\n    }\n\n    static HashMap<String, Integer> lengths(ArrayList<String> words) {\n        HashMap<String, Integer> out = new HashMap<>();\n        for (String w : words) {\n            out.put(w, w.length());\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Tally {\n    private final ArrayList<Integer> history = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    void record(int x) { history.add(x); }\n\n    ArrayList<Integer> history() { return history; }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Stats` and `Tally` force every caller onto `ArrayList` and `HashMap`.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Change the declarations, not the logic, so each one asks for the weakest type that still works. Results must stay identical for the lists the callers pass today.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Stats.total(Collection<Integer>)` and `Stats.lengths(Collection<String>)`, which both only iterate.","`Stats.lengths` returns `Map<String, Integer>`.","`Tally` stores and returns a `List<Integer>` from `history()`.","No method or field of `Stats` or `Tally` names `ArrayList`, `HashMap` or another concrete collection."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ProgramToInterfaceKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Collection;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeSet;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ProgramToInterfaceKataTest {\n    static final List<Class<?>> CONCRETE = List.of(ArrayList.class, java.util.LinkedList.class,\n        java.util.HashMap.class, java.util.TreeMap.class, java.util.LinkedHashMap.class,\n        java.util.HashSet.class, java.util.TreeSet.class, java.util.LinkedHashSet.class,\n        java.util.ArrayDeque.class);\n\n    @Check(id = \"total-sums\")\n    void totalSums() {\n        ArrayList<Integer> xs = new ArrayList<>(List.of(3, 4, 5));\n        Expect.equal(12, Stats.total(xs), \"total of 3, 4, 5\");\n        Expect.equal(0, Stats.total(new ArrayList<>()), \"total of nothing\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"lengths-maps-words\")\n    void lengthsMapsWords() {\n        ArrayList<String> words = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"kata\", \"ox\", \"kata\"));\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"kata\", 4, \"ox\", 2), Stats.lengths(words), \"lengths\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"tally-records\")\n    void tallyRecords() {\n        Tally t = new Tally();\n        t.record(2);\n        t.record(7);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(2, 7), List.copyOf(t.history()), \"the recorded history\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"total-accepts-any-collection\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void totalAcceptsAnyCollection() throws Throwable {\n        Method total = Types.staticMethod(Types.named(\"Stats\"), \"total\", Collection.class);\n        Expect.equal(6, Types.call(total, null, List.of(1, 2, 3)), \"total of an immutable List\");\n        Expect.equal(6, Types.call(total, null, new TreeSet<>(List.of(1, 2, 3))), \"total of a TreeSet\");\n        Expect.equal(6, Types.call(total, null, new ArrayDeque<>(List.of(1, 2, 3))), \"total of an ArrayDeque\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"lengths-accepts-any-collection\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void lengthsAcceptsAnyCollection() throws Throwable {\n        Method lengths = Types.staticMethod(Types.named(\"Stats\"), \"lengths\", Collection.class);\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"ab\", 2, \"c\", 1), Types.call(lengths, null, new TreeSet<>(List.of(\"ab\", \"c\"))),\n            \"lengths of a TreeSet\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"signatures-name-no-concrete-class\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void signaturesNameNoConcreteClass() {\n        List<String> offenders = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (String name : List.of(\"Stats\", \"Tally\")) {\n            Class<?> c = Types.named(name);\n            for (Method m : c.getDeclaredMethods()) {\n                if (m.isSynthetic()) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                if (CONCRETE.contains(m.getReturnType())) {\n                    offenders.add(name + \".\" + m.getName() + \" returns \" + m.getReturnType().getSimpleName());\n                }\n                for (Class<?> p : m.getParameterTypes()) {\n                    if (CONCRETE.contains(p)) {\n                        offenders.add(name + \".\" + m.getName() + \" takes \" + p.getSimpleName());\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            for (var f : c.getDeclaredFields()) {\n                if (CONCRETE.contains(f.getType())) {\n                    offenders.add(name + \".\" + f.getName() + \" is declared as \" + f.getType().getSimpleName());\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(offenders.isEmpty(), \"Declare the capability, not the class: \" + offenders);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"lengths-returns-an-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void lengthsReturnsAnInterface() {\n        Method lengths = Types.staticMethod(Types.named(\"Stats\"), \"lengths\", Collection.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(lengths.getReturnType().isInterface() && Map.class.isAssignableFrom(lengths.getReturnType()),\n            \"lengths should return Map, not \" + lengths.getReturnType().getSimpleName());\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isStatic(lengths.getModifiers()), \"lengths should stay static\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Declare capabilities, not collection classes"},{"checks":[{"id":"withdraw-within-balance","kind":"behaviour","title":"Withdrawing within the balance works"},{"id":"overdraft-allowed","kind":"behaviour","title":"The overdraft is usable"},{"id":"rejected-withdrawal-changes-nothing","kind":"behaviour","title":"A refused withdrawal changes nothing"},{"id":"transfer-moves-money","kind":"behaviour","title":"A transfer moves the money"},{"id":"failed-transfer-changes-nothing","kind":"behaviour","title":"A refused transfer changes nothing"},{"id":"account-owns-the-rules","kind":"design","title":"Account offers withdraw and deposit"},{"id":"no-raw-state-exposed","kind":"design","title":"Account no longer exposes setBalance or the overdraft"},{"id":"teller-does-not-ask","kind":"design","title":"Teller never asks for state"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Count how many times `Teller` reaches into `Account` for numbers it then computes with. The rule \"can this be afforded?\" is knowledge about the account, so it belongs inside it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Give `Account` `withdraw(long)` that checks and mutates itself, and `deposit(long)`. `Teller.withdraw` becomes one delegating call, and `transfer` tells one account to withdraw and the other to deposit.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The rule moves, unchanged:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["boolean withdraw(long amount) {","    if (amount > balance + overdraft) return false;","    balance -= amount;","    return true;","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"tell-dont-ask","kind":"refactor","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Accounts.java","source":"final class Account {\n    private final long overdraft;\n    private long balance;\n\n    Account(long balance, long overdraft) {\n        this.balance = balance;\n        this.overdraft = overdraft;\n    }\n\n    long getBalance() { return balance; }\n\n    boolean withdraw(long amount) {\n        if (amount > balance + overdraft) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        balance -= amount;\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    void deposit(long amount) { balance += amount; }\n}\n\nfinal class Teller {\n    boolean withdraw(Account a, long amount) {\n        return a.withdraw(amount);\n    }\n\n    boolean transfer(Account from, Account to, long amount) {\n        if (from.withdraw(amount)) {\n            to.deposit(amount);\n            return true;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Accounts.java","source":"// Teller asks for the data, decides, then writes the result back.\nfinal class Account {\n    private final long overdraft;\n    private long balance;\n\n    Account(long balance, long overdraft) {\n        this.balance = balance;\n        this.overdraft = overdraft;\n    }\n\n    long getBalance() { return balance; }\n    void setBalance(long balance) { this.balance = balance; }\n    long getOverdraft() { return overdraft; }\n}\n\nfinal class Teller {\n    boolean withdraw(Account a, long amount) {\n        if (a.getBalance() + a.getOverdraft() >= amount) {\n            a.setBalance(a.getBalance() - amount);\n            return true;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    boolean transfer(Account from, Account to, long amount) {\n        if (withdraw(from, amount)) {\n            to.setBalance(to.getBalance() + amount);\n            return true;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Teller` reads an account's balance and overdraft, decides, then writes the new balance back.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Move the rule to where the data lives, so no caller can forget it. `Teller.withdraw` and `Teller.transfer` must return and change exactly what they do now, including leaving everything untouched when they refuse.","type":"p"},{"items":["`boolean Account.withdraw(long amount)`: false and no change when `amount` exceeds balance plus overdraft.","`void Account.deposit(long amount)`.","Remove `setBalance` and `getOverdraft`; keep `getBalance()` for reading.","`Teller` keeps its two methods but never reads or writes account state."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"TellDontAskKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass TellDontAskKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"withdraw-within-balance\")\n    void withdrawWithinBalance() {\n        Account a = new Account(100, 0);\n        Expect.isTrue(new Teller().withdraw(a, 40), \"a withdrawal within the balance should succeed\");\n        Expect.equal(60L, a.getBalance(), \"balance after withdrawing 40\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"overdraft-allowed\")\n    void overdraftAllowed() {\n        Account a = new Account(100, 50);\n        Expect.isTrue(new Teller().withdraw(a, 150), \"100 plus a 50 overdraft covers 150\");\n        Expect.equal(-50L, a.getBalance(), \"balance after using the overdraft\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rejected-withdrawal-changes-nothing\")\n    void rejectedWithdrawalChangesNothing() {\n        Account a = new Account(100, 50);\n        Expect.isTrue(!new Teller().withdraw(a, 151), \"151 exceeds balance plus overdraft\");\n        Expect.equal(100L, a.getBalance(), \"balance after a rejected withdrawal\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"transfer-moves-money\")\n    void transferMovesMoney() {\n        Account from = new Account(100, 0);\n        Account to = new Account(5, 0);\n        Expect.isTrue(new Teller().transfer(from, to, 70), \"the transfer should succeed\");\n        Expect.equal(30L, from.getBalance(), \"source balance\");\n        Expect.equal(75L, to.getBalance(), \"target balance\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"failed-transfer-changes-nothing\")\n    void failedTransferChangesNothing() {\n        Account from = new Account(10, 0);\n        Account to = new Account(5, 0);\n        Expect.isTrue(!new Teller().transfer(from, to, 11), \"the transfer should be refused\");\n        Expect.equal(10L, from.getBalance(), \"source balance\");\n        Expect.equal(5L, to.getBalance(), \"target balance\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"account-owns-the-rules\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void accountOwnsTheRules() {\n        Class<?> account = Types.named(\"Account\");\n        Method withdraw = Types.method(account, \"withdraw\", long.class);\n        Expect.equal(boolean.class, withdraw.getReturnType(), \"Account.withdraw's return type\");\n        Types.method(account, \"deposit\", long.class);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-raw-state-exposed\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noRawStateExposed() {\n        List<String> leaks = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (Method m : Types.named(\"Account\").getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            String n = m.getName();\n            if (n.equals(\"setBalance\") || n.equals(\"getOverdraft\") || n.equals(\"overdraft\")) {\n                leaks.add(n);\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(leaks.isEmpty(), \"Account still hands out its internals: \" + leaks);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"teller-does-not-ask\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void tellerDoesNotAsk() {\n        var teller = Source.type(\"Teller\");\n        Expect.none(teller.calls(\"getBalance\"), \"Teller still asks for the balance\");\n        Expect.none(teller.calls(\"getOverdraft\"), \"Teller still asks for the overdraft\");\n        Expect.none(teller.calls(\"setBalance\"), \"Teller still writes the balance back\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Tell the Account instead of asking it"},{"checks":[{"id":"csv-output","kind":"behaviour","title":"CSV output is unchanged"},{"id":"json-output","kind":"behaviour","title":"JSON output is unchanged"},{"id":"empty-totals","kind":"behaviour","title":"Empty totals render as before"},{"id":"unknown-format","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unknown formats are rejected"},{"id":"report-has-factory-method","kind":"design","title":"Report is abstract with one Sink factory method"},{"id":"render-uses-the-hook","kind":"design","title":"render gets its Sink from the factory method"},{"id":"report-does-not-choose-a-sink","kind":"design","title":"Report never creates a concrete Sink"},{"id":"report-keeps-no-format","kind":"design","title":"Report no longer stores a format name"},{"id":"format-lookup-in-reports","kind":"design","title":"Reports.forFormat picks the Report"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Find what varies: which `Sink` gets created. The rest of `render` is the same for every format. Separate the step that varies from the steps that do not.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Declare a `protected abstract Sink createSink()` in an abstract `Report`, keep `render` as the fixed algorithm that calls it, and move each `new` into `CsvReport` or `JsonReport`. Choose the subclass in `Reports`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The creator calls its own hook:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["abstract class Report {","    protected abstract Sink createSink();","    final String render(Map<String, Integer> totals) {","        Sink sink = createSink();","        totals.forEach(sink::write);","        return sink.close();","    }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"factory-method","kind":"refactor","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Report.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\ninterface Sink {\n    void write(String name, int value);\n    String close();\n}\n\nfinal class CsvSink implements Sink {\n    private final List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();\n    public void write(String name, int value) { rows.add(name + \",\" + value); }\n    public String close() { return String.join(\"\\n\", rows); }\n}\n\nfinal class JsonSink implements Sink {\n    private final List<String> fields = new ArrayList<>();\n    public void write(String name, int value) {\n        fields.add(\"\\\"\" + name + \"\\\":\" + value);\n    }\n    public String close() { return \"{\" + String.join(\",\", fields) + \"}\"; }\n}\n\nabstract class Report {\n    protected abstract Sink createSink();\n\n    final String render(Map<String, Integer> totals) {\n        Sink sink = createSink();\n        totals.forEach(sink::write);\n        return sink.close();\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class CsvReport extends Report {\n    protected Sink createSink() { return new CsvSink(); }\n}\n\nfinal class JsonReport extends Report {\n    protected Sink createSink() { return new JsonSink(); }\n}\n\nfinal class Reports {\n    private Reports() { }\n\n    static Report forFormat(String format) {\n        return switch (format) {\n            case \"csv\" -> new CsvReport();\n            case \"json\" -> new JsonReport();\n            default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(\n                \"unknown format: \" + format);\n        };\n    }\n\n    static String render(String format, Map<String, Integer> totals) {\n        return forFormat(format).render(totals);\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Report.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\ninterface Sink {\n    void write(String name, int value);\n    String close();\n}\n\nfinal class CsvSink implements Sink {\n    private final List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();\n    public void write(String name, int value) { rows.add(name + \",\" + value); }\n    public String close() { return String.join(\"\\n\", rows); }\n}\n\nfinal class JsonSink implements Sink {\n    private final List<String> fields = new ArrayList<>();\n    public void write(String name, int value) {\n        fields.add(\"\\\"\" + name + \"\\\":\" + value);\n    }\n    public String close() { return \"{\" + String.join(\",\", fields) + \"}\"; }\n}\n\n// Every new export format is another branch in this class.\nfinal class Report {\n    private final String format;\n\n    Report(String format) { this.format = format; }\n\n    String render(Map<String, Integer> totals) {\n        Sink sink;\n        if (format.equals(\"csv\")) {\n            sink = new CsvSink();\n        } else if (format.equals(\"json\")) {\n            sink = new JsonSink();\n        } else {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown format: \" + format);\n        }\n        totals.forEach(sink::write);\n        return sink.close();\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use this entry point. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Reports {\n    private Reports() { }\n\n    static String render(String format, Map<String, Integer> totals) {\n        return new Report(format).render(totals);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Report` decides which `Sink` to build with an `if` chain on a format name.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Refactor it into a **factory method**. `Reports.render(format, totals)` must keep returning exactly what it returns now, and `Sink`, `CsvSink` and `JsonSink` stay as they are.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Report` becomes `abstract` with one abstract method returning a `Sink`, and a `render(Map<String, Integer>)` that calls it.","Add one subclass per format: `CsvReport` and `JsonReport`.","`Reports.forFormat(String)` returns the right `Report`; unknown formats throw `IllegalArgumentException`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"FactoryMethodKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass FactoryMethodKataTest {\n    static final Map<String, Integer> TOTALS =\n        new TreeMap<>(Map.of(\"eu\", 5, \"us\", 7));\n\n    static Method hookOf(Class<?> report) {\n        java.util.List<Method> abstracts = new java.util.ArrayList<>();\n        for (Method m : report.getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            if (Modifier.isAbstract(m.getModifiers())) abstracts.add(m);\n        }\n        Expect.equal(1, abstracts.size(), \"abstract methods declared by Report\");\n        return abstracts.get(0);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"csv-output\")\n    void csvOutput() {\n        Expect.equal(\"eu,5\\nus,7\", Reports.render(\"csv\", TOTALS), \"csv report\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"json-output\")\n    void jsonOutput() {\n        Expect.equal(\"{\\\"eu\\\":5,\\\"us\\\":7}\", Reports.render(\"json\", TOTALS), \"json report\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"empty-totals\")\n    void emptyTotals() {\n        Expect.equal(\"\", Reports.render(\"csv\", Map.of()), \"empty csv\");\n        Expect.equal(\"{}\", Reports.render(\"json\", Map.of()), \"empty json\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-format\")\n    void unknownFormat() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> Reports.render(\"xml\", TOTALS), \"an unknown format\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"report-has-factory-method\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void reportHasFactoryMethod() {\n        Class<?> report = Types.named(\"Report\");\n        Class<?> sink = Types.named(\"Sink\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isAbstract(report.getModifiers()),\n            \"Report should be abstract: subclasses decide which Sink to create\");\n        Method hook = hookOf(report);\n        Expect.equal(sink, hook.getReturnType(),\n            \"the return type of Report.\" + hook.getName());\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"render-uses-the-hook\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void renderUsesTheHook() {\n        Method hook = hookOf(Types.named(\"Report\"));\n        var render = Source.type(\"Report\").method(\"render\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!render.calls(hook.getName()).isEmpty(),\n            \"Report.render should obtain its Sink by calling \" + hook.getName() + \"()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"report-does-not-choose-a-sink\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void reportDoesNotChooseASink() {\n        var report = Source.type(\"Report\");\n        Expect.none(report.news(\"CsvSink\"), \"Report still creates a CsvSink itself\");\n        Expect.none(report.news(\"JsonSink\"), \"Report still creates a JsonSink itself\");\n        Expect.none(report.comparedStrings(), \"Report still compares format names\");\n        Expect.none(report.switches(), \"Report still switches on the format\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"report-keeps-no-format\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void reportKeepsNoFormat() {\n        Class<?> report = Types.named(\"Report\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(report, String.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"Report should no longer store the format name\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"format-lookup-in-reports\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void formatLookupInReports() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> report = Types.named(\"Report\");\n        Method forFormat = Types.staticMethod(Types.named(\"Reports\"), \"forFormat\", String.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(report.isAssignableFrom(forFormat.getReturnType()),\n            \"Reports.forFormat should return a Report\");\n        Expect.isTrue(report.isInstance(Types.call(forFormat, null, \"csv\")),\n            \"csv should resolve to a Report\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> Types.call(forFormat, null, \"xml\"), \"an unknown format in forFormat\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Let each report choose its own sink"},{"checks":[{"id":"local-family","kind":"behaviour","title":"LocalInfra produces local products"},{"id":"cloud-family","kind":"behaviour","title":"CloudInfra produces cloud products"},{"id":"cloud-needs-a-bucket","kind":"behaviour","title":"CloudInfra rejects a blank bucket"},{"id":"uploader-follows-its-family","kind":"behaviour","title":"Uploader uses the family it is given"},{"id":"env-selects-a-family","kind":"behaviour","title":"Infras.forEnv picks a family"},{"id":"families-implement-the-factory","kind":"design","title":"Both families implement Infra"},{"id":"uploader-holds-only-the-factory","kind":"design","title":"Uploader holds a private final Infra"},{"id":"uploader-ignores-concrete-families","kind":"design","title":"Uploader never names a concrete family"},{"id":"families-do-not-mix","kind":"design","title":"Each family stays within itself"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The point is consistency: a blob store and a bus must come from the same environment. The thing that varies is the whole family, so one object should hand out all of its products.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`LocalInfra` and `CloudInfra` each return their own `BlobStore` and `EventBus` (lambdas work, since both are single-method). `Uploader` stores only an `Infra` and calls `blobs()` and `events()`. Only `Infras` chooses a family.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The client sees only the factory:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["String upload(String key, String body) {","    String where = infra.blobs().put(key, body);","    return infra.events().publish(\"uploaded\", where);","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"abstract-factory","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Products.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Products.java","source":"interface BlobStore {\n    /** Stores the body and returns where it now lives. */\n    String put(String key, String body);\n}\n\ninterface EventBus {\n    /** Publishes the message and returns the delivery receipt. */\n    String publish(String topic, String message);\n}\n\n/** One consistent family of products. */\ninterface Infra {\n    BlobStore blobs();\n    EventBus events();\n}\n"},{"name":"Infra.java","source":"record LocalInfra() implements Infra {\n    public BlobStore blobs() { return (key, body) -> \"file:/data/\" + key; }\n    public EventBus events() {\n        return (topic, msg) -> \"mem-bus/\" + topic + \": \" + msg;\n    }\n}\n\nrecord CloudInfra(String bucket) implements Infra {\n    CloudInfra {\n        if (bucket == null || bucket.isBlank()) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"bucket\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    public BlobStore blobs() {\n        return (key, body) -> \"s3://\" + bucket + \"/\" + key;\n    }\n    public EventBus events() {\n        return (topic, msg) -> \"sns/\" + topic + \": \" + msg;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Uploader {\n    private final Infra infra;\n\n    Uploader(Infra infra) { this.infra = infra; }\n\n    String upload(String key, String body) {\n        String where = infra.blobs().put(key, body);\n        return infra.events().publish(\"uploaded\", where);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Infras {\n    private Infras() { }\n\n    static Infra forEnv(String env) {\n        return switch (env) {\n            case \"dev\" -> new LocalInfra();\n            case \"prod\" -> new CloudInfra(\"acme-prod\");\n            default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"env: \" + env);\n        };\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Products.java","source":"interface BlobStore {\n    /** Stores the body and returns where it now lives. */\n    String put(String key, String body);\n}\n\ninterface EventBus {\n    /** Publishes the message and returns the delivery receipt. */\n    String publish(String topic, String message);\n}\n\n/** One consistent family of products. */\ninterface Infra {\n    BlobStore blobs();\n    EventBus events();\n}\n"},{"name":"Infra.java","source":"// Family 1: everything on the local machine.\n// put(\"a.csv\", ..)   -> \"file:/data/a.csv\"\n// publish(\"t\", \"m\")  -> \"mem-bus/t: m\"\nrecord LocalInfra() implements Infra {\n    public BlobStore blobs() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n    public EventBus events() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Family 2: everything in the cloud, in one bucket (never blank).\n// put(\"a.csv\", ..)   -> \"s3://<bucket>/a.csv\"\n// publish(\"t\", \"m\")  -> \"sns/t: m\"\nrecord CloudInfra(String bucket) implements Infra {\n    public BlobStore blobs() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n    public EventBus events() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Stores the body, then publishes the location on topic \"uploaded\".\nfinal class Uploader {\n    Uploader(Infra infra) { }\n\n    String upload(String key, String body) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\n// \"dev\" -> LocalInfra, \"prod\" -> CloudInfra(\"acme-prod\"), else IAE.\nfinal class Infras {\n    private Infras() { }\n\n    static Infra forEnv(String env) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Uploader` needs a blob store and an event bus that belong to the same environment.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`BlobStore`, `EventBus` and the **abstract factory** `Infra` are given (read-only). Implement the two families, the client and the selector.","type":"p"},{"items":["`LocalInfra()` and `CloudInfra(String bucket)` implement `Infra`; the comments in `Infra.java` give each product's output. A blank bucket throws `IllegalArgumentException`.","`Uploader(Infra)`: `upload(key, body)` stores the body, then publishes the location on topic `uploaded` and returns the receipt.","`Infras.forEnv(String)`: `dev` is local, `prod` is `CloudInfra(\"acme-prod\")`, anything else throws `IllegalArgumentException`."],"type":"bullets"},{"text":"`Uploader` must never name a concrete family.","type":"p"}],"tests":[{"name":"AbstractFactoryKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass AbstractFactoryKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"local-family\")\n    void localFamily() {\n        Infra infra = new LocalInfra();\n        Expect.equal(\"file:/data/a.csv\", infra.blobs().put(\"a.csv\", \"x\"), \"local blob location\");\n        Expect.equal(\"mem-bus/t: m\", infra.events().publish(\"t\", \"m\"), \"local bus receipt\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cloud-family\")\n    void cloudFamily() {\n        Infra infra = new CloudInfra(\"acme\");\n        Expect.equal(\"s3://acme/a.csv\", infra.blobs().put(\"a.csv\", \"x\"), \"cloud blob location\");\n        Expect.equal(\"sns/t: m\", infra.events().publish(\"t\", \"m\"), \"cloud bus receipt\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cloud-needs-a-bucket\")\n    void cloudNeedsABucket() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> new CloudInfra(\" \"), \"a blank bucket\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> new CloudInfra(null), \"a null bucket\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"uploader-follows-its-family\")\n    void uploaderFollowsItsFamily() {\n        Expect.equal(\"mem-bus/uploaded: file:/data/q3.csv\",\n            new Uploader(new LocalInfra()).upload(\"q3.csv\", \"...\"), \"upload on local infra\");\n        Expect.equal(\"sns/uploaded: s3://acme/q3.csv\",\n            new Uploader(new CloudInfra(\"acme\")).upload(\"q3.csv\", \"...\"), \"upload on cloud infra\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"env-selects-a-family\")\n    void envSelectsAFamily() {\n        Expect.equal(\"mem-bus/uploaded: file:/data/k\",\n            new Uploader(Infras.forEnv(\"dev\")).upload(\"k\", \"\"), \"dev\");\n        Expect.equal(\"sns/uploaded: s3://acme-prod/k\",\n            new Uploader(Infras.forEnv(\"prod\")).upload(\"k\", \"\"), \"prod\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> Infras.forEnv(\"qa\"), \"an unknown env\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"families-implement-the-factory\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void familiesImplementTheFactory() {\n        Class<?> infra = Types.named(\"Infra\");\n        Expect.isTrue(infra.isAssignableFrom(Types.named(\"LocalInfra\")),\n            \"LocalInfra should implement Infra\");\n        Expect.isTrue(infra.isAssignableFrom(Types.named(\"CloudInfra\")),\n            \"CloudInfra should implement Infra\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"uploader-holds-only-the-factory\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void uploaderHoldsOnlyTheFactory() {\n        Class<?> uploader = Types.named(\"Uploader\");\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(uploader, Types.named(\"Infra\"));\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()) && Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n            \"Uploader.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n        Types.constructor(uploader, Types.named(\"Infra\"));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"uploader-ignores-concrete-families\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void uploaderIgnoresConcreteFamilies() {\n        var uploader = Source.type(\"Uploader\");\n        Expect.none(uploader.mentions(\"LocalInfra\"), \"Uploader still names LocalInfra\");\n        Expect.none(uploader.mentions(\"CloudInfra\"), \"Uploader still names CloudInfra\");\n        Expect.none(uploader.instanceofs(), \"Uploader inspects the family's concrete type\");\n        Expect.none(uploader.comparedStrings(), \"Uploader still branches on the environment\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"families-do-not-mix\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void familiesDoNotMix() {\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"LocalInfra\").mentions(\"CloudInfra\"),\n            \"LocalInfra should not touch the cloud family\");\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"CloudInfra\").mentions(\"LocalInfra\"),\n            \"CloudInfra should not touch the local family\");\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"LocalInfra\").mentions(\"sns\"), \"LocalInfra mentions sns\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Local and cloud infrastructure families"},{"checks":[{"id":"defaults","kind":"behaviour","title":"Defaults are GET and 30 seconds"},{"id":"fluent-chain","kind":"behaviour","title":"Every setting reaches the product"},{"id":"headers-keep-order-and-repeats","kind":"behaviour","title":"Headers keep order and repeats"},{"id":"rejects-get-with-body","kind":"behaviour","title":"A GET with a body is rejected"},{"id":"rejects-bad-timeout","kind":"behaviour","title":"Zero or negative timeouts are rejected"},{"id":"rejects-blank-uri","kind":"behaviour","title":"A blank URI is rejected by build()"},{"id":"builder-reusable","kind":"behaviour","title":"A builder can build twice, independently"},{"id":"product-immutable","kind":"design","title":"The product is immutable"},{"id":"defensive-copy","kind":"design","title":"Later builder calls cannot change a product"},{"id":"fluent-returns-builder","kind":"design","title":"Setters return the Builder"},{"id":"no-telescoping-constructor","kind":"design","title":"No telescoping constructors"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Collect the parts one at a time in a mutable helper, validate everything once at the end, and only then create the immutable product.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`Builder` keeps fields with the defaults and a `List<Header>`. Each setter assigns and returns `this`. `build()` validates, then calls the record constructor. Copy the list in the record's compact constructor.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Copy on the way into the product:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["record HttpRequest(String method, String uri, List<Header> headers,","                   String body, Duration timeout) {","    HttpRequest {","        headers = List.copyOf(headers);","    }","    // ...","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"builder","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"HttpRequest.java","source":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord Header(String name, String value) { }\n\nrecord HttpRequest(String method, String uri, List<Header> headers,\n                   String body, Duration timeout) {\n    HttpRequest {\n        headers = List.copyOf(headers);\n    }\n\n    static Builder builder(String uri) { return new Builder(uri); }\n\n    static final class Builder {\n        private final String uri;\n        private String method = \"GET\";\n        private final List<Header> headers = new ArrayList<>();\n        private String body;\n        private Duration timeout = Duration.ofSeconds(30);\n\n        private Builder(String uri) { this.uri = uri; }\n\n        Builder method(String method) { this.method = method; return this; }\n\n        Builder header(String name, String value) {\n            headers.add(new Header(name, value));\n            return this;\n        }\n\n        Builder body(String body) { this.body = body; return this; }\n\n        Builder timeout(Duration timeout) {\n            this.timeout = timeout;\n            return this;\n        }\n\n        HttpRequest build() {\n            if (uri == null || uri.isBlank()) {\n                throw new IllegalStateException(\"blank uri\");\n            }\n            if (timeout == null || timeout.isZero() || timeout.isNegative()) {\n                throw new IllegalStateException(\"timeout must be positive\");\n            }\n            if (method.equals(\"GET\") && body != null) {\n                throw new IllegalStateException(\"GET with a body\");\n            }\n            return new HttpRequest(method, uri, headers, body, timeout);\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"HttpRequest.java","source":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord Header(String name, String value) { }\n\nrecord HttpRequest(String method, String uri, List<Header> headers,\n                   String body, Duration timeout) {\n\n    // Starts a builder. Never throws: validation belongs to build().\n    static Builder builder(String uri) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    static final class Builder {\n        private Builder(String uri) { }\n\n        Builder method(String method) {\n            throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n        }\n\n        Builder header(String name, String value) {\n            throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n        }\n\n        Builder body(String body) {\n            throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n        }\n\n        Builder timeout(Duration timeout) {\n            throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n        }\n\n        HttpRequest build() {\n            throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A request has many optional parts and some illegal combinations. Make a **builder** that only produces valid, immutable requests.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`HttpRequest` is a record; `HttpRequest.builder(String uri)` returns its nested `Builder`. Fill in the signatures already declared in `HttpRequest.java`:","type":"p"},{"items":["`method`, `header(name, value)` (repeatable, call order kept), `body` and `timeout` all return the builder.","Defaults: method `GET`, timeout 30 seconds, no headers, no body.","`build()` throws `IllegalStateException` for a `GET` with a body, a missing or non-positive timeout, or a blank URI.","Products never change afterwards: not through the builder, not through `headers()`.","The builder can be reused: each `build()` gives an equal, independent request."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"BuilderKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass BuilderKataTest {\n    static HttpRequest.Builder base() {\n        return HttpRequest.builder(\"https://api.local/items\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"defaults\")\n    void defaults() {\n        HttpRequest r = base().build();\n        Expect.equal(\"GET\", r.method(), \"default method\");\n        Expect.equal(\"https://api.local/items\", r.uri(), \"uri\");\n        Expect.equal(Duration.ofSeconds(30), r.timeout(), \"default timeout\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), r.headers(), \"default headers\");\n        Expect.equal(null, r.body(), \"default body\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fluent-chain\")\n    void fluentChain() {\n        HttpRequest r = base().method(\"POST\").body(\"{}\")\n            .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(5)).header(\"X\", \"1\").build();\n        Expect.equal(\"POST\", r.method(), \"method\");\n        Expect.equal(\"{}\", r.body(), \"body\");\n        Expect.equal(Duration.ofSeconds(5), r.timeout(), \"timeout\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new Header(\"X\", \"1\")), r.headers(), \"headers\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"headers-keep-order-and-repeats\")\n    void headersKeepOrderAndRepeats() {\n        HttpRequest r = base().header(\"B\", \"2\").header(\"A\", \"1\")\n            .header(\"B\", \"3\").build();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new Header(\"B\", \"2\"), new Header(\"A\", \"1\"),\n            new Header(\"B\", \"3\")), r.headers(), \"headers in call order\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rejects-get-with-body\")\n    void rejectsGetWithBody() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            () -> base().body(\"x\").build(), \"a GET with a body\");\n        base().method(\"PUT\").body(\"x\").build();\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rejects-bad-timeout\")\n    void rejectsBadTimeout() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            () -> base().timeout(Duration.ZERO).build(), \"a zero timeout\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            () -> base().timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(-1)).build(), \"a negative timeout\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rejects-blank-uri\")\n    void rejectsBlankUri() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            () -> HttpRequest.builder(\"  \").build(), \"a blank uri\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"builder-reusable\")\n    void builderReusable() {\n        HttpRequest.Builder b = base().header(\"A\", \"1\");\n        HttpRequest first = b.build();\n        HttpRequest second = b.build();\n        Expect.equal(first, second, \"two builds from the same builder\");\n        Expect.isTrue(first.headers() != second.headers() || first.headers().isEmpty(),\n            \"the two products should not share a header list\");\n        b.header(\"B\", \"2\");\n        Expect.equal(1, first.headers().size(), \"the first product after the builder moved on\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"product-immutable\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void productImmutable() {\n        for (Field f : HttpRequest.class.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers()) || f.isSynthetic()) continue;\n            int m = f.getModifiers();\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(m) && Modifier.isFinal(m),\n                \"HttpRequest.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n        }\n        List<Header> headers = base().header(\"A\", \"1\").build().headers();\n        Expect.raises(UnsupportedOperationException.class,\n            () -> headers.add(new Header(\"B\", \"2\")), \"adding to HttpRequest.headers()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"defensive-copy\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void defensiveCopy() {\n        HttpRequest.Builder b = base().header(\"A\", \"1\");\n        HttpRequest r = b.build();\n        b.header(\"B\", \"2\").method(\"POST\").body(\"x\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new Header(\"A\", \"1\")), r.headers(), \"headers after the builder changed\");\n        Expect.equal(\"GET\", r.method(), \"method after the builder changed\");\n        Expect.equal(null, r.body(), \"body after the builder changed\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fluent-returns-builder\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void fluentReturnsBuilder() {\n        Class<?> builder = HttpRequest.Builder.class;\n        int seen = 0;\n        for (Method m : builder.getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            if (m.isSynthetic() || Modifier.isPrivate(m.getModifiers())\n                    || Modifier.isStatic(m.getModifiers())) continue;\n            if (m.getName().equals(\"build\")) {\n                Expect.equal(HttpRequest.class, m.getReturnType(), \"the return type of build()\");\n            } else {\n                seen++;\n                Expect.equal(builder, m.getReturnType(),\n                    \"the return type of Builder.\" + m.getName() + \" (so calls can chain)\");\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(seen >= 4, \"Builder should keep method, header, body and timeout\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-telescoping-constructor\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noTelescopingConstructor() {\n        for (Constructor<?> c : HttpRequest.class.getDeclaredConstructors()) {\n            if (!Modifier.isPrivate(c.getModifiers())) {\n                Expect.equal(5, c.getParameterCount(),\n                    \"parameters of a non-private HttpRequest constructor (only the canonical one is allowed)\");\n            }\n        }\n        for (Constructor<?> c : HttpRequest.Builder.class.getDeclaredConstructors()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(c.getModifiers()),\n                \"Builder's constructor should be private: start from HttpRequest.builder(uri)\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Build an immutable HttpRequest"},{"checks":[{"id":"copy-has-the-same-state","kind":"behaviour","title":"A copy carries the same state"},{"id":"learning-on-the-copy-leaves-the-original","kind":"behaviour","title":"Teaching the copy leaves the original alone"},{"id":"learning-on-the-original-leaves-the-copy","kind":"behaviour","title":"Teaching the original leaves the copy alone"},{"id":"constructor-does-not-keep-the-callers-list","kind":"behaviour","title":"The constructor copies its input list"},{"id":"barracks-spawns-independent-units","kind":"behaviour","title":"Spawned units are independent"},{"id":"unknown-kind","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unknown kinds are rejected"},{"id":"copy-returns-unit","kind":"design","title":"copy() returns Unit, not Object"},{"id":"mutable-fields-are-not-shared","kind":"design","title":"No mutable field is shared by a copy"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A copy that reuses the same `List` object is a shallow copy: two references, one list. Ask which fields are mutable objects rather than values.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Give every `Unit` its own `ArrayList`. Do it in the constructor, so it covers both `copy()` and callers that pass in a list they keep using.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Copy at the boundary:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["Unit(String name, int hp, List<String> abilities) {","    this.name = name;","    this.hp = hp;","    this.abilities = new ArrayList<>(abilities);","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"prototype","kind":"fix","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Unit.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\ninterface Prototype<T> {\n    T copy();\n}\n\nfinal class Unit implements Prototype<Unit> {\n    private final String name;\n    private final int hp;\n    private final List<String> abilities;\n\n    Unit(String name, int hp, List<String> abilities) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.hp = hp;\n        this.abilities = new ArrayList<>(abilities);\n    }\n\n    public Unit copy() { return new Unit(name, hp, abilities); }\n\n    Unit learn(String ability) { abilities.add(ability); return this; }\n\n    String name() { return name; }\n    int hp() { return hp; }\n    List<String> abilities() { return List.copyOf(abilities); }\n}\n\nfinal class Barracks {\n    private final Map<String, Unit> prototypes = new HashMap<>();\n\n    void register(String kind, Unit prototype) {\n        prototypes.put(kind, prototype);\n    }\n\n    Unit spawn(String kind) {\n        Unit prototype = prototypes.get(kind);\n        if (prototype == null) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown kind: \" + kind);\n        }\n        return prototype.copy();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Unit.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\ninterface Prototype<T> {\n    T copy();\n}\n\nfinal class Unit implements Prototype<Unit> {\n    private final String name;\n    private final int hp;\n    private final List<String> abilities;\n\n    Unit(String name, int hp, List<String> abilities) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.hp = hp;\n        this.abilities = abilities;\n    }\n\n    // Spawns a new unit from this one.\n    public Unit copy() { return new Unit(name, hp, abilities); }\n\n    Unit learn(String ability) { abilities.add(ability); return this; }\n\n    String name() { return name; }\n    int hp() { return hp; }\n    List<String> abilities() { return List.copyOf(abilities); }\n}\n\n// Registry of ready-made prototypes; every spawn is a fresh copy.\nfinal class Barracks {\n    private final Map<String, Unit> prototypes = new HashMap<>();\n\n    void register(String kind, Unit prototype) {\n        prototypes.put(kind, prototype);\n    }\n\n    Unit spawn(String kind) {\n        Unit prototype = prototypes.get(kind);\n        if (prototype == null) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown kind: \" + kind);\n        }\n        return prototype.copy();\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Spawning a `Unit` from a prototype changes the prototype too.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Unit.copy()` builds a new `Unit`, but the new unit and the old one still share state. A grunt that learns `rage` teaches it to every orc ever spawned.","type":"p"},{"items":["A copy has the same name, hp and abilities as its source, and shares no mutable state with it, in either direction.","A `Unit` never keeps the list its caller passed to the constructor.","Keep the `Prototype<Unit>` contract, `Unit.copy()` returning `Unit`, and `Barracks.spawn(kind)` returning a fresh copy."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"PrototypeKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass PrototypeKataTest {\n    static Unit orc() {\n        return new Unit(\"orc\", 30, new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"slash\")));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"copy-has-the-same-state\")\n    void copyHasTheSameState() {\n        Unit original = orc();\n        Unit copy = original.copy();\n        Expect.isTrue(copy != original, \"copy() should return a new object\");\n        Expect.equal(\"orc\", copy.name(), \"copied name\");\n        Expect.equal(30, copy.hp(), \"copied hp\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"slash\"), copy.abilities(), \"copied abilities\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"learning-on-the-copy-leaves-the-original\")\n    void learningOnTheCopyLeavesTheOriginal() {\n        Unit original = orc();\n        original.copy().learn(\"rage\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"slash\"), original.abilities(),\n            \"the prototype's abilities after its copy learned one\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"learning-on-the-original-leaves-the-copy\")\n    void learningOnTheOriginalLeavesTheCopy() {\n        Unit original = orc();\n        Unit copy = original.copy();\n        original.learn(\"rage\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"slash\"), copy.abilities(),\n            \"the copy's abilities after the original learned one\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"constructor-does-not-keep-the-callers-list\")\n    void constructorDoesNotKeepTheCallersList() {\n        List<String> given = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"slash\"));\n        Unit unit = new Unit(\"orc\", 30, given);\n        given.add(\"rage\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"slash\"), unit.abilities(),\n            \"a unit's abilities after the list it was built from changed\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"barracks-spawns-independent-units\")\n    void barracksSpawnsIndependentUnits() {\n        Barracks barracks = new Barracks();\n        Unit prototype = orc();\n        barracks.register(\"orc\", prototype);\n        Unit grunt = barracks.spawn(\"orc\");\n        Unit elite = barracks.spawn(\"orc\").learn(\"rage\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"slash\"), grunt.abilities(), \"grunt\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"slash\", \"rage\"), elite.abilities(), \"elite\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"slash\"), prototype.abilities(), \"the registered prototype\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-kind\")\n    void unknownKind() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> new Barracks().spawn(\"dragon\"), \"an unknown kind\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"copy-returns-unit\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void copyReturnsUnit() {\n        Class<?> unit = Types.named(\"Unit\");\n        Class<?> contract = Types.named(\"Prototype\");\n        Expect.isTrue(contract.isAssignableFrom(unit), \"Unit should implement Prototype\");\n        Expect.equal(unit, Types.method(unit, \"copy\").getReturnType(),\n            \"the return type of Unit.copy() (callers should not need a cast)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"mutable-fields-are-not-shared\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void mutableFieldsAreNotShared() throws Exception {\n        Unit original = orc();\n        Unit copy = original.copy();\n        for (Field f : Unit.class.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers()) || f.getType().isPrimitive()) continue;\n            f.setAccessible(true);\n            Object a = f.get(original);\n            Object b = f.get(copy);\n            boolean immutable = a instanceof String || a instanceof Number\n                || a != null && a.getClass().getName().startsWith(\"java.util.ImmutableCollections\");\n            Expect.isTrue(immutable || a != b,\n                \"Unit.\" + f.getName() + \" is the same mutable object in the original and its copy\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Make unit copies independent"},{"checks":[{"id":"one-instance-under-contention","kind":"behaviour","title":"Eight racing threads share one instance"},{"id":"same-instance-every-call","kind":"behaviour","title":"get() returns the same object"},{"id":"config-still-works","kind":"behaviour","title":"The configuration still answers"},{"id":"reflection-cannot-make-a-second","kind":"behaviour","title":"Reflection cannot build a second instance"},{"id":"serialization-keeps-identity","kind":"behaviour","title":"Deserialization returns the shared instance"},{"id":"shared-field-is-safe","kind":"design","title":"No racy static instance field"},{"id":"no-open-constructor","kind":"design","title":"Constructors are private"},{"id":"get-is-still-static","kind":"design","title":"get() stays a static method"}],"hints":[[{"text":"There are three separate doors to a second instance: concurrent first calls, the reflection API, and Java serialization. Each needs its own answer. The class loader already makes one of them safe for free.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Put the instance in a private nested `Holder` class so the JVM initializes it once, on first use. Make the constructor refuse a second call, and give the class a `readResolve` that returns the shared instance.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Two guards on the holder idiom:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["private AppConfig() {","    if (Holder.INSTANCE != null) {","        throw new IllegalStateException(\"already created\");","    }","    Probe.constructed();","}","private Object readResolve() { return get(); }"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"singleton","kind":"fix","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Probe.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Probe.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\n// Test seam: keep it as it is. The constructor of AppConfig must call\n// Probe.constructed() exactly once per instance it creates.\nfinal class Probe {\n    static final AtomicInteger CREATED = new AtomicInteger();\n    static volatile Runnable onConstruct = () -> { };\n\n    private Probe() { }\n\n    static void constructed() {\n        onConstruct.run();\n        CREATED.incrementAndGet();\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"AppConfig.java","source":"import java.io.Serializable;\n\nfinal class AppConfig implements Serializable {\n    private static final class Holder {\n        static final AppConfig INSTANCE = new AppConfig();\n    }\n\n    private AppConfig() {\n        if (Holder.INSTANCE != null) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"already created\");\n        }\n        Probe.constructed();\n    }\n\n    static AppConfig get() { return Holder.INSTANCE; }\n\n    String region() { return \"eu-west-1\"; }\n\n    private Object readResolve() { return get(); }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Probe.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\n// Test seam: keep it as it is. The constructor of AppConfig must call\n// Probe.constructed() exactly once per instance it creates.\nfinal class Probe {\n    static final AtomicInteger CREATED = new AtomicInteger();\n    static volatile Runnable onConstruct = () -> { };\n\n    private Probe() { }\n\n    static void constructed() {\n        onConstruct.run();\n        CREATED.incrementAndGet();\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"AppConfig.java","source":"import java.io.Serializable;\n\n// Meant to be the one shared configuration of the process.\nfinal class AppConfig implements Serializable {\n    private static AppConfig instance;\n\n    private AppConfig() { Probe.constructed(); }\n\n    static AppConfig get() {\n        if (instance == null) {\n            instance = new AppConfig();\n        }\n        return instance;\n    }\n\n    String region() { return \"eu-west-1\"; }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"`AppConfig.get()` is supposed to give every thread the same object. It does not.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Three things break the guarantee: threads can race through lazy creation, reflection can call the private constructor, and deserialization quietly makes a new instance. Fix `AppConfig` so that exactly one instance exists, however it is reached.","type":"p"},{"items":["Keep `AppConfig.get()`, `region()` and `Serializable`.","Keep the constructor calling `Probe.constructed()` once per instance. `Probe.java` is a read-only test seam.","Lazy initialization is fine, an `enum` or holder class is welcome, but a plain unsynchronized check is not."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"SingletonKataTest.java","source":"import java.io.ByteArrayInputStream;\nimport java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream;\nimport java.io.ObjectInputStream;\nimport java.io.ObjectOutputStream;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass SingletonKataTest {\n    // Must stay the first check: it needs AppConfig to be untouched so far.\n    @Check(id = \"one-instance-under-contention\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void oneInstanceUnderContention() {\n        Probe.CREATED.set(0);\n        Probe.onConstruct = () -> Stress.pause(40);\n        List<AppConfig> seen = Stress.race(8, AppConfig::get);\n        Probe.onConstruct = () -> { };\n        Expect.equal(1, Probe.CREATED.get(),\n            \"AppConfig instances constructed by 8 threads calling get() together\");\n        for (AppConfig c : seen) {\n            Expect.isTrue(c == seen.get(0), \"the 8 threads were handed different instances\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"same-instance-every-call\")\n    void sameInstanceEveryCall() {\n        Expect.isTrue(AppConfig.get() == AppConfig.get(), \"get() should always return the same object\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"config-still-works\")\n    void configStillWorks() {\n        Expect.equal(\"eu-west-1\", AppConfig.get().region(), \"region()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"reflection-cannot-make-a-second\", kind = Kind.BEHAVIOUR)\n    void reflectionCannotMakeASecond() throws Exception {\n        AppConfig shared = AppConfig.get();\n        for (Constructor<?> c : AppConfig.class.getDeclaredConstructors()) {\n            c.setAccessible(true);\n            Object[] args = new Object[c.getParameterCount()];\n            Class<?>[] types = c.getParameterTypes();\n            for (int i = 0; i < args.length; i++) {\n                if (types[i] == int.class) args[i] = 0;\n                else if (types[i] == String.class) args[i] = \"X\";\n            }\n            try {\n                Object other = c.newInstance(args);\n                Expect.isTrue(other == shared,\n                    \"Reflection built a second AppConfig through its private constructor\");\n            } catch (java.lang.reflect.InvocationTargetException | IllegalArgumentException\n                     | InstantiationException e) {\n                // refused: good\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"serialization-keeps-identity\")\n    void serializationKeepsIdentity() throws Exception {\n        AppConfig shared = AppConfig.get();\n        Expect.isTrue(shared instanceof java.io.Serializable, \"AppConfig should stay Serializable\");\n        ByteArrayOutputStream bytes = new ByteArrayOutputStream();\n        try (ObjectOutputStream out = new ObjectOutputStream(bytes)) {\n            out.writeObject(shared);\n        }\n        Object back;\n        try (ObjectInputStream in = new ObjectInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream(bytes.toByteArray())) {\n            @Override\n            protected Class<?> resolveClass(java.io.ObjectStreamClass d) throws java.io.IOException,\n                    ClassNotFoundException {\n                return Class.forName(d.getName(), false, AppConfig.class.getClassLoader());\n            }\n        }) {\n            back = in.readObject();\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(back == shared,\n            \"Deserializing AppConfig produced a second instance\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shared-field-is-safe\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void sharedFieldIsSafe() {\n        for (Field f : AppConfig.class.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (f.getType() != AppConfig.class || !Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers())) continue;\n            int m = f.getModifiers();\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(m) || Modifier.isVolatile(m),\n                \"AppConfig.\" + f.getName() + \" is a lazily written static that is neither final nor volatile\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-open-constructor\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noOpenConstructor() {\n        for (Constructor<?> c : AppConfig.class.getDeclaredConstructors()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(c.getModifiers()),\n                \"AppConfig's constructor should be private\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"get-is-still-static\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void getIsStillStatic() {\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isStatic(Types.staticMethod(AppConfig.class, \"get\").getModifiers()),\n            \"AppConfig.get() should be static\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Make AppConfig a real singleton"},{"checks":[{"id":"fahrenheit-is-converted","kind":"behaviour","title":"Fahrenheit is converted to Celsius"},{"id":"celsius-passes-through","kind":"behaviour","title":"Celsius passes through"},{"id":"offline-is-empty","kind":"behaviour","title":"An offline sensor gives an empty reading"},{"id":"unknown-unit-is-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unknown units are rejected"},{"id":"one-poll-per-reading","kind":"behaviour","title":"Each reading polls once"},{"id":"every-reading-is-fresh","kind":"behaviour","title":"Readings are never cached"},{"id":"adapter-is-a-thermometer","kind":"design","title":"The adapter implements Thermometer"},{"id":"adapter-wraps-instead-of-extending","kind":"design","title":"The adapter holds the sensor, privately"},{"id":"legacy-format-stays-inside","kind":"design","title":"The sensor's text format stays inside"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The caller wants one interface, the vendor offers another. Do the translation (text to a typed number, units, absence) in one place that implements the interface callers expect.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`SensorThermometer` implements `Thermometer` and keeps a `private final LegacySensor`. In `celsius()`, poll, split the text at the colon, and switch on the unit.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The core of the translation:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["String raw = sensor.poll().trim();","if (raw.isEmpty()) return OptionalDouble.empty();","String[] parts = raw.split(\":\", 2);","double v = Double.parseDouble(parts[1]);","return switch (parts[0]) {","    case \"C\" -> OptionalDouble.of(v);","    case \"F\" -> OptionalDouble.of((v - 32) * 5 / 9);","    default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(raw);","};"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"adapter","kind":"implement","minutes":15,"readOnly":["Legacy.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Legacy.java","source":"/** What the rest of the system expects. */\ninterface Thermometer {\n    /** Degrees Celsius, or empty when no reading is available. */\n    java.util.OptionalDouble celsius();\n}\n\n/**\n * The vendor's sensor driver. It cannot change.\n * poll() returns text such as \"F:98.6\" or \"C:21.5\", or \"\" when the sensor\n * is offline. A script of readings is replayed one per poll; the last repeats.\n */\nfinal class LegacySensor {\n    private final String[] script;\n    private int polls;\n\n    LegacySensor(String... script) { this.script = script; }\n\n    String poll() {\n        String reading = script[Math.min(polls, script.length - 1)];\n        polls++;\n        return reading;\n    }\n\n    int polls() { return polls; }\n}\n"},{"name":"SensorThermometer.java","source":"import java.util.OptionalDouble;\n\nfinal class SensorThermometer implements Thermometer {\n    private final LegacySensor sensor;\n\n    SensorThermometer(LegacySensor sensor) { this.sensor = sensor; }\n\n    public OptionalDouble celsius() {\n        String raw = sensor.poll().trim();\n        if (raw.isEmpty()) {\n            return OptionalDouble.empty();\n        }\n        String[] parts = raw.split(\":\", 2);\n        double value = Double.parseDouble(parts[1]);\n        return switch (parts[0]) {\n            case \"C\" -> OptionalDouble.of(value);\n            case \"F\" -> OptionalDouble.of((value - 32) * 5 / 9);\n            default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unit: \" + raw);\n        };\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Legacy.java","source":"/** What the rest of the system expects. */\ninterface Thermometer {\n    /** Degrees Celsius, or empty when no reading is available. */\n    java.util.OptionalDouble celsius();\n}\n\n/**\n * The vendor's sensor driver. It cannot change.\n * poll() returns text such as \"F:98.6\" or \"C:21.5\", or \"\" when the sensor\n * is offline. A script of readings is replayed one per poll; the last repeats.\n */\nfinal class LegacySensor {\n    private final String[] script;\n    private int polls;\n\n    LegacySensor(String... script) { this.script = script; }\n\n    String poll() {\n        String reading = script[Math.min(polls, script.length - 1)];\n        polls++;\n        return reading;\n    }\n\n    int polls() { return polls; }\n}\n"},{"name":"SensorThermometer.java","source":"import java.util.OptionalDouble;\n\n// Adapts LegacySensor to Thermometer.\n//   \"C:21.5\" -> 21.5      \"F:212\" -> 100.0      \"\" -> empty\n// Any other unit (for example \"K:300\") throws IllegalArgumentException.\n// Every celsius() call polls the sensor exactly once.\nfinal class SensorThermometer implements Thermometer {\n    SensorThermometer(LegacySensor sensor) { }\n\n    public OptionalDouble celsius() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"The system speaks `Thermometer`; the vendor driver speaks text.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Thermometer` and `LegacySensor` (in `Legacy.java`, read-only) cannot change. Write the **adapter** `SensorThermometer(LegacySensor)` so that anything that needs a `Thermometer` can use the sensor.","type":"p"},{"items":["`celsius()` polls the sensor once per call and returns degrees Celsius as an `OptionalDouble`.","`\"C:21.5\"` gives 21.5, `\"F:212\"` gives 100.0, and an empty reading gives `OptionalDouble.empty()`.","Any other unit throws `IllegalArgumentException`.","The adapter wraps the sensor; it does not extend it."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"AdapterKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.OptionalDouble;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass AdapterKataTest {\n    static Thermometer over(String... script) {\n        return new SensorThermometer(new LegacySensor(script));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fahrenheit-is-converted\")\n    void fahrenheitIsConverted() {\n        Expect.equal(100.0, over(\"F:212\").celsius().getAsDouble(), \"212 F\");\n        Expect.equal(0.0, over(\"F:32.0\").celsius().getAsDouble(), \"32 F\");\n        Expect.equal(37.0, Math.round(over(\"F:98.6\").celsius().getAsDouble() * 10) / 10.0, \"98.6 F\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"celsius-passes-through\")\n    void celsiusPassesThrough() {\n        Expect.equal(21.5, over(\"C:21.5\").celsius().getAsDouble(), \"21.5 C\");\n        Expect.equal(-4.0, over(\"C:-4\").celsius().getAsDouble(), \"-4 C\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"offline-is-empty\")\n    void offlineIsEmpty() {\n        Expect.equal(OptionalDouble.empty(), over(\"\").celsius(), \"an offline sensor\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-unit-is-rejected\")\n    void unknownUnitIsRejected() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> over(\"K:300\").celsius(), \"a reading in kelvin\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"one-poll-per-reading\")\n    void onePollPerReading() {\n        LegacySensor sensor = new LegacySensor(\"C:1\");\n        Thermometer t = new SensorThermometer(sensor);\n        Expect.equal(0, sensor.polls(), \"polls before the first reading\");\n        t.celsius();\n        Expect.equal(1, sensor.polls(), \"polls after one reading\");\n        t.celsius();\n        Expect.equal(2, sensor.polls(), \"polls after two readings\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"every-reading-is-fresh\")\n    void everyReadingIsFresh() {\n        Thermometer t = over(\"C:10\", \"F:50\", \"\", \"C:12\");\n        Expect.equal(10.0, t.celsius().getAsDouble(), \"first\");\n        Expect.equal(10.0, t.celsius().getAsDouble(), \"second (50 F)\");\n        Expect.equal(OptionalDouble.empty(), t.celsius(), \"third (offline)\");\n        Expect.equal(12.0, t.celsius().getAsDouble(), \"fourth\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"adapter-is-a-thermometer\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void adapterIsAThermometer() {\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.named(\"Thermometer\").isAssignableFrom(Types.named(\"SensorThermometer\")),\n            \"SensorThermometer should implement Thermometer\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"adapter-wraps-instead-of-extending\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void adapterWrapsInsteadOfExtending() {\n        Class<?> adapter = Types.named(\"SensorThermometer\");\n        Expect.equal(Object.class, adapter.getSuperclass(),\n            \"the superclass of SensorThermometer (wrap the sensor, do not extend it)\");\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(adapter, Types.named(\"LegacySensor\"));\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()) && Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n            \"SensorThermometer.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n        Types.constructor(adapter, Types.named(\"LegacySensor\"));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"legacy-format-stays-inside\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void legacyFormatStaysInside() {\n        for (var m : Types.named(\"SensorThermometer\").getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            if (!Modifier.isPrivate(m.getModifiers()) && !m.isSynthetic()) {\n                Expect.isTrue(m.getReturnType() != String.class,\n                    \"SensorThermometer.\" + m.getName() + \" leaks the sensor's text format\");\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"Thermometer\").mentions(\"LegacySensor\"),\n            \"Thermometer should not know the legacy sensor\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Adapt a legacy sensor to Thermometer"},{"checks":[{"id":"email-alert","kind":"behaviour","title":"Email alerts are unchanged"},{"id":"email-digest","kind":"behaviour","title":"Email digests are unchanged"},{"id":"sms-short-messages","kind":"behaviour","title":"Short SMS messages are unchanged"},{"id":"sms-cuts-long-messages","kind":"behaviour","title":"Long SMS messages are still cut"},{"id":"unknown-channel","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unknown channels are rejected"},{"id":"channel-is-an-interface","kind":"design","title":"Channel is a one-method interface"},{"id":"message-holds-the-channel","kind":"design","title":"Message holds a final Channel"},{"id":"combination-classes-are-gone","kind":"design","title":"No class per kind and channel"},{"id":"messages-accept-any-channel","kind":"design","title":"Alert and Digest accept any Channel"},{"id":"messages-do-not-know-channels","kind":"design","title":"Messages never name a concrete channel"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Two things vary independently: what is said (alert, digest) and how it travels (email, SMS). Inheritance multiplies them. Keep one of them behind a reference instead.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Make the delivery mechanism a `Channel` interface with `Email` and `Sms`. `Message` holds a `Channel`; `Alert` and `Digest` build the text and hand it to `channel.send`. `Messages` maps names to channels.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The abstraction delegates to the implementor:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["abstract class Message {","    protected final Channel channel;","    protected Message(Channel channel) { this.channel = channel; }","    abstract String deliver(String to);","}","// Alert.deliver:","//   channel.send(to, \"ALERT: \" + problem)"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"bridge","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Messages.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\ninterface Channel {\n    String send(String to, String text);\n}\n\nrecord Email() implements Channel {\n    public String send(String to, String text) {\n        return \"email:\" + to + \" <- \" + text;\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Sms() implements Channel {\n    public String send(String to, String text) {\n        String cut = text.length() > 30 ? text.substring(0, 27) + \"...\" : text;\n        return \"sms:\" + to + \" <- \" + cut;\n    }\n}\n\nabstract class Message {\n    protected final Channel channel;\n\n    protected Message(Channel channel) { this.channel = channel; }\n\n    abstract String deliver(String to);\n}\n\nfinal class Alert extends Message {\n    private final String problem;\n\n    Alert(Channel channel, String problem) {\n        super(channel);\n        this.problem = problem;\n    }\n\n    String deliver(String to) { return channel.send(to, \"ALERT: \" + problem); }\n}\n\nfinal class Digest extends Message {\n    private final List<String> items;\n\n    Digest(Channel channel, List<String> items) {\n        super(channel);\n        this.items = items;\n    }\n\n    String deliver(String to) {\n        return channel.send(to, items.size() + \" items: \" + items);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Messages {\n    private Messages() { }\n\n    private static Channel channel(String name) {\n        return switch (name) {\n            case \"email\" -> new Email();\n            case \"sms\" -> new Sms();\n            default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(name);\n        };\n    }\n\n    static Message alert(String channel, String problem) {\n        return new Alert(channel(channel), problem);\n    }\n\n    static Message digest(String channel, List<String> items) {\n        return new Digest(channel(channel), items);\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Messages.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\nabstract class Message {\n    abstract String deliver(String to);\n}\n\n// Two kinds of message times two channels: one class per combination.\nfinal class EmailAlert extends Message {\n    private final String problem;\n    EmailAlert(String problem) { this.problem = problem; }\n    String deliver(String to) {\n        return \"email:\" + to + \" <- ALERT: \" + problem;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class SmsAlert extends Message {\n    private final String problem;\n    SmsAlert(String problem) { this.problem = problem; }\n    String deliver(String to) {\n        return \"sms:\" + to + \" <- \" + cut(\"ALERT: \" + problem);\n    }\n    private static String cut(String s) {\n        return s.length() > 30 ? s.substring(0, 27) + \"...\" : s;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class EmailDigest extends Message {\n    private final List<String> items;\n    EmailDigest(List<String> items) { this.items = items; }\n    String deliver(String to) {\n        return \"email:\" + to + \" <- \" + items.size() + \" items: \" + items;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class SmsDigest extends Message {\n    private final List<String> items;\n    SmsDigest(List<String> items) { this.items = items; }\n    String deliver(String to) {\n        return \"sms:\" + to + \" <- \" + cut(items.size() + \" items: \" + items);\n    }\n    private static String cut(String s) {\n        return s.length() > 30 ? s.substring(0, 27) + \"...\" : s;\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use these entry points. Keep their signatures and behaviour.\nfinal class Messages {\n    private Messages() { }\n\n    static Message alert(String channel, String problem) {\n        return switch (channel) {\n            case \"email\" -> new EmailAlert(problem);\n            case \"sms\" -> new SmsAlert(problem);\n            default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(channel);\n        };\n    }\n\n    static Message digest(String channel, List<String> items) {\n        return switch (channel) {\n            case \"email\" -> new EmailDigest(items);\n            case \"sms\" -> new SmsDigest(items);\n            default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(channel);\n        };\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Two kinds of message times two channels is four classes. A third channel makes six.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Refactor with a **bridge** so message kinds and channels vary separately. `Messages.alert(channel, problem)` and `Messages.digest(channel, items)` must keep returning messages whose `deliver(to)` output is unchanged, including the SMS cut-off.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `interface Channel` with `String send(String to, String text)`, implemented by `Email` and `Sms` (Sms owns the cut-off).","`Message` keeps a `Channel`, set by `Message(Channel)`.","Replace the four combination classes with `Alert(Channel, String)` and `Digest(Channel, List<String>)`.","Unknown channel names still throw `IllegalArgumentException`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"BridgeKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass BridgeKataTest {\n    static final List<String> ITEMS = List.of(\"a\", \"b\");\n    static final List<String> MANY = List.of(\"disk\", \"memory\", \"network\", \"cpu\");\n\n    @Check(id = \"email-alert\")\n    void emailAlert() {\n        Expect.equal(\"email:ann <- ALERT: disk full\",\n            Messages.alert(\"email\", \"disk full\").deliver(\"ann\"), \"email alert\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"email-digest\")\n    void emailDigest() {\n        Expect.equal(\"email:bo <- 2 items: [a, b]\",\n            Messages.digest(\"email\", ITEMS).deliver(\"bo\"), \"email digest\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sms-short-messages\")\n    void smsShortMessages() {\n        Expect.equal(\"sms:ann <- ALERT: disk full\",\n            Messages.alert(\"sms\", \"disk full\").deliver(\"ann\"), \"sms alert\");\n        Expect.equal(\"sms:bo <- 2 items: [a, b]\",\n            Messages.digest(\"sms\", ITEMS).deliver(\"bo\"), \"sms digest\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sms-cuts-long-messages\")\n    void smsCutsLongMessages() {\n        Expect.equal(\"sms:bo <- 4 items: [disk, memory, net...\",\n            Messages.digest(\"sms\", MANY).deliver(\"bo\"), \"long sms digest\");\n        Expect.equal(\"sms:ann <- ALERT: the database is on f...\",\n            Messages.alert(\"sms\", \"the database is on fire today\").deliver(\"ann\"), \"long sms alert\");\n        Expect.equal(\"email:bo <- 4 items: [disk, memory, network, cpu]\",\n            Messages.digest(\"email\", MANY).deliver(\"bo\"), \"email never cuts\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-channel\")\n    void unknownChannel() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> Messages.alert(\"pager\", \"x\"), \"an unknown channel for an alert\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> Messages.digest(\"pager\", ITEMS), \"an unknown channel for a digest\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"channel-is-an-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void channelIsAnInterface() {\n        Class<?> channel = Types.named(\"Channel\");\n        Expect.isTrue(channel.isInterface(), \"Channel should be an interface\");\n        Method send = Types.singleAbstractMethod(channel);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(String.class, String.class), List.of(send.getParameterTypes()),\n            \"the parameters of Channel.\" + send.getName());\n        Expect.equal(String.class, send.getReturnType(), \"the return type of Channel.\" + send.getName());\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"message-holds-the-channel\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void messageHoldsTheChannel() {\n        Class<?> message = Types.named(\"Message\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isAbstract(message.getModifiers()), \"Message should stay abstract\");\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(message, Types.named(\"Channel\"));\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()), \"Message.\" + f.getName() + \" should be final\");\n        Types.constructor(message, Types.named(\"Channel\"));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"combination-classes-are-gone\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void combinationClassesAreGone() {\n        for (String name : List.of(\"EmailAlert\", \"SmsAlert\", \"EmailDigest\", \"SmsDigest\")) {\n            boolean exists = true;\n            try {\n                Types.named(name);\n            } catch (CheckFailure e) {\n                exists = false;\n            }\n            Expect.isTrue(!exists, name + \" is still a class: a message kind and a channel should vary separately\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"messages-accept-any-channel\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void messagesAcceptAnyChannel() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> channel = Types.named(\"Channel\");\n        Object pager = Types.implement(channel, a -> \"pager:\" + a[0] + \"/\" + a[1]);\n        Constructor<?> alert = Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Alert\"), channel, String.class);\n        Constructor<?> digest = Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Digest\"), channel, List.class);\n        Object a = Types.create(alert, pager, \"disk full\");\n        Object d = Types.create(digest, pager, ITEMS);\n        Expect.equal(\"pager:ann/ALERT: disk full\",\n            Types.call(Types.method(a.getClass(), \"deliver\", String.class), a, \"ann\"),\n            \"an Alert over a channel it has never seen\");\n        Expect.equal(\"pager:bo/2 items: [a, b]\",\n            Types.call(Types.method(d.getClass(), \"deliver\", String.class), d, \"bo\"),\n            \"a Digest over a channel it has never seen\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"messages-do-not-know-channels\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void messagesDoNotKnowChannels() {\n        Class<?> channel = Types.named(\"Channel\");\n        for (String name : List.of(\"Message\", \"Alert\", \"Digest\")) {\n            Class<?> type = Types.named(name);\n            for (Field f : type.getDeclaredFields()) {\n                Expect.isTrue(!isConcreteChannel(channel, f.getType()),\n                    name + \".\" + f.getName() + \" is a concrete channel; depend on Channel instead\");\n            }\n            for (Constructor<?> c : type.getDeclaredConstructors()) {\n                for (Class<?> p : c.getParameterTypes()) {\n                    Expect.isTrue(!isConcreteChannel(channel, p),\n                        name + \" takes a concrete channel in its constructor\");\n                }\n            }\n            Expect.none(Source.type(name).comparedStrings(), name + \" still branches on a channel name\");\n            Expect.none(Source.type(name).instanceofs(), name + \" inspects the channel's concrete type\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    static boolean isConcreteChannel(Class<?> channel, Class<?> t) {\n        return !t.isInterface() && channel.isAssignableFrom(t);\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Untangle message kinds from channels"},{"checks":[{"id":"size-sums-recursively","kind":"behaviour","title":"Size sums the whole subtree"},{"id":"empty-dir","kind":"behaviour","title":"An empty Dir is size 0 with no files"},{"id":"file-count","kind":"behaviour","title":"fileCount counts leaves at any depth"},{"id":"find-by-name","kind":"behaviour","title":"find locates files and Dirs by name"},{"id":"find-first-match","kind":"behaviour","title":"find is depth-first, in order"},{"id":"dir-copies-its-children","kind":"behaviour","title":"Dir copies the list it is given"},{"id":"dir-is-a-node","kind":"design","title":"Dir is a Node holding a List of children"},{"id":"dir-treats-children-alike","kind":"design","title":"Dir never asks what kind a child is"},{"id":"any-node-fits-inside","kind":"design","title":"Dir works with a Node it has never seen"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A `Dir` is a `Node` that contains `Node`s. Because a child can be a `File` or another `Dir`, ask the child; each kind of `Node` knows how to answer for itself.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Store `List.copyOf(children)` in a `private final List<Node>`. `size()` and `fileCount()` map over the children through the `Node` interface and sum. The varargs constructor can delegate to the list one.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`find` returns itself on a match, otherwise asks each child:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["if (name.equals(wanted)) return Optional.of(this);","for (Node child : children) {","    Optional<Node> hit = child.find(wanted);","    if (hit.isPresent()) return hit;","}","return Optional.empty();"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"composite","kind":"implement","minutes":15,"readOnly":["File.java","Node.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Node.java","source":"import java.util.Optional;\n\ninterface Node {\n    String name();\n\n    long size();\n\n    int fileCount();\n\n    // Depth-first, children in order; this node itself is checked first.\n    Optional<Node> find(String name);\n}\n"},{"name":"File.java","source":"import java.util.Optional;\n\nrecord File(String name, long size) implements Node {\n    public int fileCount() { return 1; }\n\n    public Optional<Node> find(String wanted) {\n        return name.equals(wanted) ? Optional.of(this) : Optional.empty();\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Dir.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\nfinal class Dir implements Node {\n    private final String name;\n    private final List<Node> children;\n\n    Dir(String name, Node... children) {\n        this(name, List.of(children));\n    }\n\n    Dir(String name, List<Node> children) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.children = List.copyOf(children);\n    }\n\n    public String name() { return name; }\n\n    public long size() {\n        return children.stream().mapToLong(Node::size).sum();\n    }\n\n    public int fileCount() {\n        return children.stream().mapToInt(Node::fileCount).sum();\n    }\n\n    public Optional<Node> find(String wanted) {\n        if (name.equals(wanted)) return Optional.of(this);\n        for (Node child : children) {\n            Optional<Node> hit = child.find(wanted);\n            if (hit.isPresent()) return hit;\n        }\n        return Optional.empty();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Node.java","source":"import java.util.Optional;\n\ninterface Node {\n    String name();\n\n    long size();\n\n    int fileCount();\n\n    // Depth-first, children in order; this node itself is checked first.\n    Optional<Node> find(String name);\n}\n"},{"name":"File.java","source":"import java.util.Optional;\n\nrecord File(String name, long size) implements Node {\n    public int fileCount() { return 1; }\n\n    public Optional<Node> find(String wanted) {\n        return name.equals(wanted) ? Optional.of(this) : Optional.empty();\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Dir.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\n// A directory: a Node that holds other Nodes.\nfinal class Dir implements Node {\n    Dir(String name, Node... children) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    Dir(String name, List<Node> children) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public String name() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public long size() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public int fileCount() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public Optional<Node> find(String name) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A file and a folder should answer the same questions, so callers never ask which one they hold.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Node` and `File` are given. Implement the **composite**: `Dir` in `Dir.java`.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Dir(String name, Node... children)` and `Dir(String name, List<Node> children)`; a `Dir` keeps its own copy of the list.","`size()` is the sum of its children's sizes; `fileCount()` the sum of theirs (an empty `Dir` has 0).","`find(name)` checks the `Dir` itself first, then each child in order, depth-first.","Work through the `Node` interface only: `Dir` must not test what kind of child it holds."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"CompositeKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass CompositeKataTest {\n    static Node tree() {\n        return new Dir(\"project\",\n            new File(\"README.md\", 200),\n            new Dir(\"src\",\n                new File(\"Main.java\", 700),\n                new File(\"Util.java\", 300)),\n            new Dir(\"docs\"));\n    }\n\n    /** A leaf the learner has never seen. */\n    static final class Fixed implements Node {\n        public String name() { return \"fixed\"; }\n        public long size() { return 1000; }\n        public int fileCount() { return 7; }\n        public Optional<Node> find(String n) { return Optional.empty(); }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"size-sums-recursively\")\n    void sizeSumsRecursively() {\n        Expect.equal(1200L, tree().size(), \"size of the whole tree\");\n        Expect.equal(1000L, ((Dir) tree().find(\"src\").get()).size(), \"size of src\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"empty-dir\")\n    void emptyDir() {\n        Dir empty = new Dir(\"docs\");\n        Expect.equal(0L, empty.size(), \"size of an empty Dir\");\n        Expect.equal(0, empty.fileCount(), \"fileCount of an empty Dir\");\n        Expect.equal(\"docs\", empty.name(), \"name of the Dir\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"file-count\")\n    void fileCount() {\n        Expect.equal(3, tree().fileCount(), \"files in the whole tree\");\n        Dir nested = new Dir(\"a\", new Dir(\"b\", new Dir(\"c\", new File(\"x\", 1))));\n        Expect.equal(1, nested.fileCount(), \"files under three nested Dirs\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"find-by-name\")\n    void findByName() {\n        Node root = tree();\n        Expect.equal(\"Util.java\", root.find(\"Util.java\").orElseThrow().name(), \"find a nested file\");\n        Expect.equal(\"src\", root.find(\"src\").orElseThrow().name(), \"find a Dir\");\n        Expect.equal(\"project\", root.find(\"project\").orElseThrow().name(), \"find the root itself\");\n        Expect.isTrue(root.find(\"nope\").isEmpty(), \"find of a missing name should be empty\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"find-first-match\")\n    void findFirstMatch() {\n        Node root = new Dir(\"r\",\n            new Dir(\"a\", new File(\"same\", 1)),\n            new File(\"same\", 2));\n        Expect.equal(1L, root.find(\"same\").orElseThrow().size(),\n            \"find should be depth-first and in order\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"dir-copies-its-children\")\n    void dirCopiesItsChildren() {\n        List<Node> kids = new ArrayList<>(List.of(new File(\"a\", 5)));\n        Dir dir = new Dir(\"d\", kids);\n        kids.add(new File(\"b\", 6));\n        Expect.equal(5L, dir.size(), \"a Dir should keep its own copy of the list\");\n        Expect.equal(1, dir.fileCount(), \"fileCount after the caller changed its list\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"dir-is-a-node\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void dirIsANode() {\n        Class<?> dir = Types.named(\"Dir\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Node.class.isAssignableFrom(dir), \"Dir should implement Node\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!Types.fieldsOfType(dir, List.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"Dir should hold its children in a List<Node>\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"dir-treats-children-alike\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void dirTreatsChildrenAlike() {\n        var dir = Source.type(\"Dir\");\n        Expect.none(dir.instanceofs(), \"Dir asks what kind of Node a child is\");\n        Expect.none(dir.switches(), \"Dir switches on the kind of child\");\n        Expect.none(dir.mentions(\"File\"), \"Dir should not know about File\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"any-node-fits-inside\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void anyNodeFitsInside() {\n        Dir dir = new Dir(\"odd\", new Fixed(), new File(\"f\", 1), new Dir(\"in\", new Fixed()));\n        Expect.equal(2001L, dir.size(), \"size with a Node type Dir has never seen\");\n        Expect.equal(15, dir.fileCount(), \"fileCount with a Node type Dir has never seen\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Build a directory tree that sizes itself"},{"checks":[{"id":"plain","kind":"behaviour","title":"No options sends the message as is"},{"id":"prefix-only","kind":"behaviour","title":"A tag prefixes the message"},{"id":"shout-only","kind":"behaviour","title":"Shout upper-cases the message"},{"id":"shout-and-prefix","kind":"behaviour","title":"Tag and shout combine as before"},{"id":"decorators-wrap-a-notifier","kind":"design","title":"Prefixing and Shouting each wrap a Notifier"},{"id":"no-combination-classes","kind":"design","title":"The combination subclasses are gone"},{"id":"stack-in-any-order","kind":"design","title":"Decorators stack in any order"},{"id":"wraps-any-notifier","kind":"design","title":"Decorators wrap a Notifier they have never seen"},{"id":"create-does-not-branch-on-combos","kind":"design","title":"create builds one base and stacks on it"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Find what varies independently: adding a tag and shouting. Each is one small behaviour that could wrap any `Notifier` and still be a `Notifier`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Write `Prefixing` and `Shouting` as `Notifier`s with a `private final Notifier next`. Each changes the message and calls `next.send(...)`. `create` builds a `ListNotifier` and wraps it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Then `create` becomes:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["Notifier n = new ListNotifier(out);","if (tag != null) n = new Prefixing(n, tag);","if (shout) n = new Shouting(n);","return n;"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"decorator","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Notifier.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\ninterface Notifier {\n    void send(String message);\n}\n\nfinal class ListNotifier implements Notifier {\n    private final List<String> out;\n\n    ListNotifier(List<String> out) { this.out = out; }\n\n    public void send(String message) { out.add(message); }\n}\n\nfinal class Prefixing implements Notifier {\n    private final Notifier next;\n    private final String tag;\n\n    Prefixing(Notifier next, String tag) {\n        this.next = next;\n        this.tag = tag;\n    }\n\n    public void send(String message) { next.send(\"[\" + tag + \"] \" + message); }\n}\n\nfinal class Shouting implements Notifier {\n    private final Notifier next;\n\n    Shouting(Notifier next) { this.next = next; }\n\n    public void send(String message) { next.send(message.toUpperCase()); }\n}\n\nfinal class Notifiers {\n    private Notifiers() { }\n\n    static Notifier create(String tag, boolean shout, List<String> out) {\n        Notifier n = new ListNotifier(out);\n        if (tag != null) n = new Prefixing(n, tag);\n        if (shout) n = new Shouting(n);\n        return n;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Notifier.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\ninterface Notifier {\n    void send(String message);\n}\n\nfinal class ListNotifier implements Notifier {\n    private final List<String> out;\n\n    ListNotifier(List<String> out) { this.out = out; }\n\n    public void send(String message) { out.add(message); }\n}\n\n// One subclass per combination: a third option doubles the list again.\nfinal class PrefixedListNotifier extends ListNotifierBase {\n    PrefixedListNotifier(List<String> out, String tag) {\n        super(out, tag, false);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class ShoutingListNotifier extends ListNotifierBase {\n    ShoutingListNotifier(List<String> out) { super(out, null, true); }\n}\n\nfinal class ShoutingPrefixedListNotifier extends ListNotifierBase {\n    ShoutingPrefixedListNotifier(List<String> out, String tag) {\n        super(out, tag, true);\n    }\n}\n\nabstract class ListNotifierBase implements Notifier {\n    private final List<String> out;\n    private final String tag;\n    private final boolean shout;\n\n    ListNotifierBase(List<String> out, String tag, boolean shout) {\n        this.out = out; this.tag = tag; this.shout = shout;\n    }\n\n    public void send(String message) {\n        String text = shout ? message.toUpperCase() : message;\n        out.add(tag == null ? text : \"[\" + tag + \"] \" + text);\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use this entry point. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Notifiers {\n    private Notifiers() { }\n\n    static Notifier create(String tag, boolean shout, List<String> out) {\n        if (tag != null && shout) {\n            return new ShoutingPrefixedListNotifier(out, tag);\n        }\n        if (tag != null) return new PrefixedListNotifier(out, tag);\n        if (shout) return new ShoutingListNotifier(out);\n        return new ListNotifier(out);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A new option should add one class, not double the list of subclasses.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Notifiers.create(tag, shout, out)` must keep returning a `Notifier` that behaves exactly as now. Replace the per-combination subclasses with **decorators** over `Notifier`.","type":"p"},{"items":["Keep `Notifier` and `ListNotifier`.","Add `Prefixing(Notifier next, String tag)`: sends `[tag] message`.","Add `Shouting(Notifier next)`: sends the message in upper case.","Delete the three combination classes and `ListNotifierBase`.","`create` stacks the decorators; the tag keeps its case, so `Shouting` is the outer one."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"DecoratorKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass DecoratorKataTest {\n    static List<String> sendVia(String tag, boolean shout, String msg) {\n        List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        Notifiers.create(tag, shout, out).send(msg);\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    static Notifier wrap(String type, Notifier next) throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> c = Types.named(type);\n        if (type.equals(\"Prefixing\")) {\n            return (Notifier) Types.create(Types.constructor(c, Notifier.class, String.class), next, \"T\");\n        }\n        return (Notifier) Types.create(Types.constructor(c, Notifier.class), next);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"plain\")\n    void plain() {\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"disk 91%\"), sendVia(null, false, \"disk 91%\"), \"no options\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"prefix-only\")\n    void prefixOnly() {\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"[ops] disk 91%\"), sendVia(\"ops\", false, \"disk 91%\"), \"a tag\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shout-only\")\n    void shoutOnly() {\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"DISK 91%\"), sendVia(null, true, \"disk 91%\"), \"shout\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shout-and-prefix\")\n    void shoutAndPrefix() {\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"[ops] DISK 91%\"), sendVia(\"ops\", true, \"disk 91%\"),\n            \"a tag and shout (the tag keeps its case)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"decorators-wrap-a-notifier\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void decoratorsWrapANotifier() {\n        for (String name : List.of(\"Prefixing\", \"Shouting\")) {\n            Class<?> c = Types.named(name);\n            Expect.isTrue(Notifier.class.isAssignableFrom(c), name + \" should implement Notifier\");\n            Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(c, Notifier.class);\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n                name + \".\" + f.getName() + \" should be final\");\n        }\n        Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Prefixing\"), Notifier.class, String.class);\n        Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Shouting\"), Notifier.class);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-combination-classes\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noCombinationClasses() {\n        for (String old : List.of(\"PrefixedListNotifier\", \"ShoutingListNotifier\",\n                \"ShoutingPrefixedListNotifier\", \"ListNotifierBase\")) {\n            boolean exists;\n            try {\n                Types.named(old);\n                exists = true;\n            } catch (CheckFailure e) {\n                exists = false;\n            }\n            Expect.isTrue(!exists, old + \" is still there: one class per combination does not scale\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"stack-in-any-order\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void stackInAnyOrder() throws Throwable {\n        List<String> a = new ArrayList<>();\n        wrap(\"Shouting\", wrap(\"Prefixing\", new ListNotifier(a))).send(\"hi\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"[T] HI\"), a, \"Shouting around Prefixing\");\n        List<String> b = new ArrayList<>();\n        wrap(\"Prefixing\", wrap(\"Shouting\", new ListNotifier(b))).send(\"hi\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"[T] HI\"), b, \"Prefixing around Shouting\");\n        List<String> c = new ArrayList<>();\n        wrap(\"Shouting\", wrap(\"Shouting\", new ListNotifier(c))).send(\"hi\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"HI\"), c, \"a decorator applied twice\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"wraps-any-notifier\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void wrapsAnyNotifier() throws Throwable {\n        List<String> seen = new ArrayList<>();\n        Notifier custom = m -> seen.add(\"custom:\" + m);\n        wrap(\"Prefixing\", custom).send(\"x\");\n        wrap(\"Shouting\", custom).send(\"y\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"custom:[T] x\", \"custom:Y\"), seen,\n            \"decorators around a Notifier they have never seen\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"create-does-not-branch-on-combos\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void createDoesNotBranchOnCombos() {\n        var create = Source.type(\"Notifiers\").method(\"create\");\n        Expect.atMost(2, create.news(\"ListNotifier\"), \"Notifiers.create builds the base more than once\");\n        Expect.none(create.news(\"ListNotifierBase\"), \"Notifiers.create still builds a combination class\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Stop subclassing for every notifier combo"},{"checks":[{"id":"order-is-placed","kind":"behaviour","title":"An order is placed and numbered"},{"id":"out-of-stock","kind":"behaviour","title":"Too many units are rejected for stock"},{"id":"payment-failure-releases-stock","kind":"behaviour","title":"A declined card gives the stock back"},{"id":"nothing-booked-on-rejection","kind":"behaviour","title":"Rejections book no shipment"},{"id":"facade-has-place","kind":"design","title":"OrderService.place returns an Outcome"},{"id":"facade-owns-the-subsystems","kind":"design","title":"OrderService owns the subsystems"},{"id":"storefront-sees-only-the-facade","kind":"design","title":"Storefront never names a subsystem"},{"id":"storefront-holds-no-subsystem","kind":"design","title":"Storefront keeps no subsystem fields"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Placing an order is one idea for the caller, yet the steps and the undo rule are spread through the web layer. Name that one idea and move the steps behind it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Create `OrderService` with the three subsystems as private fields and a `place` method that returns an `Outcome`. `Storefront` keeps only an `OrderService` and formats the reply.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"In `OrderService.place`, reserve, charge (release on failure), then book. In `Storefront`:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["return switch (orders.place(id, qty, card, address)) {","    case Outcome.Placed p -> \"OK \" + p.tracking();","    case Outcome.Rejected r -> \"REJECTED \" + r.reason();","};"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"facade","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Subsystems.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Subsystems.java","source":"final class Inventory {\n    private int stock = 3;\n\n    boolean reserve(String sku, int qty) {\n        if (qty > stock) return false;\n        stock -= qty;\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    void release(String sku, int qty) { stock += qty; }\n}\n\nfinal class Payments {\n    boolean charge(String card, long cents) {\n        return !card.startsWith(\"0000\");\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Shipping {\n    private int booked;\n\n    String book(String sku, String address) {\n        booked++;\n        return \"TRK-\" + sku + \"-\" + booked;\n    }\n}\n\nsealed interface Outcome {\n    record Placed(String tracking) implements Outcome { }\n\n    record Rejected(String reason) implements Outcome { }\n}\n"},{"name":"Storefront.java","source":"final class Storefront {\n    private final OrderService orders = new OrderService();\n\n    String buy(String sku, int qty, String card, String address) {\n        String id = sku.trim().toUpperCase();\n        return switch (orders.place(id, qty, card, address)) {\n            case Outcome.Placed p -> \"OK \" + p.tracking();\n            case Outcome.Rejected r -> \"REJECTED \" + r.reason();\n        };\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"OrderService.java","source":"final class OrderService {\n    private final Inventory inventory = new Inventory();\n    private final Payments payments = new Payments();\n    private final Shipping shipping = new Shipping();\n\n    Outcome place(String sku, int qty, String card, String address) {\n        if (!inventory.reserve(sku, qty)) return new Outcome.Rejected(\"stock\");\n        if (!payments.charge(card, 1999L * qty)) {\n            inventory.release(sku, qty);\n            return new Outcome.Rejected(\"payment\");\n        }\n        return new Outcome.Placed(shipping.book(sku, address));\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Subsystems.java","source":"final class Inventory {\n    private int stock = 3;\n\n    boolean reserve(String sku, int qty) {\n        if (qty > stock) return false;\n        stock -= qty;\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    void release(String sku, int qty) { stock += qty; }\n}\n\nfinal class Payments {\n    boolean charge(String card, long cents) {\n        return !card.startsWith(\"0000\");\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Shipping {\n    private int booked;\n\n    String book(String sku, String address) {\n        booked++;\n        return \"TRK-\" + sku + \"-\" + booked;\n    }\n}\n\nsealed interface Outcome {\n    record Placed(String tracking) implements Outcome { }\n\n    record Rejected(String reason) implements Outcome { }\n}\n"},{"name":"Storefront.java","source":"// The web layer. It knows far too much about how an order is placed.\nfinal class Storefront {\n    private final Inventory inventory = new Inventory();\n    private final Payments payments = new Payments();\n    private final Shipping shipping = new Shipping();\n\n    // Callers use this. Keep its signature and replies.\n    String buy(String sku, int qty, String card, String address) {\n        String id = sku.trim().toUpperCase();\n        if (!inventory.reserve(id, qty)) {\n            return \"REJECTED stock\";\n        }\n        if (!payments.charge(card, 1999L * qty)) {\n            inventory.release(id, qty);\n            return \"REJECTED payment\";\n        }\n        return \"OK \" + shipping.book(id, address);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"The web layer juggles three subsystems and their failure rules just to place one order.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Put a **facade** in front of them. `Storefront.buy(...)` must keep returning the same replies, `OK <tracking>` or `REJECTED <reason>`, and must still trim and upper-case the SKU.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `OrderService` with `Outcome place(String sku, int qty, String card, String address)`.","`OrderService` owns `Inventory`, `Payments` and `Shipping`, runs them in order, and releases stock when payment fails.","`Storefront` talks only to `OrderService` and turns its `Outcome` into the reply text.","Leave `Subsystems.java` as it is."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"FacadeKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass FacadeKataTest {\n    static final String ADDR = \"Main St 1\";\n\n    @Check(id = \"order-is-placed\")\n    void orderIsPlaced() {\n        var shop = new Storefront();\n        Expect.equal(\"OK TRK-A1-1\", shop.buy(\" a1 \", 2, \"4111\", ADDR), \"first order\");\n        Expect.equal(\"OK TRK-B2-2\", shop.buy(\"b2\", 1, \"4111\", ADDR), \"second order\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"out-of-stock\")\n    void outOfStock() {\n        var shop = new Storefront();\n        shop.buy(\"a1\", 2, \"4111\", ADDR);\n        Expect.equal(\"REJECTED stock\", shop.buy(\"a1\", 2, \"4111\", ADDR), \"only 1 left\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"payment-failure-releases-stock\")\n    void paymentFailureReleasesStock() {\n        var shop = new Storefront();\n        Expect.equal(\"REJECTED payment\", shop.buy(\"a1\", 3, \"0000-1\", ADDR), \"declined card\");\n        Expect.equal(\"OK TRK-A1-1\", shop.buy(\"a1\", 3, \"4111\", ADDR),\n            \"the declined order must give its stock back\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"nothing-booked-on-rejection\")\n    void nothingBookedOnRejection() {\n        var shop = new Storefront();\n        shop.buy(\"a1\", 9, \"4111\", ADDR);\n        shop.buy(\"a1\", 1, \"0000\", ADDR);\n        Expect.equal(\"OK TRK-A1-1\", shop.buy(\"a1\", 1, \"4111\", ADDR),\n            \"rejected orders must not consume tracking numbers\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"facade-has-place\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void facadeHasPlace() {\n        Class<?> service = Types.named(\"OrderService\");\n        Method place = Types.method(service, \"place\",\n            String.class, int.class, String.class, String.class);\n        Expect.equal(Outcome.class, place.getReturnType(), \"OrderService.place's return type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"facade-owns-the-subsystems\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void facadeOwnsTheSubsystems() {\n        Class<?> service = Types.named(\"OrderService\");\n        Types.onlyFieldOfType(service, Inventory.class);\n        Types.onlyFieldOfType(service, Payments.class);\n        Types.onlyFieldOfType(service, Shipping.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(!Source.type(\"OrderService\").calls(\"release\").isEmpty(),\n            \"OrderService should undo the reservation when payment fails\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"storefront-sees-only-the-facade\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void storefrontSeesOnlyTheFacade() {\n        var store = Source.type(\"Storefront\");\n        for (String sub : new String[] {\"Inventory\", \"Payments\", \"Shipping\"}) {\n            Expect.none(store.mentions(sub), \"Storefront still talks to \" + sub);\n        }\n        Expect.none(store.calls(\"release\"), \"Storefront still compensates failed payments\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!store.mentions(\"OrderService\").isEmpty(),\n            \"Storefront should go through OrderService\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"storefront-holds-no-subsystem\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void storefrontHoldsNoSubsystem() {\n        Class<?> store = Types.named(\"Storefront\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(store, Inventory.class).isEmpty()\n            && Types.fieldsOfType(store, Payments.class).isEmpty()\n            && Types.fieldsOfType(store, Shipping.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"Storefront should not keep any subsystem as a field\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Give the storefront one door to ordering"},{"checks":[{"id":"draw-text","kind":"behaviour","title":"Trees draw the same text"},{"id":"many-trees-keep-their-positions","kind":"behaviour","title":"Each tree keeps its own position"},{"id":"textures-load-once-per-kind","kind":"design","title":"1000 trees of 3 kinds load at most 3 Textures"},{"id":"two-forests-share","kind":"design","title":"A second forest loads nothing new"},{"id":"factory-returns-the-same-instance","kind":"design","title":"TreeTypes.of returns one shared instance"},{"id":"tree-and-forest-do-not-build-types","kind":"design","title":"Only the factory builds TreeType and Texture"},{"id":"tree-keeps-no-appearance","kind":"design","title":"Tree keeps only extrinsic state"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Split each tree's data into what is the same for every oak (species, colour, texture) and what is unique (x, y). Share the first part, keep the second per tree.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Create `TreeType` for the shared part and `TreeTypes.of` as a cache keyed by species and colour. `Tree` becomes x, y and a `TreeType`; `Forest.plant` asks the factory.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The factory can be one map:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["private static final Map<String, TreeType> POOL =","    new ConcurrentHashMap<>();","static TreeType of(String species, String color) {","    return POOL.computeIfAbsent(species + \"/\" + color,","        k -> new TreeType(species, color,","            new Texture(species, color)));","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"flyweight","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Texture.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Texture.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\n// Expensive to build: pretend it reads and decodes an image.\nfinal class Texture {\n    private static final AtomicInteger LOADED = new AtomicInteger();\n\n    private final String species;\n    private final String color;\n\n    Texture(String species, String color) {\n        LOADED.incrementAndGet();\n        this.species = species;\n        this.color = color;\n    }\n\n    String fingerprint() {\n        return Math.abs((species + color).hashCode() % 1000) + \"\";\n    }\n\n    // How many Textures exist so far, across the whole program.\n    static int loaded() { return LOADED.get(); }\n}\n"},{"name":"Forest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\n// Shared: what a kind of tree looks like.\nrecord TreeType(String species, String color, Texture texture) {\n    String draw(int x, int y) {\n        return species + \"@\" + x + \",\" + y + \" \" + color\n            + \" #\" + texture.fingerprint();\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class TreeTypes {\n    private static final Map<String, TreeType> POOL =\n        new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n    private TreeTypes() { }\n\n    static TreeType of(String species, String color) {\n        return POOL.computeIfAbsent(species + \"/\" + color,\n            k -> new TreeType(species, color, new Texture(species, color)));\n    }\n}\n\n// Per tree: only where it stands.\nrecord Tree(int x, int y, TreeType type) {\n    String draw() { return type.draw(x, y); }\n}\n\nfinal class Forest {\n    private final List<Tree> trees = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    void plant(String species, String color, int x, int y) {\n        trees.add(new Tree(x, y, TreeTypes.of(species, color)));\n    }\n\n    int size() { return trees.size(); }\n\n    String draw(int index) { return trees.get(index).draw(); }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Texture.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\n// Expensive to build: pretend it reads and decodes an image.\nfinal class Texture {\n    private static final AtomicInteger LOADED = new AtomicInteger();\n\n    private final String species;\n    private final String color;\n\n    Texture(String species, String color) {\n        LOADED.incrementAndGet();\n        this.species = species;\n        this.color = color;\n    }\n\n    String fingerprint() {\n        return Math.abs((species + color).hashCode() % 1000) + \"\";\n    }\n\n    // How many Textures exist so far, across the whole program.\n    static int loaded() { return LOADED.get(); }\n}\n"},{"name":"Forest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// Every tree carries its own copy of what it looks like.\nfinal class Tree {\n    final int x;\n    final int y;\n    final String species;\n    final String color;\n    final Texture texture;\n\n    Tree(int x, int y, String species, String color) {\n        this.x = x;\n        this.y = y;\n        this.species = species;\n        this.color = color;\n        this.texture = new Texture(species, color);\n    }\n\n    String draw() {\n        return species + \"@\" + x + \",\" + y + \" \" + color\n            + \" #\" + texture.fingerprint();\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use Forest. Keep its signatures and the text draw() returns.\nfinal class Forest {\n    private final List<Tree> trees = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    void plant(String species, String color, int x, int y) {\n        trees.add(new Tree(x, y, species, color));\n    }\n\n    int size() { return trees.size(); }\n\n    String draw(int index) { return trees.get(index).draw(); }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A forest of a million trees builds a million identical textures.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Refactor so trees of the same species and colour **share** one object. `Forest.plant`, `size` and `draw` must return what they return now.","type":"p"},{"items":["Move what is shared (species, colour, `Texture`) into `TreeType`.","Add `TreeTypes.of(String species, String color)`: the same arguments always give the same `TreeType` instance.","`Tree` keeps only its position and its `TreeType`.","`Forest` and `Tree` never call `new Texture` or `new TreeType`.","Leave `Texture.java` as it is."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"FlyweightKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass FlyweightKataTest {\n    static final String[] KINDS = {\"oak\", \"pine\", \"birch\"};\n\n    static Forest plant(String prefix, int trees) {\n        Forest forest = new Forest();\n        for (int i = 0; i < trees; i++) {\n            String kind = prefix + KINDS[i % 3];\n            forest.plant(kind, i % 3 == 0 ? \"green\" : \"dark\", i, i * 2);\n        }\n        return forest;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"draw-text\")\n    void drawText() {\n        Forest forest = new Forest();\n        forest.plant(\"oak\", \"green\", 10, 5);\n        forest.plant(\"pine\", \"dark\", 0, 1);\n        Expect.equal(2, forest.size(), \"trees planted\");\n        Expect.equal(\"oak@10,5 green #\" + new Texture(\"oak\", \"green\").fingerprint(),\n            forest.draw(0), \"drawing the first tree\");\n        Expect.equal(\"pine@0,1 dark #\" + new Texture(\"pine\", \"dark\").fingerprint(),\n            forest.draw(1), \"drawing the second tree\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"many-trees-keep-their-positions\")\n    void manyTreesKeepTheirPositions() {\n        Forest forest = plant(\"pos-\", 300);\n        Expect.equal(300, forest.size(), \"trees planted\");\n        Expect.isTrue(forest.draw(297).startsWith(\"pos-oak@297,594 green\"),\n            \"tree 297 should still stand at 297,594 but draws \" + forest.draw(297));\n        Expect.isTrue(forest.draw(7).startsWith(\"pos-pine@7,14 dark\"),\n            \"tree 7 should still stand at 7,14 but draws \" + forest.draw(7));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"textures-load-once-per-kind\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void texturesLoadOncePerKind() {\n        int before = Texture.loaded();\n        plant(\"count-\", 1000);\n        int made = Texture.loaded() - before;\n        Expect.isTrue(made <= 3,\n            \"1000 trees of 3 kinds built \" + made + \" Textures; expected at most 3\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"two-forests-share\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void twoForestsShare() {\n        plant(\"shared-\", 30);\n        int before = Texture.loaded();\n        plant(\"shared-\", 30);\n        Expect.equal(0, Texture.loaded() - before,\n            \"a second forest of known kinds should build no new Textures\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"factory-returns-the-same-instance\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void factoryReturnsTheSameInstance() throws Throwable {\n        Method of = Types.staticMethod(Types.named(\"TreeTypes\"), \"of\", String.class, String.class);\n        Object a = Types.call(of, null, \"elm\", \"red\");\n        Object b = Types.call(of, null, \"elm\", \"red\");\n        Object c = Types.call(of, null, \"elm\", \"gold\");\n        Expect.isTrue(a == b, \"TreeTypes.of(\\\"elm\\\", \\\"red\\\") twice should be one shared object\");\n        Expect.isTrue(a != c, \"different colours should be different TreeTypes\");\n        Expect.equal(Types.named(\"TreeType\"), a.getClass(), \"what TreeTypes.of returns\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"tree-and-forest-do-not-build-types\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void treeAndForestDoNotBuildTypes() {\n        for (String owner : new String[] {\"Tree\", \"Forest\"}) {\n            var shape = Source.type(owner);\n            Expect.none(shape.news(\"Texture\"), owner + \" builds a Texture itself\");\n            Expect.none(shape.news(\"TreeType\"), owner + \" builds a TreeType itself\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"tree-keeps-no-appearance\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void treeKeepsNoAppearance() {\n        Class<?> tree = Types.named(\"Tree\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(tree, Texture.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"Tree should not hold its own Texture\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(tree, String.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"Tree should not copy the species or colour strings\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Share what every oak looks like"},{"checks":[{"id":"nothing-built-before-first-read","kind":"behaviour","title":"Creating the proxy builds nothing"},{"id":"built-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"The real Documents is built exactly once"},{"id":"same-id-read-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"A repeated id is read from the real one once"},{"id":"failures-are-not-cached","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failed read can be retried"},{"id":"concurrent-first-reads","kind":"behaviour","title":"Eight simultaneous first reads build and read once"},{"id":"proxy-is-a-documents","kind":"design","title":"CachedDocuments is a Documents with a factory"},{"id":"proxy-does-not-hardwire-the-real-one","kind":"design","title":"The proxy never names RemoteDocuments"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The proxy stands in for the real thing and adds two decisions: when to create it (first use) and when to skip it (already answered). Callers see only `Documents`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep the `Supplier`, a nullable real `Documents` created under a lock, and a `ConcurrentHashMap<String, String>` cache. `computeIfAbsent` does not store a value if the mapping function throws.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The read path can be tiny:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["public String read(String id) {","    return cache.computeIfAbsent(id, k -> real().read(k));","}","private synchronized Documents real() {","    if (real == null) real = factory.get();","    return real;","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"proxy","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Documents.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\n\ninterface Documents {\n    String read(String id);\n}\n\nfinal class RemoteDocuments implements Documents {\n    RemoteDocuments() { /* connect */ }\n\n    public String read(String id) { return \"body of \" + id; }\n}\n\nfinal class CachedDocuments implements Documents {\n    private final Supplier<Documents> factory;\n    private final Map<String, String> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n    private Documents real; // guarded by this\n\n    CachedDocuments(Supplier<Documents> factory) {\n        this.factory = factory;\n    }\n\n    public String read(String id) {\n        return cache.computeIfAbsent(id, k -> real().read(k));\n    }\n\n    private synchronized Documents real() {\n        if (real == null) real = factory.get();\n        return real;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Documents.java","source":"import java.util.function.Supplier;\n\ninterface Documents {\n    String read(String id);\n}\n\n// Opening a connection is slow; reading over it is slow too.\nfinal class RemoteDocuments implements Documents {\n    RemoteDocuments() { /* connect */ }\n\n    public String read(String id) { return \"body of \" + id; }\n}\n\n// TODO: a stand-in for any Documents that connects only when first needed\n// and never reads the same id twice.\nfinal class CachedDocuments implements Documents {\n    CachedDocuments(Supplier<Documents> factory) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public String read(String id) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"Connecting is slow and reading is slow, so do each as late and as rarely as possible.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement the **proxy** `CachedDocuments` in `Documents.java`. It is a `Documents`, built from a `Supplier<Documents>` factory.","type":"p"},{"items":["Creating it must not call the factory; the first `read` does, once, even when many threads read at the same moment.","Reading an id that was read before returns the earlier reply without touching the real `Documents`.","Different ids each reach the real `Documents` once.","If the real read throws, the exception reaches the caller and nothing is cached for that id.","Do not name `RemoteDocuments` inside the proxy."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ProxyKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ProxyKataTest {\n    /** A Documents that counts how often it is built and read. */\n    static final class Counting implements Documents {\n        final AtomicInteger built;\n        final AtomicInteger reads = new AtomicInteger();\n        boolean failNext;\n\n        Counting(AtomicInteger built) { this.built = built; built.incrementAndGet(); }\n\n        public String read(String id) {\n            reads.incrementAndGet();\n            if (failNext) { failNext = false; throw new IllegalStateException(\"down\"); }\n            Stress.pause(2);\n            return \"body of \" + id;\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"nothing-built-before-first-read\")\n    void nothingBuiltBeforeFirstRead() {\n        var built = new AtomicInteger();\n        new CachedDocuments(() -> new Counting(built));\n        Expect.equal(0, built.get(), \"real Documents built just by creating the proxy\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"built-once\")\n    void builtOnce() {\n        var built = new AtomicInteger();\n        var docs = new CachedDocuments(() -> new Counting(built));\n        docs.read(\"a\");\n        docs.read(\"b\");\n        docs.read(\"c\");\n        Expect.equal(1, built.get(), \"real Documents built after three reads\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"same-id-read-once\")\n    void sameIdReadOnce() {\n        var built = new AtomicInteger();\n        Counting[] real = new Counting[1];\n        var docs = new CachedDocuments(() -> real[0] = new Counting(built));\n        Expect.equal(\"body of a\", docs.read(\"a\"), \"first read\");\n        Expect.equal(\"body of a\", docs.read(\"a\"), \"second read\");\n        Expect.equal(1, real[0].reads.get(), \"real reads of the same id\");\n        docs.read(\"b\");\n        Expect.equal(2, real[0].reads.get(), \"a different id must reach the real thing\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"failures-are-not-cached\")\n    void failuresAreNotCached() {\n        var built = new AtomicInteger();\n        Counting[] real = new Counting[1];\n        var docs = new CachedDocuments(() -> real[0] = new Counting(built));\n        docs.read(\"warm\");\n        real[0].failNext = true;\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> docs.read(\"x\"), \"a failing read\");\n        Expect.equal(\"body of x\", docs.read(\"x\"), \"retrying after a failure\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"concurrent-first-reads\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void concurrentFirstReads() {\n        var built = new AtomicInteger();\n        Counting[] real = new Counting[1];\n        var docs = new CachedDocuments(() -> {\n            Stress.pause(10);\n            return real[0] = new Counting(built);\n        });\n        List<String> bodies = Stress.race(8, () -> docs.read(\"shared\"));\n        Expect.equal(1, built.get(), \"real Documents built by 8 simultaneous first reads\");\n        Expect.equal(1, real[0].reads.get(), \"real reads of one id by 8 threads\");\n        Expect.equal(8, (int) bodies.stream().filter(\"body of shared\"::equals).count(), \"replies\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"proxy-is-a-documents\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void proxyIsADocuments() {\n        Class<?> proxy = Types.named(\"CachedDocuments\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Documents.class.isAssignableFrom(proxy),\n            \"CachedDocuments should implement Documents so callers cannot tell\");\n        Types.constructor(proxy, java.util.function.Supplier.class);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"proxy-does-not-hardwire-the-real-one\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void proxyDoesNotHardwireTheRealOne() {\n        var proxy = Source.type(\"CachedDocuments\");\n        Expect.none(proxy.news(\"RemoteDocuments\"), \"CachedDocuments builds RemoteDocuments itself\");\n        Expect.none(proxy.instanceofs(), \"CachedDocuments inspects the concrete type of the subject\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"A lazy, caching stand-in for slow documents"},{"checks":[{"id":"small-expenses-are-automatic","kind":"behaviour","title":"Small expenses are approved automatically"},{"id":"bigger-expenses-escalate-upwards","kind":"behaviour","title":"Bigger expenses climb to manager, director, board"},{"id":"gifts-have-their-own-rule","kind":"behaviour","title":"Gifts over 50.00 are rejected"},{"id":"approver-is-a-one-method-interface","kind":"design","title":"Approver is a one-method interface"},{"id":"chain-runs-links-in-order","kind":"design","title":"The chain asks links in order and stops at an answer"},{"id":"chain-falls-through-to-board","kind":"design","title":"An unanswered request goes to the board"},{"id":"chain-does-not-know-the-rules","kind":"design","title":"ApprovalChain contains no rules"},{"id":"service-delegates-to-a-chain","kind":"design","title":"ApprovalService holds an ApprovalChain"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Every rule has the same shape: look at the expense, then either decide or say \"not mine\". Name that shape, and the nesting turns into a sequence.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Write `Approver` returning `Optional<String>`. Give `ApprovalChain` a list of approvers and loop until one answers. Build the standard chain, gift rule first, in `Approvals.standard()`; `ApprovalService` holds that chain.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"A threshold rule is one small lambda factory:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["static Approver upTo(long cents, String who) {","    return e -> e.cents() <= cents","        ? Optional.of(\"approved:\" + who)","        : Optional.empty();","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"chain-of-responsibility","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Approval.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\nrecord Expense(String employee, String category, long cents) { }\n\n// One link: answer, or stay silent so the next link can try.\ninterface Approver {\n    Optional<String> decide(Expense e);\n}\n\nfinal class ApprovalChain {\n    private final List<Approver> approvers;\n\n    ApprovalChain(List<Approver> approvers) {\n        this.approvers = List.copyOf(approvers);\n    }\n\n    String approve(Expense e) {\n        for (Approver a : approvers) {\n            Optional<String> decision = a.decide(e);\n            if (decision.isPresent()) return decision.get();\n        }\n        return \"escalate:board\";\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Approvals {\n    private Approvals() { }\n\n    static Approver upTo(long cents, String who) {\n        return e -> e.cents() <= cents\n            ? Optional.of(\"approved:\" + who) : Optional.empty();\n    }\n\n    static ApprovalChain standard() {\n        Approver gifts = e -> !e.category().equals(\"gift\")\n            ? Optional.empty()\n            : Optional.of(e.cents() > 5_000\n                ? \"rejected:policy\" : \"approved:auto\");\n        return new ApprovalChain(List.of(gifts,\n            upTo(10_000, \"auto\"),\n            upTo(100_000, \"manager\"),\n            upTo(1_000_000, \"director\")));\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class ApprovalService {\n    private final ApprovalChain chain = Approvals.standard();\n\n    String approve(Expense e) { return chain.approve(e); }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Approval.java","source":"record Expense(String employee, String category, long cents) { }\n\n// Every new rule means finding the right place inside these nested ifs.\nfinal class ApprovalService {\n    // Callers use this. Keep its signature and replies.\n    String approve(Expense e) {\n        if (e.category().equals(\"gift\")) {\n            if (e.cents() > 5_000) {\n                return \"rejected:policy\";\n            } else {\n                return \"approved:auto\";\n            }\n        } else {\n            if (e.cents() <= 10_000) {\n                return \"approved:auto\";\n            } else {\n                if (e.cents() <= 100_000) {\n                    return \"approved:manager\";\n                } else {\n                    if (e.cents() <= 1_000_000) {\n                        return \"approved:director\";\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return \"escalate:board\";\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Each approval rule is buried in the nesting of one method.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Turn the rules into a **chain of responsibility**. `ApprovalService.approve(Expense)` must return exactly what it returns now, and `Expense` stays as it is.","type":"p"},{"items":["`interface Approver` with one method, `Optional<String> decide(Expense)`: empty means \"not mine, pass it on\".","`ApprovalChain(List<Approver>)` with `String approve(Expense)`: the first present answer wins; if nobody answers, `escalate:board`.","`ApprovalChain` knows no rules; each rule lives in an `Approver`.","`ApprovalService` delegates to a chain and keeps it in a field and decides nothing itself."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ChainKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ChainKataTest {\n    static String decide(String category, long cents) {\n        return new ApprovalService().approve(new Expense(\"ann\", category, cents));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"small-expenses-are-automatic\")\n    void smallExpensesAreAutomatic() {\n        Expect.equal(\"approved:auto\", decide(\"meals\", 10_000), \"meals at 100.00\");\n        Expect.equal(\"approved:auto\", decide(\"meals\", 1), \"meals at 0.01\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bigger-expenses-escalate-upwards\")\n    void biggerExpensesEscalateUpwards() {\n        Expect.equal(\"approved:manager\", decide(\"travel\", 10_001), \"travel at 100.01\");\n        Expect.equal(\"approved:manager\", decide(\"travel\", 100_000), \"travel at 1000.00\");\n        Expect.equal(\"approved:director\", decide(\"travel\", 100_001), \"travel at 1000.01\");\n        Expect.equal(\"approved:director\", decide(\"travel\", 1_000_000), \"travel at 10000.00\");\n        Expect.equal(\"escalate:board\", decide(\"travel\", 1_000_001), \"travel above 10000.00\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"gifts-have-their-own-rule\")\n    void giftsHaveTheirOwnRule() {\n        Expect.equal(\"approved:auto\", decide(\"gift\", 5_000), \"a gift at 50.00\");\n        Expect.equal(\"rejected:policy\", decide(\"gift\", 5_001), \"a gift at 50.01\");\n        Expect.equal(\"rejected:policy\", decide(\"gift\", 500_000), \"an expensive gift\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"approver-is-a-one-method-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void approverIsAOneMethodInterface() {\n        Class<?> approver = Types.named(\"Approver\");\n        Expect.isTrue(approver.isInterface(), \"Approver should be an interface\");\n        Method m = Types.singleAbstractMethod(approver);\n        Expect.equal(Optional.class, m.getReturnType(),\n            \"Approver's method should return an Optional<String>: empty means pass it on\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(Expense.class), List.of(m.getParameterTypes()), \"its parameters\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"chain-runs-links-in-order\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void chainRunsLinksInOrder() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> approver = Types.named(\"Approver\");\n        List<String> calls = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object silent = Types.implement(approver, a -> { calls.add(\"first\"); return Optional.empty(); });\n        Object answers = Types.implement(approver, a -> { calls.add(\"second\"); return Optional.of(\"yes\"); });\n        Object never = Types.implement(approver, a -> { calls.add(\"third\"); return Optional.of(\"no\"); });\n        Object chain = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"ApprovalChain\"), List.class),\n            List.of(silent, answers, never));\n        Method approve = Types.method(chain.getClass(), \"approve\", Expense.class);\n        Object reply = Types.call(approve, chain, new Expense(\"ann\", \"x\", 1));\n        Expect.equal(\"yes\", reply, \"the first present answer wins\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"first\", \"second\"), calls, \"links asked, in order, stopping at the answer\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"chain-falls-through-to-board\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void chainFallsThroughToBoard() throws Throwable {\n        Object silent = Types.implement(Types.named(\"Approver\"), a -> Optional.empty());\n        Object chain = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"ApprovalChain\"), List.class),\n            List.of(silent, silent));\n        Method approve = Types.method(chain.getClass(), \"approve\", Expense.class);\n        Expect.equal(\"escalate:board\", Types.call(approve, chain, new Expense(\"ann\", \"x\", 1)),\n            \"a request nobody answers\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"chain-does-not-know-the-rules\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void chainDoesNotKnowTheRules() {\n        var chain = Source.type(\"ApprovalChain\");\n        Expect.none(chain.calls(\"cents\"), \"ApprovalChain reads the amount: rules belong in approvers\");\n        Expect.none(chain.calls(\"category\"), \"ApprovalChain reads the category\");\n        Expect.none(chain.comparedStrings(), \"ApprovalChain compares strings to choose a rule\");\n        Expect.none(chain.instanceofs(), \"ApprovalChain inspects the concrete approver\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-delegates-to-a-chain\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void serviceDelegatesToAChain() {\n        Types.onlyFieldOfType(Types.named(\"ApprovalService\"), Types.named(\"ApprovalChain\"));\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Untangle the expense approval ifs"},{"checks":[{"id":"insert-and-undo","kind":"behaviour","title":"Inserts can be undone one by one"},{"id":"delete-restores-what-it-removed","kind":"behaviour","title":"Undoing a delete restores the text"},{"id":"redo-replays","kind":"behaviour","title":"Redo replays undone commands in order"},{"id":"delete-recaptures-on-redo","kind":"behaviour","title":"Delete works across undo/redo cycles"},{"id":"new-command-clears-redo","kind":"behaviour","title":"A new command clears the redo list"},{"id":"empty-history-is-safe","kind":"behaviour","title":"An empty History ignores undo and redo"},{"id":"history-drives-any-command","kind":"design","title":"History drives a Command it has never seen"},{"id":"history-knows-no-edits","kind":"design","title":"History never mentions Doc, Insert or Delete"},{"id":"commands-hold-their-target","kind":"design","title":"Insert and Delete hold their Doc"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A request becomes an object that carries everything needed to do it and to reverse it. The caller that runs and remembers requests then needs no knowledge of what they do.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`Insert` and `Delete` keep a `final Doc` and their arguments. `Delete.execute` stores what `doc.delete` returns. `History` keeps two stacks of `Command`: done and undone.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The heart of `History`:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["void run(Command c) {","    c.execute(); done.push(c); undone.clear();","}","void undo() {","    if (done.isEmpty()) return;","    Command c = done.pop(); c.undo(); undone.push(c);","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"command","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Doc.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Doc.java","source":"final class Doc {\n    private final StringBuilder text = new StringBuilder();\n\n    void insert(int at, String s) { text.insert(at, s); }\n\n    // Removes [from, to) and returns what was removed.\n    String delete(int from, int to) {\n        String removed = text.substring(from, to);\n        text.delete(from, to);\n        return removed;\n    }\n\n    String text() { return text.toString(); }\n}\n\ninterface Command {\n    void execute();\n\n    void undo();\n}\n"},{"name":"Editor.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.Deque;\n\nrecord Insert(Doc doc, int at, String s) implements Command {\n    public void execute() { doc.insert(at, s); }\n\n    public void undo() { doc.delete(at, at + s.length()); }\n}\n\nfinal class Delete implements Command {\n    private final Doc doc;\n    private final int from;\n    private final int to;\n    private String removed = \"\"; // captured on every execute\n\n    Delete(Doc doc, int from, int to) {\n        this.doc = doc;\n        this.from = from;\n        this.to = to;\n    }\n\n    public void execute() { removed = doc.delete(from, to); }\n\n    public void undo() { doc.insert(from, removed); }\n}\n\nfinal class History {\n    private final Deque<Command> done = new ArrayDeque<>();\n    private final Deque<Command> undone = new ArrayDeque<>();\n\n    void run(Command c) {\n        c.execute();\n        done.push(c);\n        undone.clear();\n    }\n\n    void undo() {\n        if (done.isEmpty()) return;\n        Command c = done.pop();\n        c.undo();\n        undone.push(c);\n    }\n\n    void redo() {\n        if (undone.isEmpty()) return;\n        Command c = undone.pop();\n        c.execute();\n        done.push(c);\n    }\n\n    boolean canUndo() { return !done.isEmpty(); }\n\n    boolean canRedo() { return !undone.isEmpty(); }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Doc.java","source":"final class Doc {\n    private final StringBuilder text = new StringBuilder();\n\n    void insert(int at, String s) { text.insert(at, s); }\n\n    // Removes [from, to) and returns what was removed.\n    String delete(int from, int to) {\n        String removed = text.substring(from, to);\n        text.delete(from, to);\n        return removed;\n    }\n\n    String text() { return text.toString(); }\n}\n\ninterface Command {\n    void execute();\n\n    void undo();\n}\n"},{"name":"Editor.java","source":"// Edits as objects, so they can be undone and redone.\nfinal class Insert implements Command {\n    Insert(Doc doc, int at, String s) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public void execute() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n\n    public void undo() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n}\n\nfinal class Delete implements Command {\n    Delete(Doc doc, int from, int to) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public void execute() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n\n    public void undo() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n}\n\n// Runs commands and remembers them. It knows nothing about documents.\nfinal class History {\n    void run(Command c) { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n\n    void undo() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n\n    void redo() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n\n    boolean canUndo() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n\n    boolean canRedo() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\"); }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Make each edit an object that can run itself and take itself back.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Doc` and `Command` are given. Implement the **command** pattern in `Editor.java`.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Insert(Doc doc, int at, String s)` inserts `s` at `at`; its undo removes it.","`Delete(Doc doc, int from, int to)` removes `[from, to)`; its undo puts the removed text back. It must remember the text each time it executes.","`History`: `run(Command)` executes and records; `undo()` and `redo()` step back and forward; `canUndo()` and `canRedo()` report. Undo or redo with nothing to do is a no-op.","Running a new command discards the redo list.","`History` may only know `Command`: no `Doc`, `Insert` or `Delete`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"CommandKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass CommandKataTest {\n    static final class Recording implements Command {\n        final List<String> log;\n        final String name;\n\n        Recording(List<String> log, String name) { this.log = log; this.name = name; }\n\n        public void execute() { log.add(\"do \" + name); }\n        public void undo() { log.add(\"undo \" + name); }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"insert-and-undo\")\n    void insertAndUndo() {\n        Doc doc = new Doc();\n        History h = new History();\n        h.run(new Insert(doc, 0, \"Hello\"));\n        h.run(new Insert(doc, 5, \" world\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"Hello world\", doc.text(), \"after two inserts\");\n        h.undo();\n        Expect.equal(\"Hello\", doc.text(), \"after one undo\");\n        h.undo();\n        Expect.equal(\"\", doc.text(), \"after two undos\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"delete-restores-what-it-removed\")\n    void deleteRestoresWhatItRemoved() {\n        Doc doc = new Doc();\n        History h = new History();\n        h.run(new Insert(doc, 0, \"Hello world\"));\n        h.run(new Delete(doc, 0, 6));\n        Expect.equal(\"world\", doc.text(), \"after delete\");\n        h.undo();\n        Expect.equal(\"Hello world\", doc.text(), \"undo of delete\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"redo-replays\")\n    void redoReplays() {\n        Doc doc = new Doc();\n        History h = new History();\n        h.run(new Insert(doc, 0, \"abc\"));\n        h.run(new Delete(doc, 1, 2));\n        h.undo();\n        h.undo();\n        Expect.equal(\"\", doc.text(), \"after undoing everything\");\n        h.redo();\n        Expect.equal(\"abc\", doc.text(), \"first redo\");\n        h.redo();\n        Expect.equal(\"ac\", doc.text(), \"second redo\");\n        h.undo();\n        Expect.equal(\"abc\", doc.text(), \"undo after redo restores the deleted text\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"delete-recaptures-on-redo\")\n    void deleteRecapturesOnRedo() {\n        Doc doc = new Doc();\n        History h = new History();\n        h.run(new Insert(doc, 0, \"one two\"));\n        Delete d = new Delete(doc, 0, 3);\n        h.run(d);\n        h.undo();\n        h.undo();\n        h.redo();\n        h.redo();\n        h.undo();\n        Expect.equal(\"one two\", doc.text(), \"undo after a full undo/redo cycle\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"new-command-clears-redo\")\n    void newCommandClearsRedo() {\n        Doc doc = new Doc();\n        History h = new History();\n        h.run(new Insert(doc, 0, \"a\"));\n        h.run(new Insert(doc, 1, \"b\"));\n        h.undo();\n        Expect.isTrue(h.canRedo(), \"after an undo there is something to redo\");\n        h.run(new Insert(doc, 1, \"c\"));\n        Expect.isTrue(!h.canRedo(), \"running a new command should drop the redo stack\");\n        h.redo();\n        Expect.equal(\"ac\", doc.text(), \"redo with nothing to redo must change nothing\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"empty-history-is-safe\")\n    void emptyHistoryIsSafe() {\n        History h = new History();\n        Expect.isTrue(!h.canUndo() && !h.canRedo(), \"a new History has nothing to undo or redo\");\n        h.undo();\n        h.redo();\n        Expect.isTrue(!h.canUndo() && !h.canRedo(), \"undo/redo on an empty History must be no-ops\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"history-drives-any-command\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void historyDrivesAnyCommand() {\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        History h = new History();\n        h.run(new Recording(log, \"a\"));\n        h.run(new Recording(log, \"b\"));\n        h.undo();\n        h.redo();\n        h.undo();\n        h.undo();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"do a\", \"do b\", \"undo b\", \"do b\", \"undo b\", \"undo a\"), log,\n            \"History with Commands it has never seen\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"history-knows-no-edits\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void historyKnowsNoEdits() {\n        var history = Source.type(\"History\");\n        for (String name : new String[] {\"Doc\", \"Insert\", \"Delete\"}) {\n            Expect.none(history.mentions(name), \"History mentions \" + name + \": it should only know Command\");\n        }\n        Expect.none(history.instanceofs(), \"History inspects the concrete type of a Command\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(Types.named(\"History\"), Doc.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"History should not hold a Doc\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"commands-hold-their-target\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void commandsHoldTheirTarget() {\n        for (String name : new String[] {\"Insert\", \"Delete\"}) {\n            Class<?> c = Types.named(name);\n            Expect.isTrue(Command.class.isAssignableFrom(c), name + \" should implement Command\");\n            Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(c, Doc.class);\n            Expect.isTrue(java.lang.reflect.Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n                name + \".\" + f.getName() + \" should be final\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Undo and redo for a text editor"},{"checks":[{"id":"flag-lookup","kind":"behaviour","title":"A flag reads the context, unbound flags fail"},{"id":"not-and-or","kind":"behaviour","title":"Not, And and Or follow their truth tables"},{"id":"short-circuit","kind":"behaviour","title":"And and Or skip the branch they do not need"},{"id":"same-tree-many-contexts","kind":"behaviour","title":"One tree evaluates against many contexts"},{"id":"parse-evaluates","kind":"behaviour","title":"Parsed sentences give the right answers"},{"id":"parse-rejects-bad-input","kind":"behaviour","title":"Malformed sentences are rejected"},{"id":"nodes-evaluate-themselves","kind":"design","title":"Nodes evaluate without switching on types"},{"id":"nodes-are-immutable","kind":"design","title":"Nodes hold only final fields"},{"id":"parse-builds-the-nodes","kind":"design","title":"Parsing builds the tree and stops there"},{"id":"operands-are-any-rule","kind":"design","title":"Operators accept any Rule"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Each grammar rule is a class. A terminal answers directly from the context; a nonterminal asks its children and combines the answers. No central `switch` should decide how to evaluate.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Write `eval` in each record: `Flag` reads the map, `Not`, `And`, `Or` call `eval` on their children. For `parse`, read tokens recursively: `(` starts an operator, then its operands, then `)`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`&&` and `||` short-circuit for free. The parser's core:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["Rule rule = switch (op) {","    case \"not\" -> new Not(read(tokens));","    case \"and\" -> new And(read(tokens), read(tokens));","    case \"or\" -> new Or(read(tokens), read(tokens));","    default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(op);","};"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"interpreter","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"readOnly":["Rule.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Rule.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\n\n// Given. Every node of the rule tree is a Rule.\ninterface Rule {\n    boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags);\n}\n"},{"name":"Rules.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.Deque;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nrecord Flag(String name) implements Rule {\n    public boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags) {\n        Boolean value = flags.get(name);\n        if (value == null) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"unbound \" + name);\n        }\n        return value;\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Not(Rule operand) implements Rule {\n    public boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags) {\n        return !operand.eval(flags);\n    }\n}\n\nrecord And(Rule left, Rule right) implements Rule {\n    public boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags) {\n        return left.eval(flags) && right.eval(flags);\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Or(Rule left, Rule right) implements Rule {\n    public boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags) {\n        return left.eval(flags) || right.eval(flags);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Rules {\n    private Rules() { }\n\n    static Rule parse(String source) {\n        String spaced = source.replace(\"(\", \" ( \").replace(\")\", \" ) \");\n        Deque<String> tokens =\n            new ArrayDeque<>(List.of(spaced.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\")));\n        Rule rule = read(tokens);\n        if (!tokens.isEmpty()) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"extra input: \" + tokens);\n        }\n        return rule;\n    }\n\n    private static Rule read(Deque<String> tokens) {\n        String token = next(tokens);\n        if (token.equals(\")\")) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unexpected )\");\n        }\n        if (!token.equals(\"(\")) {\n            if (!token.matches(\"[a-z][a-z0-9_]*\")) {\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"bad flag: \" + token);\n            }\n            return new Flag(token);\n        }\n        String op = next(tokens);\n        Rule rule = switch (op) {\n            case \"not\" -> new Not(read(tokens));\n            case \"and\" -> new And(read(tokens), read(tokens));\n            case \"or\" -> new Or(read(tokens), read(tokens));\n            default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"operator: \" + op);\n        };\n        if (!next(tokens).equals(\")\")) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"expected )\");\n        }\n        return rule;\n    }\n\n    private static String next(Deque<String> tokens) {\n        if (tokens.isEmpty()) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unexpected end\");\n        }\n        return tokens.removeFirst();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Rule.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\n\n// Given. Every node of the rule tree is a Rule.\ninterface Rule {\n    boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags);\n}\n"},{"name":"Rules.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\n\n// Eligibility rules over named flags, e.g. (and pro (not trial)).\n// Each class below is a node of the rule tree.\nrecord Flag(String name) implements Rule {\n    public boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Not(Rule operand) implements Rule {\n    public boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\nrecord And(Rule left, Rule right) implements Rule {\n    public boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Or(Rule left, Rule right) implements Rule {\n    public boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Rules {\n    private Rules() { }\n\n    /** Builds the tree for the text. It must not evaluate anything. */\n    static Rule parse(String source) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Marketing writes rules like `(and pro (not trial))`. Make each grammar rule a class that evaluates itself.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Rule` is given: `boolean eval(Map<String, Boolean> flags)`. Fill in `Rules.java`.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Flag(String name)` returns its flag, or throws `IllegalStateException` if the flag is unbound.","`Not(Rule)`, `And(Rule, Rule)` and `Or(Rule, Rule)` combine their children. `And` and `Or` must short-circuit.","`Rules.parse(String)` builds the tree from the text: a flag name, `(not r)`, `(and r r)` or `(or r r)`, with any amount of whitespace.","`parse` never evaluates. Malformed input throws `IllegalArgumentException`.","One parsed tree must evaluate against many contexts."],"type":"bullets"},{"text":"Do not change `Rule` or the constructors above.","type":"p"}],"tests":[{"name":"InterpreterKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass InterpreterKataTest {\n    static final Map<String, Boolean> ENV =\n        Map.of(\"pro\", true, \"trial\", false, \"eu\", true);\n\n    static final Rule BOOM = flags -> {\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"evaluated a branch it should skip\");\n    };\n\n    static Rule flag(String n) { return new Flag(n); }\n\n    static boolean run(Rule rule) { return rule.eval(ENV); }\n\n    @Check(id = \"flag-lookup\")\n    void flagLookup() {\n        Expect.equal(true, run(flag(\"pro\")), \"a true flag\");\n        Expect.equal(false, run(flag(\"trial\")), \"a false flag\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            () -> run(flag(\"ghost\")), \"a flag that is not in the context\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"not-and-or\")\n    void notAndOr() {\n        Expect.equal(true, run(new Not(flag(\"trial\"))), \"not false\");\n        Expect.equal(false, run(new Not(flag(\"pro\"))), \"not true\");\n        Expect.equal(true, run(new And(flag(\"pro\"), flag(\"eu\"))), \"true and true\");\n        Expect.equal(false, run(new And(flag(\"pro\"), flag(\"trial\"))), \"true and false\");\n        Expect.equal(true, run(new Or(flag(\"trial\"), flag(\"eu\"))), \"false or true\");\n        Expect.equal(false, run(new Or(flag(\"trial\"), new Not(flag(\"eu\")))), \"false or false\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"short-circuit\")\n    void shortCircuit() {\n        Expect.equal(false, run(new And(flag(\"trial\"), BOOM)), \"false and <skipped>\");\n        Expect.equal(true, run(new Or(flag(\"pro\"), BOOM)), \"true or <skipped>\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"same-tree-many-contexts\")\n    void sameTreeManyContexts() {\n        Rule rule = new And(flag(\"pro\"), new Not(flag(\"trial\")));\n        Expect.equal(true, rule.eval(Map.of(\"pro\", true, \"trial\", false)), \"first context\");\n        Expect.equal(false, rule.eval(Map.of(\"pro\", true, \"trial\", true)), \"second context\");\n        Expect.equal(false, rule.eval(Map.of(\"pro\", false, \"trial\", false)), \"third context\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"parse-evaluates\")\n    void parseEvaluates() {\n        Expect.equal(true, run(Rules.parse(\"pro\")), \"a lone flag\");\n        Expect.equal(true, run(Rules.parse(\"(not trial)\")), \"(not trial)\");\n        Expect.equal(false, run(Rules.parse(\"(and pro (or trial (not eu)))\")),\n            \"(and pro (or trial (not eu)))\");\n        Expect.equal(true, run(Rules.parse(\"(and pro (or trial eu))\")),\n            \"(and pro (or trial eu))\");\n        Expect.equal(true, run(Rules.parse(\"  ( and   pro eu )  \")),\n            \"a sentence with extra spaces\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"parse-rejects-bad-input\")\n    void parseRejectsBadInput() {\n        for (String bad : List.of(\"\", \"(and pro)\", \"(xor pro eu)\", \"(and pro eu\",\n                \"pro eu\", \")\", \"(not)\", \"(and pro eu))\", \"(not a b)\")) {\n            Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n                () -> Rules.parse(bad), \"parsing \\\"\" + bad + \"\\\"\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"nodes-evaluate-themselves\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void nodesEvaluateThemselves() {\n        for (String name : List.of(\"Flag\", \"Not\", \"And\", \"Or\")) {\n            var eval = Source.type(name).method(\"eval\");\n            Expect.none(eval.switches(), name + \".eval switches instead of just evaluating\");\n            Expect.none(eval.instanceofs(), name + \".eval inspects node types\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"nodes-are-immutable\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void nodesAreImmutable() {\n        for (String name : List.of(\"Flag\", \"Not\", \"And\", \"Or\")) {\n            for (var f : Types.named(name).getDeclaredFields()) {\n                if (f.isSynthetic() || java.lang.reflect.Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers())) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                Expect.isTrue(java.lang.reflect.Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n                    name + \".\" + f.getName() + \" should be final\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"parse-builds-the-nodes\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void parseBuildsTheNodes() {\n        Expect.equal(And.class, Rules.parse(\"(and pro eu)\").getClass(), \"(and pro eu)\");\n        Expect.equal(Or.class, Rules.parse(\"(or pro eu)\").getClass(), \"(or pro eu)\");\n        Expect.equal(Not.class, Rules.parse(\"(not pro)\").getClass(), \"(not pro)\");\n        Expect.equal(Flag.class, Rules.parse(\"pro\").getClass(), \"pro\");\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"Rules\").calls(\"eval\"),\n            \"Rules.parse should only build the tree, never evaluate it\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"operands-are-any-rule\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void operandsAreAnyRule() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> rule = Types.named(\"Rule\");\n        Object yes = Types.implement(rule, args -> true);\n        Object no = Types.implement(rule, args -> false);\n        Object and = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"And\"), rule, rule), yes, no);\n        Object or = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Or\"), rule, rule), yes, no);\n        Object not = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Not\"), rule), no);\n        Expect.equal(false, ((Rule) and).eval(ENV), \"And over rules it has never seen\");\n        Expect.equal(true, ((Rule) or).eval(ENV), \"Or over rules it has never seen\");\n        Expect.equal(true, ((Rule) not).eval(ENV), \"Not over a rule it has never seen\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Evaluate eligibility rules as a tree"},{"checks":[{"id":"oldest-first","kind":"behaviour","title":"Elements come out oldest first"},{"id":"wraps-when-full","kind":"behaviour","title":"A full buffer overwrites the oldest element"},{"id":"empty-and-exhausted","kind":"behaviour","title":"Running out of elements raises NoSuchElementException"},{"id":"has-next-does-not-advance","kind":"behaviour","title":"hasNext() does not move the cursor"},{"id":"independent-iterators","kind":"behaviour","title":"Two cursors move independently"},{"id":"fail-fast","kind":"behaviour","title":"A stale cursor throws ConcurrentModificationException"},{"id":"fresh-iterator-after-change","kind":"behaviour","title":"A new cursor sees the changed buffer"},{"id":"remove-unsupported","kind":"behaviour","title":"remove() is unsupported"},{"id":"buffer-is-not-its-own-cursor","kind":"design","title":"The buffer hands out separate cursor objects"},{"id":"storage-stays-private","kind":"design","title":"The storage is not exposed"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Traversal state (how far you are) does not belong in the collection. Put it in a small cursor object that the buffer creates on every `iterator()` call.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Return an anonymous `Iterator<T>` that remembers `modCount` when created and keeps its own `offset`. The element at `offset` lives at slot `(start + offset) % slots.length`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Core of the cursor:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["private final int expected = modCount;","private int offset;","public boolean hasNext() { return offset < size; }","public T next() {","    if (expected != modCount) throw new ConcurrentModificationException();","    if (offset >= size) throw new NoSuchElementException();","    return (T) slots[(start + offset++) % slots.length];","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"iterator","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"solution":[{"name":"RingBuffer.java","source":"import java.util.ConcurrentModificationException;\nimport java.util.Iterator;\nimport java.util.NoSuchElementException;\n\nfinal class RingBuffer<T> implements Iterable<T> {\n    private final Object[] slots;\n    private int start;\n    private int size;\n    private int modCount;\n\n    RingBuffer(int capacity) {\n        if (capacity < 1) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"capacity\");\n        }\n        slots = new Object[capacity];\n    }\n\n    int size() { return size; }\n\n    void add(T item) {\n        if (size < slots.length) {\n            slots[(start + size) % slots.length] = item;\n            size++;\n        } else {\n            slots[start] = item;\n            start = (start + 1) % slots.length;\n        }\n        modCount++;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public Iterator<T> iterator() {\n        return new Iterator<>() {\n            private final int expected = modCount;\n            private int offset;\n\n            public boolean hasNext() { return offset < size; }\n\n            @SuppressWarnings(\"unchecked\")\n            public T next() {\n                if (expected != modCount) {\n                    throw new ConcurrentModificationException();\n                }\n                if (offset >= size) {\n                    throw new NoSuchElementException();\n                }\n                return (T) slots[(start + offset++) % slots.length];\n            }\n        };\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"RingBuffer.java","source":"import java.util.Iterator;\n\n// Keeps the most recent log lines. When full, add() overwrites the oldest.\nfinal class RingBuffer<T> implements Iterable<T> {\n    private final Object[] slots;\n    private int start;     // index of the oldest element\n    private int size;\n    private int modCount;  // bump it on every add\n\n    RingBuffer(int capacity) {\n        if (capacity < 1) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"capacity\");\n        }\n        slots = new Object[capacity];\n    }\n\n    int size() { return size; }\n\n    void add(T item) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public Iterator<T> iterator() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A log viewer keeps the latest lines in a ring buffer. Make it `Iterable` without exposing its array.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Finish `RingBuffer<T>` in `RingBuffer.java`; the constructor and `size()` are done.","type":"p"},{"items":["`add(T)` appends. When the buffer is full it overwrites the oldest element.","`iterator()` walks from the oldest element to the newest, so `for (T x : buffer)` works.","Every call returns an independent cursor; `hasNext()` never advances it.","`next()` past the end throws `NoSuchElementException`; `remove()` is unsupported.","The cursor is fail-fast: if the buffer was changed by `add` after the cursor was created, `next()` throws `ConcurrentModificationException`."],"type":"bullets"},{"text":"Keep the storage private.","type":"p"}],"tests":[{"name":"IteratorKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Collection;\nimport java.util.ConcurrentModificationException;\nimport java.util.Iterator;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.NoSuchElementException;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass IteratorKataTest {\n    static RingBuffer<String> buffer(int capacity, String... items) {\n        var b = new RingBuffer<String>(capacity);\n        for (String s : items) {\n            b.add(s);\n        }\n        return b;\n    }\n\n    static List<String> drain(Iterable<String> source) {\n        List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (String s : source) {\n            out.add(s);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"oldest-first\")\n    void oldestFirst() {\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a\", \"b\"), drain(buffer(3, \"a\", \"b\")), \"a half-full buffer\");\n        Expect.equal(2, buffer(3, \"a\", \"b\").size(), \"size\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"wraps-when-full\")\n    void wrapsWhenFull() {\n        var b = buffer(3, \"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"c\", \"d\", \"e\"), drain(b), \"after overwriting the oldest\");\n        Expect.equal(3, b.size(), \"size stays at capacity\");\n        b.add(\"f\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"d\", \"e\", \"f\"), drain(b), \"after one more add\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"empty-and-exhausted\")\n    void emptyAndExhausted() {\n        Iterator<String> empty = buffer(2).iterator();\n        Expect.isTrue(!empty.hasNext(), \"an empty buffer has no next\");\n        Expect.raises(NoSuchElementException.class, empty::next, \"next() on an empty buffer\");\n        Iterator<String> it = buffer(2, \"a\").iterator();\n        it.next();\n        Expect.isTrue(!it.hasNext(), \"no next after the last element\");\n        Expect.raises(NoSuchElementException.class, it::next, \"next() past the end\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"has-next-does-not-advance\")\n    void hasNextDoesNotAdvance() {\n        Iterator<String> it = buffer(3, \"a\", \"b\").iterator();\n        Expect.isTrue(it.hasNext() && it.hasNext() && it.hasNext(), \"hasNext\");\n        Expect.equal(\"a\", it.next(), \"first next after hasNext calls\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"independent-iterators\")\n    void independentIterators() {\n        var b = buffer(3, \"a\", \"b\", \"c\");\n        Iterator<String> one = b.iterator();\n        Iterator<String> two = b.iterator();\n        Expect.equal(\"a\", one.next(), \"one, first\");\n        Expect.equal(\"a\", two.next(), \"two, first\");\n        Expect.equal(\"b\", one.next(), \"one, second\");\n        Expect.equal(\"b\", two.next(), \"two, second\");\n        Expect.equal(\"c\", one.next(), \"one, third\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fail-fast\")\n    void failFast() {\n        var b = buffer(3, \"a\", \"b\");\n        Iterator<String> it = b.iterator();\n        it.next();\n        b.add(\"c\");\n        Expect.raises(ConcurrentModificationException.class, it::next,\n            \"next() after the buffer changed\");\n        var full = buffer(2, \"a\", \"b\");\n        Iterator<String> it2 = full.iterator();\n        full.add(\"c\");\n        Expect.raises(ConcurrentModificationException.class, it2::next,\n            \"next() after an overwrite\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fresh-iterator-after-change\")\n    void freshIteratorAfterChange() {\n        var b = buffer(2, \"a\", \"b\");\n        b.iterator();\n        b.add(\"c\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"b\", \"c\"), drain(b), \"a new iterator after the change\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"remove-unsupported\")\n    void removeUnsupported() {\n        Iterator<String> it = buffer(2, \"a\", \"b\").iterator();\n        it.next();\n        Expect.raises(UnsupportedOperationException.class, it::remove, \"Iterator.remove()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"buffer-is-not-its-own-cursor\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void bufferIsNotItsOwnCursor() {\n        Class<?> type = Types.named(\"RingBuffer\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!Iterator.class.isAssignableFrom(type),\n            \"RingBuffer should hand out cursors, not be one\");\n        var b = buffer(2, \"a\");\n        Iterator<String> one = b.iterator();\n        Iterator<String> two = b.iterator();\n        Expect.isTrue(one != two, \"iterator() should return a new cursor every call\");\n        Expect.isTrue(one != (Object) b && one.getClass() != type,\n            \"the cursor should be its own object\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"storage-stays-private\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void storageStaysPrivate() {\n        Class<?> type = Types.named(\"RingBuffer\");\n        for (Method m : type.getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            if (m.isSynthetic() || Modifier.isPrivate(m.getModifiers())) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            Class<?> r = m.getReturnType();\n            Expect.isTrue(!r.isArray() && !Collection.class.isAssignableFrom(r),\n                \"RingBuffer.\" + m.getName() + \" exposes its storage; callers should iterate\");\n        }\n        for (var f : type.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(f.isSynthetic() || Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()),\n                \"RingBuffer.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"A fail-fast ring buffer you can loop over"},{"checks":[{"id":"starts-disabled","kind":"behaviour","title":"A new form starts empty and disabled"},{"id":"needs-name-and-terms","kind":"behaviour","title":"Submit needs a name and accepted terms"},{"id":"submit-sends-and-resets","kind":"behaviour","title":"Submit sends the name and resets the form"},{"id":"disabled-click-ignored","kind":"behaviour","title":"A disabled Submit does nothing"},{"id":"can-submit-again","kind":"behaviour","title":"The form can be submitted twice"},{"id":"dialog-interface","kind":"design","title":"Dialog is a one-method interface"},{"id":"widgets-know-only-the-dialog","kind":"design","title":"Widgets reference only the Dialog"},{"id":"widgets-report-to-the-dialog","kind":"design","title":"Widgets report their changes to any Dialog"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Widgets are coupled in a many-to-many web. Route everything through one object that all of them know, and move the knowledge of who reacts to whom into that object.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Give each widget a `Dialog` instead of references to its neighbours. Let `SignupForm` implement `Dialog`: it creates the widgets with `this`, and `changed` decides what to update.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The mediator's whole job:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["public void changed(Object source) {","    if (source == submit) {","        sent.add(name.text());","        name.clear();","        terms.uncheck();","    }","    submit.setEnabled(terms.checked() && !name.text().isBlank());","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"mediator","kind":"refactor","minutes":25,"solution":[{"name":"Widgets.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Objects;\n\ninterface Dialog {\n    void changed(Object source);\n}\n\nfinal class TextBox {\n    private final Dialog dialog;\n    private String text = \"\";\n\n    TextBox(Dialog dialog) { this.dialog = Objects.requireNonNull(dialog); }\n\n    String text() { return text; }\n\n    void type(String value) {\n        text = value;\n        dialog.changed(this);\n    }\n\n    void clear() { text = \"\"; }\n}\n\nfinal class Checkbox {\n    private final Dialog dialog;\n    private boolean checked;\n\n    Checkbox(Dialog dialog) { this.dialog = Objects.requireNonNull(dialog); }\n\n    boolean checked() { return checked; }\n\n    void toggle() {\n        checked = !checked;\n        dialog.changed(this);\n    }\n\n    void uncheck() { checked = false; }\n}\n\nfinal class Button {\n    private final Dialog dialog;\n    private boolean enabled;\n\n    Button(Dialog dialog) { this.dialog = Objects.requireNonNull(dialog); }\n\n    boolean enabled() { return enabled; }\n\n    void setEnabled(boolean value) { enabled = value; }\n\n    void click() {\n        if (enabled) {\n            dialog.changed(this);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class SignupForm implements Dialog {\n    final TextBox name = new TextBox(this);\n    final Checkbox terms = new Checkbox(this);\n    final Button submit = new Button(this);\n    private final List<String> sent = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    List<String> sent() { return sent; }\n\n    @Override\n    public void changed(Object source) {\n        if (source == submit) {\n            sent.add(name.text());\n            name.clear();\n            terms.uncheck();\n        }\n        submit.setEnabled(terms.checked() && !name.text().isBlank());\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Widgets.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// Sign-up form: Submit is enabled only with a name and accepted terms.\n// Every widget knows the others, so every new rule touches all of them.\nfinal class TextBox {\n    Button submit;\n    Checkbox terms;\n    private String text = \"\";\n\n    String text() { return text; }\n\n    void type(String value) {\n        text = value;\n        submit.setEnabled(!text.isBlank() && terms.checked());\n    }\n\n    void clear() {\n        text = \"\";\n        submit.setEnabled(false);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Checkbox {\n    Button submit;\n    TextBox name;\n    private boolean checked;\n\n    boolean checked() { return checked; }\n\n    void toggle() {\n        checked = !checked;\n        submit.setEnabled(checked && !name.text().isBlank());\n    }\n\n    void uncheck() {\n        checked = false;\n        submit.setEnabled(false);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Button {\n    TextBox name;\n    Checkbox terms;\n    List<String> sent;\n    private boolean enabled;\n\n    boolean enabled() { return enabled; }\n\n    void setEnabled(boolean value) { enabled = value; }\n\n    void click() {\n        if (!enabled) {\n            return;\n        }\n        sent.add(name.text());\n        name.clear();\n        terms.uncheck();\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class SignupForm {\n    final TextBox name = new TextBox();\n    final Checkbox terms = new Checkbox();\n    final Button submit = new Button();\n    private final List<String> sent = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    SignupForm() {\n        name.submit = submit;\n        name.terms = terms;\n        terms.submit = submit;\n        terms.name = name;\n        submit.name = name;\n        submit.terms = terms;\n        submit.sent = sent;\n    }\n\n    List<String> sent() { return sent; }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Each widget holds references to the others, so every new rule edits all of them.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Introduce a **mediator**. `SignupForm` and its widgets must keep behaving exactly as they do now.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `interface Dialog { void changed(Object source); }`.","`TextBox`, `Checkbox` and `Button` each get a constructor taking a `Dialog`, keep it in one `private final` field, and report to it when the user acts (`type`, `toggle`, `click`).","Widgets keep their own state and methods, but no widget may reference another widget type.","`SignupForm` owns the rules (when Submit is enabled, what a click does) and keeps its fields and `sent()`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"MediatorKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass MediatorKataTest {\n    static final List<String> WIDGETS = List.of(\"TextBox\", \"Checkbox\", \"Button\");\n\n    @Check(id = \"starts-disabled\")\n    void startsDisabled() {\n        var form = new SignupForm();\n        Expect.isTrue(!form.submit.enabled(), \"Submit should start disabled\");\n        Expect.equal(\"\", form.name.text(), \"the name\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!form.terms.checked(), \"terms should start unchecked\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"needs-name-and-terms\")\n    void needsNameAndTerms() {\n        var form = new SignupForm();\n        form.name.type(\"ann\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!form.submit.enabled(), \"a name alone is not enough\");\n        form.terms.toggle();\n        Expect.isTrue(form.submit.enabled(), \"name and terms enable Submit\");\n        form.name.type(\"  \");\n        Expect.isTrue(!form.submit.enabled(), \"a blank name disables Submit\");\n        form.name.type(\"ann\");\n        form.terms.toggle();\n        Expect.isTrue(!form.submit.enabled(), \"unchecking terms disables Submit\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"submit-sends-and-resets\")\n    void submitSendsAndResets() {\n        var form = new SignupForm();\n        form.name.type(\"ann\");\n        form.terms.toggle();\n        form.submit.click();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ann\"), form.sent(), \"what was sent\");\n        Expect.equal(\"\", form.name.text(), \"the name after sending\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!form.terms.checked(), \"terms after sending\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!form.submit.enabled(), \"Submit after sending\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"disabled-click-ignored\")\n    void disabledClickIgnored() {\n        var form = new SignupForm();\n        form.name.type(\"ann\");\n        form.submit.click();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), form.sent(), \"a click while disabled\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"can-submit-again\")\n    void canSubmitAgain() {\n        var form = new SignupForm();\n        form.name.type(\"ann\");\n        form.terms.toggle();\n        form.submit.click();\n        form.name.type(\"bo\");\n        form.terms.toggle();\n        form.submit.click();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ann\", \"bo\"), form.sent(), \"two submissions\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"dialog-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void dialogInterface() {\n        Class<?> dialog = Types.named(\"Dialog\");\n        Expect.isTrue(dialog.isInterface(), \"Dialog should be an interface\");\n        Method m = Types.singleAbstractMethod(dialog);\n        Expect.equal(\"changed\", m.getName(), \"the method name\");\n        Expect.equal(1, m.getParameterCount(), \"changed's parameter count\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"widgets-know-only-the-dialog\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void widgetsKnowOnlyTheDialog() {\n        Class<?> dialog = Types.named(\"Dialog\");\n        for (String name : WIDGETS) {\n            Class<?> widget = Types.named(name);\n            Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(widget, dialog);\n            int mod = f.getModifiers();\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(mod) && Modifier.isFinal(mod),\n                name + \".\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n            Types.constructor(widget, dialog);\n            for (String other : WIDGETS) {\n                Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(widget, Types.named(other)).isEmpty(),\n                    name + \" still holds a \" + other);\n                if (!other.equals(name)) {\n                    Expect.none(Source.type(name).mentions(other),\n                        name + \" still mentions \" + other);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"widgets-report-to-the-dialog\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void widgetsReportToTheDialog() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> dialog = Types.named(\"Dialog\");\n        List<Object> seen = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object stub = Types.implement(dialog, args -> { seen.add(args[0]); return null; });\n\n        Object box = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"TextBox\"), dialog), stub);\n        Types.call(Types.method(box.getClass(), \"type\", String.class), box, \"ann\");\n        Expect.isTrue(seen.contains(box), \"TextBox.type should tell the dialog\");\n        Expect.equal(\"ann\", Types.call(Types.method(box.getClass(), \"text\"), box), \"the text kept by TextBox\");\n\n        Object check = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Checkbox\"), dialog), stub);\n        Types.call(Types.method(check.getClass(), \"toggle\"), check);\n        Expect.isTrue(seen.contains(check), \"Checkbox.toggle should tell the dialog\");\n        Expect.equal(true, Types.call(Types.method(check.getClass(), \"checked\"), check), \"the state kept by Checkbox\");\n\n        Object button = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Button\"), dialog), stub);\n        Types.call(Types.method(button.getClass(), \"setEnabled\", boolean.class), button, true);\n        Types.call(Types.method(button.getClass(), \"click\"), button);\n        Expect.isTrue(seen.contains(button), \"Button.click should tell the dialog\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Untangle the sign-up form widgets"},{"checks":[{"id":"restores-text-and-cursor","kind":"behaviour","title":"Restore brings back text and cursor"},{"id":"snapshot-is-a-copy","kind":"behaviour","title":"Later edits do not change a snapshot"},{"id":"snapshots-are-independent","kind":"behaviour","title":"Several snapshots coexist"},{"id":"undo-steps-back","kind":"behaviour","title":"Undo walks back through checkpoints"},{"id":"undo-with-nothing-saved","kind":"behaviour","title":"Undo with no checkpoint returns false"},{"id":"checkpoint-after-undo","kind":"behaviour","title":"Checkpoints still work after an undo"},{"id":"memento-is-its-own-type","kind":"design","title":"save() returns a dedicated memento type"},{"id":"memento-exposes-nothing","kind":"design","title":"The memento offers no way to read state"},{"id":"memento-is-immutable","kind":"design","title":"The memento's fields are final"},{"id":"history-never-reads-state","kind":"design","title":"History only stores and hands back mementos"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Only the originator understands its own state, so only it should create and open snapshots. The caretaker stores them blindly. Copy mutable state; never share the `StringBuilder`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Declare a nested `Memento` type with no readable members, backed by a private immutable record inside `Editor`. `History` keeps a `Deque` of them and calls only `save` and `restore`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The originator side:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["sealed interface Memento permits Snapshot { }","private record Snapshot(String text, int cursor) implements Memento { }","Memento save() { return new Snapshot(text.toString(), cursor); }","void restore(Memento m) {","    var s = (Snapshot) m;","    text = new StringBuilder(s.text());","    cursor = s.cursor();","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"memento","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"solution":[{"name":"Editor.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.Deque;\n\nfinal class Editor {\n    /** Opaque to everyone except Editor. */\n    sealed interface Memento permits Snapshot { }\n\n    private record Snapshot(String text, int cursor) implements Memento { }\n\n    private StringBuilder text = new StringBuilder();\n    private int cursor;\n\n    String text() { return text.toString(); }\n\n    int cursor() { return cursor; }\n\n    void type(String s) {\n        text.insert(cursor, s);\n        cursor += s.length();\n    }\n\n    void delete(int count) {\n        int n = Math.min(count, cursor);\n        text.delete(cursor - n, cursor);\n        cursor -= n;\n    }\n\n    void moveTo(int position) {\n        cursor = Math.max(0, Math.min(position, text.length()));\n    }\n\n    Memento save() {\n        return new Snapshot(text.toString(), cursor);\n    }\n\n    void restore(Memento memento) {\n        var s = (Snapshot) memento;\n        text = new StringBuilder(s.text());\n        cursor = s.cursor();\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class History {\n    private final Editor editor;\n    private final Deque<Editor.Memento> checkpoints = new ArrayDeque<>();\n\n    History(Editor editor) { this.editor = editor; }\n\n    void checkpoint() {\n        checkpoints.push(editor.save());\n    }\n\n    boolean undo() {\n        if (checkpoints.isEmpty()) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        editor.restore(checkpoints.pop());\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Editor.java","source":"// A tiny text editor. type, delete and moveTo already work.\nfinal class Editor {\n    private StringBuilder text = new StringBuilder();\n    private int cursor;\n\n    String text() { return text.toString(); }\n\n    int cursor() { return cursor; }\n\n    void type(String s) {\n        text.insert(cursor, s);\n        cursor += s.length();\n    }\n\n    /** Removes up to count characters before the cursor. */\n    void delete(int count) {\n        int n = Math.min(count, cursor);\n        text.delete(cursor - n, cursor);\n        cursor -= n;\n    }\n\n    void moveTo(int position) {\n        cursor = Math.max(0, Math.min(position, text.length()));\n    }\n\n    // TODO: return a snapshot of the editor's state.\n    Object save() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    // TODO: put the editor back into the state of that snapshot.\n    void restore(Object snapshot) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\n// The caretaker: remembers snapshots so the user can undo.\nfinal class History {\n    History(Editor editor) {\n        // TODO\n    }\n\n    /** Remembers the editor's current state. */\n    void checkpoint() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Restores the latest checkpoint; false if there is none. */\n    boolean undo() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Give the editor undo without letting anyone outside it read or forge its state.","type":"lead"},{"text":"In `Editor.java`, `type`, `delete`, `moveTo`, `text()` and `cursor()` already work.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Editor.save()` returns a **memento** of the text and cursor; `Editor.restore(m)` returns the editor to it. Replace the `Object` placeholders with a dedicated type that exposes nothing.","A snapshot is immutable and unaffected by later edits. Restoring one twice gives the same result.","`History(Editor)` is the caretaker: `checkpoint()` stores the current snapshot, `undo()` restores the latest one and returns `true`, or returns `false` when none is left.","`History` never looks inside a snapshot or reads the editor's state."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"MementoKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass MementoKataTest {\n    static Editor editorWith(String text) {\n        var e = new Editor();\n        e.type(text);\n        return e;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"restores-text-and-cursor\")\n    void restoresTextAndCursor() {\n        var e = editorWith(\"Hello\");\n        e.moveTo(2);\n        var saved = e.save();\n        e.type(\"XY\");\n        e.delete(1);\n        e.moveTo(0);\n        e.restore(saved);\n        Expect.equal(\"Hello\", e.text(), \"the text\");\n        Expect.equal(2, e.cursor(), \"the cursor\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"snapshot-is-a-copy\")\n    void snapshotIsACopy() {\n        var e = editorWith(\"ab\");\n        var saved = e.save();\n        e.type(\"cd\");\n        e.restore(saved);\n        Expect.equal(\"ab\", e.text(), \"after the first restore\");\n        e.type(\"Z\");\n        e.restore(saved);\n        Expect.equal(\"ab\", e.text(), \"restoring the same snapshot again\");\n        Expect.equal(2, e.cursor(), \"the cursor after restoring again\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"snapshots-are-independent\")\n    void snapshotsAreIndependent() {\n        var e = editorWith(\"a\");\n        var first = e.save();\n        e.type(\"b\");\n        var second = e.save();\n        e.restore(first);\n        Expect.equal(\"a\", e.text(), \"the first snapshot\");\n        e.restore(second);\n        Expect.equal(\"ab\", e.text(), \"the second snapshot\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"undo-steps-back\")\n    void undoStepsBack() {\n        var e = new Editor();\n        var history = new History(e);\n        history.checkpoint();\n        e.type(\"A\");\n        history.checkpoint();\n        e.type(\"B\");\n        Expect.isTrue(history.undo(), \"first undo\");\n        Expect.equal(\"A\", e.text(), \"after the first undo\");\n        Expect.isTrue(history.undo(), \"second undo\");\n        Expect.equal(\"\", e.text(), \"after the second undo\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"undo-with-nothing-saved\")\n    void undoWithNothingSaved() {\n        var e = editorWith(\"keep\");\n        var history = new History(e);\n        Expect.isTrue(!history.undo(), \"undo without a checkpoint\");\n        Expect.equal(\"keep\", e.text(), \"the text is left alone\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"checkpoint-after-undo\")\n    void checkpointAfterUndo() {\n        var e = new Editor();\n        var history = new History(e);\n        history.checkpoint();\n        e.type(\"a\");\n        history.undo();\n        e.type(\"b\");\n        history.checkpoint();\n        e.type(\"c\");\n        history.undo();\n        Expect.equal(\"b\", e.text(), \"undo after a new checkpoint\");\n        Expect.equal(1, e.cursor(), \"the cursor\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"memento-is-its-own-type\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void mementoIsItsOwnType() {\n        Class<?> type = Types.method(Types.named(\"Editor\"), \"save\").getReturnType();\n        Expect.isTrue(type.getClassLoader() == Editor.class.getClassLoader()\n                && type != Editor.class,\n            \"save() should return a dedicated memento type, not \" + type.getSimpleName());\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"memento-exposes-nothing\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void mementoExposesNothing() {\n        Class<?> type = Types.method(Types.named(\"Editor\"), \"save\").getReturnType();\n        for (Method m : type.getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            String n = m.getName();\n            if (m.isSynthetic() || n.equals(\"equals\") || n.equals(\"hashCode\")\n                    || n.equals(\"toString\")) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(m.getModifiers()),\n                type.getSimpleName() + \".\" + n + \" lets the caretaker read the state\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"memento-is-immutable\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void mementoIsImmutable() {\n        Object saved = editorWith(\"x\").save();\n        for (var f : saved.getClass().getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (f.isSynthetic() || Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers())) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n                saved.getClass().getSimpleName() + \".\" + f.getName() + \" should be final\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"history-never-reads-state\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void historyNeverReadsState() {\n        var history = Source.type(\"History\");\n        Expect.none(history.calls(\"text\"), \"History reads the editor's text\");\n        Expect.none(history.calls(\"cursor\"), \"History reads the editor's cursor\");\n        Expect.none(history.calls(\"type\"), \"History edits the editor\");\n        Expect.none(history.calls(\"delete\"), \"History edits the editor\");\n        Expect.none(history.calls(\"moveTo\"), \"History edits the editor\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Undo for an editor with opaque snapshots"},{"checks":[{"id":"delivers-in-order","kind":"behaviour","title":"Listeners hear a change in subscription order"},{"id":"unchanged-price-is-silent","kind":"behaviour","title":"An unchanged price notifies nobody"},{"id":"cancel-stops-delivery","kind":"behaviour","title":"A cancelled listener hears nothing more"},{"id":"cancel-during-notify","kind":"behaviour","title":"A listener can cancel itself while notified"},{"id":"subscribe-during-notify","kind":"behaviour","title":"A listener can subscribe another while notified"},{"id":"cancel-is-per-registration","kind":"behaviour","title":"A handle removes only its own registration"},{"id":"notify-outside-lock","kind":"design","title":"Listeners are not called under a lock"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Run the failing checks and read the exception. The loop in `set` walks a list that a listener is allowed to change. Decide which list the loop should walk: the live one, or a stable view of it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Iterate over a snapshot (`CopyOnWriteArrayList`, or copy before looping). Separately, `remove(listener)` removes by equality, so wrap each subscription in its own small object and remove that.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Identity-based registration:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["var registration = new Registration(listener);","registrations.add(registration);","return () -> registrations.remove(registration);"],"type":"code"},{"text":"Registration has no `equals`, so a second run removes nothing.","type":"p"}]],"itemId":"observer","kind":"fix","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Ticker.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;\n\n@FunctionalInterface\ninterface PriceListener {\n    void onChange(String symbol, int oldPrice, int newPrice);\n}\n\nfinal class Ticker {\n    /** One subscription; identity, not the listener, is what cancel removes. */\n    private static final class Registration {\n        final PriceListener listener;\n\n        Registration(PriceListener listener) { this.listener = listener; }\n    }\n\n    private final List<Registration> registrations =\n        new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();\n    private final String symbol;\n    private int price;\n\n    Ticker(String symbol, int price) {\n        this.symbol = symbol;\n        this.price = price;\n    }\n\n    Runnable subscribe(PriceListener listener) {\n        var registration = new Registration(listener);\n        registrations.add(registration);\n        return () -> registrations.remove(registration);\n    }\n\n    void set(int newPrice) {\n        if (newPrice == price) {\n            return;\n        }\n        int old = price;\n        price = newPrice;\n        for (Registration r : registrations) {\n            r.listener.onChange(symbol, old, newPrice);\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Ticker.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n@FunctionalInterface\ninterface PriceListener {\n    void onChange(String symbol, int oldPrice, int newPrice);\n}\n\n// Listeners come and go at any time, even from inside a notification.\nfinal class Ticker {\n    private final List<PriceListener> listeners = new ArrayList<>();\n    private final String symbol;\n    private int price;\n\n    Ticker(String symbol, int price) {\n        this.symbol = symbol;\n        this.price = price;\n    }\n\n    Runnable subscribe(PriceListener listener) {\n        listeners.add(listener);\n        return () -> listeners.remove(listener);\n    }\n\n    void set(int newPrice) {\n        if (newPrice == price) {\n            return;\n        }\n        int old = price;\n        price = newPrice;\n        for (PriceListener l : listeners) {\n            l.onChange(symbol, old, newPrice);\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Alerts that unsubscribe themselves, or subscribe others, crash `Ticker` mid-notification.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Fix `Ticker` so these hold. Keep `PriceListener`, `Ticker(String, int)`, `set(int)` and `Runnable subscribe(PriceListener)` as they are.","type":"p"},{"items":["A listener may subscribe or cancel from inside `onChange`. Every listener present when `set` started is still notified, once, in subscription order.","A listener subscribed during a notification first hears the next change.","Each `subscribe` call is its own registration. Running its handle removes exactly that registration, however many times it is run, even if the same listener was subscribed twice.","Do not call listeners while holding a lock."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ObserverKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ObserverKataTest {\n    static PriceListener logTo(List<String> log, String name) {\n        return (s, o, n) -> log.add(name + \" \" + o + \"->\" + n);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"delivers-in-order\")\n    void deliversInOrder() {\n        var ticker = new Ticker(\"ACME\", 100);\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        ticker.subscribe(logTo(log, \"a\"));\n        ticker.subscribe(logTo(log, \"b\"));\n        ticker.set(105);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a 100->105\", \"b 100->105\"), log, \"one change\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unchanged-price-is-silent\")\n    void unchangedPriceIsSilent() {\n        var ticker = new Ticker(\"ACME\", 100);\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        ticker.subscribe(logTo(log, \"a\"));\n        ticker.set(100);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), log, \"setting the same price\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cancel-stops-delivery\")\n    void cancelStopsDelivery() {\n        var ticker = new Ticker(\"ACME\", 100);\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        Runnable cancel = ticker.subscribe(logTo(log, \"a\"));\n        ticker.subscribe(logTo(log, \"b\"));\n        ticker.set(101);\n        cancel.run();\n        ticker.set(102);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a 100->101\", \"b 100->101\", \"b 101->102\"), log,\n            \"deliveries around a cancel\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cancel-during-notify\")\n    void cancelDuringNotify() {\n        var ticker = new Ticker(\"ACME\", 100);\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        Runnable[] cancelFirst = new Runnable[1];\n        cancelFirst[0] = ticker.subscribe((s, o, n) -> {\n            log.add(\"once \" + n);\n            cancelFirst[0].run();\n        });\n        ticker.subscribe(logTo(log, \"b\"));\n        ticker.subscribe(logTo(log, \"c\"));\n        ticker.set(101);\n        ticker.set(102);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"once 101\", \"b 100->101\", \"c 100->101\",\n                \"b 101->102\", \"c 101->102\"), log,\n            \"a listener that unsubscribes itself while being notified\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"subscribe-during-notify\")\n    void subscribeDuringNotify() {\n        var ticker = new Ticker(\"ACME\", 100);\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        boolean[] added = new boolean[1];\n        ticker.subscribe((s, o, n) -> {\n            log.add(\"first \" + n);\n            if (!added[0]) {\n                added[0] = true;\n                ticker.subscribe(logTo(log, \"late\"));\n            }\n        });\n        ticker.set(101);\n        ticker.set(102);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"first 101\", \"first 102\", \"late 101->102\"), log,\n            \"a listener subscribed during a notification hears the next change only\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cancel-is-per-registration\")\n    void cancelIsPerRegistration() {\n        var ticker = new Ticker(\"ACME\", 100);\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        PriceListener shared = logTo(log, \"x\");\n        Runnable first = ticker.subscribe(shared);\n        Runnable second = ticker.subscribe(shared);\n        first.run();\n        first.run();\n        ticker.set(101);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"x 100->101\"), log,\n            \"the other registration of the same listener after cancelling one twice\");\n        second.run();\n        ticker.set(102);\n        Expect.equal(1, log.size(), \"deliveries after cancelling both registrations\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"notify-outside-lock\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void notifyOutsideLock() {\n        var hits = Source.type(\"Ticker\").method(\"set\").calls(\"onChange\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!hits.isEmpty(), \"Ticker.set should still call onChange\");\n        Expect.none(hits.stream().filter(h -> h.insideSynchronized()).toList(),\n            \"Ticker.set calls listeners while holding a lock; a listener could deadlock it\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Stop listeners from breaking the ticker"},{"checks":[{"id":"happy-path","kind":"behaviour","title":"New, paid, shipped read as before"},{"id":"cancel-before-shipping","kind":"behaviour","title":"New and paid orders can be cancelled"},{"id":"illegal-events-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"Illegal events raise and change nothing"},{"id":"cancelled-is-final","kind":"behaviour","title":"A cancelled order accepts no events"},{"id":"state-interface","kind":"design","title":"OrderState returns the next state"},{"id":"order-holds-one-state","kind":"design","title":"Order holds one private OrderState"},{"id":"order-does-not-branch","kind":"design","title":"Order has no status switches"},{"id":"one-class-per-phase","kind":"design","title":"Each phase is its own class"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Find what varies: what each event does depends on the phase. Give the phase an object of its own, so that `Order` no longer asks which phase it is in.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Declare `OrderState` with a default for every event that rejects it, then let each phase override only the events it allows. An event returns the successor state, which `Order` stores.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"A record per phase carries its own data:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["record Paid(String receipt) implements OrderState {","    public OrderState ship(String tracking) {","        return new Shipped(tracking);","    }","    // cancel() and describe() ...","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"state","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Order.java","source":"final class Order {\n    private OrderState state = new Fresh();\n\n    void pay(String receipt) {\n        state = state.pay(receipt);\n    }\n\n    void ship(String tracking) {\n        state = state.ship(tracking);\n    }\n\n    void cancel() {\n        state = state.cancel();\n    }\n\n    String describe() {\n        return state.describe();\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"OrderState.java","source":"import java.util.Objects;\n\ninterface OrderState {\n    default OrderState pay(String receipt) {\n        throw reject(\"pay\");\n    }\n\n    default OrderState ship(String tracking) {\n        throw reject(\"ship\");\n    }\n\n    default OrderState cancel() {\n        throw reject(\"cancel\");\n    }\n\n    String describe();\n\n    private IllegalStateException reject(String event) {\n        String where = describe();\n        return new IllegalStateException(event + \" not allowed in \" + where);\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Fresh() implements OrderState {\n    public OrderState pay(String receipt) {\n        return new Paid(Objects.requireNonNull(receipt));\n    }\n\n    public OrderState cancel() {\n        return new Cancelled();\n    }\n\n    public String describe() {\n        return \"New\";\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Paid(String receipt) implements OrderState {\n    public OrderState ship(String tracking) {\n        return new Shipped(Objects.requireNonNull(tracking));\n    }\n\n    public OrderState cancel() {\n        return new Cancelled();\n    }\n\n    public String describe() {\n        return \"Paid[\" + receipt + \"]\";\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Shipped(String tracking) implements OrderState {\n    public String describe() {\n        return \"Shipped[\" + tracking + \"]\";\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Cancelled() implements OrderState {\n    public String describe() {\n        return \"Cancelled\";\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Order.java","source":"import java.util.Objects;\n\nenum Status { NEW, PAID, SHIPPED, CANCELLED }\n\n// Every new status means another case in every method of this class.\nfinal class Order {\n    private Status status = Status.NEW;\n    private String receipt;\n    private String tracking;\n\n    void pay(String receipt) {\n        switch (status) {\n            case NEW -> {\n                this.receipt = Objects.requireNonNull(receipt);\n                status = Status.PAID;\n            }\n            default -> throw reject(\"pay\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    void ship(String tracking) {\n        switch (status) {\n            case PAID -> {\n                this.tracking = Objects.requireNonNull(tracking);\n                status = Status.SHIPPED;\n            }\n            default -> throw reject(\"ship\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    void cancel() {\n        switch (status) {\n            case NEW, PAID -> status = Status.CANCELLED;\n            default -> throw reject(\"cancel\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    String describe() {\n        return switch (status) {\n            case NEW -> \"New\";\n            case PAID -> \"Paid[\" + receipt + \"]\";\n            case SHIPPED -> \"Shipped[\" + tracking + \"]\";\n            case CANCELLED -> \"Cancelled\";\n        };\n    }\n\n    private IllegalStateException reject(String event) {\n        String where = describe();\n        return new IllegalStateException(event + \" not allowed in \" + where);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Order` switches on a status enum in every method.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Refactor to the **State** pattern: each phase of an order becomes an object that decides what every event does. The public behaviour of `Order` must not change, including which events are rejected with `IllegalStateException`.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `interface OrderState` with `OrderState pay(String)`, `OrderState ship(String)`, `OrderState cancel()`, each returning the next state, and `String describe()`.","Make one class per phase: new, paid, shipped, cancelled. Receipt and tracking live only in the states that have them.","`Order` keeps a single private `OrderState` and forwards events: `state = state.pay(r)`. Keep `new Order()`. The `Status` enum goes away."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"StateKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass StateKataTest {\n    static Order paid() {\n        Order o = new Order();\n        o.pay(\"R-1\");\n        return o;\n    }\n\n    static void rejects(Runnable event, Order o, String what) {\n        String before = o.describe();\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, event::run, what);\n        Expect.equal(before, o.describe(), what + \" must leave the order as it was\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"happy-path\")\n    void happyPath() {\n        Order o = new Order();\n        Expect.equal(\"New\", o.describe(), \"a fresh order\");\n        o.pay(\"R-1\");\n        Expect.equal(\"Paid[R-1]\", o.describe(), \"after pay\");\n        o.ship(\"TRK-9\");\n        Expect.equal(\"Shipped[TRK-9]\", o.describe(), \"after ship\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cancel-before-shipping\")\n    void cancelBeforeShipping() {\n        Order fresh = new Order();\n        fresh.cancel();\n        Expect.equal(\"Cancelled\", fresh.describe(), \"cancelling a new order\");\n        Order paid = paid();\n        paid.cancel();\n        Expect.equal(\"Cancelled\", paid.describe(), \"cancelling a paid order\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"illegal-events-rejected\")\n    void illegalEventsRejected() {\n        Order fresh = new Order();\n        rejects(() -> fresh.ship(\"T\"), fresh, \"ship on a new order\");\n        Order paid = paid();\n        rejects(() -> paid.pay(\"R-2\"), paid, \"paying twice\");\n        Order shipped = paid();\n        shipped.ship(\"T\");\n        rejects(() -> shipped.cancel(), shipped, \"cancel after shipping\");\n        rejects(() -> shipped.pay(\"R\"), shipped, \"pay after shipping\");\n        rejects(() -> shipped.ship(\"T2\"), shipped, \"shipping twice\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cancelled-is-final\")\n    void cancelledIsFinal() {\n        Order o = paid();\n        o.cancel();\n        rejects(() -> o.cancel(), o, \"cancelling twice\");\n        rejects(() -> o.pay(\"R\"), o, \"pay after cancel\");\n        rejects(() -> o.ship(\"T\"), o, \"ship after cancel\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"state-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void stateInterface() {\n        Class<?> state = Types.named(\"OrderState\");\n        Expect.isTrue(state.isInterface(), \"OrderState should be an interface\");\n        for (String[] event : new String[][] {{\"pay\"}, {\"ship\"}}) {\n            Method m = Types.method(state, event[0], String.class);\n            Expect.equal(state, m.getReturnType(), \"return type of OrderState.\" + event[0]);\n        }\n        Method cancel = Types.method(state, \"cancel\");\n        Expect.equal(state, cancel.getReturnType(), \"OrderState.cancel's return type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"order-holds-one-state\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void orderHoldsOneState() {\n        Class<?> state = Types.named(\"OrderState\");\n        Class<?> order = Types.named(\"Order\");\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(order, state);\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()), \"Order.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private\");\n        for (Field other : order.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(!other.getType().isEnum(),\n                \"Order still keeps a status enum in \" + other.getName());\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(order, String.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"Order should not keep the receipt or tracking itself; they belong to the states that have them\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"order-does-not-branch\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void orderDoesNotBranch() {\n        var order = Source.type(\"Order\");\n        Expect.none(order.switches(), \"Order still switches on its status\");\n        Expect.none(order.instanceofs(), \"Order inspects the concrete state\");\n        Expect.none(order.mentions(\"Status\"), \"Order still refers to the Status enum\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"one-class-per-phase\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void oneClassPerPhase() throws Throwable {\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(Types.named(\"Order\"), Types.named(\"OrderState\"));\n        Set<Class<?>> seen = new HashSet<>();\n        Order o = new Order();\n        seen.add(f.get(o).getClass());\n        o.pay(\"R-1\");\n        seen.add(f.get(o).getClass());\n        o.ship(\"TRK-9\");\n        seen.add(f.get(o).getClass());\n        Order cancelled = new Order();\n        cancelled.cancel();\n        seen.add(f.get(cancelled).getClass());\n        Expect.equal(4, seen.size(), \"state classes for New, Paid, Shipped and Cancelled\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Give each order status its own state"},{"checks":[{"id":"known-codes","kind":"behaviour","title":"Known codes give the same totals"},{"id":"flat-floors-at-zero","kind":"behaviour","title":"A flat discount never goes below zero"},{"id":"bulk-threshold","kind":"behaviour","title":"BULK applies from 100.00"},{"id":"unknown-code","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unknown codes are rejected"},{"id":"policy-interface","kind":"design","title":"DiscountPolicy is a one-method interface"},{"id":"checkout-holds-policy","kind":"design","title":"Checkout holds a private final policy"},{"id":"checkout-does-not-branch","kind":"design","title":"Checkout has no code branches"},{"id":"any-policy-works","kind":"design","title":"Checkout accepts a policy it has never seen"},{"id":"lookup-in-discounts","kind":"design","title":"Codes are resolved in Discounts"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Find what varies: the rule that turns a subtotal into a total. `Checkout` should only know that *some* rule does that. Give that rule a name.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Give `Checkout` a `private final DiscountPolicy` set in its constructor. The string code belongs where policies are chosen, not where they are used.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Back `Discounts.forCode` with a `Map<String, DiscountPolicy>`. Then:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["static BigDecimal total(String code, List<BigDecimal> prices) {","    return new Checkout(Discounts.forCode(code)).total(prices);","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"strategy","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Checkout.java","source":"import java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.math.RoundingMode;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Objects;\n\nfinal class Checkout {\n    private final DiscountPolicy policy;\n\n    Checkout(DiscountPolicy policy) {\n        this.policy = Objects.requireNonNull(policy, \"policy\");\n    }\n\n    BigDecimal total(List<BigDecimal> prices) {\n        BigDecimal subtotal =\n            prices.stream().reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);\n        return policy.apply(subtotal).setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Pricing {\n    private Pricing() { }\n\n    static BigDecimal total(String code, List<BigDecimal> prices) {\n        return new Checkout(Discounts.forCode(code)).total(prices);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"DiscountPolicy.java","source":"import java.math.BigDecimal;\n\n@FunctionalInterface\ninterface DiscountPolicy {\n    BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal subtotal);\n}\n\nrecord PercentOff(int percent) implements DiscountPolicy {\n    PercentOff {\n        if (percent < 0 || percent > 100) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"percent\");\n        }\n    }\n    public BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal subtotal) {\n        return subtotal.multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(100 - percent, 2));\n    }\n}\n\nrecord FlatOff(BigDecimal amount) implements DiscountPolicy {\n    public BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal subtotal) {\n        return subtotal.subtract(amount).max(BigDecimal.ZERO);\n    }\n}\n\nrecord AtLeast(BigDecimal threshold, DiscountPolicy then)\n        implements DiscountPolicy {\n    public BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal subtotal) {\n        return subtotal.compareTo(threshold) >= 0\n            ? then.apply(subtotal)\n            : subtotal;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Discounts.java","source":"import java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nfinal class Discounts {\n    private static final Map<String, DiscountPolicy> BY_CODE = Map.of(\n        \"NONE\", subtotal -> subtotal,\n        \"SPRING10\", new PercentOff(10),\n        \"WELCOME\", new FlatOff(new BigDecimal(\"7.50\")),\n        \"BULK\", new AtLeast(new BigDecimal(\"100.00\"), new PercentOff(15)));\n\n    private Discounts() { }\n\n    static DiscountPolicy forCode(String code) {\n        DiscountPolicy policy = BY_CODE.get(code);\n        if (policy == null) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown code: \" + code);\n        }\n        return policy;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Checkout.java","source":"import java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.math.RoundingMode;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// Marketing adds a promotion every month, and every time this class changes.\nfinal class Checkout {\n    private final String code;\n\n    Checkout(String code) { this.code = code; }\n\n    BigDecimal total(List<BigDecimal> prices) {\n        BigDecimal subtotal =\n            prices.stream().reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);\n        BigDecimal result;\n        if (code.equals(\"NONE\")) {\n            result = subtotal;\n        } else if (code.equals(\"SPRING10\")) {\n            result = subtotal.multiply(new BigDecimal(\"0.90\"));\n        } else if (code.equals(\"WELCOME\")) {\n            result = subtotal.subtract(new BigDecimal(\"7.50\"))\n                .max(BigDecimal.ZERO);\n        } else if (code.equals(\"BULK\")) {\n            result = subtotal.compareTo(new BigDecimal(\"100.00\")) >= 0\n                ? subtotal.multiply(new BigDecimal(\"0.85\"))\n                : subtotal;\n        } else {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown code: \" + code);\n        }\n        return result.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN);\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use this entry point. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Pricing {\n    private Pricing() { }\n\n    static BigDecimal total(String code, List<BigDecimal> prices) {\n        return new Checkout(code).total(prices);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Every new promotion is another branch in `Checkout`.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Refactor so a new promotion is a new **strategy**, not an edit to `Checkout`. `Pricing.total(code, prices)` must keep returning exactly what it returns now.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `interface DiscountPolicy` with one method, `BigDecimal apply(BigDecimal subtotal)`.","`Checkout(DiscountPolicy)` sums the prices, delegates, and rounds to 2 places.","Resolve codes in `Discounts.forCode(String)`; unknown codes throw `IllegalArgumentException`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"StrategyKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass StrategyKataTest {\n    static final List<BigDecimal> CART =\n        List.of(new BigDecimal(\"19.99\"), new BigDecimal(\"30.01\"));\n\n    static String total(String code, List<BigDecimal> prices) {\n        return Pricing.total(code, prices).toPlainString();\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"known-codes\")\n    void knownCodes() {\n        Expect.equal(\"50.00\", total(\"NONE\", CART), \"NONE\");\n        Expect.equal(\"45.00\", total(\"SPRING10\", CART), \"SPRING10\");\n        Expect.equal(\"42.50\", total(\"WELCOME\", CART), \"WELCOME\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"flat-floors-at-zero\")\n    void flatFloorsAtZero() {\n        Expect.equal(\"0.00\", total(\"WELCOME\", List.of(new BigDecimal(\"5.00\"))),\n            \"WELCOME on a 5.00 cart\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bulk-threshold\")\n    void bulkThreshold() {\n        Expect.equal(\"99.99\", total(\"BULK\", List.of(new BigDecimal(\"99.99\"))), \"BULK below 100\");\n        Expect.equal(\"85.00\", total(\"BULK\", List.of(new BigDecimal(\"100.00\"))), \"BULK at 100\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-code\")\n    void unknownCode() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> Pricing.total(\"BOGUS\", CART), \"an unknown code\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"policy-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void policyInterface() {\n        Class<?> policy = Types.named(\"DiscountPolicy\");\n        Expect.isTrue(policy.isInterface(), \"DiscountPolicy should be an interface\");\n        Method apply = Types.singleAbstractMethod(policy);\n        Expect.equal(\"apply\", apply.getName(), \"the method name\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(BigDecimal.class), List.of(apply.getParameterTypes()), \"apply's parameters\");\n        Expect.equal(BigDecimal.class, apply.getReturnType(), \"apply's return type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"checkout-holds-policy\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void checkoutHoldsPolicy() {\n        Class<?> policy = Types.named(\"DiscountPolicy\");\n        Class<?> checkout = Types.named(\"Checkout\");\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(checkout, policy);\n        int m = f.getModifiers();\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(m) && Modifier.isFinal(m),\n            \"Checkout.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(checkout, String.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"Checkout should no longer keep the discount code\");\n        Types.constructor(checkout, policy);   // fails: \"Checkout needs a constructor Checkout(DiscountPolicy)\"\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"checkout-does-not-branch\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void checkoutDoesNotBranch() {\n        var checkout = Source.type(\"Checkout\");\n        Expect.none(checkout.comparedStrings(), \"Checkout still compares discount codes\");\n        Expect.none(checkout.switches(), \"Checkout still switches on the discount\");\n        Expect.none(checkout.instanceofs(), \"Checkout inspects the policy's concrete type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"any-policy-works\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void anyPolicyWorks() throws Exception {\n        Class<?> policy = Types.named(\"DiscountPolicy\");\n        Object half = Types.implement(policy, args -> ((BigDecimal) args[0]).divide(BigDecimal.TWO));\n        Constructor<?> c = Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Checkout\"), policy);\n        Object checkout = c.newInstance(half);\n        Method total = Types.method(checkout.getClass(), \"total\", List.class);\n        Expect.equal(\"25.00\", ((BigDecimal) total.invoke(checkout, CART)).toPlainString(),\n            \"Checkout with a policy it has never seen\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"lookup-in-discounts\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void lookupInDiscounts() throws Exception {\n        Class<?> policy = Types.named(\"DiscountPolicy\");\n        Method forCode = Types.staticMethod(Types.named(\"Discounts\"), \"forCode\", String.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(policy.isAssignableFrom(forCode.getReturnType()),\n            \"Discounts.forCode should return a DiscountPolicy\");\n        Expect.isTrue(policy.isInstance(forCode.invoke(null, \"SPRING10\")),\n            \"SPRING10 should resolve to a policy\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Take the promotions out of Checkout"},{"checks":[{"id":"csv-import","kind":"behaviour","title":"CSV rows import as before"},{"id":"pipe-import","kind":"behaviour","title":"Pipe rows import as before"},{"id":"comments-only-in-pipe","kind":"behaviour","title":"Only pipe files ignore # lines"},{"id":"closes-after-bad-row","kind":"behaviour","title":"A bad row still logs close"},{"id":"shared-abstract-base","kind":"design","title":"Both importers extend one abstract class"},{"id":"run-is-final","kind":"design","title":"The template run is final"},{"id":"steps-are-not-public","kind":"design","title":"The abstract steps are not public"},{"id":"subclasses-only-parse","kind":"design","title":"Subclasses hold no skeleton code"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Compare the two classes line by line. The order of the steps is identical; only splitting a row and the comment rule differ. The sequence is what should be written once.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Create an abstract class holding `saved`, `log` and a `final run`. Add an abstract `parse(String)` step and a hook `ignore(String)` with a default. Both importers extend it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The skeleton calls the steps, and the subclass fills them:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["if (line.isBlank() || ignore(line)) {","    continue;","}","User u = parse(line);","// ...","protected abstract User parse(String line);","protected boolean ignore(String line) { return false; }"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"template-method","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Importer.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord User(String name, int age) { }\n\nabstract class Importer {\n    private final List<User> saved = new ArrayList<>();\n    private final List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    final int run(List<String> lines) {\n        log.add(\"open\");\n        int count = 0;\n        try {\n            for (String line : lines) {\n                if (line.isBlank() || ignore(line)) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                User u = parse(line);\n                if (u.age() < 18) {\n                    log.add(\"skip \" + u.name());\n                    continue;\n                }\n                saved.add(u);\n                count++;\n            }\n            log.add(\"saved \" + count);\n            return count;\n        } finally {\n            log.add(\"close\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    protected abstract User parse(String line);\n\n    protected boolean ignore(String line) {\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    List<User> saved() { return saved; }\n\n    List<String> log() { return log; }\n}\n\nfinal class CsvImporter extends Importer {\n    @Override\n    protected User parse(String line) {\n        String[] f = line.split(\",\");\n        return new User(f[0].trim(), Integer.parseInt(f[1].trim()));\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class PipeImporter extends Importer {\n    @Override\n    protected boolean ignore(String line) {\n        return line.startsWith(\"#\");\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    protected User parse(String line) {\n        String[] f = line.split(\"\\\\|\");\n        return new User(f[0].trim(), Integer.parseInt(f[1].trim()));\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Importers.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord User(String name, int age) { }\n\n// Two importers repeat the same skeleton and differ only in the format.\nfinal class CsvImporter {\n    private final List<User> saved = new ArrayList<>();\n    private final List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    int run(List<String> lines) {\n        log.add(\"open\");\n        int count = 0;\n        try {\n            for (String line : lines) {\n                if (line.isBlank()) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                String[] f = line.split(\",\");\n                User u = new User(f[0].trim(), Integer.parseInt(f[1].trim()));\n                if (u.age() < 18) {\n                    log.add(\"skip \" + u.name());\n                    continue;\n                }\n                saved.add(u);\n                count++;\n            }\n            log.add(\"saved \" + count);\n            return count;\n        } finally {\n            log.add(\"close\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    List<User> saved() { return saved; }\n\n    List<String> log() { return log; }\n}\n\nfinal class PipeImporter {\n    private final List<User> saved = new ArrayList<>();\n    private final List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    int run(List<String> lines) {\n        log.add(\"open\");\n        int count = 0;\n        try {\n            for (String line : lines) {\n                if (line.isBlank() || line.startsWith(\"#\")) {\n                    continue;\n                }\n                String[] f = line.split(\"\\\\|\");\n                User u = new User(f[0].trim(), Integer.parseInt(f[1].trim()));\n                if (u.age() < 18) {\n                    log.add(\"skip \" + u.name());\n                    continue;\n                }\n                saved.add(u);\n                count++;\n            }\n            log.add(\"saved \" + count);\n            return count;\n        } finally {\n            log.add(\"close\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    List<User> saved() { return saved; }\n\n    List<String> log() { return log; }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`CsvImporter` and `PipeImporter` copy the same skeleton.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Refactor to a **template method**: one abstract class owns the fixed sequence, and each importer supplies only what differs. `run(List<String>)`, `saved()` and `log()` must behave exactly as they do now, including logging `close` when a row fails.","type":"p"},{"items":["Move the skeleton (open, skip blank lines, parse, filter minors, store, report, close) into one abstract superclass of both importers.","Its `run(List<String>)` is `final`. The steps subclasses fill in are not `public`.","`CsvImporter` and `PipeImporter` keep their no-argument constructors and contain only format knowledge: how to split a row, and that pipe files ignore `#` lines."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"TemplateMethodKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass TemplateMethodKataTest {\n    static final List<String> CSV = List.of(\n        \"ana, 31\", \"\", \"kid, 12\", \"bo,40\");\n    static final List<String> PIPE = List.of(\n        \"# staff\", \"ana | 31\", \"kid|12\", \"   \", \"bo|40\");\n    static final List<User> ADULTS = List.of(new User(\"ana\", 31), new User(\"bo\", 40));\n\n    @Check(id = \"csv-import\")\n    void csvImport() {\n        CsvImporter importer = new CsvImporter();\n        Expect.equal(2, importer.run(CSV), \"rows saved\");\n        Expect.equal(ADULTS, importer.saved(), \"saved users\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"open\", \"skip kid\", \"saved 2\", \"close\"), importer.log(), \"log\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"pipe-import\")\n    void pipeImport() {\n        PipeImporter importer = new PipeImporter();\n        Expect.equal(2, importer.run(PIPE), \"rows saved\");\n        Expect.equal(ADULTS, importer.saved(), \"saved users\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"open\", \"skip kid\", \"saved 2\", \"close\"), importer.log(), \"log\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"comments-only-in-pipe\")\n    void commentsOnlyInPipe() {\n        CsvImporter csv = new CsvImporter();\n        Expect.raises(RuntimeException.class,\n            () -> csv.run(List.of(\"# staff\")), \"a '#' line in CSV is a bad row\");\n        PipeImporter pipe = new PipeImporter();\n        Expect.equal(0, pipe.run(List.of(\"# a|b\", \"#\", \"\")), \"only comments\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"closes-after-bad-row\")\n    void closesAfterBadRow() {\n        PipeImporter importer = new PipeImporter();\n        Expect.raises(NumberFormatException.class,\n            () -> importer.run(List.of(\"ana|31\", \"bo|old\", \"cy|20\")), \"a bad age\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"open\", \"close\"), importer.log(), \"log after the failure\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new User(\"ana\", 31)), importer.saved(), \"rows before the failure\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shared-abstract-base\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void sharedAbstractBase() {\n        Class<?> csv = Types.named(\"CsvImporter\");\n        Class<?> pipe = Types.named(\"PipeImporter\");\n        Class<?> base = csv.getSuperclass();\n        Expect.isTrue(base != Object.class, \"CsvImporter needs a common superclass for the skeleton\");\n        Expect.isTrue(pipe.getSuperclass() == base, \"PipeImporter should extend the same superclass as CsvImporter\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isAbstract(base.getModifiers()), base.getSimpleName() + \" should be abstract\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"run-is-final\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void runIsFinal() {\n        Class<?> base = Types.named(\"CsvImporter\").getSuperclass();\n        Method run = Types.method(base, \"run\", List.class);\n        int m = run.getModifiers();\n        Expect.equal(base, run.getDeclaringClass(), \"the class declaring run\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(m), base.getSimpleName() + \".run is the template and should be final\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!Modifier.isPrivate(m), base.getSimpleName() + \".run should be callable by clients\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"steps-are-not-public\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void stepsAreNotPublic() {\n        Class<?> base = Types.named(\"CsvImporter\").getSuperclass();\n        int abstracts = 0;\n        for (Method m : base.getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            if (Modifier.isAbstract(m.getModifiers())) {\n                abstracts++;\n                Expect.isTrue(!Modifier.isPublic(m.getModifiers()),\n                    \"Step \" + m.getName() + \" is abstract and should not be public; only the template is\");\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(abstracts > 0, base.getSimpleName() + \" needs an abstract step for the format\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"subclasses-only-parse\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void subclassesOnlyParse() {\n        for (String name : List.of(\"CsvImporter\", \"PipeImporter\")) {\n            var shape = Source.type(name);\n            Expect.none(shape.mentions(\"log\"), name + \" still writes the log itself\");\n            Expect.none(shape.mentions(\"saved\"), name + \" still stores users itself\");\n            Expect.none(shape.calls(\"isBlank\"), name + \" still skips blank lines itself\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Share one import skeleton between two importers"},{"checks":[{"id":"eval","kind":"behaviour","title":"Eval computes the value"},{"id":"show","kind":"behaviour","title":"Show prints parenthesised text"},{"id":"depth","kind":"behaviour","title":"Depth measures the tree"},{"id":"each-node-picks-its-method","kind":"behaviour","title":"Each node calls its own visit method"},{"id":"new-operation-needs-no-change","kind":"behaviour","title":"A visitor written elsewhere works"},{"id":"operations-do-not-test-types","kind":"design","title":"Operations never test node types"},{"id":"operations-recurse-through-accept","kind":"design","title":"Operations recurse with accept"},{"id":"nodes-know-no-operations","kind":"design","title":"Nodes do not name operations"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Double dispatch: the node knows its own type, the visitor knows the operation. Each `accept` hands `this` to the visit method that matches the node. That is the only thing a node does.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Write `accept` as a single return in every record. In the operations, evaluate a child with `child.accept(this)` and combine the results; the visitor's result type `R` carries the answer.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Node side, then operation side:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["record Neg(Expr operand) implements Expr {","    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> v) {","        return v.visitNeg(this);","    }","}","// in Eval:","public Integer visitNeg(Neg n) { return -n.operand().accept(this); }"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"visitor","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["ExprVisitor.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Expr.java","source":"sealed interface Expr permits Num, Add, Mul, Neg {\n    <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor);\n}\n\nrecord Num(int value) implements Expr {\n    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor) {\n        return visitor.visitNum(this);\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Add(Expr left, Expr right) implements Expr {\n    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor) {\n        return visitor.visitAdd(this);\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Mul(Expr left, Expr right) implements Expr {\n    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor) {\n        return visitor.visitMul(this);\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Neg(Expr operand) implements Expr {\n    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor) {\n        return visitor.visitNeg(this);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Operations.java","source":"final class Eval implements ExprVisitor<Integer> {\n    public Integer visitNum(Num n) {\n        return n.value();\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitAdd(Add a) {\n        return a.left().accept(this) + a.right().accept(this);\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitMul(Mul m) {\n        return m.left().accept(this) * m.right().accept(this);\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitNeg(Neg n) {\n        return -n.operand().accept(this);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Show implements ExprVisitor<String> {\n    public String visitNum(Num n) {\n        return String.valueOf(n.value());\n    }\n\n    public String visitAdd(Add a) {\n        String l = a.left().accept(this);\n        return \"(\" + l + \" + \" + a.right().accept(this) + \")\";\n    }\n\n    public String visitMul(Mul m) {\n        String l = m.left().accept(this);\n        return \"(\" + l + \" * \" + m.right().accept(this) + \")\";\n    }\n\n    public String visitNeg(Neg n) {\n        return \"-(\" + n.operand().accept(this) + \")\";\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Depth implements ExprVisitor<Integer> {\n    public Integer visitNum(Num n) {\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitAdd(Add a) {\n        return 1 + Math.max(a.left().accept(this), a.right().accept(this));\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitMul(Mul m) {\n        return 1 + Math.max(m.left().accept(this), m.right().accept(this));\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitNeg(Neg n) {\n        return 1 + n.operand().accept(this);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"ExprVisitor.java","source":"interface ExprVisitor<R> {\n    R visitNum(Num n);\n\n    R visitAdd(Add a);\n\n    R visitMul(Mul m);\n\n    R visitNeg(Neg n);\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Expr.java","source":"sealed interface Expr permits Num, Add, Mul, Neg {\n    <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor);\n}\n\nrecord Num(int value) implements Expr {\n    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Add(Expr left, Expr right) implements Expr {\n    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Mul(Expr left, Expr right) implements Expr {\n    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\nrecord Neg(Expr operand) implements Expr {\n    public <R> R accept(ExprVisitor<R> visitor) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Operations.java","source":"// Evaluates the tree: Num is its value, Neg negates, Add and Mul combine.\nfinal class Eval implements ExprVisitor<Integer> {\n    public Integer visitNum(Num n) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitAdd(Add a) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitMul(Mul m) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitNeg(Neg n) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Prints fully parenthesised text: ((2 + 3) * 4) and -(5).\nfinal class Show implements ExprVisitor<String> {\n    public String visitNum(Num n) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public String visitAdd(Add a) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public String visitMul(Mul m) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public String visitNeg(Neg n) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Depth of the tree: a Num is 1, any other node is 1 + its deepest child.\nfinal class Depth implements ExprVisitor<Integer> {\n    public Integer visitNum(Num n) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitAdd(Add a) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitMul(Mul m) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public Integer visitNeg(Neg n) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"ExprVisitor.java","source":"interface ExprVisitor<R> {\n    R visitNum(Num n);\n\n    R visitAdd(Add a);\n\n    R visitMul(Mul m);\n\n    R visitNeg(Neg n);\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Expressions are a stable tree; the operations over it keep growing.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Finish the **Visitor** over `Expr` (`Num`, `Add`, `Mul`, `Neg`). `ExprVisitor<R>` is given and must not change.","type":"p"},{"items":["Each node's `accept(ExprVisitor<R>)` calls the visit method for its own type and returns its result.","`Eval` returns the value as `Integer`.","`Show` returns fully parenthesised text: `((2 + 3) * 4)`, `-(5)`, a lone number as `9`.","`Depth` returns 1 for a number, otherwise 1 plus its deepest child.","Operations reach children only through `accept(this)`: no `instanceof`, no `switch`, and no operation named in a node class."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"VisitorKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass VisitorKataTest {\n    // ((2 + 3) * 4) + -(5)\n    static final Expr TREE = new Add(\n        new Mul(new Add(new Num(2), new Num(3)), new Num(4)),\n        new Neg(new Num(5)));\n\n    /** Not part of the kata: a visitor written by \"someone else\". */\n    static final class Count implements ExprVisitor<Integer> {\n        public Integer visitNum(Num n) { return 1; }\n        public Integer visitAdd(Add a) { return 1 + a.left().accept(this) + a.right().accept(this); }\n        public Integer visitMul(Mul m) { return 1 + m.left().accept(this) + m.right().accept(this); }\n        public Integer visitNeg(Neg n) { return 1 + n.operand().accept(this); }\n    }\n\n    /** Records which visit method each node picks. */\n    static final class Spy implements ExprVisitor<String> {\n        public String visitNum(Num n) { return \"num\"; }\n        public String visitAdd(Add a) { return \"add\"; }\n        public String visitMul(Mul m) { return \"mul\"; }\n        public String visitNeg(Neg n) { return \"neg\"; }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"eval\")\n    void eval() {\n        Expect.equal(15, TREE.accept(new Eval()), \"value of the tree\");\n        Expect.equal(-7, new Neg(new Num(7)).accept(new Eval()), \"a negated number\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"show\")\n    void show() {\n        Expect.equal(\"(((2 + 3) * 4) + -(5))\", TREE.accept(new Show()), \"text of the tree\");\n        Expect.equal(\"9\", new Num(9).accept(new Show()), \"a lone number\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"depth\")\n    void depth() {\n        Expect.equal(4, TREE.accept(new Depth()), \"depth of the tree\");\n        Expect.equal(1, new Num(1).accept(new Depth()), \"depth of a number\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"each-node-picks-its-method\")\n    void eachNodePicksItsMethod() {\n        Spy spy = new Spy();\n        Expect.equal(\"num\", new Num(1).accept(spy), \"Num.accept\");\n        Expect.equal(\"add\", new Add(new Num(1), new Num(2)).accept(spy), \"Add.accept\");\n        Expect.equal(\"mul\", new Mul(new Num(1), new Num(2)).accept(spy), \"Mul.accept\");\n        Expect.equal(\"neg\", new Neg(new Num(1)).accept(spy), \"Neg.accept\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"new-operation-needs-no-change\")\n    void newOperationNeedsNoChange() {\n        Expect.equal(8, TREE.accept(new Count()), \"node count from a visitor the nodes never saw\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"operations-do-not-test-types\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void operationsDoNotTestTypes() {\n        for (String name : List.of(\"Eval\", \"Show\", \"Depth\")) {\n            var op = Source.type(name);\n            Expect.none(op.instanceofs(), name + \" asks nodes for their type with instanceof\");\n            Expect.none(op.switches(), name + \" switches on node types instead of dispatching\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"operations-recurse-through-accept\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void operationsRecurseThroughAccept() {\n        for (String name : List.of(\"Eval\", \"Show\", \"Depth\")) {\n            Expect.isTrue(!Source.type(name).calls(\"accept\").isEmpty(),\n                name + \" should reach child nodes through accept(this)\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"nodes-know-no-operations\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void nodesKnowNoOperations() {\n        List<String> ops = List.of(\"Eval\", \"Show\", \"Depth\");\n        List<kata.Hit> hits = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (String node : List.of(\"Num\", \"Add\", \"Mul\", \"Neg\", \"Expr\")) {\n            for (String op : ops) {\n                hits.addAll(Source.type(node).mentions(op));\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.none(hits, \"A node class mentions an operation; operations should live in visitors only\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Add three operations to an expression tree"},{"checks":[{"id":"constructor-copies-list","kind":"behaviour","title":"Changing the source list does not leak in"},{"id":"constructor-copies-date","kind":"behaviour","title":"Changing the source Date does not leak in"},{"id":"stops-getter-is-safe","kind":"behaviour","title":"stops() cannot be used to change the route"},{"id":"departure-getter-is-safe","kind":"behaviour","title":"departure() cannot be used to change the route"},{"id":"withers-derive-new-routes","kind":"behaviour","title":"Withers leave the original unchanged"},{"id":"shared-base-under-contention","kind":"behaviour","title":"Eight threads derive from one base safely"},{"id":"all-fields-final","kind":"design","title":"Route and all its fields are final"},{"id":"no-mutators","kind":"design","title":"Route has no void mutators"},{"id":"withers-never-return-this","kind":"design","title":"Withers build a new Route"}],"hints":[[{"text":"An object is immutable only if nobody holds a reference that can change it. Look for every place a mutable object crosses the boundary: going in, coming out, and the methods that edit `this`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Copy defensively on the way in (constructor) and on the way out (`Date`). Make `name` final. A wither builds a modified copy and calls the constructor; it never writes a field.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The constructor makes the copies, so the withers can reuse it:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["this.stops = List.copyOf(stops);","this.departure = new Date(departure.getTime());","// wither:","List<String> next = new ArrayList<>(stops);","next.add(stop);","return new Route(name, next, departure);"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"immutable-object","kind":"fix","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Route.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Date;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nfinal class Route {\n    private final String name;\n    private final List<String> stops;\n    private final Date departure;\n\n    Route(String name, List<String> stops, Date departure) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.stops = List.copyOf(stops);\n        this.departure = new Date(departure.getTime());\n    }\n\n    String name() {\n        return name;\n    }\n\n    List<String> stops() {\n        return stops;\n    }\n\n    Date departure() {\n        return new Date(departure.getTime());\n    }\n\n    Route withName(String newName) {\n        return new Route(newName, stops, departure);\n    }\n\n    Route withStop(String stop) {\n        List<String> next = new ArrayList<>(stops);\n        next.add(stop);\n        return new Route(name, next, departure);\n    }\n\n    static Route sample() {\n        List<String> stops = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"A\", \"B\"));\n        return new Route(\"R1\", stops, new Date(0L));\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Route.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Date;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// Meant to be an immutable value shared between threads. It is not.\nfinal class Route {\n    private String name;\n    private final List<String> stops;\n    private final Date departure;\n\n    Route(String name, List<String> stops, Date departure) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.stops = stops;\n        this.departure = departure;\n    }\n\n    String name() {\n        return name;\n    }\n\n    List<String> stops() {\n        return stops;\n    }\n\n    Date departure() {\n        return departure;\n    }\n\n    // Derive a route with another name.\n    Route withName(String newName) {\n        this.name = newName;\n        return this;\n    }\n\n    // Derive a route with one more stop at the end.\n    Route withStop(String stop) {\n        stops.add(stop);\n        return this;\n    }\n\n    static Route sample() {\n        List<String> stops = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"A\", \"B\"));\n        return new Route(\"R1\", stops, new Date(0L));\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"`Route` is shared between threads, but callers can change it in three ways.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Make `Route` an **immutable object**. Keep the constructor, the accessors, `withName`, `withStop` and `sample()` as they are; only their behaviour changes.","type":"p"},{"items":["The constructor must not keep the caller's list or `Date`.","`stops()` and `departure()` must not let a caller change the route (a copy or an unmodifiable view).","`withName` and `withStop` return a new `Route` and leave the original untouched.","Every field is `final`, and `Route` has no setter."],"type":"bullets"},{"text":"`departure` stays a `java.util.Date`.","type":"p"}],"tests":[{"name":"ImmutableObjectKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Date;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ImmutableObjectKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"constructor-copies-list\")\n    void constructorCopiesList() {\n        List<String> source = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\"A\", \"B\"));\n        Route route = new Route(\"R1\", source, new Date(0L));\n        source.add(\"X\");\n        source.set(0, \"Z\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"A\", \"B\"), route.stops(), \"stops after the caller changed its list\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"constructor-copies-date\")\n    void constructorCopiesDate() {\n        Date when = new Date(1000L);\n        Route route = new Route(\"R1\", List.of(\"A\"), when);\n        when.setTime(0L);\n        Expect.equal(1000L, route.departure().getTime(), \"departure after the caller changed its Date\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"stops-getter-is-safe\")\n    void stopsGetterIsSafe() {\n        Route route = Route.sample();\n        try {\n            route.stops().add(\"X\");\n            route.stops().clear();\n        } catch (UnsupportedOperationException expected) {\n            // an unmodifiable view is as good as a copy\n        }\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"A\", \"B\"), route.stops(), \"stops after a caller mutated what stops() returned\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"departure-getter-is-safe\")\n    void departureGetterIsSafe() {\n        Route route = Route.sample();\n        route.departure().setTime(5000L);\n        Expect.equal(0L, route.departure().getTime(), \"departure after a caller mutated what departure() returned\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"withers-derive-new-routes\")\n    void withersDeriveNewRoutes() {\n        Route base = Route.sample();\n        Route renamed = base.withName(\"R2\");\n        Route longer = base.withStop(\"C\");\n        Expect.equal(\"R2\", renamed.name(), \"derived name\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"), longer.stops(), \"derived stops\");\n        Expect.equal(\"R1\", base.name(), \"the base name\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"A\", \"B\"), base.stops(), \"the base stops\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"A\", \"B\"), renamed.stops(), \"stops carried to the renamed route\");\n        Expect.isTrue(renamed != base && longer != base, \"a derived route should be a new object\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shared-base-under-contention\", timeoutMs = 5000, repeat = 5)\n    void sharedBaseUnderContention() {\n        Route base = Route.sample();\n        AtomicInteger next = new AtomicInteger();\n        List<Route> derived = Stress.race(8, () -> base.withStop(\"S\" + next.getAndIncrement()));\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"A\", \"B\"), base.stops(), \"the shared base after 8 threads derived from it\");\n        Set<String> last = new HashSet<>();\n        for (Route r : derived) {\n            Expect.equal(3, r.stops().size(), \"stops of a derived route\");\n            last.add(r.stops().get(2));\n        }\n        Expect.equal(8, last.size(), \"distinct final stops, one per thread\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"all-fields-final\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void allFieldsFinal() {\n        Class<?> route = Types.named(\"Route\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(route.getModifiers()), \"Route should be final so nobody can subclass it\");\n        for (Field f : route.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (!f.isSynthetic() && !Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers())) {\n                Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n                    \"Route.\" + f.getName() + \" should be final: final fields are what make publication safe\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-mutators\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noMutators() {\n        for (Method m : Types.named(\"Route\").getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            if (!m.isSynthetic() && !Modifier.isStatic(m.getModifiers())) {\n                Expect.isTrue(m.getReturnType() != void.class,\n                    \"Route.\" + m.getName() + \" returns void, so it can only be a mutator\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"withers-never-return-this\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void withersNeverReturnThis() {\n        var route = Source.type(\"Route\");\n        for (String wither : List.of(\"withName\", \"withStop\")) {\n            Expect.none(route.method(wither).mentions(\"this\"),\n                \"Route.\" + wither + \" still touches or returns this instead of building a new Route\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Make Route really immutable"},{"checks":[{"id":"take-waits-for-put","kind":"behaviour","title":"take() waits for an item"},{"id":"put-waits-while-full","kind":"behaviour","title":"put() waits while the slot is full"},{"id":"fifo-handoff","kind":"behaviour","title":"50 items arrive in order"},{"id":"producers-and-consumers","kind":"behaviour","title":"Three producers and three consumers finish"},{"id":"timed-take","kind":"behaviour","title":"take(timeout) returns an item or empty"},{"id":"timed-take-wakes-on-put","kind":"behaviour","title":"A timed take wakes when an item arrives"},{"id":"interrupt-wakes-taker","kind":"behaviour","title":"Interrupting a waiter throws"},{"id":"wakeup-without-change-is-ignored","kind":"behaviour","title":"A wakeup with a false guard keeps waiting"},{"id":"timed-take-keeps-waiting","kind":"behaviour","title":"A timed take waits out the remaining time"},{"id":"no-polling","kind":"design","title":"No sleeping or spinning"},{"id":"no-single-notify","kind":"design","title":"No lone notify()"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Each operation has a guard: put needs an empty slot, take needs an item. The thread should sleep until the guard can hold, and after waking it must check again, because another thread may have got there first.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Make the methods `synchronized`, wait in a `while` loop on the guard, and call `notifyAll()` after every change of state. For the timed take, compute a deadline once and recompute the time left after every wakeup.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The classic shape:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["synchronized T take() throws InterruptedException {","    while (item == null) {","        wait();","    }","    T taken = item;","    item = null;","    notifyAll();","    return taken;","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"guarded-suspension","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"solution":[{"name":"Slot.java","source":"import java.util.Objects;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\n\nfinal class Slot<T> {\n    private T item;\n\n    synchronized void put(T newItem) throws InterruptedException {\n        Objects.requireNonNull(newItem, \"item\");\n        while (item != null) {\n            wait();\n        }\n        item = newItem;\n        notifyAll();\n    }\n\n    synchronized T take() throws InterruptedException {\n        while (item == null) {\n            wait();\n        }\n        return removeItem();\n    }\n\n    synchronized Optional<T> take(long timeoutMs) throws InterruptedException {\n        long left = TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS.toNanos(timeoutMs);\n        long deadline = System.nanoTime() + left;\n        while (item == null) {\n            left = deadline - System.nanoTime();\n            if (left <= 0) {\n                return Optional.empty();\n            }\n            TimeUnit.NANOSECONDS.timedWait(this, left);\n        }\n        return Optional.of(removeItem());\n    }\n\n    private T removeItem() {\n        T taken = item;\n        item = null;\n        notifyAll();\n        return taken;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Slot.java","source":"import java.util.Optional;\n\n// A one-item hand-off between threads.\nfinal class Slot<T> {\n    // Blocks while the slot is full, then stores the item. Null is rejected.\n    void put(T item) throws InterruptedException {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    // Blocks while the slot is empty, then removes and returns the item.\n    T take() throws InterruptedException {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    // Like take(), but gives up after timeoutMs milliseconds with empty.\n    Optional<T> take(long timeoutMs) throws InterruptedException {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"Producers and consumers share one slot; each must wait until its guard holds.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `Slot<T>`, a one-item hand-off (**guarded suspension**). Waiting must block the thread, with no polling.","type":"p"},{"items":["`void put(T item)` waits while the slot is full, then stores the item. `null` throws `NullPointerException`.","`T take()` waits while the slot is empty, then removes and returns the item.","`Optional<T> take(long timeoutMs)` does the same but returns `Optional.empty()` once `timeoutMs` has really passed.","Every wait throws `InterruptedException` when interrupted.","A wakeup is not proof that the guard holds: recheck it."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"GuardedSuspensionKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass GuardedSuspensionKataTest {\n    interface Body<V> {\n        V run() throws Exception;\n    }\n\n    /** A thread that records what its body returned or threw. */\n    static final class Call<V> extends Thread {\n        private final Body<V> body;\n        volatile V value;\n        volatile Throwable error;\n\n        Call(Body<V> body) {\n            super(null, null, \"kata-call\", 0);\n            this.body = body;\n            setDaemon(true);\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public void run() {\n            try {\n                value = body.run();\n            } catch (Throwable t) {\n                error = t;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static <V> Call<V> start(Body<V> body) {\n        Call<V> call = new Call<>(body);\n        call.start();\n        return call;\n    }\n\n    /** Waits until the thread is parked; fails if it finished instead of waiting. */\n    static void awaitBlocked(Call<?> call, String what) {\n        long end = System.nanoTime() + 2_000_000_000L;\n        while (System.nanoTime() < end) {\n            Thread.State state = call.getState();\n            if (state == Thread.State.WAITING || state == Thread.State.TIMED_WAITING\n                    || state == Thread.State.BLOCKED) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (state == Thread.State.TERMINATED) {\n                Expect.fail(what + \" should wait, but it returned or threw \" + call.error);\n            }\n            Thread.yield();\n        }\n        Expect.fail(what + \" never blocked; is it spinning?\");\n    }\n\n    static <V> V finish(Call<V> call, String what) throws Exception {\n        call.join(3000);\n        Expect.isTrue(!call.isAlive(), what + \" did not finish\");\n        if (call.error != null) {\n            Expect.fail(what + \" threw \" + call.error);\n        }\n        return call.value;\n    }\n\n    static void spuriousWakeup(Object monitor) {\n        synchronized (monitor) {\n            monitor.notifyAll();\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"take-waits-for-put\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void takeWaitsForPut() throws Exception {\n        Slot<String> slot = new Slot<>();\n        Call<String> taker = start(slot::take);\n        awaitBlocked(taker, \"take() on an empty slot\");\n        slot.put(\"m1\");\n        Expect.equal(\"m1\", finish(taker, \"take()\"), \"the item taken\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"put-waits-while-full\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void putWaitsWhileFull() throws Exception {\n        Slot<String> slot = new Slot<>();\n        slot.put(\"a\");\n        Call<String> putter = start(() -> {\n            slot.put(\"b\");\n            return \"done\";\n        });\n        awaitBlocked(putter, \"put() on a full slot\");\n        Expect.equal(\"a\", slot.take(), \"the first item, not overwritten\");\n        finish(putter, \"put()\");\n        Expect.equal(\"b\", slot.take(), \"the second item\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fifo-handoff\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void fifoHandoff() throws Exception {\n        Slot<Integer> slot = new Slot<>();\n        Call<String> producer = start(() -> {\n            for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n                slot.put(i);\n            }\n            return \"done\";\n        });\n        List<Integer> got = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n            got.add(slot.take());\n        }\n        finish(producer, \"the producer\");\n        List<Integer> expected = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n            expected.add(i);\n        }\n        Expect.equal(expected, got, \"items in the order they were put\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"producers-and-consumers\", timeoutMs = 5000, repeat = 5)\n    void producersAndConsumers() {\n        Slot<Integer> slot = new Slot<>();\n        AtomicInteger index = new AtomicInteger();\n        List<Integer> sums = Stress.race(6, () -> {\n            int k = index.getAndIncrement();\n            int sum = 0;\n            for (int j = 0; j < 20; j++) {\n                if (k < 3) {\n                    slot.put(k * 100 + j);\n                } else {\n                    sum += slot.take();\n                }\n            }\n            return sum;\n        });\n        int total = 0;\n        for (int s : sums) {\n            total += s;\n        }\n        Expect.equal(6570, total, \"sum of everything consumed\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"timed-take\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void timedTake() throws Exception {\n        Slot<String> slot = new Slot<>();\n        Optional<String> none = Expect.completesWithin(2000, () -> slot.take(30), \"take(30) on an empty slot\");\n        Expect.equal(Optional.empty(), none, \"take(30) on an empty slot\");\n        slot.put(\"m1\");\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"m1\"), slot.take(30), \"take(30) when an item is there\");\n        Expect.equal(Optional.empty(), slot.take(10), \"the slot should be empty after a take\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"timed-take-wakes-on-put\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void timedTakeWakesOnPut() throws Exception {\n        Slot<String> slot = new Slot<>();\n        Call<Optional<String>> taker = start(() -> slot.take(4000));\n        awaitBlocked(taker, \"take(4000) on an empty slot\");\n        slot.put(\"m1\");\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"m1\"), finish(taker, \"take(4000)\"), \"the item taken\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"interrupt-wakes-taker\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void interruptWakesTaker() throws Exception {\n        Slot<String> slot = new Slot<>();\n        Call<String> taker = start(slot::take);\n        awaitBlocked(taker, \"take() on an empty slot\");\n        taker.interrupt();\n        taker.join(3000);\n        Expect.isTrue(!taker.isAlive(), \"an interrupted take() should stop waiting\");\n        Expect.isTrue(taker.error instanceof InterruptedException,\n            \"an interrupted take() should throw InterruptedException but got \" + taker.error);\n        slot.put(\"m1\");\n        Expect.equal(\"m1\", slot.take(), \"the slot after an interrupted taker\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"wakeup-without-change-is-ignored\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void wakeupWithoutChangeIsIgnored() throws Exception {\n        Slot<String> slot = new Slot<>();\n        Call<String> taker = start(slot::take);\n        awaitBlocked(taker, \"take() on an empty slot\");\n        spuriousWakeup(slot);\n        taker.join(100);\n        Expect.isTrue(taker.isAlive(),\n            \"take() returned after a wakeup although the slot is empty; recheck the guard in a while loop\");\n        slot.put(\"m1\");\n        Expect.equal(\"m1\", finish(taker, \"take()\"), \"the item taken\");\n\n        slot.put(\"a\");\n        Call<String> putter = start(() -> {\n            slot.put(\"b\");\n            return \"done\";\n        });\n        awaitBlocked(putter, \"put() on a full slot\");\n        spuriousWakeup(slot);\n        putter.join(100);\n        Expect.isTrue(putter.isAlive(),\n            \"put() went ahead after a wakeup although the slot is full; recheck the guard in a while loop\");\n        Expect.equal(\"a\", slot.take(), \"the first item, not overwritten\");\n        finish(putter, \"put()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"timed-take-keeps-waiting\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void timedTakeKeepsWaiting() throws Exception {\n        Slot<String> slot = new Slot<>();\n        Call<Long> taker = start(() -> {\n            long t0 = System.nanoTime();\n            Optional<String> r = slot.take(300);\n            if (r.isPresent()) {\n                throw new IllegalStateException(\"got \" + r.get());\n            }\n            return (System.nanoTime() - t0) / 1_000_000;\n        });\n        awaitBlocked(taker, \"take(300) on an empty slot\");\n        spuriousWakeup(slot);\n        long elapsed = finish(taker, \"take(300)\");\n        Expect.isTrue(elapsed >= 250,\n            \"take(300) gave up after \" + elapsed + \" ms because of a wakeup; keep waiting for the remaining time\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-polling\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noPolling() {\n        var slot = Source.type(\"Slot\");\n        Expect.none(slot.calls(\"sleep\"), \"Slot polls with sleep; wait for a signal instead\");\n        Expect.none(slot.calls(\"yield\"), \"Slot spins with yield; wait for a signal instead\");\n        Expect.none(slot.calls(\"onSpinWait\"), \"Slot spins; wait for a signal instead\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-single-notify\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noSingleNotify() {\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"Slot\").calls(\"notify\"),\n            \"notify() can wake the wrong kind of waiter (a producer instead of a consumer); wake them all or use two Conditions\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"A hand-off slot that waits instead of spinning"},{"checks":[{"id":"sums-every-amount","kind":"behaviour","title":"Every amount is summed and process returns"},{"id":"more-consumers-than-amounts","kind":"behaviour","title":"Idle consumers still stop"},{"id":"empty-input","kind":"behaviour","title":"No amounts: consumers stop, total is 0"},{"id":"zero-and-negative-amounts-count","kind":"behaviour","title":"Zero and negative amounts are real jobs"},{"id":"no-consumer-left-running","kind":"behaviour","title":"No consumer thread outlives process"},{"id":"queue-stays-bounded","kind":"design","title":"The queue stays bounded"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A consumer blocked in `take()` cannot tell \"the producer is slow\" from \"the producer is done\". The queue is the only channel between them, so the end of the work has to travel through it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"After the last real job, put one stop marker on the queue per consumer. A consumer that takes the marker leaves its loop. Compare with `==` against a single shared `Job` instance, not by value.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"In the producer and the consumer:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["private static final Job STOP = new Job(0);","// producer, after the real jobs:","for (int c = 0; c < consumers; c++) queue.put(STOP);","// consumer:","for (Job job; (job = queue.take()) != STOP; ) {","    total.addAndGet(job.amount());","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"producer-consumer","kind":"fix","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Pipeline.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ArrayBlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\nrecord Job(int amount) { }\n\nfinal class Pipeline {\n    // Compared by identity, so no real amount can ever equal it.\n    private static final Job STOP = new Job(0);\n    private final BlockingQueue<Job> queue = new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(2);\n\n    long process(List<Integer> amounts, int consumers)\n            throws InterruptedException {\n        AtomicLong total = new AtomicLong();\n        List<Thread> threads = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int c = 0; c < consumers; c++) {\n            Thread t = new Thread(() -> consume(total));\n            t.start();\n            threads.add(t);\n        }\n        for (int amount : amounts) {\n            queue.put(new Job(amount));\n        }\n        for (int c = 0; c < consumers; c++) {\n            queue.put(STOP);\n        }\n        for (Thread t : threads) {\n            t.join();\n        }\n        return total.get();\n    }\n\n    private void consume(AtomicLong total) {\n        try {\n            for (Job job; (job = queue.take()) != STOP; ) {\n                total.addAndGet(job.amount());\n            }\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Pipeline.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ArrayBlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\n\nrecord Job(int amount) { }\n\n// One producer (the caller) feeds a bounded queue; consumer threads add\n// the amounts up. process() should return once the work is done.\nfinal class Pipeline {\n    private final BlockingQueue<Job> queue = new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(2);\n\n    long process(List<Integer> amounts, int consumers)\n            throws InterruptedException {\n        AtomicLong total = new AtomicLong();\n        List<Thread> threads = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int c = 0; c < consumers; c++) {\n            Thread t = new Thread(() -> consume(total));\n            t.start();\n            threads.add(t);\n        }\n        for (int amount : amounts) {\n            queue.put(new Job(amount));\n        }\n        for (Thread t : threads) {\n            t.join();\n        }\n        return total.get();\n    }\n\n    private void consume(AtomicLong total) {\n        try {\n            while (true) {\n                total.addAndGet(queue.take().amount());\n            }\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"`Pipeline.process` never returns: its consumers wait for work that will never come.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Fix `Pipeline` so `process(amounts, consumers)` returns the sum of all amounts once every consumer thread has finished.","type":"p"},{"items":["Keep `process(List<Integer>, int)`, the `Job` record and the bounded `BlockingQueue<Job>`.","Every consumer must exit by itself: do not interrupt them and do not poll with timeouts.","A real amount may be `0` or negative, so the end signal must not be confused with a real job."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ProducerConsumerKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ProducerConsumerKataTest {\n    static long run(List<Integer> amounts, int consumers) {\n        return Expect.completesWithin(1500,\n            () -> new Pipeline().process(amounts, consumers),\n            \"process(\" + amounts.size() + \" amounts, \" + consumers\n            + \" consumers)\");\n    }\n\n    static List<Integer> upTo(int n) {\n        List<Integer> all = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            all.add(i);\n        }\n        return all;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sums-every-amount\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void sumsEveryAmount() {\n        Expect.equal(55L, run(upTo(10), 3), \"total of 1..10\");\n        Expect.equal(20100L, run(upTo(200), 5), \"total of 1..200\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"more-consumers-than-amounts\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void moreConsumersThanAmounts() {\n        Expect.equal(5L, run(List.of(5), 4), \"total of one amount\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"empty-input\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void emptyInput() {\n        Expect.equal(0L, run(List.of(), 2), \"total of no amounts\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"zero-and-negative-amounts-count\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void zeroAndNegativeAmountsCount() {\n        Expect.equal(6L, run(List.of(0, -1, 7, 0, 0, 5, -5), 2),\n            \"total with zero and negative amounts\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-consumer-left-running\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void noConsumerLeftRunning() throws Exception {\n        Set<Thread> before = Thread.getAllStackTraces().keySet();\n        run(upTo(20), 3);\n        List<String> leaked = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (Thread t : Thread.getAllStackTraces().keySet()) {\n            if (before.contains(t) || t.isDaemon()\n                    || t.getName().startsWith(\"kata\")) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            t.join(500);\n            if (t.isAlive()) {\n                leaked.add(t.getName());\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(leaked.isEmpty(), \"Consumer threads are still \"\n            + \"running after process() returned: \" + leaked);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"queue-stays-bounded\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void queueStaysBounded() throws Exception {\n        Pipeline pipeline = new Pipeline();\n        Field found = null;\n        for (Field f : Pipeline.class.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (BlockingQueue.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType())) {\n                found = f;\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(found != null,\n            \"Pipeline should keep its BlockingQueue in a field\");\n        found.setAccessible(true);\n        BlockingQueue<?> queue = (BlockingQueue<?>) found.get(pipeline);\n        Expect.isTrue(queue.remainingCapacity() + queue.size() <= 1000,\n            \"The queue must stay bounded so the producer feels backpressure\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":20,"title":"Fix the pipeline whose consumers never end"},{"checks":[{"id":"runs-every-task","kind":"behaviour","title":"Every submitted task runs"},{"id":"never-more-workers-than-threads","kind":"behaviour","title":"At most N tasks run at once"},{"id":"threads-are-reused","kind":"behaviour","title":"Workers are reused across tasks"},{"id":"execute-waits-when-queue-is-full","kind":"behaviour","title":"A full queue makes execute wait"},{"id":"shutdown-finishes-queued-tasks","kind":"behaviour","title":"shutdown drains the queue first"},{"id":"rejects-after-shutdown","kind":"behaviour","title":"Tasks are rejected after shutdown"},{"id":"failing-task-keeps-worker-alive","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failing task does not kill a worker"},{"id":"workers-exit-on-shutdown","kind":"behaviour","title":"Workers exit when shutdown returns"},{"id":"queue-is-bounded","kind":"design","title":"Tasks wait in a bounded BlockingQueue"},{"id":"builds-its-own-workers","kind":"design","title":"The pool builds its own workers"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A pool is a producer-consumer pair inside one object: `execute` is the producer, and each worker loops taking a task and running it. The queue gives you both the waiting and the bound.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Create the workers in the constructor, each running a `take()` loop on an `ArrayBlockingQueue<Runnable>`. For shutdown, set a flag so `execute` rejects, then queue one stop marker per worker and join them. Catch `RuntimeException` around each task.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The worker loop:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["for (Runnable r; (r = queue.take()) != STOP; ) {","    try {","        r.run();","    } catch (RuntimeException e) {","        // keep the worker alive","    }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"thread-pool","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"solution":[{"name":"MiniPool.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ArrayBlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Executor;\nimport java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException;\n\nfinal class MiniPool implements Executor {\n    private static final Runnable STOP = () -> { };\n    private final BlockingQueue<Runnable> queue;\n    private final List<Thread> workers = new ArrayList<>();\n    private volatile boolean closed;\n\n    MiniPool(int threads, int capacity) {\n        queue = new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(capacity);\n        for (int i = 0; i < threads; i++) {\n            workers.add(Thread.ofPlatform().start(this::loop));\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void execute(Runnable task) {\n        if (closed) {\n            throw new RejectedExecutionException(\"pool is shut down\");\n        }\n        try {\n            queue.put(task);\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n            throw new RejectedExecutionException(e);\n        }\n    }\n\n    void shutdown() throws InterruptedException {\n        closed = true;\n        // One stop marker per worker, queued behind the pending tasks.\n        for (int i = 0; i < workers.size(); i++) {\n            queue.put(STOP);\n        }\n        for (Thread worker : workers) {\n            worker.join();\n        }\n    }\n\n    private void loop() {\n        try {\n            for (Runnable r; (r = queue.take()) != STOP; ) {\n                try {\n                    r.run();\n                } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n                    // A failing task must not kill its worker.\n                }\n            }\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"MiniPool.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.Executor;\n\n// A small fixed pool: a bounded queue of tasks and worker threads.\n// Build the bodies; the signatures are what the tests call.\nfinal class MiniPool implements Executor {\n    /** Starts {@code threads} workers that read a queue of {@code capacity}. */\n    MiniPool(int threads, int capacity) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Queues the task, waiting while the queue is full. Once shutdown has\n     * begun it throws RejectedExecutionException.\n     */\n    @Override\n    public void execute(Runnable task) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Rejects new tasks, lets every queued task finish, and returns once\n     * all workers have exited.\n     */\n    void shutdown() throws InterruptedException {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"Implement `MiniPool`: a fixed set of reusable workers fed by a bounded queue.","type":"lead"},{"items":["`MiniPool(int threads, int capacity)` starts `threads` workers at once. Tasks wait in a queue of `capacity`.","`execute(Runnable)` queues a task, waiting while the queue is full. After `shutdown()` has begun it throws `RejectedExecutionException`.","A task that throws must not kill its worker.","`shutdown()` lets every queued task finish, then returns once all workers have exited.","Build it yourself: no `Executors`, no `ThreadPoolExecutor`, and no thread per task."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ThreadPoolKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;\nimport java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicReference;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ThreadPoolKataTest {\n    /** Waits at the gate, giving up after five seconds. */\n    static void waitAt(CountDownLatch gate) {\n        try {\n            gate.await(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void await(CountDownLatch latch, String what) throws Exception {\n        if (!latch.await(2, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {\n            throw new CheckFailure(what);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static Thread background(Expect.ThrowingRunnable action,\n            AtomicReference<Throwable> error) {\n        Thread t = new Thread(null, () -> {\n            try {\n                action.run();\n            } catch (Throwable e) {\n                error.set(e);\n            }\n        }, \"kata-caller\", 0);\n        t.setDaemon(true);\n        t.start();\n        return t;\n    }\n\n    static void shutdownWithin(MiniPool pool, long ms) {\n        Expect.completesWithin(ms, () -> {\n            pool.shutdown();\n            return null;\n        }, \"shutdown()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"runs-every-task\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void runsEveryTask() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(4, 8);\n        AtomicInteger done = new AtomicInteger();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 200; i++) {\n            pool.execute(done::incrementAndGet);\n        }\n        shutdownWithin(pool, 3000);\n        Expect.equal(200, done.get(), \"tasks run after shutdown() returned\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"never-more-workers-than-threads\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void neverMoreWorkersThanThreads() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(3, 10);\n        CountDownLatch gate = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        CountDownLatch started = new CountDownLatch(3);\n        AtomicInteger running = new AtomicInteger();\n        AtomicInteger most = new AtomicInteger();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n            pool.execute(() -> {\n                most.accumulateAndGet(running.incrementAndGet(), Math::max);\n                started.countDown();\n                waitAt(gate);\n                running.decrementAndGet();\n            });\n        }\n        await(started, \"Three tasks never ran at the same time\");\n        Stress.pause(30);\n        gate.countDown();\n        shutdownWithin(pool, 3000);\n        Expect.equal(3, most.get(), \"tasks running at the same time\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"threads-are-reused\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void threadsAreReused() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(2, 4);\n        Set<Thread> used = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n            pool.execute(() -> used.add(Thread.currentThread()));\n        }\n        shutdownWithin(pool, 3000);\n        Expect.isTrue(used.size() >= 1 && used.size() <= 2,\n            \"50 tasks ran on \" + used.size() + \" threads; a pool of 2 \"\n            + \"should reuse its workers\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!used.contains(Thread.currentThread()),\n            \"tasks should not run on the caller's thread\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"execute-waits-when-queue-is-full\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void executeWaitsWhenQueueIsFull() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(1, 1);\n        CountDownLatch gate = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        CountDownLatch started = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        AtomicInteger done = new AtomicInteger();\n        pool.execute(() -> {\n            started.countDown();\n            waitAt(gate);\n            done.incrementAndGet();\n        });\n        await(started, \"The first task never started\");\n        pool.execute(done::incrementAndGet);\n        AtomicReference<Throwable> error = new AtomicReference<>();\n        Thread third = background(() -> pool.execute(done::incrementAndGet),\n            error);\n        third.join(80);\n        Expect.isTrue(third.isAlive(), \"execute() should wait while the \"\n            + \"queue is full, but it returned\");\n        gate.countDown();\n        third.join(2000);\n        Expect.isTrue(!third.isAlive(), \"execute() never returned after \"\n            + \"room appeared in the queue\");\n        Expect.isTrue(error.get() == null, \"execute() raised \" + error.get());\n        shutdownWithin(pool, 3000);\n        Expect.equal(3, done.get(), \"tasks run\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shutdown-finishes-queued-tasks\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void shutdownFinishesQueuedTasks() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(1, 10);\n        CountDownLatch gate = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        CountDownLatch started = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        AtomicInteger done = new AtomicInteger();\n        pool.execute(() -> {\n            started.countDown();\n            waitAt(gate);\n            done.incrementAndGet();\n        });\n        await(started, \"The first task never started\");\n        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n            pool.execute(done::incrementAndGet);\n        }\n        AtomicReference<Throwable> error = new AtomicReference<>();\n        Thread closer = background(pool::shutdown, error);\n        closer.join(80);\n        Expect.isTrue(closer.isAlive(), \"shutdown() returned while tasks \"\n            + \"were still queued\");\n        gate.countDown();\n        closer.join(3000);\n        Expect.isTrue(!closer.isAlive(), \"shutdown() never returned\");\n        Expect.isTrue(error.get() == null, \"shutdown() raised \" + error.get());\n        Expect.equal(6, done.get(), \"tasks run before shutdown() returned\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rejects-after-shutdown\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void rejectsAfterShutdown() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(2, 2);\n        shutdownWithin(pool, 3000);\n        Expect.raises(RejectedExecutionException.class,\n            () -> pool.execute(() -> { }), \"execute() after shutdown()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"failing-task-keeps-worker-alive\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void failingTaskKeepsWorkerAlive() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(1, 4);\n        AtomicInteger done = new AtomicInteger();\n        pool.execute(() -> {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"boom\");\n        });\n        pool.execute(done::incrementAndGet);\n        pool.execute(done::incrementAndGet);\n        shutdownWithin(pool, 3000);\n        Expect.equal(2, done.get(),\n            \"tasks run after an earlier task threw\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"workers-exit-on-shutdown\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void workersExitOnShutdown() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(3, 4);\n        Set<Thread> used = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n        CountDownLatch all = new CountDownLatch(3);\n        CountDownLatch gate = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n            pool.execute(() -> {\n                used.add(Thread.currentThread());\n                all.countDown();\n                waitAt(gate);\n            });\n        }\n        await(all, \"Three workers never ran\");\n        gate.countDown();\n        shutdownWithin(pool, 3000);\n        for (Thread worker : used) {\n            worker.join(1000);\n            Expect.isTrue(!worker.isAlive(), \"Worker \" + worker.getName()\n                + \" is still alive after shutdown()\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"queue-is-bounded\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void queueIsBounded() throws Exception {\n        MiniPool pool = new MiniPool(1, 5);\n        Field found = null;\n        for (Field f : MiniPool.class.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (BlockingQueue.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType())) {\n                found = f;\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(found != null,\n            \"MiniPool should keep its tasks in a BlockingQueue field\");\n        found.setAccessible(true);\n        BlockingQueue<?> queue = (BlockingQueue<?>) found.get(pool);\n        Expect.equal(5, queue.remainingCapacity() + queue.size(),\n            \"capacity of the task queue\");\n        pool.shutdown();\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"builds-its-own-workers\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void buildsItsOwnWorkers() {\n        var pool = Source.type(\"MiniPool\");\n        for (String borrowed : List.of(\"Executors\", \"ThreadPoolExecutor\",\n                \"ForkJoinPool\", \"CompletableFuture\")) {\n            Expect.none(pool.mentions(borrowed), \"MiniPool borrows \"\n                + borrowed + \" instead of building the pool itself\");\n        }\n        var execute = pool.method(\"execute\");\n        Expect.none(execute.news(\"Thread\"),\n            \"execute() creates a thread per task\");\n        Expect.none(execute.calls(\"start\"),\n            \"execute() starts a thread per task\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":20,"title":"Build a tiny fixed thread pool"},{"checks":[{"id":"summary-chains-both-lookups","kind":"behaviour","title":"summary combines user and balance"},{"id":"pair-joins-two-lookups","kind":"behaviour","title":"pair joins two lookups"},{"id":"failure-reaches-the-caller","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failed lookup fails the future"},{"id":"fallback-replaces-failure","kind":"behaviour","title":"summaryOrFallback recovers from failure"},{"id":"no-blocking-calls","kind":"design","title":"No stage blocks with get or join"},{"id":"stages-are-composed","kind":"design","title":"Stages are chained, not nested"},{"id":"single-thread-pool-does-not-starve","kind":"design","title":"One I/O thread is enough"},{"id":"independent-lookups-start-together","kind":"design","title":"Independent lookups start together"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A pipeline that blocks on `get()` holds a thread idle and, on a small pool, can wait for a task that no thread is free to run. Instead of waiting for a value, say what to do when it arrives.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Use `thenCompose` when the next stage returns a future (`balance` needs the user), `thenCombine` for two independent futures, and `exceptionally` to turn a failure into a value. Each method becomes one expression.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The dependent and independent shapes:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["return userName(id).thenCompose(user ->","    balance(user).thenApply(owed -> user + \" owes \" + owed));","","return userName(a).thenCombine(userName(b), (x, y) -> x + \"+\" + y);"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"future-promise","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Billing.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Executor;\n\nfinal class Billing {\n    private final Executor io;\n\n    Billing(Executor io) {\n        this.io = io;\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<String> userName(int id) {\n        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {\n            if (id <= 0) {\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"no user \" + id);\n            }\n            return \"user-\" + id;\n        }, io);\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<Integer> balance(String user) {\n        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> user.length() * 6, io);\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<String> summary(int id) {\n        return userName(id).thenCompose(user ->\n            balance(user).thenApply(owed -> user + \" owes \" + owed));\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<String> pair(int a, int b) {\n        return userName(a).thenCombine(userName(b), (x, y) -> x + \"+\" + y);\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<String> summaryOrFallback(int id) {\n        return summary(id).exceptionally(error -> {\n            Throwable cause = error;\n            while (cause.getCause() != null) {\n                cause = cause.getCause();\n            }\n            return \"fallback: \" + cause.getMessage();\n        });\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Billing.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CompletionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Executor;\n\n// Every pipeline below parks a pool thread on get() while it waits.\nfinal class Billing {\n    private final Executor io;\n\n    Billing(Executor io) {\n        this.io = io;\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<String> userName(int id) {\n        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {\n            if (id <= 0) {\n                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"no user \" + id);\n            }\n            return \"user-\" + id;\n        }, io);\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<Integer> balance(String user) {\n        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> user.length() * 6, io);\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<String> summary(int id) {\n        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {\n            try {\n                String user = userName(id).get();\n                int owed = balance(user).get();\n                return user + \" owes \" + owed;\n            } catch (ExecutionException | InterruptedException e) {\n                throw new CompletionException(e.getCause());\n            }\n        }, io);\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<String> pair(int a, int b) {\n        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {\n            try {\n                return userName(a).get() + \"+\" + userName(b).get();\n            } catch (ExecutionException | InterruptedException e) {\n                throw new CompletionException(e.getCause());\n            }\n        }, io);\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<String> summaryOrFallback(int id) {\n        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {\n            try {\n                return summary(id).get();\n            } catch (ExecutionException | InterruptedException e) {\n                Throwable cause = e;\n                while (cause.getCause() != null) {\n                    cause = cause.getCause();\n                }\n                return \"fallback: \" + cause.getMessage();\n            }\n        }, io);\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"Each `Billing` pipeline parks a pool thread on `get()` while it waits for the next stage.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Rebuild `summary`, `pair` and `summaryOrFallback` as pure `CompletableFuture` compositions. Results and failures must stay the same.","type":"p"},{"items":["Keep `Billing(Executor io)`, `userName`, `balance` and the three method signatures, each returning a `CompletableFuture<String>`.","No `get()` or `join()` inside the three methods.","Lookups that do not depend on each other must be submitted together.","Everything must still work on an executor with one thread."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"FuturePromiseKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.Queue;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Executor;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Executors;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass FuturePromiseKataTest {\n    static final Set<String> BLOCKING = Set.of(\"get\", \"join\", \"getNow\",\n        \"resultNow\", \"await\");\n    static final Set<String> COMPOSING = Set.of(\"thenCompose\", \"thenApply\",\n        \"thenCombine\", \"handle\", \"exceptionally\", \"whenComplete\",\n        \"thenAccept\", \"thenRun\", \"thenComposeAsync\", \"thenApplyAsync\",\n        \"thenCombineAsync\", \"handleAsync\", \"exceptionallyCompose\", \"allOf\",\n        \"anyOf\", \"applyToEither\");\n\n    static ExecutorService pool(int threads) {\n        return Executors.newFixedThreadPool(threads, r -> {\n            Thread t = new Thread(r, \"kata-io\");\n            t.setDaemon(true);\n            return t;\n        });\n    }\n\n    static <T> T await(CompletableFuture<T> future, String what)\n            throws Throwable {\n        try {\n            return future.get(2, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n        } catch (java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException e) {\n            throw new CheckFailure(what + \" did not complete within 2000 ms\");\n        } catch (ExecutionException e) {\n            throw e.getCause();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static Throwable root(Throwable t) {\n        while (t.getCause() != null) {\n            t = t.getCause();\n        }\n        return t;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"summary-chains-both-lookups\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void summaryChainsBothLookups() throws Throwable {\n        Billing billing = new Billing(pool(4));\n        Expect.equal(\"user-7 owes 36\", await(billing.summary(7), \"summary(7)\"),\n            \"summary(7)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"pair-joins-two-lookups\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void pairJoinsTwoLookups() throws Throwable {\n        Billing billing = new Billing(pool(4));\n        Expect.equal(\"user-3+user-4\", await(billing.pair(3, 4), \"pair(3, 4)\"),\n            \"pair(3, 4)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"failure-reaches-the-caller\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void failureReachesTheCaller() throws Throwable {\n        Billing billing = new Billing(pool(4));\n        Throwable error = Expect.raises(Throwable.class,\n            () -> await(billing.summary(0), \"summary(0)\"), \"summary(0)\");\n        Throwable cause = root(error);\n        Expect.isTrue(cause instanceof IllegalArgumentException\n                && \"no user 0\".equals(cause.getMessage()),\n            \"summary(0) should fail with the lookup's \"\n            + \"IllegalArgumentException(\\\"no user 0\\\"), not \" + cause);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fallback-replaces-failure\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void fallbackReplacesFailure() throws Throwable {\n        Billing billing = new Billing(pool(4));\n        Expect.equal(\"fallback: no user 0\",\n            await(billing.summaryOrFallback(0), \"summaryOrFallback(0)\"),\n            \"summaryOrFallback(0)\");\n        Expect.equal(\"user-2 owes 36\",\n            await(billing.summaryOrFallback(2), \"summaryOrFallback(2)\"),\n            \"summaryOrFallback(2)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-blocking-calls\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noBlockingCalls() {\n        var billing = Source.type(\"Billing\");\n        for (String name : new String[] {\"summary\", \"pair\",\n                \"summaryOrFallback\"}) {\n            var method = billing.method(name);\n            for (String call : BLOCKING) {\n                Expect.none(method.calls(call), \"Billing.\" + name\n                    + \" blocks a thread with \" + call + \"()\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"stages-are-composed\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void stagesAreComposed() {\n        var billing = Source.type(\"Billing\");\n        for (String name : new String[] {\"summary\", \"pair\",\n                \"summaryOrFallback\"}) {\n            var method = billing.method(name);\n            boolean composed = COMPOSING.stream()\n                .anyMatch(c -> !method.calls(c).isEmpty());\n            Expect.isTrue(composed, \"Billing.\" + name + \" should be built \"\n                + \"from the futures with thenCompose, thenCombine, \"\n                + \"thenApply or exceptionally\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"single-thread-pool-does-not-starve\", kind = Kind.DESIGN,\n        timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void singleThreadPoolDoesNotStarve() throws Throwable {\n        Billing billing = new Billing(pool(1));\n        Expect.equal(\"user-7 owes 36\",\n            await(billing.summary(7), \"summary(7) on one I/O thread\"),\n            \"summary(7) on one I/O thread\");\n        Expect.equal(\"user-1+user-2\",\n            await(billing.pair(1, 2), \"pair(1, 2) on one I/O thread\"),\n            \"pair(1, 2) on one I/O thread\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"independent-lookups-start-together\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void independentLookupsStartTogether() {\n        Queue<Runnable> submitted = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        Executor manual = submitted::add;\n        Billing billing = new Billing(manual);\n        billing.pair(3, 4);\n        Expect.equal(2, submitted.size(),\n            \"lookups submitted before any of them has run\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":20,"title":"Compose the Billing futures, do not block"},{"checks":[{"id":"cached-price-is-returned","kind":"behaviour","title":"A cached price is returned without loading"},{"id":"miss-loads-and-caches","kind":"behaviour","title":"A miss is loaded once and cached"},{"id":"concurrent-misses-load-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"Eight simultaneous misses load once"},{"id":"readers-share-the-lock","kind":"behaviour","title":"Cached reads share the read lock"},{"id":"loader-failure-releases-locks","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failing loader leaves no lock held"},{"id":"loader-runs-under-the-write-lock","kind":"design","title":"The loader runs under the write lock only"},{"id":"lock-is-private-final","kind":"design","title":"The lock is a private final field"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A thread that holds the read lock asks for the write lock, which waits until all readers leave, including itself. Which lock should the thread hold at the moment it decides it must load?","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Look in the cache under the read lock and release it in a `finally` before you take the write lock. Under the write lock look again, because another thread may have loaded the sku while you waited.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"After the read section ends:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["lock.writeLock().lock();","try {","    Integer cached = prices.get(sku);","    if (cached == null) {","        cached = loader.apply(sku);","        prices.put(sku, cached);","    }","    return cached;","} finally { lock.writeLock().unlock(); }"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"read-write-lock","kind":"fix","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"PriceBook.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantReadWriteLock;\nimport java.util.function.Function;\n\nfinal class PriceBook {\n    private final ReentrantReadWriteLock lock = new ReentrantReadWriteLock();\n    private final Map<String, Integer> prices = new HashMap<>();\n    private final Function<String, Integer> loader;\n\n    PriceBook(Function<String, Integer> loader) {\n        this.loader = loader;\n    }\n\n    void put(String sku, int price) {\n        lock.writeLock().lock();\n        try {\n            prices.put(sku, price);\n        } finally {\n            lock.writeLock().unlock();\n        }\n    }\n\n    Integer price(String sku) {\n        lock.readLock().lock();\n        try {\n            Integer cached = prices.get(sku);\n            if (cached != null) {\n                return cached;\n            }\n        } finally {\n            lock.readLock().unlock();\n        }\n        // A read lock cannot be upgraded: release it, then take the\n        // write lock and look again, because another writer may have won.\n        lock.writeLock().lock();\n        try {\n            Integer cached = prices.get(sku);\n            if (cached == null) {\n                cached = loader.apply(sku);\n                prices.put(sku, cached);\n            }\n            return cached;\n        } finally {\n            lock.writeLock().unlock();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"PriceBook.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantReadWriteLock;\nimport java.util.function.Function;\n\n// Many threads read prices; a missing price is loaded once and cached.\nfinal class PriceBook {\n    private final ReentrantReadWriteLock lock = new ReentrantReadWriteLock();\n    private final Map<String, Integer> prices = new HashMap<>();\n    private final Function<String, Integer> loader;\n\n    PriceBook(Function<String, Integer> loader) {\n        this.loader = loader;\n    }\n\n    void put(String sku, int price) {\n        lock.writeLock().lock();\n        try {\n            prices.put(sku, price);\n        } finally {\n            lock.writeLock().unlock();\n        }\n    }\n\n    Integer price(String sku) {\n        lock.readLock().lock();\n        try {\n            Integer cached = prices.get(sku);\n            if (cached != null) {\n                return cached;\n            }\n            lock.writeLock().lock();\n            try {\n                Integer loaded = loader.apply(sku);\n                prices.put(sku, loaded);\n                return loaded;\n            } finally {\n                lock.writeLock().unlock();\n            }\n        } finally {\n            lock.readLock().unlock();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"`PriceBook.price(sku)` hangs the first time it meets a sku it has not cached.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Fix `PriceBook` so a missing price is loaded exactly once and cached, even when many threads ask at the same time, while cached prices are still read in parallel.","type":"p"},{"items":["Keep `PriceBook(Function<String, Integer> loader)`, `put(sku, price)` and `price(sku)`, and keep the single `ReentrantReadWriteLock`.","The loader runs under the write lock, and its failure must reach the caller without leaving any lock held.","Cached reads must keep using the read lock only."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ReadWriteLockKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantReadWriteLock;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ReadWriteLockKataTest {\n    static ReentrantReadWriteLock lockOf(PriceBook book) throws Throwable {\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(PriceBook.class,\n            ReentrantReadWriteLock.class);\n        f.setAccessible(true);\n        return (ReentrantReadWriteLock) f.get(book);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cached-price-is-returned\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void cachedPriceIsReturned() {\n        var loads = new AtomicInteger();\n        var book = new PriceBook(sku -> loads.incrementAndGet());\n        book.put(\"apple\", 3);\n        Expect.equal(3, Expect.completesWithin(1000,\n            () -> book.price(\"apple\"), \"price(\\\"apple\\\") for a cached sku\"),\n            \"price(\\\"apple\\\")\");\n        Expect.equal(0, loads.get(), \"loader calls for a cached sku\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"miss-loads-and-caches\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void missLoadsAndCaches() {\n        var loads = new AtomicInteger();\n        var book = new PriceBook(sku -> 40 + loads.incrementAndGet());\n        Expect.equal(41, Expect.completesWithin(1000,\n            () -> book.price(\"pear\"), \"price(\\\"pear\\\") for a missing sku\"),\n            \"first price(\\\"pear\\\")\");\n        Expect.equal(41, Expect.completesWithin(1000,\n            () -> book.price(\"pear\"), \"second price(\\\"pear\\\")\"),\n            \"second price(\\\"pear\\\")\");\n        Expect.equal(1, loads.get(), \"loader calls for one sku\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"concurrent-misses-load-once\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void concurrentMissesLoadOnce() {\n        var loads = new AtomicInteger();\n        var book = new PriceBook(sku -> {\n            Stress.pause(10);\n            return 40 + loads.incrementAndGet();\n        });\n        var prices = Expect.completesWithin(2500,\n            () -> Stress.race(8, () -> book.price(\"plum\")),\n            \"8 threads asking for the same missing sku\");\n        Expect.equal(1, loads.get(), \"loader calls for 8 simultaneous misses\");\n        Expect.equal(8L, prices.stream().filter(p -> p == 41).count(),\n            \"threads that got the loaded price\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"readers-share-the-lock\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void readersShareTheLock() throws Throwable {\n        var book = new PriceBook(sku -> 0);\n        book.put(\"fig\", 9);\n        var rw = lockOf(book);\n        try (var reader = Stress.holdLock(rw.readLock())) {\n            Expect.equal(9, Expect.completesWithin(500,\n                () -> book.price(\"fig\"),\n                \"price(\\\"fig\\\") while another thread is reading\"),\n                \"price(\\\"fig\\\")\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"loader-failure-releases-locks\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void loaderFailureReleasesLocks() throws Throwable {\n        var book = new PriceBook(sku -> {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"catalog down\");\n        });\n        var rw = lockOf(book);\n        var thrown = Expect.completesWithin(1000, () -> {\n            try {\n                book.price(\"kiwi\");\n                return null;\n            } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n                return e;\n            }\n        }, \"price(\\\"kiwi\\\") with a failing loader\");\n        Expect.isTrue(thrown != null && \"catalog down\".equals(thrown.getMessage()),\n            \"the loader's IllegalStateException should reach the caller\");\n        Expect.equal(0, rw.getReadLockCount(), \"read locks still held\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!rw.isWriteLocked(), \"the write lock is still held\");\n        Expect.completesWithin(1000, () -> {\n            book.put(\"kiwi\", 5);\n            return null;\n        }, \"put after a failed load\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"loader-runs-under-the-write-lock\", kind = Kind.DESIGN,\n        timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void loaderRunsUnderTheWriteLock() throws Throwable {\n        var rwRef = new java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicReference<\n            ReentrantReadWriteLock>();\n        var seen = new AtomicInteger(-1);\n        var book = new PriceBook(sku -> {\n            var rw = rwRef.get();\n            boolean ok = rw.getReadHoldCount() == 0\n                && rw.isWriteLockedByCurrentThread();\n            seen.set(ok ? 1 : 0);\n            return 1;\n        });\n        rwRef.set(lockOf(book));\n        Expect.completesWithin(1000, () -> book.price(\"lime\"),\n            \"price(\\\"lime\\\") for a missing sku\");\n        Expect.isTrue(seen.get() != -1, \"the loader was never called\");\n        Expect.isTrue(seen.get() == 1, \"the loader should run holding the \"\n            + \"write lock and no read lock\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"lock-is-private-final\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void lockIsPrivateFinal() {\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(PriceBook.class,\n            ReentrantReadWriteLock.class);\n        int m = f.getModifiers();\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(m) && Modifier.isFinal(m),\n            \"PriceBook.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":20,"title":"Fix the PriceBook that freezes on a miss"},{"checks":[{"id":"one-instance-under-contention","kind":"behaviour","title":"Eight racing callers build one Config"},{"id":"mode-is-visible","kind":"behaviour","title":"The built Config is usable"},{"id":"fast-path-does-not-lock","kind":"behaviour","title":"A built Config is returned without the lock"},{"id":"instance-is-volatile","kind":"design","title":"The shared field is volatile"},{"id":"single-read-on-fast-path","kind":"design","title":"The fast path reads the field once"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Walk through two threads that both see `instance == null`. The first takes the lock and builds. What does the second do when it gets the lock? Then ask what makes a half-built object visible to a reader without a lock.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Check the field again inside the `synchronized` block. Declare the field `volatile` so a reader cannot see a reference before the constructor's writes. On the unlocked path, read the field into a local once and use only that local.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The shape is:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["Config local = instance;","if (local == null) {","    synchronized (Config.class) {","        local = instance;","        if (local == null) instance = local = new Config();","    }","}","return local;"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"double-checked-locking","kind":"fix","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Config.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\nfinal class Config {\n    static final AtomicInteger CREATED = new AtomicInteger();\n    // Test hook: runs at the start of the constructor. Keep it.\n    static volatile Runnable onConstruct = () -> { };\n\n    private static volatile Config instance;\n    private final Map<String, String> settings;\n\n    private Config() {\n        onConstruct.run();\n        CREATED.incrementAndGet();\n        settings = Map.of(\"mode\", \"prod\");\n    }\n\n    static Config get() {\n        Config local = instance;\n        if (local == null) {\n            synchronized (Config.class) {\n                local = instance;\n                if (local == null) {\n                    instance = local = new Config();\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return local;\n    }\n\n    String mode() {\n        return settings.get(\"mode\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Config.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\n// Everyone calls Config.get(). It must build exactly one Config, and it\n// must not make callers queue up once the Config exists.\nfinal class Config {\n    static final AtomicInteger CREATED = new AtomicInteger();\n    // Test hook: runs at the start of the constructor. Keep it.\n    static volatile Runnable onConstruct = () -> { };\n\n    private static Config instance;\n    private final Map<String, String> settings;\n\n    private Config() {\n        onConstruct.run();\n        CREATED.incrementAndGet();\n        settings = Map.of(\"mode\", \"prod\");\n    }\n\n    static Config get() {\n        if (instance == null) {\n            synchronized (Config.class) {\n                instance = new Config();\n            }\n        }\n        return instance;\n    }\n\n    String mode() {\n        return settings.get(\"mode\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"`Config.get()` is meant to be a double-checked lazy singleton. It is not.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Fix `Config.get()` so that however many threads call it at once, exactly one `Config` is built, and callers never take the class lock once it exists.","type":"p"},{"items":["Keep the `static` field `instance`, the `CREATED` counter and the `onConstruct` hook.","Keep the lazy, double-checked shape: no eager initialization, no holder class, and no `synchronized` on the method.","Fix every defect in `get()`, including the one the tests cannot observe directly."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"DoubleCheckedLockingKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass DoubleCheckedLockingKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"one-instance-under-contention\", timeoutMs = 5000, repeat = 10)\n    void oneInstanceUnderContention() {\n        Types.setStatic(Config.class, \"instance\", null);\n        Config.CREATED.set(0);\n        Config.onConstruct = () -> Stress.pause(20);\n        List<Config> all = Stress.race(8, Config::get);\n        Expect.equal(1, Config.CREATED.get(),\n            \"Config constructor calls for 8 simultaneous callers\");\n        Expect.equal(1, new HashSet<>(all).size(),\n            \"distinct Config objects handed out\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"mode-is-visible\")\n    void modeIsVisible() {\n        Types.setStatic(Config.class, \"instance\", null);\n        Config.onConstruct = () -> { };\n        Expect.equal(\"prod\", Config.get().mode(), \"Config.get().mode()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fast-path-does-not-lock\")\n    void fastPathDoesNotLock() {\n        Types.setStatic(Config.class, \"instance\", null);\n        Config.onConstruct = () -> { };\n        Config first = Config.get();\n        try (var hold = Stress.holdMonitor(Config.class)) {\n            Config again = Expect.completesWithin(300, Config::get,\n                \"Config.get() while another thread holds the class monitor\");\n            Expect.isTrue(again == first, \"get() should return the same Config\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"instance-is-volatile\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void instanceIsVolatile() {\n        var field = Types.onlyStaticFieldOfType(Config.class, Config.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isVolatile(field.getModifiers()),\n            \"Config.\" + field.getName() + \" is read without a lock, so it \"\n            + \"should be volatile\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"single-read-on-fast-path\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void singleReadOnFastPath() {\n        var field = Types.onlyStaticFieldOfType(Config.class, Config.class);\n        var reads = Source.type(\"Config\").method(\"get\")\n            .fieldReads(field.getName()).stream()\n            .filter(h -> !h.insideSynchronized()).toList();\n        Expect.atMost(1, reads,\n            \"get() reads the field more than once outside the lock; \"\n            + \"read it into a local\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":15,"title":"Fix the lazily built Config"},{"checks":[{"id":"add-returns-the-new-total","kind":"behaviour","title":"add and total resolve to the right values"},{"id":"requests-run-in-submission-order","kind":"behaviour","title":"Requests run in arrival order"},{"id":"every-call-runs-on-one-scheduler-thread","kind":"behaviour","title":"Only the scheduler thread touches the servant"},{"id":"caller-does-not-wait","kind":"behaviour","title":"Callers never wait for a busy servant"},{"id":"failure-reaches-the-future","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failing request fails only its future"},{"id":"close-finishes-accepted-work","kind":"behaviour","title":"close drains accepted work and stops"},{"id":"refuses-requests-after-close","kind":"behaviour","title":"Requests after close are refused"},{"id":"servant-is-private-final","kind":"design","title":"The servant is a private final field"},{"id":"no-locking-around-the-servant","kind":"design","title":"No lock guards the servant"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Turn each call into a message. The caller only creates a future and leaves the message in an inbox. Thread safety then comes from who reads the inbox, not from locks around the servant.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep a `LinkedBlockingQueue<Runnable>` and start one thread in the constructor that loops on `take()`. Each message runs the servant call and completes the future, or completes it exceptionally. `close()` queues a stop marker and joins.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The enqueue step:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["var result = new CompletableFuture<Integer>();","inbox.add(() -> {","    try { result.complete(request.get()); }","    catch (RuntimeException e) {","        result.completeExceptionally(e);","    }","});","return result;"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"active-object","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"readOnly":["Counter.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Counter.java","source":"import java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\n// The servant. It is not thread-safe on purpose: exactly one thread may\n// ever call it. It records every thread that does.\nclass Counter {\n    private final Set<Thread> callers = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n    private int total;\n\n    int add(int n) {\n        callers.add(Thread.currentThread());\n        if (n < 0) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"negative: \" + n);\n        }\n        return total += n;\n    }\n\n    int total() {\n        callers.add(Thread.currentThread());\n        return total;\n    }\n\n    Set<Thread> callers() {\n        return Set.copyOf(callers);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"ActiveCounter.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;\nimport java.util.concurrent.LinkedBlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\n\nfinal class ActiveCounter implements AutoCloseable {\n    private static final Runnable STOP = () -> { };\n    private final Counter servant;\n    private final BlockingQueue<Runnable> inbox = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();\n    private final Thread scheduler;\n    private volatile boolean closed;\n\n    ActiveCounter(Counter servant) {\n        this.servant = servant;\n        scheduler = Thread.ofPlatform().start(this::loop);\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<Integer> add(int n) {\n        return enqueue(() -> servant.add(n));\n    }\n\n    CompletableFuture<Integer> total() {\n        return enqueue(servant::total);\n    }\n\n    private CompletableFuture<Integer> enqueue(Supplier<Integer> request) {\n        if (closed) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"closed\");\n        }\n        var result = new CompletableFuture<Integer>();\n        inbox.add(() -> {\n            try {\n                result.complete(request.get());\n            } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n                result.completeExceptionally(e);\n            }\n        });\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    private void loop() {\n        try {\n            for (Runnable r; (r = inbox.take()) != STOP; ) {\n                r.run();\n            }\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void close() {\n        closed = true;\n        inbox.add(STOP);\n        try {\n            scheduler.join();\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Counter.java","source":"import java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\n// The servant. It is not thread-safe on purpose: exactly one thread may\n// ever call it. It records every thread that does.\nclass Counter {\n    private final Set<Thread> callers = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();\n    private int total;\n\n    int add(int n) {\n        callers.add(Thread.currentThread());\n        if (n < 0) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"negative: \" + n);\n        }\n        return total += n;\n    }\n\n    int total() {\n        callers.add(Thread.currentThread());\n        return total;\n    }\n\n    Set<Thread> callers() {\n        return Set.copyOf(callers);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"ActiveCounter.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;\n\n// Callers get a future at once; one scheduler thread runs the requests\n// against the servant, one at a time, in the order they arrived.\nfinal class ActiveCounter implements AutoCloseable {\n    /** Starts the scheduler thread. */\n    ActiveCounter(Counter servant) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Resolves to the servant's new total. */\n    CompletableFuture<Integer> add(int n) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Resolves to the servant's current total. */\n    CompletableFuture<Integer> total() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Finishes the requests already accepted, stops the scheduler and\n     * returns once it has exited. Later requests are refused.\n     */\n    @Override\n    public void close() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"`Counter` is not thread-safe. Give it an asynchronous front that never needs a lock.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `ActiveCounter(Counter servant)`. Callers get a `CompletableFuture<Integer>` immediately; a single scheduler thread runs every request against the servant. `Counter` is given: do not edit it.","type":"p"},{"items":["`add(int)` resolves to the new total, `total()` to the current one.","Requests run one at a time, in arrival order, only on the scheduler thread. Callers never block.","A request that throws fails its own future; later requests still run.","`close()` finishes accepted requests, stops the scheduler, returns after it exited, and refuses later requests."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ActiveObjectKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.locks.Lock;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ActiveObjectKataTest {\n    static int value(CompletableFuture<Integer> future, String what)\n            throws Throwable {\n        try {\n            return future.get(2, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n        } catch (TimeoutException e) {\n            throw new CheckFailure(what + \" did not complete within 2000 ms\");\n        } catch (ExecutionException e) {\n            throw e.getCause();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class GatedCounter extends Counter {\n        final CountDownLatch entered = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        final CountDownLatch gate = new CountDownLatch(1);\n\n        @Override\n        int add(int n) {\n            entered.countDown();\n            try {\n                gate.await(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n            } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n            }\n            return super.add(n);\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"add-returns-the-new-total\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void addReturnsTheNewTotal() throws Throwable {\n        try (var active = new ActiveCounter(new Counter())) {\n            Expect.equal(5, value(active.add(5), \"add(5)\"), \"add(5)\");\n            Expect.equal(12, value(active.add(7), \"add(7)\"), \"add(7)\");\n            Expect.equal(12, value(active.total(), \"total()\"), \"total()\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"requests-run-in-submission-order\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void requestsRunInSubmissionOrder() throws Throwable {\n        try (var active = new ActiveCounter(new Counter())) {\n            List<CompletableFuture<Integer>> all = new ArrayList<>();\n            for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n                all.add(active.add(1));\n            }\n            for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n                Expect.equal(i + 1, value(all.get(i), \"request \" + (i + 1)),\n                    \"result of request \" + (i + 1));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"every-call-runs-on-one-scheduler-thread\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void everyCallRunsOnOneSchedulerThread() throws Throwable {\n        Counter servant = new Counter();\n        try (var active = new ActiveCounter(servant)) {\n            List<List<CompletableFuture<Integer>>> batches = Stress.race(8,\n                () -> {\n                    List<CompletableFuture<Integer>> mine = new ArrayList<>();\n                    for (int i = 0; i < 25; i++) {\n                        mine.add(active.add(1));\n                    }\n                    return mine;\n                });\n            for (var batch : batches) {\n                for (var f : batch) {\n                    value(f, \"a concurrent add\");\n                }\n            }\n            Expect.equal(200, value(active.total(), \"total()\"),\n                \"total after 8 threads added 25 times each\");\n            var callers = servant.callers();\n            Expect.equal(1, callers.size(),\n                \"threads that touched the servant\");\n            Thread only = callers.iterator().next();\n            Expect.isTrue(only != Thread.currentThread()\n                    && !only.getName().startsWith(\"kata-race\"),\n                \"the servant ran on a caller's thread; it must run on the \"\n                + \"scheduler thread\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"caller-does-not-wait\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void callerDoesNotWait() throws Throwable {\n        GatedCounter servant = new GatedCounter();\n        try (var active = new ActiveCounter(servant)) {\n            var first = active.add(1);\n            Expect.isTrue(servant.entered.await(2, TimeUnit.SECONDS),\n                \"The scheduler never started the first request\");\n            var second = Expect.completesWithin(500, () -> active.add(2),\n                \"add(2) while the scheduler is busy\");\n            var total = Expect.completesWithin(500, active::total,\n                \"total() while the scheduler is busy\");\n            Expect.isTrue(!first.isDone() && !second.isDone(),\n                \"Requests finished although the servant is still busy\");\n            servant.gate.countDown();\n            Expect.equal(1, value(first, \"add(1)\"), \"add(1)\");\n            Expect.equal(3, value(second, \"add(2)\"), \"add(2)\");\n            Expect.equal(3, value(total, \"total()\"), \"total()\");\n        } finally {\n            servant.gate.countDown();\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"failure-reaches-the-future\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void failureReachesTheFuture() throws Throwable {\n        try (var active = new ActiveCounter(new Counter())) {\n            Expect.equal(4, value(active.add(4), \"add(4)\"), \"add(4)\");\n            Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n                () -> value(active.add(-1), \"add(-1)\"), \"add(-1)\");\n            Expect.equal(9, value(active.add(5), \"add(5)\"),\n                \"add(5) after a failed request\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"close-finishes-accepted-work\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void closeFinishesAcceptedWork() throws Throwable {\n        Counter servant = new Counter();\n        var active = new ActiveCounter(servant);\n        List<CompletableFuture<Integer>> all = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n            all.add(active.add(1));\n        }\n        Expect.completesWithin(2000, () -> {\n            active.close();\n            return null;\n        }, \"close()\");\n        for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n            Expect.isTrue(all.get(i).isDone(),\n                \"Request \" + (i + 1) + \" was dropped by close()\");\n        }\n        Expect.equal(50, value(all.get(49), \"last add\"), \"last result\");\n        Thread scheduler = servant.callers().iterator().next();\n        scheduler.join(1000);\n        Expect.isTrue(!scheduler.isAlive(),\n            \"The scheduler thread is still alive after close()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"refuses-requests-after-close\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void refusesRequestsAfterClose() throws Throwable {\n        var active = new ActiveCounter(new Counter());\n        active.close();\n        boolean refused = Expect.completesWithin(1500, () -> {\n            try {\n                active.add(1).get(1, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n                return false;\n            } catch (ExecutionException | RuntimeException e) {\n                return true;\n            }\n        }, \"add(1) after close()\");\n        Expect.isTrue(refused, \"add(1) after close() should be refused, \"\n            + \"by an exception or a failed future\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"servant-is-private-final\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void servantIsPrivateFinal() {\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(ActiveCounter.class, Counter.class);\n        int m = f.getModifiers();\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(m) && Modifier.isFinal(m),\n            \"ActiveCounter.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-locking-around-the-servant\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noLockingAroundTheServant() {\n        for (Field f : ActiveCounter.class.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(!Lock.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType())\n                    && !java.util.concurrent.Semaphore.class\n                        .isAssignableFrom(f.getType()),\n                \"ActiveCounter.\" + f.getName() + \" is a lock; the single \"\n                + \"scheduler thread should make locks unnecessary\");\n        }\n        var type = Source.type(\"ActiveCounter\");\n        Expect.none(type.mentions(\"ReentrantLock\"),\n            \"ActiveCounter takes a lock around the servant\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":20,"title":"Make Counter an active object"},{"checks":[{"id":"dispatches-by-operation","kind":"behaviour","title":"Each event reaches its handler"},{"id":"keeps-order-across-batches","kind":"behaviour","title":"Events keep their select order"},{"id":"run-ends-when-select-is-empty","kind":"behaviour","title":"run ends on an empty batch"},{"id":"later-handler-replaces-earlier","kind":"behaviour","title":"A new handler replaces the old one"},{"id":"unregistered-operation-fails-loudly","kind":"behaviour","title":"An unhandled Op is an error"},{"id":"handlers-run-on-the-calling-thread","kind":"behaviour","title":"Handlers run on the caller's thread"},{"id":"stop-ends-the-loop-after-the-batch","kind":"behaviour","title":"stop finishes the batch, then ends"},{"id":"handlers-can-register-handlers","kind":"behaviour","title":"A handler can register more handlers"},{"id":"no-branching-on-the-operation","kind":"design","title":"Dispatch is a lookup, not branches"},{"id":"registry-is-a-private-final-map","kind":"design","title":"Handlers live in a private final Map"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A reactor separates three jobs: waiting for readiness (the `Demultiplexer`), choosing a handler, and the handler's work. The loop knows nothing about what an operation means, only which handler is registered for it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep a private final `EnumMap<Op, Handler>`. `run()` loops: ask `demux.select()`, stop on an empty list or when a `stopped` flag is set, otherwise look up `handlers.get(event.op())` for each event in the batch.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The loop:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["while (!stopped && !(batch = demux.select()).isEmpty()) {","    for (Ready event : batch) {","        Handler h = handlers.get(event.op());","        if (h == null) throw new IllegalStateException(","            \"no handler for \" + event.op());","        h.handle(event);","    }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"reactor","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Events.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Events.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\nenum Op { ACCEPT, READ, CLOSE }\n\nrecord Ready(String channel, Op op, String data) { }\n\n/** Blocks until something is ready; an empty list means \"no more events\". */\ninterface Demultiplexer {\n    List<Ready> select();\n}\n\n@FunctionalInterface\ninterface Handler {\n    void handle(Ready event);\n}\n"},{"name":"Reactor.java","source":"import java.util.EnumMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nfinal class Reactor {\n    private final Demultiplexer demux;\n    private final Map<Op, Handler> handlers = new EnumMap<>(Op.class);\n    private boolean stopped;\n\n    Reactor(Demultiplexer demux) {\n        this.demux = demux;\n    }\n\n    Reactor on(Op op, Handler handler) {\n        handlers.put(op, handler);\n        return this;\n    }\n\n    void run() {\n        stopped = false;\n        List<Ready> batch;\n        while (!stopped && !(batch = demux.select()).isEmpty()) {\n            for (Ready event : batch) {\n                Handler handler = handlers.get(event.op());\n                if (handler == null) {\n                    throw new IllegalStateException(\n                        \"no handler for \" + event.op());\n                }\n                handler.handle(event);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    void stop() {\n        stopped = true;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Events.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\nenum Op { ACCEPT, READ, CLOSE }\n\nrecord Ready(String channel, Op op, String data) { }\n\n/** Blocks until something is ready; an empty list means \"no more events\". */\ninterface Demultiplexer {\n    List<Ready> select();\n}\n\n@FunctionalInterface\ninterface Handler {\n    void handle(Ready event);\n}\n"},{"name":"Reactor.java","source":"// A single-threaded event loop: wait for ready events, hand each one to\n// the handler registered for its operation.\nfinal class Reactor {\n    Reactor(Demultiplexer demux) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Registers the handler for an operation, replacing any earlier one. */\n    Reactor on(Op op, Handler handler) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * Calls select() again and again, dispatching every event of a batch in\n     * order on this thread, until select() returns an empty list or stop()\n     * was called (the current batch is finished first).\n     */\n    void run() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Ends run() after the batch being dispatched. */\n    void stop() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"Implement `Reactor`: wait for ready events, then dispatch each to the handler registered for its operation.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Events.java` is given (`Op`, `Ready`, `Demultiplexer`, `Handler`); do not edit it.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Reactor(Demultiplexer)`, and `on(Op, Handler)` returns the reactor; a later handler for the same `Op` replaces the earlier one.","`run()` calls `select()` repeatedly and dispatches each batch in order, on the calling thread, until `select()` returns an empty list.","`stop()` ends `run()` once the current batch is dispatched.","An event whose `Op` has no handler throws `IllegalStateException` naming the `Op`.","Handlers may call `on` during dispatch; later events see it. Look handlers up in a registry: no `switch` or `if` per `Op`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ReactorKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Deque;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicReference;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ReactorKataTest {\n    static Ready ev(String channel, Op op, String data) {\n        return new Ready(channel, op, data);\n    }\n\n    /** Hands out scripted batches, then empty lists, and counts calls. */\n    static class Script implements Demultiplexer {\n        final Deque<List<Ready>> batches = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        int selects;\n\n        @SafeVarargs\n        Script(List<Ready>... all) {\n            for (List<Ready> b : all) {\n                batches.add(b);\n            }\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public List<Ready> select() {\n            selects++;\n            return batches.isEmpty() ? List.of() : batches.poll();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void runWithin(Reactor reactor) {\n        Expect.completesWithin(2000, () -> {\n            reactor.run();\n            return null;\n        }, \"Reactor.run()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"dispatches-by-operation\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void dispatchesByOperation() {\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        Script script = new Script(List.of(\n            ev(\"c1\", Op.ACCEPT, \"\"), ev(\"c1\", Op.READ, \"hi\"),\n            ev(\"c1\", Op.CLOSE, \"\")));\n        Reactor reactor = new Reactor(script)\n            .on(Op.ACCEPT, e -> log.add(\"accept \" + e.channel()))\n            .on(Op.READ, e -> log.add(\"read \" + e.data()))\n            .on(Op.CLOSE, e -> log.add(\"close \" + e.channel()));\n        runWithin(reactor);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"accept c1\", \"read hi\", \"close c1\"), log,\n            \"handler calls\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"keeps-order-across-batches\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void keepsOrderAcrossBatches() {\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        Script script = new Script(\n            List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"1\"), ev(\"b\", Op.READ, \"2\")),\n            List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"3\")),\n            List.of(ev(\"b\", Op.READ, \"4\"), ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"5\")));\n        runWithin(new Reactor(script).on(Op.READ, e -> log.add(e.data())));\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"1\", \"2\", \"3\", \"4\", \"5\"), log, \"events handled\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"run-ends-when-select-is-empty\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void runEndsWhenSelectIsEmpty() {\n        Script script = new Script(List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"x\")),\n            List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"y\")));\n        runWithin(new Reactor(script).on(Op.READ, e -> { }));\n        Expect.equal(3, script.selects, \"calls to select()\");\n        Script none = new Script();\n        runWithin(new Reactor(none));\n        Expect.equal(1, none.selects, \"calls to select() with no events\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"later-handler-replaces-earlier\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void laterHandlerReplacesEarlier() {\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        Script script = new Script(List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"x\")));\n        runWithin(new Reactor(script)\n            .on(Op.READ, e -> log.add(\"old\"))\n            .on(Op.READ, e -> log.add(\"new\")));\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"new\"), log, \"handlers that ran\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unregistered-operation-fails-loudly\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void unregisteredOperationFailsLoudly() {\n        Script script = new Script(List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.CLOSE, \"\")));\n        Reactor reactor = new Reactor(script).on(Op.READ, e -> { });\n        IllegalStateException e = Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            reactor::run, \"run() with an event nobody handles\");\n        Expect.isTrue(e.getMessage() != null\n                && e.getMessage().contains(\"CLOSE\"),\n            \"The message should name the operation, but was: \"\n            + e.getMessage());\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"handlers-run-on-the-calling-thread\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void handlersRunOnTheCallingThread() {\n        AtomicReference<Thread> seen = new AtomicReference<>();\n        Script script = new Script(List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"x\")));\n        Reactor reactor = new Reactor(script)\n            .on(Op.READ, e -> seen.set(Thread.currentThread()));\n        reactor.run();\n        Expect.isTrue(seen.get() == Thread.currentThread(),\n            \"A handler ran on \" + (seen.get() == null ? \"no thread\"\n            : seen.get().getName()) + \"; a reactor dispatches on the thread \"\n            + \"that called run()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"stop-ends-the-loop-after-the-batch\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void stopEndsTheLoopAfterTheBatch() {\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        Script script = new Script(\n            List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.CLOSE, \"\"), ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"same batch\")),\n            List.of(ev(\"a\", Op.READ, \"next batch\")));\n        AtomicReference<Reactor> self = new AtomicReference<>();\n        Reactor reactor = new Reactor(script)\n            .on(Op.CLOSE, e -> self.get().stop())\n            .on(Op.READ, e -> log.add(e.data()));\n        self.set(reactor);\n        runWithin(reactor);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"same batch\"), log, \"events handled\");\n        Expect.equal(1, script.selects, \"calls to select()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"handlers-can-register-handlers\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void handlersCanRegisterHandlers() {\n        List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n        Script script = new Script(\n            List.of(ev(\"c\", Op.ACCEPT, \"\"), ev(\"c\", Op.READ, \"first\")),\n            List.of(ev(\"c\", Op.READ, \"second\")));\n        AtomicReference<Reactor> self = new AtomicReference<>();\n        Reactor reactor = new Reactor(script).on(Op.ACCEPT, e ->\n            self.get().on(Op.READ, r -> log.add(r.channel() + \":\" + r.data())));\n        self.set(reactor);\n        runWithin(reactor);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"c:first\", \"c:second\"), log, \"reads handled\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-branching-on-the-operation\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noBranchingOnTheOperation() {\n        var reactor = Source.type(\"Reactor\");\n        Expect.none(reactor.switches(), \"Reactor switches on the operation\");\n        Expect.none(reactor.instanceofs(), \"Reactor inspects event types\");\n        for (Op op : Op.values()) {\n            Expect.none(reactor.mentions(op.name()), \"Reactor names \"\n                + op + \"; it should only look handlers up by operation\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"registry-is-a-private-final-map\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void registryIsAPrivateFinalMap() {\n        Field found = null;\n        for (Field f : Reactor.class.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (Map.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType())) {\n                found = f;\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(found != null,\n            \"Reactor should keep its handlers in a Map field\");\n        int m = found.getModifiers();\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(m) && Modifier.isFinal(m),\n            \"Reactor.\" + found.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":15,"title":"Write a single-threaded Reactor"},{"checks":[{"id":"sums-edge-ranges","kind":"behaviour","title":"Empty, tiny and offset ranges sum correctly"},{"id":"sums-do-not-overflow","kind":"behaviour","title":"The sum is accumulated as a long"},{"id":"matches-a-sequential-sum","kind":"behaviour","title":"A million elements match a plain loop"},{"id":"leaves-tile-the-range","kind":"behaviour","title":"Direct sums cover the range exactly"},{"id":"small-ranges-are-not-split","kind":"behaviour","title":"Splitting stops at the threshold"},{"id":"halves-run-at-the-same-time","kind":"behaviour","title":"Two halves really run in parallel"},{"id":"splits-with-fork-and-join","kind":"design","title":"compute splits with fork and join"},{"id":"no-threads-of-its-own","kind":"design","title":"The task brings no threads of its own"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Fork/join is divide and conquer with a cutoff: below the threshold a plain loop is cheaper than scheduling, above it the range splits in two independent halves. Decide the base case first.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"In the recursive case build two `SumTask`s for `[from, mid)` and `[mid, to)`. Fork one so another worker can steal it, compute the other directly on this thread, and only then join the forked one.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The recursive case:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["int mid = (from + to) >>> 1;","var left = new SumTask(data, from, mid, threshold);","var right = new SumTask(data, mid, to, threshold);","left.fork();","long rightSum = right.compute();","return left.join() + rightSum;"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"fork-join","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"SumTask.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.RecursiveTask;\nimport java.util.function.BiConsumer;\n\n@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nfinal class SumTask extends RecursiveTask<Long> {\n    // Test hook: called with (from, to) for every range summed directly.\n    // Keep it.\n    static volatile BiConsumer<Integer, Integer> onLeaf = (from, to) -> { };\n\n    private final int[] data;\n    private final int from;\n    private final int to;\n    private final int threshold;\n\n    SumTask(int[] data, int from, int to, int threshold) {\n        this.data = data;\n        this.from = from;\n        this.to = to;\n        this.threshold = threshold;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    protected Long compute() {\n        if (to - from <= threshold) {\n            onLeaf.accept(from, to);\n            long sum = 0;\n            for (int i = from; i < to; i++) {\n                sum += data[i];\n            }\n            return sum;\n        }\n        int mid = (from + to) >>> 1;\n        var left = new SumTask(data, from, mid, threshold);\n        var right = new SumTask(data, mid, to, threshold);\n        left.fork();\n        long rightSum = right.compute();\n        return left.join() + rightSum;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"SumTask.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.RecursiveTask;\nimport java.util.function.BiConsumer;\n\n// Sums data[from, to). Large ranges are split and summed in parallel;\n// ranges of at most `threshold` elements are summed directly.\n@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nfinal class SumTask extends RecursiveTask<Long> {\n    // Test hook: called with (from, to) for every range summed directly.\n    // Keep it.\n    static volatile BiConsumer<Integer, Integer> onLeaf = (from, to) -> { };\n\n    private final int[] data;\n    private final int from;\n    private final int to;\n    private final int threshold;\n\n    SumTask(int[] data, int from, int to, int threshold) {\n        this.data = data;\n        this.from = from;\n        this.to = to;\n        this.threshold = threshold;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    protected Long compute() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"Implement `SumTask.compute()`: sum an `int[]` range by splitting it until the pieces are small.","type":"lead"},{"items":["`SumTask(int[] data, int from, int to, int threshold)` sums `data[from, to)` as a `long`; the constructor is given.","A range of at most `threshold` elements is summed directly in a loop. Call `onLeaf.accept(from, to)` just before, and keep that hook.","A larger range is cut at the middle into two `SumTask`s: fork one, compute the other yourself, then join.","Do not create threads, executors or streams: the caller supplies the `ForkJoinPool`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ForkJoinKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Collections;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ForkJoinPool;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicBoolean;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ForkJoinKataTest {\n    static long sum(int[] data, int from, int to, int threshold) {\n        ForkJoinPool pool = new ForkJoinPool(4);\n        try {\n            return Expect.completesWithin(3000,\n                () -> pool.invoke(new SumTask(data, from, to, threshold)),\n                \"SumTask over [\" + from + \", \" + to + \")\");\n        } finally {\n            pool.shutdown();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static int[] counting(int n) {\n        int[] data = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            data[i] = i % 100 - 30;\n        }\n        return data;\n    }\n\n    static long expected(int[] data, int from, int to) {\n        long s = 0;\n        for (int i = from; i < to; i++) {\n            s += data[i];\n        }\n        return s;\n    }\n\n    /** Returns the ranges summed directly, in start order. */\n    static List<int[]> leaves(int n, int threshold) {\n        List<int[]> seen = Collections.synchronizedList(new ArrayList<>());\n        SumTask.onLeaf = (f, t) -> seen.add(new int[] {f, t});\n        try {\n            sum(new int[n], 0, n, threshold);\n        } finally {\n            SumTask.onLeaf = (f, t) -> { };\n        }\n        List<int[]> sorted = new ArrayList<>(seen);\n        sorted.sort((a, b) -> Integer.compare(a[0], b[0]));\n        return sorted;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sums-edge-ranges\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void sumsEdgeRanges() {\n        int[] data = counting(50);\n        Expect.equal(0L, sum(data, 0, 0, 4), \"an empty range\");\n        Expect.equal(expected(data, 7, 8), sum(data, 7, 8, 4),\n            \"a single element\");\n        Expect.equal(expected(data, 0, 50), sum(data, 0, 50, 1000),\n            \"a range below the threshold\");\n        Expect.equal(expected(data, 5, 43), sum(data, 5, 43, 4),\n            \"a range that does not start at 0\");\n        Expect.equal(expected(data, 0, 50), sum(data, 0, 50, 1),\n            \"a threshold of 1\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sums-do-not-overflow\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void sumsDoNotOverflow() {\n        int[] big = new int[100];\n        java.util.Arrays.fill(big, Integer.MAX_VALUE);\n        Expect.equal(100L * Integer.MAX_VALUE, sum(big, 0, 100, 8),\n            \"100 elements of Integer.MAX_VALUE\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"matches-a-sequential-sum\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void matchesASequentialSum() {\n        int[] data = counting(1_000_000);\n        Expect.equal(expected(data, 0, data.length),\n            sum(data, 0, data.length, 1_000), \"one million elements\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"leaves-tile-the-range\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void leavesTileTheRange() {\n        for (int[] c : new int[][] {{1000, 100}, {1001, 7}, {64, 1}}) {\n            List<int[]> seen = leaves(c[0], c[1]);\n            int next = 0;\n            for (int[] leaf : seen) {\n                Expect.equal(next, leaf[0], \"start of the next range for \"\n                    + c[0] + \" elements, threshold \" + c[1]);\n                Expect.isTrue(leaf[1] - leaf[0] <= c[1],\n                    \"Range [\" + leaf[0] + \", \" + leaf[1] + \") is longer \"\n                    + \"than the threshold \" + c[1]);\n                next = leaf[1];\n            }\n            Expect.equal(c[0], next, \"end of the last range for \"\n                + c[0] + \" elements, threshold \" + c[1]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"small-ranges-are-not-split\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void smallRangesAreNotSplit() {\n        List<int[]> seen = leaves(100, 100);\n        Expect.equal(1, seen.size(), \"ranges for 100 elements, threshold 100\");\n        Expect.equal(0, seen.get(0)[0], \"start of the only range\");\n        Expect.equal(100, seen.get(0)[1], \"end of the only range\");\n        Expect.isTrue(leaves(1000, 100).size() <= 40,\n            \"1000 elements with threshold 100 were cut into too many tiny \"\n            + \"ranges; stop splitting as soon as a range fits the threshold\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"halves-run-at-the-same-time\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void halvesRunAtTheSameTime() {\n        CountDownLatch two = new CountDownLatch(2);\n        AtomicBoolean waited = new AtomicBoolean();\n        AtomicBoolean overlapped = new AtomicBoolean();\n        SumTask.onLeaf = (f, t) -> {\n            two.countDown();\n            if (waited.compareAndSet(false, true)) {\n                try {\n                    if (two.await(1500, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS)) {\n                        overlapped.set(true);\n                    }\n                } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n                }\n            }\n        };\n        try {\n            sum(counting(4000), 0, 4000, 100);\n        } finally {\n            SumTask.onLeaf = (f, t) -> { };\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(overlapped.get(), \"No two ranges were ever summed at \"\n            + \"the same time: fork() one half, compute() the other, then \"\n            + \"join() the first\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"splits-with-fork-and-join\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void splitsWithForkAndJoin() {\n        var compute = Source.type(\"SumTask\").method(\"compute\");\n        boolean forkJoin = !compute.calls(\"fork\").isEmpty()\n            && !compute.calls(\"join\").isEmpty();\n        boolean invokeAll = !compute.calls(\"invokeAll\").isEmpty();\n        Expect.isTrue(forkJoin || invokeAll, \"compute() should split the \"\n            + \"work with fork() and join(), or with invokeAll()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-threads-of-its-own\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noThreadsOfItsOwn() {\n        var task = Source.type(\"SumTask\");\n        Expect.none(task.news(\"Thread\"), \"SumTask creates threads itself\");\n        Expect.none(task.mentions(\"Executors\"),\n            \"SumTask runs its work on its own executor\");\n        Expect.none(task.mentions(\"parallelStream\"),\n            \"SumTask hands the work to a parallel stream\");\n        Expect.none(task.mentions(\"ForkJoinPool\"),\n            \"SumTask should leave the pool to its caller\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":20,"title":"Split a big sum with fork/join"},{"checks":[{"id":"lend-and-return","kind":"behaviour","title":"Lending and returning behave as before"},{"id":"unknown-book","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unknown books give 404"},{"id":"return-not-lent","kind":"behaviour","title":"Returning a free book gives 409"},{"id":"layers-exist","kind":"design","title":"Repository, service and controller exist"},{"id":"controller-skips-data","kind":"design","title":"The controller never touches the data layer"},{"id":"controller-uses-service","kind":"design","title":"The controller holds only the service"},{"id":"service-skips-presentation","kind":"design","title":"The service knows nothing of presentation"},{"id":"service-runs-on-any-repository","kind":"design","title":"The service works on any repository"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Three jobs share one class: talking to the user, deciding what may happen, and keeping books. Each job becomes a layer that may only call the one below it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`LoanController` holds a `private final LoanService`. `LoanService` holds a `BookRepository` and returns `Book`s or throws. `InMemoryBookRepository` owns the map. `Library.open` builds all three.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The controller keeps only the translation of outcomes:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["String lend(String isbn) {","    try { return \"200 \" + service.lend(isbn).title(); }","    catch (IllegalArgumentException e) { return \"404 \" + e.getMessage(); }","    catch (IllegalStateException e) { return \"409 \" + e.getMessage(); }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"layered-architecture","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Library.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\nrecord Book(String isbn, String title, boolean onLoan) { }\n\n// Callers start here. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Library {\n    private Library() { }\n\n    static LoanController open(List<Book> books) {\n        InMemoryBookRepository repository = new InMemoryBookRepository();\n        books.forEach(repository::save);\n        return new LoanController(new LoanService(repository));\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"BookRepository.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\n// Data layer.\ninterface BookRepository {\n    Book find(String isbn);\n\n    void save(Book book);\n}\n\nfinal class InMemoryBookRepository implements BookRepository {\n    private final Map<String, Book> rows = new HashMap<>();\n\n    public Book find(String isbn) { return rows.get(isbn); }\n\n    public void save(Book book) { rows.put(book.isbn(), book); }\n}\n"},{"name":"LoanService.java","source":"// Business layer: the lending rules, with no idea how they are shown.\nfinal class LoanService {\n    private final BookRepository books;\n\n    LoanService(BookRepository books) { this.books = books; }\n\n    Book lend(String isbn) {\n        Book book = require(isbn);\n        if (book.onLoan()) throw new IllegalStateException(\"already on loan\");\n        return store(new Book(isbn, book.title(), true));\n    }\n\n    Book giveBack(String isbn) {\n        Book book = require(isbn);\n        if (!book.onLoan()) throw new IllegalStateException(\"not on loan\");\n        return store(new Book(isbn, book.title(), false));\n    }\n\n    private Book require(String isbn) {\n        Book book = books.find(isbn);\n        if (book == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown book\");\n        return book;\n    }\n\n    private Book store(Book book) {\n        books.save(book);\n        return book;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"LoanController.java","source":"// Presentation layer: turns outcomes into status lines.\nfinal class LoanController {\n    private final LoanService service;\n\n    LoanController(LoanService service) { this.service = service; }\n\n    String lend(String isbn) {\n        try {\n            return \"200 \" + service.lend(isbn).title();\n        } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {\n            return \"404 \" + e.getMessage();\n        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n            return \"409 \" + e.getMessage();\n        }\n    }\n\n    String giveBack(String isbn) {\n        try {\n            return \"200 \" + service.giveBack(isbn).title();\n        } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {\n            return \"404 \" + e.getMessage();\n        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n            return \"409 \" + e.getMessage();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Library.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nrecord Book(String isbn, String title, boolean onLoan) { }\n\n// Presentation, business rules and storage all live in this one class.\nfinal class LoanController {\n    private final Map<String, Book> rows = new HashMap<>();\n\n    LoanController(List<Book> books) {\n        for (Book book : books) {\n            rows.put(book.isbn(), book);\n        }\n    }\n\n    String lend(String isbn) {\n        Book book = rows.get(isbn);\n        if (book == null) return \"404 unknown book\";\n        if (book.onLoan()) return \"409 already on loan\";\n        rows.put(isbn, new Book(isbn, book.title(), true));\n        return \"200 \" + book.title();\n    }\n\n    String giveBack(String isbn) {\n        Book book = rows.get(isbn);\n        if (book == null) return \"404 unknown book\";\n        if (!book.onLoan()) return \"409 not on loan\";\n        rows.put(isbn, new Book(isbn, book.title(), false));\n        return \"200 \" + book.title();\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers start here. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Library {\n    private Library() { }\n\n    static LoanController open(List<Book> books) {\n        return new LoanController(books);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`LoanController` formats replies, applies lending rules and stores books, all at once.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Split it into three layers. `Library.open(List<Book>)` and every reply line must stay exactly as they are.","type":"p"},{"items":["Data: `interface BookRepository` with `Book find(String isbn)` (null when absent) and `void save(Book)`, plus an in-memory implementation.","Business: `LoanService(BookRepository)` with `Book lend(String)` and `Book giveBack(String)`. Unknown book: `IllegalArgumentException`; wrong state: `IllegalStateException`.","Presentation: `LoanController(LoanService)` only turns outcomes into `200`, `404` and `409` lines.","Dependencies point down only. `Library.open` does the wiring."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"LayeredKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Proxy;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass LayeredKataTest {\n    static LoanController desk() {\n        return Library.open(List.of(\n            new Book(\"111\", \"Refactoring\", false),\n            new Book(\"222\", \"Domain-Driven Design\", true)));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"lend-and-return\")\n    void lendAndReturn() {\n        var desk = desk();\n        Expect.equal(\"200 Refactoring\", desk.lend(\"111\"), \"lending a free book\");\n        Expect.equal(\"409 already on loan\", desk.lend(\"111\"), \"lending it again\");\n        Expect.equal(\"200 Refactoring\", desk.giveBack(\"111\"), \"returning it\");\n        Expect.equal(\"200 Refactoring\", desk.lend(\"111\"), \"lending after return\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-book\")\n    void unknownBook() {\n        Expect.equal(\"404 unknown book\", desk().lend(\"999\"), \"lend\");\n        Expect.equal(\"404 unknown book\", desk().giveBack(\"999\"), \"giveBack\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"return-not-lent\")\n    void returnNotLent() {\n        Expect.equal(\"409 not on loan\", desk().giveBack(\"111\"), \"returning a free book\");\n        Expect.equal(\"200 Domain-Driven Design\", desk().giveBack(\"222\"), \"returning a lent book\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"layers-exist\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void layersExist() {\n        Class<?> repo = Types.named(\"BookRepository\");\n        Expect.isTrue(repo.isInterface(), \"BookRepository should be an interface\");\n        Types.method(repo, \"find\", String.class);\n        Types.method(repo, \"save\", Book.class);\n        Types.constructor(Types.named(\"LoanService\"), repo);\n        Types.constructor(Types.named(\"LoanController\"), Types.named(\"LoanService\"));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"controller-skips-data\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void controllerSkipsData() {\n        var controller = Source.type(\"LoanController\");\n        Expect.none(controller.mentions(\"BookRepository\"),\n            \"LoanController reaches into the data layer\");\n        Expect.none(controller.mentions(\"InMemoryBookRepository\"),\n            \"LoanController reaches into the data layer\");\n        Expect.none(controller.mentions(\"Map\"), \"LoanController still holds storage\");\n        Expect.none(controller.mentions(\"HashMap\"), \"LoanController still holds storage\");\n        Expect.none(controller.news(\"Book\"), \"LoanController builds domain objects itself\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"controller-uses-service\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void controllerUsesService() {\n        Class<?> service = Types.named(\"LoanService\");\n        var f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(Types.named(\"LoanController\"), service);\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()) && Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n            \"LoanController.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-skips-presentation\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void serviceSkipsPresentation() {\n        var service = Source.type(\"LoanService\");\n        Expect.none(service.mentions(\"LoanController\"),\n            \"LoanService refers to the presentation layer above it\");\n        Class<?> repo = Types.named(\"BookRepository\");\n        Types.onlyFieldOfType(Types.named(\"LoanService\"), repo);\n        Method lend = Types.method(Types.named(\"LoanService\"), \"lend\", String.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(lend.getReturnType() == Book.class,\n            \"LoanService.lend should return a Book, not a status line\");\n        Expect.none(service.news(\"InMemoryBookRepository\"),\n            \"LoanService picks its own storage instead of using the interface\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-runs-on-any-repository\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void serviceRunsOnAnyRepository() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> repo = Types.named(\"BookRepository\");\n        List<Book> saved = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object stub = Proxy.newProxyInstance(repo.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[] {repo},\n            (p, m, a) -> switch (m.getName()) {\n                case \"find\" -> new Book(\"1\", \"Kata\", false);\n                case \"save\" -> { saved.add((Book) a[0]); yield null; }\n                default -> null;\n            });\n        Object service = Types.create(Types.constructor(Types.named(\"LoanService\"), repo), stub);\n        Object lent = Types.call(Types.method(service.getClass(), \"lend\", String.class), service, \"1\");\n        Expect.equal(new Book(\"1\", \"Kata\", true), lent, \"the book LoanService returns\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new Book(\"1\", \"Kata\", true)), saved, \"what reached the repository\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Split the loan desk into layers"},{"checks":[{"id":"invalid-email","kind":"behaviour","title":"Invalid emails are refused without mail"},{"id":"duplicate-email","kind":"behaviour","title":"Duplicates are refused without a second mail"},{"id":"welcome-mail","kind":"behaviour","title":"A welcome mail goes to the new user"},{"id":"ports-exist","kind":"design","title":"UserStore and Mailer are interfaces"},{"id":"domain-takes-ports","kind":"design","title":"Registration receives its ports and a Clock"},{"id":"domain-has-no-infrastructure","kind":"design","title":"Registration holds no infrastructure"},{"id":"domain-uses-the-injected-clock","kind":"design","title":"Registration runs on a fake store, mailer and clock"},{"id":"store-decides-duplicates","kind":"design","title":"The store port decides what a duplicate is"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The rules should not know that mail goes over SMTP, that users live in a `Set`, or that time comes from the OS. Each of those is something the outside world provides.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Declare `UserStore` and `Mailer` next to `Registration` and pass them, plus a `Clock`, to its constructor. Move the `Set` into a `MemoryUserStore` and the `SmtpClient` call into an `SmtpMailer`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Inside the core, ask the injected clock, then assemble in `Wiring`:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["LocalDate trialEnd = LocalDate.now(clock).plusDays(14);","mailer.send(email, \"Welcome, trial ends \" + trialEnd);","// Wiring.create():","new Registration(new MemoryUserStore(), new SmtpMailer(),","    Clock.systemDefaultZone());"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"hexagonal","kind":"refactor","minutes":25,"solution":[{"name":"Signup.java","source":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// The \"SMTP server\": delivered mail lands in SmtpClient.OUTBOX.\nfinal class SmtpClient {\n    static final List<String> OUTBOX = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    private SmtpClient() { }\n\n    static void send(String to, String body) {\n        OUTBOX.add(to + \": \" + body);\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers start here. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Wiring {\n    private Wiring() { }\n\n    static Registration create() {\n        return new Registration(\n            new MemoryUserStore(), new SmtpMailer(), Clock.systemDefaultZone());\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Registration.java","source":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\n\n// Ports: what the domain needs from the outside.\ninterface UserStore {\n    boolean exists(String email);\n\n    void add(String email);\n}\n\ninterface Mailer {\n    void send(String to, String body);\n}\n\n// The hexagon: rules only, no infrastructure.\nfinal class Registration {\n    private final UserStore store;\n    private final Mailer mailer;\n    private final Clock clock;\n\n    Registration(UserStore store, Mailer mailer, Clock clock) {\n        this.store = store;\n        this.mailer = mailer;\n        this.clock = clock;\n    }\n\n    String register(String email) {\n        if (!email.contains(\"@\")) return \"invalid\";\n        if (store.exists(email)) return \"duplicate\";\n        store.add(email);\n        LocalDate trialEnd = LocalDate.now(clock).plusDays(14);\n        mailer.send(email, \"Welcome, trial ends \" + trialEnd);\n        return \"registered\";\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Adapters.java","source":"import java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\n// Adapters: infrastructure plugged into the ports.\nfinal class MemoryUserStore implements UserStore {\n    private final Set<String> emails = new HashSet<>();\n\n    public boolean exists(String email) { return emails.contains(email); }\n\n    public void add(String email) { emails.add(email); }\n}\n\nfinal class SmtpMailer implements Mailer {\n    public void send(String to, String body) { SmtpClient.send(to, body); }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Signup.java","source":"import java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\n// The \"SMTP server\": delivered mail lands in SmtpClient.OUTBOX.\nfinal class SmtpClient {\n    static final java.util.List<String> OUTBOX = new java.util.ArrayList<>();\n\n    private SmtpClient() { }\n\n    static void send(String to, String body) {\n        OUTBOX.add(to + \": \" + body);\n    }\n}\n\n// The domain talks to SMTP and to the system clock directly.\nfinal class Registration {\n    private final Set<String> emails = new HashSet<>();\n\n    String register(String email) {\n        if (!email.contains(\"@\")) return \"invalid\";\n        if (!emails.add(email)) return \"duplicate\";\n        LocalDate trialEnd = LocalDate.now().plusDays(14);\n        SmtpClient.send(email, \"Welcome, trial ends \" + trialEnd);\n        return \"registered\";\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers start here. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Wiring {\n    private Wiring() { }\n\n    static Registration create() {\n        return new Registration();\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Registration` sends mail through `SmtpClient` and reads the system clock, so it cannot run without them.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Make it a hexagon: pure rules behind ports, infrastructure in adapters. `Wiring.create()` and every result string must keep working, and `SmtpClient` stays as the fake SMTP server.","type":"p"},{"items":["`interface UserStore` with `boolean exists(String)` and `void add(String)`.","`interface Mailer` with `void send(String to, String body)`.","`Registration(UserStore, Mailer, java.time.Clock)` keeps the rules and no infrastructure.","Adapters implement the ports. `Wiring.create()` assembles them."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"HexagonalKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Proxy;\nimport java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.time.ZoneOffset;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass HexagonalKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"invalid-email\")\n    void invalidEmail() {\n        SmtpClient.OUTBOX.clear();\n        Expect.equal(\"invalid\", Wiring.create().register(\"nobody\"), \"an email without @\");\n        Expect.equal(0, SmtpClient.OUTBOX.size(), \"mails sent for an invalid email\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"duplicate-email\")\n    void duplicateEmail() {\n        SmtpClient.OUTBOX.clear();\n        var app = Wiring.create();\n        Expect.equal(\"registered\", app.register(\"ana@x.org\"), \"first registration\");\n        Expect.equal(\"duplicate\", app.register(\"ana@x.org\"), \"second registration\");\n        Expect.equal(1, SmtpClient.OUTBOX.size(), \"welcome mails sent\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"welcome-mail\")\n    void welcomeMail() {\n        SmtpClient.OUTBOX.clear();\n        Wiring.create().register(\"ana@x.org\");\n        Expect.equal(1, SmtpClient.OUTBOX.size(), \"welcome mails sent\");\n        Expect.isTrue(SmtpClient.OUTBOX.get(0).startsWith(\"ana@x.org: Welcome, trial ends \"),\n            \"the mail should be addressed to ana@x.org, got \" + SmtpClient.OUTBOX.get(0));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"ports-exist\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void portsExist() {\n        Class<?> store = Types.named(\"UserStore\");\n        Class<?> mailer = Types.named(\"Mailer\");\n        Expect.isTrue(store.isInterface() && mailer.isInterface(),\n            \"UserStore and Mailer should be interfaces\");\n        Types.method(store, \"exists\", String.class);\n        Types.method(store, \"add\", String.class);\n        Types.method(mailer, \"send\", String.class, String.class);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"domain-takes-ports\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void domainTakesPorts() {\n        Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Registration\"),\n            Types.named(\"UserStore\"), Types.named(\"Mailer\"), Clock.class);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"domain-has-no-infrastructure\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void domainHasNoInfrastructure() {\n        var domain = Source.type(\"Registration\");\n        Expect.none(domain.mentions(\"SmtpClient\"), \"Registration still calls SMTP directly\");\n        Expect.none(domain.mentions(\"OUTBOX\"), \"Registration still touches the outbox\");\n        Expect.none(domain.news(\"HashSet\"), \"Registration still keeps the storage itself\");\n        Expect.none(domain.calls(\"currentTimeMillis\"), \"Registration reads the system clock\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"domain-uses-the-injected-clock\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void domainUsesTheInjectedClock() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> store = Types.named(\"UserStore\");\n        Class<?> mailer = Types.named(\"Mailer\");\n        Set<String> known = new HashSet<>();\n        List<String> mails = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object fakeStore = Proxy.newProxyInstance(store.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[] {store},\n            (p, m, a) -> m.getName().equals(\"exists\") ? known.contains((String) a[0])\n                : known.add((String) a[0]));\n        Object fakeMailer = Proxy.newProxyInstance(mailer.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[] {mailer},\n            (p, m, a) -> mails.add(a[0] + \": \" + a[1]));\n        Clock clock = Clock.fixed(Instant.parse(\"2026-03-10T00:00:00Z\"), ZoneOffset.UTC);\n        Object app = Types.create(\n            Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Registration\"), store, mailer, Clock.class),\n            fakeStore, fakeMailer, clock);\n        var register = Types.method(app.getClass(), \"register\", String.class);\n        Expect.equal(\"registered\", Types.call(register, app, \"ana@x.org\"), \"register\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ana@x.org: Welcome, trial ends 2026-03-24\"), mails,\n            \"mails produced with the fixed clock\");\n        Expect.equal(\"duplicate\", Types.call(register, app, \"ana@x.org\"), \"register again\");\n        Expect.equal(1, mails.size(), \"mails after a duplicate\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"store-decides-duplicates\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void storeDecidesDuplicates() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> store = Types.named(\"UserStore\");\n        Class<?> mailer = Types.named(\"Mailer\");\n        List<String> mails = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object taken = Proxy.newProxyInstance(store.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[] {store},\n            (p, m, a) -> m.getName().equals(\"exists\"));\n        Object fakeMailer = Proxy.newProxyInstance(mailer.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[] {mailer},\n            (p, m, a) -> mails.add((String) a[0]));\n        Object app = Types.create(\n            Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Registration\"), store, mailer, Clock.class),\n            taken, fakeMailer, Clock.systemUTC());\n        var register = Types.method(app.getClass(), \"register\", String.class);\n        Expect.equal(\"duplicate\", Types.call(register, app, \"bo@x.org\"),\n            \"an email the store already knows\");\n        Expect.equal(0, mails.size(), \"mails for a known email\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Put ports around the registration core"},{"checks":[{"id":"model-clamps","kind":"behaviour","title":"The target stays between 10 and 30"},{"id":"model-notifies","kind":"behaviour","title":"Every listener hears every change"},{"id":"view-renders","kind":"behaviour","title":"The view writes the target"},{"id":"controller-drives-model","kind":"behaviour","title":"Up and down adjust; others are reported"},{"id":"full-loop","kind":"behaviour","title":"Input, model and view work together"},{"id":"model-knows-no-view","kind":"design","title":"The model knows neither view nor controller"},{"id":"view-only-observes","kind":"design","title":"The view only observes the model"},{"id":"controller-does-not-render","kind":"design","title":"The controller does not render"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Ask of each class: what does it own, and what may it know? State and rules belong to the model. Showing belongs to the view. Translating input into model calls belongs to the controller.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The model keeps a `List<ModelListener>` and calls it after each `adjust`. `TextView` implements `ModelListener` and only writes to its `Consumer`. `Controller` holds the `Thermostat` and a `Consumer<String>` for errors.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Core of the model and controller:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["void adjust(int delta) {","    target = Math.max(10, Math.min(30, target + delta));","    for (ModelListener l : List.copyOf(listeners)) l.changed(target);","}","// Controller.onInput: \"up\" -> adjust(1), \"down\" -> adjust(-1)"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"mvc","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"readOnly":["ModelListener.java"],"solution":[{"name":"ModelListener.java","source":"// Given. The model tells its listeners about every change.\ninterface ModelListener {\n    void changed(int target);\n}\n"},{"name":"Thermostat.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// Model: owns the target temperature and the rules for changing it.\nfinal class Thermostat {\n    private final List<ModelListener> listeners = new ArrayList<>();\n    private int target;\n\n    Thermostat(int target) {\n        this.target = target;\n    }\n\n    int target() {\n        return target;\n    }\n\n    void addListener(ModelListener listener) {\n        listeners.add(listener);\n    }\n\n    void adjust(int delta) {\n        target = Math.max(10, Math.min(30, target + delta));\n        for (ModelListener listener : List.copyOf(listeners)) {\n            listener.changed(target);\n        }\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"TextView.java","source":"import java.util.function.Consumer;\n\n// View: shows the target to whoever listens on `out`.\nfinal class TextView implements ModelListener {\n    private final Consumer<String> out;\n\n    TextView(Consumer<String> out) {\n        this.out = out;\n    }\n\n    public void changed(int target) {\n        out.accept(\"Target: \" + target + \"C\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Controller.java","source":"import java.util.function.Consumer;\n\n// Controller: turns user input into calls on the model.\nfinal class Controller {\n    private final Thermostat model;\n    private final Consumer<String> messages;\n\n    Controller(Thermostat model, Consumer<String> messages) {\n        this.model = model;\n        this.messages = messages;\n    }\n\n    void onInput(String command) {\n        switch (command) {\n            case \"up\" -> model.adjust(1);\n            case \"down\" -> model.adjust(-1);\n            default -> messages.accept(\"Unknown: \" + command);\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"ModelListener.java","source":"// Given. The model tells its listeners about every change.\ninterface ModelListener {\n    void changed(int target);\n}\n"},{"name":"Thermostat.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// Model: owns the target temperature and the rules for changing it.\nfinal class Thermostat {\n    private final List<ModelListener> listeners = new ArrayList<>();\n    private int target;\n\n    Thermostat(int target) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    int target() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void addListener(ModelListener listener) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void adjust(int delta) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"TextView.java","source":"import java.util.function.Consumer;\n\n// View: shows the target to whoever listens on `out`.\nfinal class TextView implements ModelListener {\n    TextView(Consumer<String> out) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public void changed(int target) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Controller.java","source":"import java.util.function.Consumer;\n\n// Controller: turns user input into calls on the model.\nfinal class Controller {\n    Controller(Thermostat model, Consumer<String> messages) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void onInput(String command) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Wire a thermostat so the model, the view and the controller each do one job and know the least possible.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`ModelListener` is given. Fill in the three skeletons.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Thermostat` (model): `target()`; `adjust(int delta)` clamps the target to 10..30 and tells every listener the new target, even when it did not move.","`TextView(Consumer<String>)` (view): a `ModelListener` that writes `Target: 23C` style lines.","`Controller(Thermostat, Consumer<String>)`: `onInput(\"up\")` and `\"down\"` adjust by 1; anything else sends `Unknown: <text>` to the consumer.","The model knows no view or controller; the view never changes the model."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"MvcKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass MvcKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"model-clamps\")\n    void modelClamps() {\n        Thermostat t = new Thermostat(29);\n        t.adjust(5);\n        Expect.equal(30, t.target(), \"target after +5 from 29\");\n        t.adjust(-100);\n        Expect.equal(10, t.target(), \"target after -100\");\n        t.adjust(3);\n        Expect.equal(13, t.target(), \"target after +3\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"model-notifies\")\n    void modelNotifies() {\n        Thermostat t = new Thermostat(20);\n        List<Integer> a = new ArrayList<>();\n        List<Integer> b = new ArrayList<>();\n        t.addListener(a::add);\n        t.addListener(b::add);\n        t.adjust(1);\n        t.adjust(20);\n        t.adjust(1);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(21, 30, 30), a, \"first listener saw\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(21, 30, 30), b, \"second listener saw\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"view-renders\")\n    void viewRenders() {\n        List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        new TextView(out::add).changed(23);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"Target: 23C\"), out, \"what the view shows\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"controller-drives-model\")\n    void controllerDrivesModel() {\n        Thermostat t = new Thermostat(29);\n        List<String> messages = new ArrayList<>();\n        Controller c = new Controller(t, messages::add);\n        c.onInput(\"up\");\n        c.onInput(\"up\");\n        c.onInput(\"down\");\n        Expect.equal(29, t.target(), \"target after up, up, down from 29\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), messages, \"messages for valid commands\");\n        c.onInput(\"sing\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"Unknown: sing\"), messages, \"message for an unknown command\");\n        Expect.equal(29, t.target(), \"target after an unknown command\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"full-loop\")\n    void fullLoop() {\n        List<String> screen = new ArrayList<>();\n        Thermostat t = new Thermostat(29);\n        t.addListener(new TextView(screen::add));\n        Controller c = new Controller(t, screen::add);\n        for (String input : List.of(\"up\", \"up\", \"down\", \"sing\")) {\n            c.onInput(input);\n        }\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"Target: 30C\", \"Target: 30C\", \"Target: 29C\", \"Unknown: sing\"), screen,\n            \"the screen\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"model-knows-no-view\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void modelKnowsNoView() {\n        var model = Source.type(\"Thermostat\");\n        Expect.none(model.mentions(\"TextView\"), \"Thermostat refers to the view\");\n        Expect.none(model.mentions(\"Controller\"), \"Thermostat refers to the controller\");\n        Expect.none(model.mentions(\"Consumer\"), \"Thermostat prints or displays on its own\");\n        Expect.none(model.mentions(\"System\"), \"Thermostat prints or displays on its own\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"view-only-observes\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void viewOnlyObserves() {\n        Expect.isTrue(ModelListener.class.isAssignableFrom(Types.named(\"TextView\")),\n            \"TextView should implement ModelListener\");\n        var view = Source.type(\"TextView\");\n        Expect.none(view.mentions(\"Thermostat\"), \"TextView holds the model\");\n        Expect.none(view.calls(\"adjust\"), \"TextView changes the model\");\n        Expect.none(view.mentions(\"Controller\"), \"TextView refers to the controller\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"controller-does-not-render\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void controllerDoesNotRender() {\n        var controller = Source.type(\"Controller\");\n        Expect.none(controller.mentions(\"TextView\"), \"Controller refers to the view\");\n        Expect.none(controller.mentions(\"System\"), \"Controller prints directly\");\n        Expect.none(controller.calls(\"target\"), \"Controller reads model state to decide the output\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(Types.named(\"Controller\"), Types.named(\"Thermostat\"))\n            .stream().allMatch(f -> Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers())),\n            \"Controller's model field should be final\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Build a thermostat in Model, View, Controller"},{"checks":[{"id":"starts-disabled","kind":"behaviour","title":"A fresh form cannot be submitted"},{"id":"can-submit-rule","kind":"behaviour","title":"canSubmit follows the email and password rules"},{"id":"bindings-see-changes","kind":"behaviour","title":"A bound view sees canSubmit change"},{"id":"submit-reports-outcome","kind":"behaviour","title":"submit sets Welcome or Denied"},{"id":"invalid-form-is-not-sent","kind":"behaviour","title":"An invalid form never reaches auth"},{"id":"state-is-observable","kind":"design","title":"The state is exposed as Observable fields"},{"id":"viewmodel-knows-no-view","kind":"design","title":"The ViewModel references no view type"},{"id":"derived-state-is-computed-once","kind":"design","title":"canSubmit reacts instead of being polled"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A view should be able to subscribe and render, and the ViewModel should never call the view. Everything the screen shows becomes an `Observable`; everything it can do becomes a method.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep the `auth` predicate in a private field. In the constructor, `bind` on `email` and `password` to a private `refresh()` that sets `canSubmit` from both values. `submit()` returns early when `canSubmit` is false.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The reactive core:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["email.bind(e -> refresh());","password.bind(p -> refresh());","// refresh():","canSubmit.set(email.get().contains(\"@\")","    && password.get().length() >= 8);"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"mvvm","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Observable.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Observable.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Objects;\nimport java.util.function.Consumer;\n\n// Given. A value holder that tells subscribers when the value changes.\nfinal class Observable<T> {\n    private final List<Consumer<T>> subscribers = new ArrayList<>();\n    private T value;\n\n    Observable(T initial) { this.value = initial; }\n\n    T get() { return value; }\n\n    // Does nothing when the value is equal to the current one.\n    void set(T next) {\n        if (Objects.equals(value, next)) return;\n        value = next;\n        for (Consumer<T> s : List.copyOf(subscribers)) s.accept(next);\n    }\n\n    // Calls the subscriber now with the current value, then on every change.\n    void bind(Consumer<T> subscriber) {\n        subscribers.add(subscriber);\n        subscriber.accept(value);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"SignInViewModel.java","source":"import java.util.function.BiPredicate;\n\n// ViewModel: the screen's state and actions, with no view in sight.\nfinal class SignInViewModel {\n    final Observable<String> email = new Observable<>(\"\");\n    final Observable<String> password = new Observable<>(\"\");\n    final Observable<Boolean> canSubmit = new Observable<>(false);\n    final Observable<String> status = new Observable<>(\"\");\n    private final BiPredicate<String, String> auth;\n\n    SignInViewModel(BiPredicate<String, String> auth) {\n        this.auth = auth;\n        email.bind(e -> refresh());\n        password.bind(p -> refresh());\n    }\n\n    private void refresh() {\n        canSubmit.set(email.get().contains(\"@\")\n            && password.get().length() >= 8);\n    }\n\n    void submit() {\n        if (!canSubmit.get()) return;\n        boolean ok = auth.test(email.get(), password.get());\n        status.set(ok ? \"Welcome\" : \"Denied\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Observable.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Objects;\nimport java.util.function.Consumer;\n\n// Given. A value holder that tells subscribers when the value changes.\nfinal class Observable<T> {\n    private final List<Consumer<T>> subscribers = new ArrayList<>();\n    private T value;\n\n    Observable(T initial) { this.value = initial; }\n\n    T get() { return value; }\n\n    // Does nothing when the value is equal to the current one.\n    void set(T next) {\n        if (Objects.equals(value, next)) return;\n        value = next;\n        for (Consumer<T> s : List.copyOf(subscribers)) s.accept(next);\n    }\n\n    // Calls the subscriber now with the current value, then on every change.\n    void bind(Consumer<T> subscriber) {\n        subscribers.add(subscriber);\n        subscriber.accept(value);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"SignInViewModel.java","source":"import java.util.function.BiPredicate;\n\n// ViewModel: the screen's state and actions, with no view in sight.\nfinal class SignInViewModel {\n    final Observable<String> email = new Observable<>(\"\");\n    final Observable<String> password = new Observable<>(\"\");\n    final Observable<Boolean> canSubmit = new Observable<>(false);\n    final Observable<String> status = new Observable<>(\"\");\n\n    SignInViewModel(BiPredicate<String, String> auth) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void submit() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A sign-in screen needs state a view can bind to and an action it can call, without the model ever seeing a view.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Observable<T>` is given and must stay as it is. Implement `SignInViewModel(BiPredicate<String, String> auth)`, where `auth.test(email, password)` says whether the sign-in works.","type":"p"},{"items":["Fields `email`, `password`, `canSubmit` (starts `false`) and `status` (starts `\"\"`), all `Observable`.","`canSubmit` is true when `email` contains `@` and `password` has at least 8 characters, and follows every change by itself.","`submit()` does nothing unless `canSubmit`; otherwise `status` becomes `Welcome` or `Denied`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"MvvmKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass MvvmKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"starts-disabled\")\n    void startsDisabled() {\n        var vm = new SignInViewModel((e, p) -> true);\n        Expect.equal(false, vm.canSubmit.get(), \"canSubmit at the start\");\n        Expect.equal(\"\", vm.status.get(), \"status at the start\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"can-submit-rule\")\n    void canSubmitRule() {\n        var vm = new SignInViewModel((e, p) -> true);\n        vm.email.set(\"ana@x.org\");\n        Expect.equal(false, vm.canSubmit.get(), \"email only\");\n        vm.password.set(\"1234567\");\n        Expect.equal(false, vm.canSubmit.get(), \"7-character password\");\n        vm.password.set(\"12345678\");\n        Expect.equal(true, vm.canSubmit.get(), \"8-character password\");\n        vm.email.set(\"ana\");\n        Expect.equal(false, vm.canSubmit.get(), \"email without @\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bindings-see-changes\")\n    void bindingsSeeChanges() {\n        var vm = new SignInViewModel((e, p) -> true);\n        List<Boolean> seen = new ArrayList<>();\n        vm.canSubmit.bind(seen::add);\n        vm.email.set(\"a@x\");\n        vm.password.set(\"12345678\");\n        vm.password.set(\"123456789\");\n        vm.password.set(\"x\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(false, true, false), seen, \"values a view bound to canSubmit saw\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"submit-reports-outcome\")\n    void submitReportsOutcome() {\n        var vm = new SignInViewModel((e, p) -> p.startsWith(\"hunter\"));\n        vm.email.set(\"ana@x.org\");\n        vm.password.set(\"wrongwrong\");\n        vm.submit();\n        Expect.equal(\"Denied\", vm.status.get(), \"status after a bad password\");\n        vm.password.set(\"hunter22!\");\n        vm.submit();\n        Expect.equal(\"Welcome\", vm.status.get(), \"status after a good password\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"invalid-form-is-not-sent\")\n    void invalidFormIsNotSent() {\n        List<String> calls = new ArrayList<>();\n        var vm = new SignInViewModel((e, p) -> calls.add(e));\n        vm.email.set(\"ana@x.org\");\n        vm.password.set(\"short\");\n        vm.submit();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), calls, \"authentication calls for an invalid form\");\n        Expect.equal(\"\", vm.status.get(), \"status after an ignored submit\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"state-is-observable\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void stateIsObservable() {\n        Class<?> vm = Types.named(\"SignInViewModel\");\n        for (String name : List.of(\"email\", \"password\", \"canSubmit\", \"status\")) {\n            Field f;\n            try {\n                f = vm.getDeclaredField(name);\n            } catch (NoSuchFieldException e) {\n                Expect.fail(\"SignInViewModel needs a field named \" + name);\n                return;\n            }\n            Expect.isTrue(f.getType() == Observable.class,\n                \"SignInViewModel.\" + name + \" should be an Observable\");\n            Expect.isTrue(!Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()) && Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n                \"SignInViewModel.\" + name + \" should be final and visible to a view\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"viewmodel-knows-no-view\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void viewmodelKnowsNoView() {\n        for (Field f : Types.named(\"SignInViewModel\").getDeclaredFields()) {\n            String type = f.getType().getName();\n            Expect.isTrue(f.getType() == Observable.class || type.startsWith(\"java.\"),\n                \"SignInViewModel.\" + f.getName() + \" has type \" + type\n                + \", which looks like a view or toolkit type\");\n        }\n        var source = Source.type(\"SignInViewModel\");\n        Expect.none(source.mentions(\"System\"), \"SignInViewModel prints instead of exposing state\");\n        Expect.none(source.calls(\"println\"), \"SignInViewModel prints instead of exposing state\");\n        Expect.none(source.mentions(\"Thread\"), \"SignInViewModel manages threads of its own\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"derived-state-is-computed-once\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void derivedStateIsComputedOnce() {\n        var vm = Source.type(\"SignInViewModel\");\n        Expect.none(vm.mentions(\"Timer\"), \"SignInViewModel polls instead of reacting\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!vm.calls(\"bind\").isEmpty(),\n            \"canSubmit should be derived by reacting to email and password with bind\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Build a sign-in ViewModel"},{"checks":[{"id":"overdue-are-reminded","kind":"behaviour","title":"Overdue invoices are mailed"},{"id":"later-runs-add-up","kind":"behaviour","title":"Each run mails again"},{"id":"collaborators-are-injected","kind":"design","title":"Collaborators arrive through the constructor"},{"id":"no-hard-wiring","kind":"design","title":"No new, no static singleton inside the reminder"},{"id":"clock-is-injected","kind":"design","title":"The reminder follows the injected clock"},{"id":"missing-collaborator-fails-early","kind":"design","title":"A null collaborator fails at construction"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Look at every noun the reminder gets for free: a store, a mail gateway, the date. Each is a dependency hidden inside the class. Turn each into something the constructor receives.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Extract `InvoiceSource` and `Mailer` interfaces, hold all three collaborators in `private final` fields, and move the `new` calls into `Reminders.create()`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Ask the injected clock for today and wire the singleton in the root:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["LocalDate today = LocalDate.now(clock);","// Reminders.create():","Mailer mailer = (to, body) -> MailGateway.INSTANCE.send(to, body);","return new InvoiceReminder(","    new InvoiceStore(), mailer, Clock.systemDefaultZone());"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"dependency-injection","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Reminders.java","source":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord Invoice(String id, String customer, LocalDate due) { }\n\n// A process-wide mail gateway. Delivered mail lands in SENT.\nfinal class MailGateway {\n    static final MailGateway INSTANCE = new MailGateway();\n    static final List<String> SENT = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    private MailGateway() { }\n\n    void send(String to, String body) {\n        SENT.add(to + \": \" + body);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class InvoiceStore implements InvoiceSource {\n    public List<Invoice> all() {\n        return List.of(\n            new Invoice(\"A-1\", \"ana\", LocalDate.parse(\"2020-01-01\")),\n            new Invoice(\"A-2\", \"bo\", LocalDate.parse(\"2999-01-01\")),\n            new Invoice(\"A-3\", \"cy\", LocalDate.parse(\"2020-06-01\")));\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers start here. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Reminders {\n    private Reminders() { }\n\n    // The composition root: the only place that chooses implementations.\n    static InvoiceReminder create() {\n        Mailer mailer = (to, body) -> MailGateway.INSTANCE.send(to, body);\n        return new InvoiceReminder(\n            new InvoiceStore(), mailer, Clock.systemDefaultZone());\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"InvoiceReminder.java","source":"import java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Objects;\n\ninterface Mailer {\n    void send(String to, String body);\n}\n\ninterface InvoiceSource {\n    List<Invoice> all();\n}\n\nfinal class InvoiceReminder {\n    private final InvoiceSource source;\n    private final Mailer mailer;\n    private final Clock clock;\n\n    InvoiceReminder(InvoiceSource source, Mailer mailer, Clock clock) {\n        this.source = Objects.requireNonNull(source);\n        this.mailer = Objects.requireNonNull(mailer);\n        this.clock = Objects.requireNonNull(clock);\n    }\n\n    int remind() {\n        LocalDate today = LocalDate.now(clock);\n        int count = 0;\n        for (Invoice inv : source.all()) {\n            if (inv.due().isBefore(today)) {\n                mailer.send(inv.customer(), inv.id() + \" overdue\");\n                count++;\n            }\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Reminders.java","source":"import java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord Invoice(String id, String customer, LocalDate due) { }\n\n// A process-wide mail gateway. Delivered mail lands in SENT.\nfinal class MailGateway {\n    static final MailGateway INSTANCE = new MailGateway();\n    static final List<String> SENT = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    private MailGateway() { }\n\n    void send(String to, String body) {\n        SENT.add(to + \": \" + body);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class InvoiceStore {\n    List<Invoice> all() {\n        return List.of(\n            new Invoice(\"A-1\", \"ana\", LocalDate.parse(\"2020-01-01\")),\n            new Invoice(\"A-2\", \"bo\", LocalDate.parse(\"2999-01-01\")),\n            new Invoice(\"A-3\", \"cy\", LocalDate.parse(\"2020-06-01\")));\n    }\n}\n\n// Builds its own collaborators and reads the system date.\nfinal class InvoiceReminder {\n    private final InvoiceStore store = new InvoiceStore();\n\n    int remind() {\n        LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();\n        int count = 0;\n        for (Invoice inv : store.all()) {\n            if (inv.due().isBefore(today)) {\n                MailGateway.INSTANCE.send(\n                    inv.customer(), inv.id() + \" overdue\");\n                count++;\n            }\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers start here. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Reminders {\n    private Reminders() { }\n\n    static InvoiceReminder create() {\n        return new InvoiceReminder();\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`InvoiceReminder` builds its own `InvoiceStore`, calls the `MailGateway` singleton and reads today's date, so no test can control it.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Inject what it needs. `Reminders.create()` is the composition root: it keeps its signature and behaviour, and it is the only place that picks implementations.","type":"p"},{"items":["`interface InvoiceSource` with `List<Invoice> all()`; `InvoiceStore` implements it.","`interface Mailer` with `void send(String to, String body)`.","`InvoiceReminder(InvoiceSource, Mailer, java.time.Clock)` with `int remind()`.","Fail fast with `NullPointerException` on a null collaborator."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"InjectionKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Proxy;\nimport java.time.Clock;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.time.LocalDate;\nimport java.time.ZoneOffset;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass InjectionKataTest {\n    static Clock at(String date) {\n        return Clock.fixed(Instant.parse(date + \"T00:00:00Z\"), ZoneOffset.UTC);\n    }\n\n    /** Builds an InvoiceReminder from fakes; returns {reminder, mails}. */\n    static Object[] build(List<Invoice> invoices, Clock clock) throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> source = Types.named(\"InvoiceSource\");\n        Class<?> mailer = Types.named(\"Mailer\");\n        List<String> mails = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object fakeSource = Proxy.newProxyInstance(source.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[] {source},\n            (p, m, a) -> invoices);\n        Object fakeMailer = Proxy.newProxyInstance(mailer.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[] {mailer},\n            (p, m, a) -> mails.add(a[0] + \": \" + a[1]));\n        Object reminder = Types.create(\n            Types.constructor(Types.named(\"InvoiceReminder\"), source, mailer, Clock.class),\n            fakeSource, fakeMailer, clock);\n        return new Object[] {reminder, mails};\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"overdue-are-reminded\")\n    void overdueAreReminded() {\n        MailGateway.SENT.clear();\n        Expect.equal(2, Reminders.create().remind(), \"reminders sent\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ana: A-1 overdue\", \"cy: A-3 overdue\"), MailGateway.SENT,\n            \"mails delivered\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"later-runs-add-up\")\n    void laterRunsAddUp() {\n        MailGateway.SENT.clear();\n        var job = Reminders.create();\n        job.remind();\n        job.remind();\n        Expect.equal(4, MailGateway.SENT.size(), \"mails after two runs\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"collaborators-are-injected\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void collaboratorsAreInjected() {\n        Class<?> reminder = Types.named(\"InvoiceReminder\");\n        Class<?> source = Types.named(\"InvoiceSource\");\n        Class<?> mailer = Types.named(\"Mailer\");\n        Expect.isTrue(source.isInterface() && mailer.isInterface(),\n            \"InvoiceSource and Mailer should be interfaces\");\n        Types.constructor(reminder, source, mailer, Clock.class);\n        for (Class<?> type : List.of(source, mailer, Clock.class)) {\n            Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(reminder, type);\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()) && Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n                \"InvoiceReminder.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-hard-wiring\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noHardWiring() {\n        var reminder = Source.type(\"InvoiceReminder\");\n        Expect.none(reminder.news(\"InvoiceStore\"), \"InvoiceReminder still creates its own store\");\n        Expect.none(reminder.mentions(\"MailGateway\"), \"InvoiceReminder still reaches a static singleton\");\n        Expect.none(reminder.mentions(\"INSTANCE\"), \"InvoiceReminder still reaches a static singleton\");\n        Expect.none(reminder.mentions(\"InvoiceStore\"), \"InvoiceReminder depends on a concrete store\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"clock-is-injected\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void clockIsInjected() throws Throwable {\n        var invoices = List.of(\n            new Invoice(\"X-1\", \"dee\", LocalDate.parse(\"2026-03-10\")),\n            new Invoice(\"X-2\", \"eli\", LocalDate.parse(\"2026-03-09\")));\n        Object[] early = build(invoices, at(\"2026-03-10\"));\n        var remind = Types.method(early[0].getClass(), \"remind\");\n        Expect.equal(1, Types.call(remind, early[0]), \"overdue on 2026-03-10\");\n        Object[] late = build(invoices, at(\"2026-04-01\"));\n        Expect.equal(2, Types.call(remind, late[0]), \"overdue on 2026-04-01\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"dee: X-1 overdue\", \"eli: X-2 overdue\"), late[1],\n            \"mails sent to the fake mailer\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"missing-collaborator-fails-early\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void missingCollaboratorFailsEarly() {\n        Class<?> source = Types.named(\"InvoiceSource\");\n        Class<?> mailer = Types.named(\"Mailer\");\n        var ctor = Types.constructor(Types.named(\"InvoiceReminder\"), source, mailer, Clock.class);\n        Expect.raises(NullPointerException.class, () -> Types.create(ctor, null, null, null),\n            \"constructing an InvoiceReminder without collaborators\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Inject the reminder's collaborators"},{"checks":[{"id":"register-and-get","kind":"behaviour","title":"get returns what register stored"},{"id":"missing-fails-fast","kind":"behaviour","title":"A missing service fails with a clear message"},{"id":"duplicate-is-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"A second registration is rejected"},{"id":"locators-are-independent","kind":"behaviour","title":"Locators do not share services"},{"id":"one-concurrent-winner","kind":"behaviour","title":"Racing registrations have one winner"},{"id":"signup-sends","kind":"behaviour","title":"SignupService sends the welcome mail"},{"id":"signup-fails-at-startup","kind":"behaviour","title":"A missing Mailer fails when SignupService is built"},{"id":"locator-state-is-per-instance","kind":"design","title":"The registry is not static"},{"id":"consumer-resolves-once","kind":"design","title":"SignupService resolves its Mailer once"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A locator is a map from type to instance. Two rules make it safe: be strict about what you register and what you hand out, and let consumers resolve what they need as early as possible.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Back `ServiceLocator` with an instance `ConcurrentHashMap<Class<?>, Object>`. Use `putIfAbsent` so two racing threads cannot both win. `SignupService` keeps a `private final Mailer` set in its constructor.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The strict core:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["if (services.putIfAbsent(type, service) != null) {","    throw new IllegalStateException(","        \"already registered: \" + type.getSimpleName());","}","// SignupService: this.mailer = locator.get(Mailer.class);"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"service-locator","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Mailer.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Mailer.java","source":"// Given. The service SignupService needs.\ninterface Mailer {\n    void send(String to, String body);\n}\n"},{"name":"ServiceLocator.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Objects;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\n// A typed registry of services. Each locator is independent.\nfinal class ServiceLocator {\n    private final Map<Class<?>, Object> services = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n    <T> void register(Class<T> type, T service) {\n        Objects.requireNonNull(type);\n        Objects.requireNonNull(service);\n        if (services.putIfAbsent(type, service) != null) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\n                \"already registered: \" + type.getSimpleName());\n        }\n    }\n\n    <T> T get(Class<T> type) {\n        Object service = services.get(type);\n        if (service == null) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\n                \"no service registered for \" + type.getSimpleName());\n        }\n        return type.cast(service);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"SignupService.java","source":"// Looks its Mailer up in a locator.\nfinal class SignupService {\n    private final Mailer mailer;\n\n    SignupService(ServiceLocator locator) {\n        this.mailer = locator.get(Mailer.class);\n    }\n\n    void signUp(String email) {\n        mailer.send(email, \"Welcome\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Mailer.java","source":"// Given. The service SignupService needs.\ninterface Mailer {\n    void send(String to, String body);\n}\n"},{"name":"ServiceLocator.java","source":"// A typed registry of services. Each locator is independent.\nfinal class ServiceLocator {\n    <T> void register(Class<T> type, T service) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    <T> T get(Class<T> type) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"SignupService.java","source":"// Looks its Mailer up in a locator.\nfinal class SignupService {\n    SignupService(ServiceLocator locator) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void signUp(String email) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A service locator hands out services by type. Make it strict, so a missing service shows up at startup, not on a customer's request.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Mailer` is given. Implement the two skeletons.","type":"p"},{"items":["`ServiceLocator.register(Class<T>, T)` stores a service. Registering a type twice throws `IllegalStateException(\"already registered: Mailer\")`, also under concurrent calls.","`ServiceLocator.get(Class<T>)` throws `IllegalStateException(\"no service registered for Mailer\")` when absent. Names are simple class names.","Each `ServiceLocator` has its own services; nothing is static.","`SignupService(ServiceLocator)` looks the `Mailer` up in its constructor, not in `signUp`; `signUp(email)` sends the body `Welcome`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"LocatorKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass LocatorKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"register-and-get\")\n    void registerAndGet() {\n        var locator = new ServiceLocator();\n        Mailer mailer = (to, body) -> { };\n        locator.register(Mailer.class, mailer);\n        locator.register(String.class, \"hello\");\n        Expect.isTrue(locator.get(Mailer.class) == mailer, \"get should return the registered instance\");\n        Expect.equal(\"hello\", locator.get(String.class), \"a second type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"missing-fails-fast\")\n    void missingFailsFast() {\n        var locator = new ServiceLocator();\n        var e = Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> locator.get(Mailer.class),\n            \"get for an unregistered type\");\n        Expect.equal(\"no service registered for Mailer\", e.getMessage(), \"the message\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"duplicate-is-rejected\")\n    void duplicateIsRejected() {\n        var locator = new ServiceLocator();\n        Mailer first = (to, body) -> { };\n        locator.register(Mailer.class, first);\n        var e = Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            () -> locator.register(Mailer.class, (to, body) -> { }), \"registering a type twice\");\n        Expect.equal(\"already registered: Mailer\", e.getMessage(), \"the message\");\n        Expect.isTrue(locator.get(Mailer.class) == first, \"the first registration should survive\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"locators-are-independent\")\n    void locatorsAreIndependent() {\n        var a = new ServiceLocator();\n        var b = new ServiceLocator();\n        a.register(Mailer.class, (to, body) -> { });\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> b.get(Mailer.class),\n            \"a second locator must not see the first one's services\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"one-concurrent-winner\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void oneConcurrentWinner() {\n        var locator = new ServiceLocator();\n        AtomicInteger next = new AtomicInteger();\n        List<Boolean> results = Stress.race(8, () -> {\n            try {\n                locator.register(Mailer.class, (to, body) -> next.incrementAndGet());\n                return true;\n            } catch (IllegalStateException e) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        });\n        Expect.equal(1, (int) results.stream().filter(r -> r).count(), \"threads whose registration won\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"signup-sends\")\n    void signupSends() {\n        var locator = new ServiceLocator();\n        List<String> sent = new ArrayList<>();\n        locator.register(Mailer.class, (to, body) -> sent.add(to + \": \" + body));\n        new SignupService(locator).signUp(\"ana\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ana: Welcome\"), sent, \"mail sent\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"signup-fails-at-startup\")\n    void signupFailsAtStartup() {\n        var locator = new ServiceLocator();\n        var e = Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> new SignupService(locator),\n            \"building SignupService without a Mailer\");\n        Expect.equal(\"no service registered for Mailer\", e.getMessage(), \"the message\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"locator-state-is-per-instance\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void locatorStateIsPerInstance() {\n        for (var f : Types.named(\"ServiceLocator\").getDeclaredFields()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(!Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers()),\n                \"ServiceLocator.\" + f.getName() + \" is shared by every locator; make it per instance\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"consumer-resolves-once\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void consumerResolvesOnce() {\n        var signup = Source.type(\"SignupService\");\n        Expect.none(signup.method(\"signUp\").calls(\"get\"),\n            \"signUp asks the locator on every call; resolve the Mailer when the service is built\");\n        var f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(Types.named(\"SignupService\"), Mailer.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()) && Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n            \"SignupService.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(Types.named(\"SignupService\"), Types.named(\"ServiceLocator\")).isEmpty(),\n            \"SignupService should not keep the locator after construction\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Build a typed service locator that fails fast"},{"checks":[{"id":"save-and-find","kind":"behaviour","title":"A saved order can be found by id"},{"id":"missing-is-empty","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unknown ids and customers give empty results"},{"id":"save-replaces","kind":"behaviour","title":"Saving an existing id replaces it"},{"id":"by-customer-sorted","kind":"behaviour","title":"Orders for a customer come back sorted by id"},{"id":"remove","kind":"behaviour","title":"Remove deletes, and tolerates unknown ids"},{"id":"results-are-snapshots","kind":"behaviour","title":"Returned lists do not change later"},{"id":"service-works-with-any-port","kind":"behaviour","title":"LoyaltyService works with any repository"},{"id":"loyalty-over-memory-repo","kind":"behaviour","title":"Points add up over the in-memory store"},{"id":"memory-repo-implements-port","kind":"design","title":"The in-memory store implements the port"},{"id":"service-depends-on-port","kind":"design","title":"LoyaltyService holds only the port"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A repository is a collection-shaped seam. The service should see only the interface, and the storage detail should live in exactly one class behind it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep a `Map<OrderId, Order>` inside `InMemoryOrderRepository`. `LoyaltyService` keeps a private final `OrderRepository` from its constructor. Filter and sort when you answer `findByCustomer`, so the result is a new list.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The query is a stream over the map values:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["return rows.values().stream()","    .filter(o -> o.customer().equals(customer))","    .sorted(Comparator.comparing(o -> o.id().value()))","    .toList();"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"repository","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Order.java","OrderRepository.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Order.java","source":"record OrderId(String value) { }\n\nrecord Order(OrderId id, String customer, int totalCents) { }\n"},{"name":"OrderRepository.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\n// The port. The domain talks to this, never to a concrete store.\ninterface OrderRepository {\n    Optional<Order> findById(OrderId id);\n    List<Order> findByCustomer(String customer);\n    void save(Order order);\n    void remove(OrderId id);\n}\n"},{"name":"InMemoryOrderRepository.java","source":"import java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\n\nfinal class InMemoryOrderRepository implements OrderRepository {\n    private final Map<OrderId, Order> rows = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n    public Optional<Order> findById(OrderId id) {\n        return Optional.ofNullable(rows.get(id));\n    }\n\n    public List<Order> findByCustomer(String customer) {\n        return rows.values().stream()\n            .filter(o -> o.customer().equals(customer))\n            .sorted(Comparator.comparing(o -> o.id().value()))\n            .toList();\n    }\n\n    public void save(Order order) {\n        rows.put(order.id(), order);\n    }\n\n    public void remove(OrderId id) {\n        rows.remove(id);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"LoyaltyService.java","source":"import java.util.Objects;\n\nfinal class LoyaltyService {\n    private final OrderRepository orders;\n\n    LoyaltyService(OrderRepository orders) {\n        this.orders = Objects.requireNonNull(orders, \"orders\");\n    }\n\n    int points(String customer) {\n        return orders.findByCustomer(customer).stream()\n            .mapToInt(o -> o.totalCents() / 100)\n            .sum();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Order.java","source":"record OrderId(String value) { }\n\nrecord Order(OrderId id, String customer, int totalCents) { }\n"},{"name":"OrderRepository.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\n// The port. The domain talks to this, never to a concrete store.\ninterface OrderRepository {\n    Optional<Order> findById(OrderId id);\n    List<Order> findByCustomer(String customer);\n    void save(Order order);\n    void remove(OrderId id);\n}\n"},{"name":"InMemoryOrderRepository.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\nfinal class InMemoryOrderRepository implements OrderRepository {\n    public Optional<Order> findById(OrderId id) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public List<Order> findByCustomer(String customer) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public void save(Order order) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    public void remove(OrderId id) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"LoyaltyService.java","source":"final class LoyaltyService {\n    LoyaltyService(OrderRepository orders) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    int points(String customer) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"The domain should ask for orders as if they lived in a collection.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`OrderRepository` is the port, already written. Implement it in memory and use it from a service.","type":"p"},{"items":["`InMemoryOrderRepository` implements `OrderRepository`. `save` inserts or replaces by id; `findById` returns an empty `Optional` for unknown ids; `remove` ignores unknown ids.","`findByCustomer` returns that customer's orders sorted by `id().value()`, as a snapshot that later saves do not change.","`LoyaltyService(OrderRepository)` gives `points(customer)`: the sum of `totalCents() / 100` over that customer's orders. It must know only the port."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"RepositoryKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass RepositoryKataTest {\n    static Order order(String id, String customer, int cents) {\n        return new Order(new OrderId(id), customer, cents);\n    }\n\n    static OrderRepository repo() {\n        return new InMemoryOrderRepository();\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"save-and-find\")\n    void saveAndFind() {\n        OrderRepository r = repo();\n        r.save(order(\"o-1\", \"ada\", 2550));\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(order(\"o-1\", \"ada\", 2550)),\n            r.findById(new OrderId(\"o-1\")), \"findById after save\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"missing-is-empty\")\n    void missingIsEmpty() {\n        Expect.equal(Optional.empty(), repo().findById(new OrderId(\"nope\")),\n            \"findById of an unknown id\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), repo().findByCustomer(\"nobody\"),\n            \"findByCustomer of an unknown customer\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"save-replaces\")\n    void saveReplaces() {\n        OrderRepository r = repo();\n        r.save(order(\"o-1\", \"ada\", 100));\n        r.save(order(\"o-1\", \"ada\", 900));\n        Expect.equal(900, r.findById(new OrderId(\"o-1\")).orElseThrow().totalCents(),\n            \"total after saving the same id twice\");\n        Expect.equal(1, r.findByCustomer(\"ada\").size(), \"orders kept for ada\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"by-customer-sorted\")\n    void byCustomerSorted() {\n        OrderRepository r = repo();\n        r.save(order(\"o-3\", \"ada\", 1));\n        r.save(order(\"o-1\", \"ada\", 2));\n        r.save(order(\"o-2\", \"bob\", 3));\n        r.save(order(\"o-10\", \"ada\", 4));\n        List<String> ids = r.findByCustomer(\"ada\").stream()\n            .map(o -> o.id().value()).toList();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"o-1\", \"o-10\", \"o-3\"), ids,\n            \"ada's orders, sorted by id text\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"remove\")\n    void remove() {\n        OrderRepository r = repo();\n        r.save(order(\"o-1\", \"ada\", 1));\n        r.remove(new OrderId(\"o-1\"));\n        r.remove(new OrderId(\"never-there\"));\n        Expect.equal(Optional.empty(), r.findById(new OrderId(\"o-1\")),\n            \"findById after remove\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), r.findByCustomer(\"ada\"), \"ada's orders after remove\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"results-are-snapshots\")\n    void resultsAreSnapshots() {\n        OrderRepository r = repo();\n        r.save(order(\"o-1\", \"ada\", 1));\n        List<Order> before = r.findByCustomer(\"ada\");\n        r.save(order(\"o-2\", \"ada\", 2));\n        Expect.equal(1, before.size(), \"a list returned earlier must not change later\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-works-with-any-port\")\n    void serviceWorksWithAnyPort() {\n        List<Order> stored = List.of(order(\"a\", \"ada\", 2550), order(\"b\", \"ada\", 1000));\n        OrderRepository fake = new OrderRepository() {\n            public Optional<Order> findById(OrderId id) { return Optional.empty(); }\n            public List<Order> findByCustomer(String c) { return new ArrayList<>(stored); }\n            public void save(Order o) { }\n            public void remove(OrderId id) { }\n        };\n        Expect.equal(35, new LoyaltyService(fake).points(\"ada\"),\n            \"points computed from a repository it has never seen\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"loyalty-over-memory-repo\")\n    void loyaltyOverMemoryRepo() {\n        OrderRepository r = repo();\n        r.save(order(\"o-1\", \"ada\", 2550));\n        r.save(order(\"o-2\", \"bob\", 900));\n        r.save(order(\"o-3\", \"ada\", 1000));\n        Expect.equal(35, new LoyaltyService(r).points(\"ada\"), \"ada's points\");\n        Expect.equal(0, new LoyaltyService(r).points(\"eve\"), \"eve's points\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"memory-repo-implements-port\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void memoryRepoImplementsPort() {\n        Class<?> port = Types.named(\"OrderRepository\");\n        Class<?> memory = Types.named(\"InMemoryOrderRepository\");\n        Expect.isTrue(port.isInterface(), \"OrderRepository should stay an interface\");\n        Expect.isTrue(port.isAssignableFrom(memory),\n            \"InMemoryOrderRepository should implement OrderRepository\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-depends-on-port\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void serviceDependsOnPort() {\n        Class<?> service = Types.named(\"LoyaltyService\");\n        Class<?> port = Types.named(\"OrderRepository\");\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(service, port);\n        Expect.isTrue(java.lang.reflect.Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n            \"LoyaltyService.\" + f.getName() + \" should be final\");\n        var shape = Source.type(\"LoyaltyService\");\n        Expect.none(shape.mentions(\"InMemoryOrderRepository\"),\n            \"LoyaltyService names the in-memory store\");\n        Expect.none(shape.news(\"InMemoryOrderRepository\"),\n            \"LoyaltyService builds its own store\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Hide order storage behind a repository"},{"checks":[{"id":"identity-map","kind":"behaviour","title":"One object per id inside a unit of work"},{"id":"unknown-id","kind":"behaviour","title":"Loading an unknown id is rejected"},{"id":"nothing-before-commit","kind":"behaviour","title":"The database is untouched until commit"},{"id":"commit-writes-changes","kind":"behaviour","title":"Commit writes inserts, updates and deletes"},{"id":"commit-order","kind":"behaviour","title":"Inserts first, then updates, then deletes"},{"id":"clean-objects-not-written","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unchanged objects produce no UPDATE"},{"id":"removed-dirty-only-deleted","kind":"behaviour","title":"A removed object is only deleted"},{"id":"commit-resets-tracking","kind":"behaviour","title":"A unit of work can be reused after commit"},{"id":"rollback","kind":"behaviour","title":"Rollback discards pending changes"},{"id":"account-knows-nothing-of-tracking","kind":"design","title":"Account stays free of tracking code"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The unit of work is a ledger of what happened during one business transaction. It needs to remember three things: what it loaded, what the loaded things looked like, and what was registered.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep a `Map<String, Account>` for identity, a `Map<String, Integer>` snapshot of balances, and lists for new and removed accounts. `commit()` compares each loaded account with its snapshot instead of asking the account whether it is dirty.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Commit in three passes over your tracking data:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["for (Account a : created) { next.put(a.id, a.balance); log.add(\"INSERT \" + a.id); }","for (Account a : loaded.values()) {","    if (removed.contains(a) || a.balance == snapshot.get(a.id)) continue;","    next.put(a.id, a.balance); log.add(\"UPDATE \" + a.id);","}","for (Account a : removed) { next.remove(a.id); log.add(\"DELETE \" + a.id); }"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"unit-of-work","kind":"implement","minutes":30,"readOnly":["Account.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Account.java","source":"final class Account {\n    final String id;\n    int balance;\n\n    Account(String id, int balance) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.balance = balance;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"UnitOfWork.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.LinkedHashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\n\nfinal class UnitOfWork {\n    private final Map<String, Integer> db;\n    private final Map<String, Account> loaded = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n    private final Map<String, Integer> snapshot = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n    private final List<Account> created = new ArrayList<>();\n    private final List<Account> removed = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    UnitOfWork(Map<String, Integer> db) {\n        this.db = db;\n    }\n\n    Account load(String id) {\n        Account known = loaded.get(id);\n        if (known != null) return known;\n        Integer stored = db.get(id);\n        if (stored == null) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown account: \" + id);\n        }\n        Account account = new Account(id, stored);\n        loaded.put(id, account);\n        snapshot.put(id, stored);\n        return account;\n    }\n\n    void registerNew(Account account) {\n        created.add(account);\n    }\n\n    void registerRemoved(Account account) {\n        removed.add(account);\n    }\n\n    List<String> commit() {\n        var log = new ArrayList<String>();\n        var next = new TreeMap<>(db);\n        for (Account a : created) {\n            next.put(a.id, a.balance);\n            log.add(\"INSERT \" + a.id);\n        }\n        for (Account a : loaded.values()) {\n            if (removed.contains(a)) continue;\n            if (a.balance == snapshot.get(a.id)) continue;\n            next.put(a.id, a.balance);\n            log.add(\"UPDATE \" + a.id);\n        }\n        for (Account a : removed) {\n            next.remove(a.id);\n            log.add(\"DELETE \" + a.id);\n        }\n        db.clear();\n        db.putAll(next);\n        for (Account a : removed) {\n            loaded.remove(a.id);\n            snapshot.remove(a.id);\n        }\n        for (Account a : created) {\n            loaded.put(a.id, a);\n        }\n        loaded.values().forEach(a -> snapshot.put(a.id, a.balance));\n        created.clear();\n        removed.clear();\n        return log;\n    }\n\n    void rollback() {\n        loaded.values().forEach(a -> a.balance = snapshot.get(a.id));\n        created.clear();\n        removed.clear();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Account.java","source":"final class Account {\n    final String id;\n    int balance;\n\n    Account(String id, int balance) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.balance = balance;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"UnitOfWork.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\n// Tracks what a business transaction touched and writes it once, in order.\nfinal class UnitOfWork {\n    UnitOfWork(Map<String, Integer> db) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    Account load(String id) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void registerNew(Account account) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void registerRemoved(Account account) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    List<String> commit() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void rollback() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Load accounts, change them freely, and write everything once at commit.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`UnitOfWork(Map<String, Integer> db)` works on a `db` of balances by id. `Account` is given and must stay a plain object.","type":"p"},{"items":["`load(id)` returns one `Account` per id (an identity map), snapshotting its balance. Unknown ids throw `IllegalArgumentException`.","`registerNew(a)` and `registerRemoved(a)` record intent. Nothing touches `db` until `commit()`.","`commit()` returns the log, in this order: `INSERT id` for new accounts, `UPDATE id` for loaded ones whose balance differs from the snapshot, then `DELETE id`. A removed account is only deleted.","After `commit()` the unit of work starts clean and can be reused.","`rollback()` restores loaded balances and forgets pending new and removed accounts."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"UnitOfWorkKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass UnitOfWorkKataTest {\n    static TreeMap<String, Integer> db() {\n        return new TreeMap<>(Map.of(\"a\", 100, \"b\", 50, \"c\", 7));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"identity-map\")\n    void identityMap() {\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db());\n        Account first = work.load(\"a\");\n        Expect.isTrue(first == work.load(\"a\"), \"loading the same id twice gives the same object\");\n        Expect.equal(100, first.balance, \"loaded balance\");\n        Expect.isTrue(first != work.load(\"b\"), \"different ids are different objects\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-id\")\n    void unknownId() {\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db());\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> work.load(\"zzz\"),\n            \"loading an id that is not in the database\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"nothing-before-commit\")\n    void nothingBeforeCommit() {\n        var db = db();\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db);\n        work.load(\"a\").balance = 1;\n        work.registerNew(new Account(\"d\", 5));\n        work.registerRemoved(work.load(\"c\"));\n        Expect.equal(db(), db, \"the database before commit\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"commit-writes-changes\")\n    void commitWritesChanges() {\n        var db = db();\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db);\n        work.load(\"a\").balance -= 30;\n        work.load(\"b\");\n        work.registerNew(new Account(\"d\", 5));\n        work.registerRemoved(work.load(\"c\"));\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"INSERT d\", \"UPDATE a\", \"DELETE c\"), work.commit(), \"commit log\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"a\", 70, \"b\", 50, \"d\", 5), db, \"the database after commit\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"commit-order\")\n    void commitOrder() {\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db());\n        work.registerRemoved(work.load(\"c\"));\n        work.load(\"b\").balance = 51;\n        work.load(\"a\").balance = 99;\n        work.registerNew(new Account(\"x\", 1));\n        work.registerNew(new Account(\"y\", 2));\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"INSERT x\", \"INSERT y\", \"UPDATE b\", \"UPDATE a\", \"DELETE c\"),\n            work.commit(), \"inserts, then updates (in load order), then deletes\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"clean-objects-not-written\")\n    void cleanObjectsNotWritten() {\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db());\n        work.load(\"a\");\n        Account b = work.load(\"b\");\n        b.balance += 5;\n        b.balance -= 5;\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), work.commit(), \"loaded but unchanged objects\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"removed-dirty-only-deleted\")\n    void removedDirtyOnlyDeleted() {\n        var db = db();\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db);\n        Account c = work.load(\"c\");\n        c.balance = 0;\n        work.registerRemoved(c);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"DELETE c\"), work.commit(), \"a changed object that is also removed\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!db.containsKey(\"c\"), \"c should be gone\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"commit-resets-tracking\")\n    void commitResetsTracking() {\n        var db = db();\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db);\n        Account a = work.load(\"a\");\n        a.balance = 1;\n        work.registerNew(new Account(\"d\", 5));\n        work.commit();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), work.commit(), \"a second commit with no changes\");\n        a.balance = 2;\n        work.load(\"d\").balance = 6;\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"UPDATE a\", \"UPDATE d\"), work.commit(), \"changes after a commit\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"a\", 2, \"b\", 50, \"c\", 7, \"d\", 6), db, \"the database at the end\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rollback\")\n    void rollback() {\n        var db = db();\n        var work = new UnitOfWork(db);\n        Account a = work.load(\"a\");\n        a.balance = 1;\n        work.registerNew(new Account(\"d\", 5));\n        work.registerRemoved(work.load(\"c\"));\n        work.rollback();\n        Expect.equal(100, a.balance, \"a loaded object after rollback\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), work.commit(), \"commit after rollback\");\n        Expect.equal(db(), db, \"the database after rollback\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"account-knows-nothing-of-tracking\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void accountKnowsNothing() {\n        var account = Source.type(\"Account\");\n        Expect.none(account.mentions(\"UnitOfWork\"), \"Account refers to the unit of work\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(Types.named(\"Account\"), Types.named(\"UnitOfWork\")).isEmpty(),\n            \"Account should not hold a UnitOfWork\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Track changes in a unit of work"},{"checks":[{"id":"find-maps-columns","kind":"behaviour","title":"find turns a row into a Customer"},{"id":"find-missing-is-empty","kind":"behaviour","title":"An unknown id gives an empty Optional"},{"id":"save-writes-row","kind":"behaviour","title":"save inserts a row"},{"id":"save-updates-and-lowercases","kind":"behaviour","title":"save updates and lowercases the address"},{"id":"corrupt-row-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"A row with a bad email is rejected"},{"id":"customer-has-no-row-in-its-api","kind":"design","title":"Customer's API has no Row in it"},{"id":"customer-source-free-of-table","kind":"design","title":"Customer knows nothing of columns"},{"id":"mapper-owns-conversion","kind":"design","title":"CustomerMapper builds both sides"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Who should know that the table has an `emailAddr` column? Not the domain object. The thing between domain and table needs to be a separate class that owns that translation.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Delete `fromRow` and `toRow` from `Customer`. Give `CustomerMapper` two private methods, one per direction, and call them from `find` and `save`. The lower-casing moves with `toRow`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"In the mapper:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["private Row toRow(Customer c) {","    return new Row(c.id(), c.name(),","        c.email().value().toLowerCase());","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"data-mapper","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Email.java","Row.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Row.java","source":"// One row of the CUSTOMER table.\nrecord Row(long id, String name, String emailAddr) { }\n"},{"name":"Email.java","source":"record Email(String value) {\n    Email {\n        if (!value.contains(\"@\")) throw new IllegalArgumentException(value);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Customer.java","source":"final class Customer {\n    private final long id;\n    private final String name;\n    private Email email;\n\n    Customer(long id, String name, Email email) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.name = name;\n        this.email = email;\n    }\n\n    long id() { return id; }\n    String name() { return name; }\n    Email email() { return email; }\n    void changeEmail(Email next) { this.email = next; }\n}\n"},{"name":"CustomerMapper.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\nfinal class CustomerMapper {\n    private final Map<Long, Row> table;\n\n    CustomerMapper(Map<Long, Row> table) {\n        this.table = table;\n    }\n\n    Optional<Customer> find(long id) {\n        return Optional.ofNullable(table.get(id)).map(this::toDomain);\n    }\n\n    void save(Customer customer) {\n        table.put(customer.id(), toRow(customer));\n    }\n\n    private Customer toDomain(Row row) {\n        return new Customer(row.id(), row.name(), new Email(row.emailAddr()));\n    }\n\n    private Row toRow(Customer customer) {\n        return new Row(customer.id(), customer.name(),\n            customer.email().value().toLowerCase());\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Row.java","source":"// One row of the CUSTOMER table.\nrecord Row(long id, String name, String emailAddr) { }\n"},{"name":"Email.java","source":"record Email(String value) {\n    Email {\n        if (!value.contains(\"@\")) throw new IllegalArgumentException(value);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Customer.java","source":"// The domain object also knows the table layout. Schema changes hit it.\nfinal class Customer {\n    private final long id;\n    private final String name;\n    private Email email;\n\n    Customer(long id, String name, Email email) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.name = name;\n        this.email = email;\n    }\n\n    static Customer fromRow(Row row) {\n        return new Customer(row.id(), row.name(), new Email(row.emailAddr()));\n    }\n\n    Row toRow() {\n        return new Row(id, name, email.value().toLowerCase());\n    }\n\n    long id() { return id; }\n    String name() { return name; }\n    Email email() { return email; }\n    void changeEmail(Email next) { this.email = next; }\n}\n"},{"name":"CustomerMapper.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\nfinal class CustomerMapper {\n    private final Map<Long, Row> table;\n\n    CustomerMapper(Map<Long, Row> table) {\n        this.table = table;\n    }\n\n    Optional<Customer> find(long id) {\n        return Optional.ofNullable(table.get(id)).map(Customer::fromRow);\n    }\n\n    void save(Customer customer) {\n        table.put(customer.id(), customer.toRow());\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Customer` knows the shape of its table row. Make the mapper own that knowledge.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`Customer` has `fromRow` and `toRow`, so every schema change edits the domain class. Move the conversion into `CustomerMapper`, keeping its constructor, `find(long)` and `save(Customer)`.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Customer` must no longer mention `Row` or its columns.","`CustomerMapper` converts in both directions.","Behaviour stays: `save` stores the email lower-cased, and `find` throws `IllegalArgumentException` for a corrupt row.","`Row` and `Email` are read-only."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"DataMapperKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass DataMapperKataTest {\n    static Map<Long, Row> table() {\n        var t = new HashMap<Long, Row>();\n        t.put(1L, new Row(1, \"Ada\", \"ada@old.org\"));\n        t.put(2L, new Row(2, \"Bob\", \"broken\"));\n        return t;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"find-maps-columns\")\n    void findMapsColumns() {\n        Customer c = new CustomerMapper(table()).find(1).orElseThrow();\n        Expect.equal(1L, c.id(), \"id\");\n        Expect.equal(\"Ada\", c.name(), \"name\");\n        Expect.equal(new Email(\"ada@old.org\"), c.email(), \"email\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"find-missing-is-empty\")\n    void findMissingIsEmpty() {\n        Expect.isTrue(new CustomerMapper(table()).find(99).isEmpty(), \"find of an unknown id\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"save-writes-row\")\n    void saveWritesRow() {\n        var t = table();\n        var mapper = new CustomerMapper(t);\n        mapper.save(new Customer(3, \"Cy\", new Email(\"cy@x.org\")));\n        Expect.equal(new Row(3, \"Cy\", \"cy@x.org\"), t.get(3L), \"the inserted row\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"save-updates-and-lowercases\")\n    void saveUpdatesAndLowercases() {\n        var t = table();\n        var mapper = new CustomerMapper(t);\n        Customer ada = mapper.find(1).orElseThrow();\n        ada.changeEmail(new Email(\"Ada@New.ORG\"));\n        mapper.save(ada);\n        Expect.equal(new Row(1, \"Ada\", \"ada@new.org\"), t.get(1L), \"the stored row\");\n        Expect.equal(2, t.size(), \"rows in the table\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"corrupt-row-rejected\")\n    void corruptRowRejected() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> new CustomerMapper(table()).find(2), \"find of a row with a bad email\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"customer-has-no-row-in-its-api\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void customerHasNoRowInItsApi() {\n        Class<?> customer = Types.named(\"Customer\");\n        Class<?> row = Types.named(\"Row\");\n        for (Method m : customer.getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(m.getReturnType() != row && !java.util.List.of(m.getParameterTypes()).contains(row),\n                \"Customer.\" + m.getName() + \" still deals in Row\");\n        }\n        for (Constructor<?> c : customer.getDeclaredConstructors()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(!java.util.List.of(c.getParameterTypes()).contains(row),\n                \"A Customer constructor still takes a Row\");\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(customer, row).isEmpty(), \"Customer holds a Row\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"customer-source-free-of-table\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void customerSourceFreeOfTable() {\n        var customer = Source.type(\"Customer\");\n        Expect.none(customer.mentions(\"Row\"), \"Customer still mentions Row\");\n        Expect.none(customer.mentions(\"emailAddr\"), \"Customer still knows the emailAddr column\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"mapper-owns-conversion\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void mapperOwnsConversion() {\n        var mapper = Source.type(\"CustomerMapper\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!mapper.news(\"Row\").isEmpty(),\n            \"CustomerMapper should build the Row itself\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!mapper.news(\"Customer\").isEmpty(),\n            \"CustomerMapper should build the Customer itself\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Move the table layout out of Customer"},{"checks":[{"id":"create-validates","kind":"behaviour","title":"create checks the name and percent"},{"id":"new-is-not-stored","kind":"behaviour","title":"A new flag is stored only by save"},{"id":"find-returns-fresh-copies","kind":"behaviour","title":"find builds a fresh object, edits stay local"},{"id":"update-after-edit","kind":"behaviour","title":"Edit then save updates the same row"},{"id":"all-sorted-by-name","kind":"behaviour","title":"all lists flags sorted by name"},{"id":"delete","kind":"behaviour","title":"delete removes the row"},{"id":"duplicate-insert-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"A second new flag with the same name is rejected"},{"id":"record-persists-itself","kind":"design","title":"Finders are static, save and delete are on the record"},{"id":"table-is-hidden","kind":"design","title":"The table is a private static map"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Two jobs live in one class: the object holds fields and rules, and it also knows how to read and write its own row. Finders cannot use an instance, so they are static.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Store immutable `Row` values in `TABLE`, not the flag objects. `find` builds a new `FeatureFlag` from a row and marks it persisted. `save` writes a new `Row` from the current fields.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The save rule, with a shared `checkPercent` helper for create and rollout:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["FeatureFlag save() {","    if (!persisted && TABLE.containsKey(name)) {","        throw new IllegalStateException(\"already exists: \" + name);","    }","    TABLE.put(name, new Row(enabled, percent));","    persisted = true;","    return this;","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"active-record","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"FeatureFlag.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\n\nfinal class FeatureFlag {\n    private record Row(boolean enabled, int percent) { }\n\n    private static final Map<String, Row> TABLE = new TreeMap<>();\n\n    private final String name;\n    private boolean enabled;\n    private int percent;\n    private boolean persisted;\n\n    private FeatureFlag(String name, boolean enabled, int percent) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.enabled = enabled;\n        this.percent = percent;\n    }\n\n    /** Test hook: empties the table. */\n    static void reset() { TABLE.clear(); }\n\n    static FeatureFlag create(String name, int percent) {\n        if (name == null || name.isBlank()) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"name\");\n        }\n        checkPercent(percent);\n        return new FeatureFlag(name, false, percent);\n    }\n\n    static Optional<FeatureFlag> find(String name) {\n        Row row = TABLE.get(name);\n        if (row == null) return Optional.empty();\n        var flag = new FeatureFlag(name, row.enabled(), row.percent());\n        flag.persisted = true;\n        return Optional.of(flag);\n    }\n\n    static List<FeatureFlag> all() {\n        return TABLE.keySet().stream()\n            .map(n -> find(n).orElseThrow()).toList();\n    }\n\n    void toggle() { enabled = !enabled; }\n\n    void rollout(int percent) {\n        checkPercent(percent);\n        this.percent = percent;\n    }\n\n    FeatureFlag save() {\n        if (!persisted && TABLE.containsKey(name)) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"already exists: \" + name);\n        }\n        TABLE.put(name, new Row(enabled, percent));\n        persisted = true;\n        return this;\n    }\n\n    void delete() {\n        TABLE.remove(name);\n        persisted = false;\n    }\n\n    private static void checkPercent(int percent) {\n        if (percent < 0 || percent > 100) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"percent: \" + percent);\n        }\n    }\n\n    String name() { return name; }\n    boolean enabled() { return enabled; }\n    int percent() { return percent; }\n    boolean persisted() { return persisted; }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"FeatureFlag.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\n\n// A row that knows how to save itself. The table is static, in memory.\nfinal class FeatureFlag {\n    private record Row(boolean enabled, int percent) { }\n\n    private static final Map<String, Row> TABLE = new TreeMap<>();\n\n    private final String name;\n    private boolean enabled;\n    private int percent;\n    private boolean persisted;\n\n    private FeatureFlag(String name, boolean enabled, int percent) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.enabled = enabled;\n        this.percent = percent;\n    }\n\n    /** Test hook: empties the table. */\n    static void reset() { TABLE.clear(); }\n\n    static FeatureFlag create(String name, int percent) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    static Optional<FeatureFlag> find(String name) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    static List<FeatureFlag> all() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void toggle() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void rollout(int percent) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    FeatureFlag save() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void delete() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    String name() { return name; }\n    boolean enabled() { return enabled; }\n    int percent() { return percent; }\n    boolean persisted() { return persisted; }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"An active record is a row object that also carries its own finders and persistence.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Complete `FeatureFlag`. The skeleton, the private table and `reset()` are given; keep the table private and static.","type":"p"},{"items":["`create(name, percent)` returns an unsaved, disabled flag. Throw `IllegalArgumentException` for a blank name or a percent outside 0 to 100. `rollout(p)` applies the same rule.","`save()` inserts or updates and returns `this`. Saving a never-persisted flag whose name is taken throws `IllegalStateException`.","`find(name)` returns a fresh object each time. Unsaved edits never show in the table.","`all()` returns fresh objects sorted by name.","`delete()` removes the row and clears `persisted()`; deleting an unsaved flag does nothing.","`toggle()` flips `enabled` in memory only."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ActiveRecordKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ActiveRecordKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"create-validates\")\n    void createValidates() {\n        FeatureFlag.reset();\n        FeatureFlag f = FeatureFlag.create(\"dark-mode\", 25);\n        Expect.equal(\"dark-mode\", f.name(), \"name\");\n        Expect.equal(25, f.percent(), \"percent\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!f.enabled(), \"a new flag starts disabled\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> FeatureFlag.create(\" \", 0), \"a blank name\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> FeatureFlag.create(\"x\", 101), \"percent 101\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> FeatureFlag.create(\"x\", -1), \"percent -1\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> f.rollout(150), \"rollout(150)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"new-is-not-stored\")\n    void newIsNotStored() {\n        FeatureFlag.reset();\n        FeatureFlag f = FeatureFlag.create(\"beta\", 10);\n        Expect.isTrue(!f.persisted(), \"a new flag is not persisted\");\n        Expect.isTrue(FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").isEmpty(), \"find before save\");\n        Expect.isTrue(f.save() == f, \"save returns the same record\");\n        Expect.isTrue(f.persisted(), \"persisted after save\");\n        Expect.equal(10, FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").orElseThrow().percent(), \"stored percent\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"find-returns-fresh-copies\")\n    void findReturnsFreshCopies() {\n        FeatureFlag.reset();\n        FeatureFlag.create(\"beta\", 10).save();\n        FeatureFlag a = FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").orElseThrow();\n        FeatureFlag b = FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").orElseThrow();\n        Expect.isTrue(a != b, \"find should build a new object each time\");\n        a.toggle();\n        a.rollout(90);\n        FeatureFlag c = FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").orElseThrow();\n        Expect.isTrue(!c.enabled() && c.percent() == 10, \"unsaved edits must not reach the table\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"update-after-edit\")\n    void updateAfterEdit() {\n        FeatureFlag.reset();\n        FeatureFlag.create(\"beta\", 10).save();\n        FeatureFlag f = FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").orElseThrow();\n        Expect.isTrue(f.persisted(), \"a found flag is persisted\");\n        f.toggle();\n        f.rollout(60);\n        f.save();\n        FeatureFlag g = FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").orElseThrow();\n        Expect.isTrue(g.enabled(), \"enabled after toggle and save\");\n        Expect.equal(60, g.percent(), \"percent after rollout and save\");\n        Expect.equal(1, FeatureFlag.all().size(), \"update should not add a row\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"all-sorted-by-name\")\n    void allSortedByName() {\n        FeatureFlag.reset();\n        FeatureFlag.create(\"zeta\", 1).save();\n        FeatureFlag.create(\"alpha\", 2).save();\n        FeatureFlag.create(\"mid\", 3).save();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"alpha\", \"mid\", \"zeta\"),\n            FeatureFlag.all().stream().map(FeatureFlag::name).toList(), \"names from all()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"delete\")\n    void delete() {\n        FeatureFlag.reset();\n        FeatureFlag f = FeatureFlag.create(\"beta\", 10).save();\n        f.delete();\n        Expect.isTrue(FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").isEmpty(), \"find after delete\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!f.persisted(), \"persisted after delete\");\n        FeatureFlag.create(\"never\", 1).delete();\n        f.save();\n        Expect.isTrue(FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").isPresent(), \"a deleted flag can be saved again\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"duplicate-insert-rejected\")\n    void duplicateInsertRejected() {\n        FeatureFlag.reset();\n        FeatureFlag.create(\"beta\", 10).save();\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            () -> FeatureFlag.create(\"beta\", 20).save(), \"inserting a second flag named beta\");\n        Expect.equal(10, FeatureFlag.find(\"beta\").orElseThrow().percent(), \"the original row\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"record-persists-itself\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void recordPersistsItself() {\n        Class<?> flag = Types.named(\"FeatureFlag\");\n        Method save = Types.method(flag, \"save\");\n        Method delete = Types.method(flag, \"delete\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!Modifier.isStatic(save.getModifiers()), \"save should be an instance method\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!Modifier.isStatic(delete.getModifiers()), \"delete should be an instance method\");\n        Method find = Types.staticMethod(flag, \"find\", String.class);\n        Expect.equal(Optional.class, find.getReturnType(), \"find's return type\");\n        Types.staticMethod(flag, \"all\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"table-is-hidden\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void tableIsHidden() {\n        Class<?> flag = Types.named(\"FeatureFlag\");\n        boolean found = false;\n        for (Field f : flag.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers()) && Map.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType())) {\n                found = true;\n                Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()),\n                    \"FeatureFlag.\" + f.getName() + \" holds the table and should be private\");\n            }\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(found, \"FeatureFlag should keep its table in a static Map field\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"A feature flag that saves itself"},{"checks":[{"id":"adult-rules","kind":"behaviour","title":"Adult and income searches are unchanged"},{"id":"default-rules","kind":"behaviour","title":"Default-aware searches are unchanged"},{"id":"spec-interface","kind":"design","title":"Spec<T> has one abstract method"},{"id":"specs-combine","kind":"design","title":"Specs combine with and, or and not"},{"id":"rule-factories","kind":"design","title":"Specs builds the three rules"},{"id":"finder-takes-any-spec","kind":"design","title":"find accepts a rule it has never seen"},{"id":"finders-delegate","kind":"design","title":"The old methods delegate to find"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Each method asks the same question with a different rule. Make the rule a value you can pass around and combine, then keep a single loop.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`Spec<T>` has `isSatisfiedBy` plus default `and`, `or`, `not`. `Specs` returns small lambdas. `ApplicantFinder.find(all, spec)` filters once; the five old methods build a spec and call it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The default combinators return lambdas:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["default Spec<T> and(Spec<T> other) {","    return c -> isSatisfiedBy(c) && other.isSatisfiedBy(c);","}","// adults with income:","find(all, Specs.atLeastAge(18).and(Specs.minIncome(min)))"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"specification","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"ApplicantFinder.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\nrecord Applicant(String name, int age, int income, boolean defaulted) { }\n\n// One generic search; the old entry points are just named combinations.\nfinal class ApplicantFinder {\n    private ApplicantFinder() { }\n\n    static List<Applicant> find(List<Applicant> all, Spec<Applicant> spec) {\n        return all.stream().filter(spec::isSatisfiedBy).toList();\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> adults(List<Applicant> all) {\n        return find(all, Specs.atLeastAge(18));\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> adultsWithIncome(List<Applicant> all, int min) {\n        return find(all, Specs.atLeastAge(18).and(Specs.minIncome(min)));\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> adultsWithIncomeNotDefaulted(\n            List<Applicant> all, int min) {\n        return find(all, Specs.atLeastAge(18).and(Specs.minIncome(min))\n            .and(Specs.defaulted().not()));\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> withIncomeNotDefaulted(\n            List<Applicant> all, int min) {\n        return find(all, Specs.minIncome(min).and(Specs.defaulted().not()));\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> defaultedAdults(List<Applicant> all) {\n        return find(all, Specs.atLeastAge(18).and(Specs.defaulted()));\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Spec.java","source":"@FunctionalInterface\ninterface Spec<T> {\n    boolean isSatisfiedBy(T candidate);\n\n    default Spec<T> and(Spec<T> other) {\n        return c -> isSatisfiedBy(c) && other.isSatisfiedBy(c);\n    }\n\n    default Spec<T> or(Spec<T> other) {\n        return c -> isSatisfiedBy(c) || other.isSatisfiedBy(c);\n    }\n\n    default Spec<T> not() {\n        return c -> !isSatisfiedBy(c);\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class Specs {\n    private Specs() { }\n\n    static Spec<Applicant> atLeastAge(int years) {\n        return a -> a.age() >= years;\n    }\n\n    static Spec<Applicant> minIncome(int amount) {\n        return a -> a.income() >= amount;\n    }\n\n    static Spec<Applicant> defaulted() {\n        return Applicant::defaulted;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"ApplicantFinder.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nrecord Applicant(String name, int age, int income, boolean defaulted) { }\n\n// One method per combination of rules, each with its own copy of the loop.\nfinal class ApplicantFinder {\n    private ApplicantFinder() { }\n\n    static List<Applicant> adults(List<Applicant> all) {\n        List<Applicant> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (Applicant a : all) {\n            if (a.age() >= 18) out.add(a);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> adultsWithIncome(List<Applicant> all, int min) {\n        List<Applicant> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (Applicant a : all) {\n            if (a.age() >= 18 && a.income() >= min) out.add(a);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> adultsWithIncomeNotDefaulted(\n            List<Applicant> all, int min) {\n        List<Applicant> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (Applicant a : all) {\n            if (a.age() >= 18 && a.income() >= min && !a.defaulted()) {\n                out.add(a);\n            }\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> withIncomeNotDefaulted(\n            List<Applicant> all, int min) {\n        List<Applicant> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (Applicant a : all) {\n            if (a.income() >= min && !a.defaulted()) out.add(a);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    static List<Applicant> defaultedAdults(List<Applicant> all) {\n        List<Applicant> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (Applicant a : all) {\n            if (a.age() >= 18 && a.defaulted()) out.add(a);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`ApplicantFinder` has one method per combination of rules, each with its own copy of the loop.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Make rules values you can combine. The five existing methods keep their signatures and results, and `Applicant` does not change.","type":"p"},{"items":["`interface Spec<T>` with one abstract method `boolean isSatisfiedBy(T)` and default methods `and(Spec<T>)`, `or(Spec<T>)`, `not()`.","`Specs` with static `Spec<Applicant> atLeastAge(int)`, `minIncome(int)` and `defaulted()`. Bounds are inclusive.","`ApplicantFinder.find(List<Applicant>, Spec<Applicant>)` keeps input order.","Each old method delegates to `find`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"SpecificationKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.InvocationHandler;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Proxy;\nimport java.util.function.Function;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass SpecificationKataTest {\n    static final Applicant ANA = new Applicant(\"ana\", 34, 52_000, false);\n    static final Applicant BO = new Applicant(\"bo\", 17, 60_000, false);\n    static final Applicant CY = new Applicant(\"cy\", 45, 20_000, false);\n    static final Applicant DI = new Applicant(\"di\", 29, 80_000, true);\n    static final Applicant EVE = new Applicant(\"eve\", 18, 30_000, false);\n    static final List<Applicant> ALL = List.of(ANA, BO, CY, DI, EVE);\n\n    static List<String> names(List<Applicant> found) {\n        return found.stream().map(Applicant::name).toList();\n    }\n\n    // Types.implement cannot run default methods of a package-private interface.\n    static Object rule(Class<?> spec, Function<Object, Boolean> fn) {\n        InvocationHandler h = (proxy, m, args) -> m.isDefault()\n            ? InvocationHandler.invokeDefault(proxy, m, args) : fn.apply(args[0]);\n        return Proxy.newProxyInstance(spec.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[] {spec}, h);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"adult-rules\")\n    void adultRules() {\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ana\", \"cy\", \"di\", \"eve\"), names(ApplicantFinder.adults(ALL)), \"adults\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ana\", \"di\", \"eve\"),\n            names(ApplicantFinder.adultsWithIncome(ALL, 30_000)), \"adultsWithIncome(30000)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"default-rules\")\n    void defaultRules() {\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ana\", \"eve\"),\n            names(ApplicantFinder.adultsWithIncomeNotDefaulted(ALL, 30_000)),\n            \"adultsWithIncomeNotDefaulted(30000)\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ana\", \"bo\", \"eve\"),\n            names(ApplicantFinder.withIncomeNotDefaulted(ALL, 30_000)),\n            \"withIncomeNotDefaulted(30000)\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"di\"), names(ApplicantFinder.defaultedAdults(ALL)), \"defaultedAdults\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"spec-interface\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void specInterface() {\n        Class<?> spec = Types.named(\"Spec\");\n        Expect.isTrue(spec.isInterface(), \"Spec should be an interface\");\n        Expect.isTrue(spec.getTypeParameters().length == 1, \"Spec should be generic: Spec<T>\");\n        Method test = Types.singleAbstractMethod(spec);\n        Expect.equal(\"isSatisfiedBy\", test.getName(), \"Spec's one abstract method\");\n        Expect.equal(boolean.class, test.getReturnType(), \"isSatisfiedBy's return type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"specs-combine\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void specsCombine() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> spec = Types.named(\"Spec\");\n        Object even = rule(spec, a -> ((Integer) a) % 2 == 0);\n        Object big = rule(spec, a -> ((Integer) a) > 10);\n        Method test = Types.method(spec, \"isSatisfiedBy\", Object.class);\n        Object both = Types.call(Types.method(spec, \"and\", spec), even, big);\n        Object either = Types.call(Types.method(spec, \"or\", spec), even, big);\n        Object notEven = Types.call(Types.method(spec, \"not\"), even);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(false, true, false, true),\n            List.of(Types.call(test, both, 3), Types.call(test, both, 12),\n                    Types.call(test, both, 8), Types.call(test, either, 8)),\n            \"and / or on 3, 12, 8 and 8\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(true, false), List.of(\n            Types.call(test, notEven, 3), Types.call(test, notEven, 4)), \"not\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rule-factories\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void ruleFactories() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> spec = Types.named(\"Spec\");\n        Class<?> specs = Types.named(\"Specs\");\n        Method test = Types.method(spec, \"isSatisfiedBy\", Object.class);\n        Object age = Types.call(Types.staticMethod(specs, \"atLeastAge\", int.class), null, 18);\n        Object income = Types.call(Types.staticMethod(specs, \"minIncome\", int.class), null, 30_000);\n        Object defaulted = Types.call(Types.staticMethod(specs, \"defaulted\"), null);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(true, false), List.of(\n            Types.call(test, age, EVE), Types.call(test, age, BO)), \"atLeastAge(18) on 18 and 17\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(true, false), List.of(\n            Types.call(test, income, EVE), Types.call(test, income, CY)),\n            \"minIncome(30000) on 30000 and 20000\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(true, false), List.of(\n            Types.call(test, defaulted, DI), Types.call(test, defaulted, ANA)), \"defaulted()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"finder-takes-any-spec\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void finderTakesAnySpec() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> spec = Types.named(\"Spec\");\n        Object startsWithB = rule(spec, a -> ((Applicant) a).name().startsWith(\"b\"));\n        Method find = Types.staticMethod(ApplicantFinder.class, \"find\", List.class, spec);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"bo\"), names((List<Applicant>) Types.call(find, null, ALL, startsWithB)),\n            \"find with a rule written just now\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"finders-delegate\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void findersDelegate() {\n        var finder = Source.type(\"ApplicantFinder\");\n        for (String m : List.of(\"adults\", \"adultsWithIncome\", \"adultsWithIncomeNotDefaulted\",\n                \"withIncomeNotDefaulted\", \"defaultedAdults\")) {\n            Expect.isTrue(!finder.method(m).calls(\"find\").isEmpty(),\n                \"ApplicantFinder.\" + m + \" should delegate to find(...) with a Spec\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Replace the finder explosion with specifications"},{"checks":[{"id":"show-hides-secrets","kind":"behaviour","title":"show sends no hash, email or roles"},{"id":"show-has-the-summary","kind":"behaviour","title":"show sends exactly id, displayName and admin"},{"id":"list-hides-secrets","kind":"behaviour","title":"list sends only summaries"},{"id":"register-checks-the-email","kind":"behaviour","title":"A bad email is refused by the request"},{"id":"api-returns-dtos-not-entities","kind":"design","title":"The API returns DTOs, not User"},{"id":"dto-is-plain-and-immutable","kind":"design","title":"The DTO is immutable and holds no entity"},{"id":"mapping-stays-out-of-the-entity","kind":"design","title":"User does not build the response"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Whatever type you return is your public contract. A `User` has more fields than clients should ever see, so return a smaller type made for the wire.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Add a `UserSummary` record with only the three fields, and a mapping from `User` to it. `show` and `list` map before returning. Give `RegisterRequest` a compact constructor that checks the email.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The mapping and the request guard:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["static UserSummary of(User u) {","    return new UserSummary(","        u.id(), u.firstName() + \" \" + u.lastName(), u.isAdmin());","}","// RegisterRequest { if (email == null || !email.contains(\"@\")) throw ...; }"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"dto","kind":"fix","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Json.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Json.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.LinkedHashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\n// Given. Stands in for the JSON library: it serializes every field.\nfinal class Json {\n    private Json() { }\n\n    static Map<String, Object> fields(Object body) {\n        Map<String, Object> out = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n        try {\n            for (Field f : body.getClass().getDeclaredFields()) {\n                if (Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers())) continue;\n                f.setAccessible(true);\n                out.put(f.getName(), f.get(body));\n            }\n        } catch (IllegalAccessException e) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(e);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"UserApi.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nfinal class User {\n    private final long id;\n    private final String firstName;\n    private final String lastName;\n    private final String email;\n    private final String passwordHash;\n    private final List<String> roles;\n\n    User(long id, String firstName, String lastName, String email,\n         String passwordHash, List<String> roles) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.firstName = firstName;\n        this.lastName = lastName;\n        this.email = email;\n        this.passwordHash = passwordHash;\n        this.roles = roles;\n    }\n\n    long id() { return id; }\n    String firstName() { return firstName; }\n    String lastName() { return lastName; }\n    String email() { return email; }\n    boolean isAdmin() { return roles.contains(\"ADMIN\"); }\n}\n\n// What the API says about a user, and nothing more.\nrecord UserSummary(long id, String displayName, boolean admin) {\n    static UserSummary of(User u) {\n        return new UserSummary(\n            u.id(), u.firstName() + \" \" + u.lastName(), u.isAdmin());\n    }\n}\n\n// Sent by clients to register. Validated on construction.\nrecord RegisterRequest(String firstName, String lastName, String email) {\n    RegisterRequest {\n        if (email == null || !email.contains(\"@\")) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"email\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// The public API. What it returns is what goes over the wire.\nfinal class UserApi {\n    private final List<User> users = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\n        new User(7, \"Ada\", \"Lovelace\", \"ada@x.org\", \"bcrypt:9f2c\",\n            List.of(\"ADMIN\", \"USER\")),\n        new User(8, \"Bo\", \"Ng\", \"bo@x.org\", \"bcrypt:41aa\", List.of(\"USER\"))));\n\n    UserSummary show(long id) {\n        return users.stream().filter(u -> u.id() == id).findFirst()\n            .map(UserSummary::of)\n            .orElseThrow(() -> new IllegalArgumentException(\"no user \" + id));\n    }\n\n    List<UserSummary> list() {\n        return users.stream().map(UserSummary::of).toList();\n    }\n\n    long register(RegisterRequest request) {\n        long id = 9 + users.size() - 2;\n        users.add(new User(id, request.firstName(), request.lastName(),\n            request.email(), \"bcrypt:new\", List.of(\"USER\")));\n        return id;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Json.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.LinkedHashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\n// Given. Stands in for the JSON library: it serializes every field.\nfinal class Json {\n    private Json() { }\n\n    static Map<String, Object> fields(Object body) {\n        Map<String, Object> out = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n        try {\n            for (Field f : body.getClass().getDeclaredFields()) {\n                if (Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers())) continue;\n                f.setAccessible(true);\n                out.put(f.getName(), f.get(body));\n            }\n        } catch (IllegalAccessException e) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(e);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"UserApi.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nfinal class User {\n    private final long id;\n    private final String firstName;\n    private final String lastName;\n    private final String email;\n    private final String passwordHash;\n    private final List<String> roles;\n\n    User(long id, String firstName, String lastName, String email,\n         String passwordHash, List<String> roles) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.firstName = firstName;\n        this.lastName = lastName;\n        this.email = email;\n        this.passwordHash = passwordHash;\n        this.roles = roles;\n    }\n\n    long id() { return id; }\n    String firstName() { return firstName; }\n    String lastName() { return lastName; }\n    String email() { return email; }\n    boolean isAdmin() { return roles.contains(\"ADMIN\"); }\n}\n\n// Sent by clients to register.\nrecord RegisterRequest(String firstName, String lastName, String email) { }\n\n// The public API. What it returns is what goes over the wire.\nfinal class UserApi {\n    private final List<User> users = new ArrayList<>(List.of(\n        new User(7, \"Ada\", \"Lovelace\", \"ada@x.org\", \"bcrypt:9f2c\",\n            List.of(\"ADMIN\", \"USER\")),\n        new User(8, \"Bo\", \"Ng\", \"bo@x.org\", \"bcrypt:41aa\", List.of(\"USER\"))));\n\n    User show(long id) {\n        return users.stream().filter(u -> u.id() == id).findFirst()\n            .orElseThrow(() -> new IllegalArgumentException(\"no user \" + id));\n    }\n\n    List<User> list() {\n        return List.copyOf(users);\n    }\n\n    long register(RegisterRequest request) {\n        long id = 9 + users.size() - 2;\n        users.add(new User(id, request.firstName(), request.lastName(),\n            request.email(), \"bcrypt:new\", List.of(\"USER\")));\n        return id;\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`UserApi.show` and `list` return `User` entities, and `Json.fields` serializes every field, so each response carries the `passwordHash`.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Fix it with a response DTO. `User`, `Json` and `register`'s return value must not change.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `record UserSummary(long id, String displayName, boolean admin)`; `displayName` is `firstName lastName`.","`show(long)` returns a `UserSummary` and `list()` a `List<UserSummary>`; unknown ids still throw `IllegalArgumentException`.","`RegisterRequest` validates itself: a null email or one without `@` throws `IllegalArgumentException` from its constructor.","The entity must not know how it is presented."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"DtoKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.lang.reflect.ParameterizedType;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass DtoKataTest {\n    static Map<String, Object> wire(Object body) {\n        return Json.fields(body);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"show-hides-secrets\")\n    void showHidesSecrets() {\n        var body = wire(new UserApi().show(7));\n        Expect.isTrue(!body.containsKey(\"passwordHash\"), \"show(7) sends the password hash\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!body.containsKey(\"email\") && !body.containsKey(\"roles\"),\n            \"show(7) sends private details: \" + body.keySet());\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"show-has-the-summary\")\n    void showHasTheSummary() {\n        var body = wire(new UserApi().show(7));\n        Expect.equal(Set.of(\"id\", \"displayName\", \"admin\"), body.keySet(), \"fields on the wire\");\n        Expect.equal(\"Ada Lovelace\", body.get(\"displayName\"), \"displayName\");\n        Expect.equal(true, body.get(\"admin\"), \"admin flag of Ada\");\n        Expect.equal(false, wire(new UserApi().show(8)).get(\"admin\"), \"admin flag of Bo\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"list-hides-secrets\")\n    void listHidesSecrets() {\n        for (Object item : new UserApi().list()) {\n            Expect.equal(Set.of(\"id\", \"displayName\", \"admin\"), wire(item).keySet(),\n                \"fields on the wire for list()\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"register-checks-the-email\")\n    void registerChecksTheEmail() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> new RegisterRequest(\"Bo\", \"Ng\", \"nope\"), \"an email without @\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class,\n            () -> new RegisterRequest(\"Bo\", \"Ng\", null), \"a null email\");\n        var api = new UserApi();\n        long id = api.register(new RegisterRequest(\"Cy\", \"Dee\", \"cy@x.org\"));\n        var body = wire(api.show(id));\n        Expect.equal(\"Cy Dee\", body.get(\"displayName\"), \"the registered user\");\n        Expect.equal(false, body.get(\"admin\"), \"a new user is not an admin\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"api-returns-dtos-not-entities\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void apiReturnsDtosNotEntities() throws Exception {\n        Method show = Types.method(Types.named(\"UserApi\"), \"show\", long.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(show.getReturnType() != User.class && show.getReturnType() != Object.class,\n            \"show should return a response type of its own, not the User entity\");\n        Method list = Types.method(Types.named(\"UserApi\"), \"list\");\n        Expect.isTrue(list.getGenericReturnType() instanceof ParameterizedType p\n                && p.getActualTypeArguments()[0] instanceof Class<?> c && c != User.class,\n            \"list should return a List of response objects, not of User\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"dto-is-plain-and-immutable\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void dtoIsPlainAndImmutable() {\n        Class<?> dto = Types.method(Types.named(\"UserApi\"), \"show\", long.class).getReturnType();\n        Expect.isTrue(dto != User.class, dto.getSimpleName() + \" is the entity itself\");\n        for (Field f : dto.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            if (Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers())) continue;\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n                dto.getSimpleName() + \".\" + f.getName() + \" should be final\");\n            Expect.isTrue(f.getType() != User.class && !List.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType()),\n                dto.getSimpleName() + \".\" + f.getName() + \" carries entity data or a mutable list\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"mapping-stays-out-of-the-entity\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void mappingStaysOutOfTheEntity() {\n        var user = Source.type(\"User\");\n        Expect.none(user.mentions(\"RegisterRequest\"), \"User depends on the request type\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.named(\"User\").getDeclaredMethods().length > 0\n                && java.util.Arrays.stream(Types.named(\"User\").getDeclaredMethods())\n                    .noneMatch(m -> m.getReturnType() == Types.method(\n                        Types.named(\"UserApi\"), \"show\", long.class).getReturnType()),\n            \"User should not build the response itself; map it in the DTO or a mapper\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Stop the user API leaking password hashes"},{"checks":[{"id":"discharge-reaches-everyone","kind":"behaviour","title":"Discharge still reaches billing, housekeeping and pharmacy"},{"id":"double-discharge-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"A second discharge is rejected with no side effects"},{"id":"unknown-patient","kind":"behaviour","title":"An unknown patient is rejected"},{"id":"patients-are-independent","kind":"behaviour","title":"Discharging one patient leaves others alone"},{"id":"event-names-what-happened","kind":"design","title":"PatientDischarged is a record with the facts"},{"id":"patient-records-the-event","kind":"design","title":"Patient records the event and nothing else"},{"id":"patient-knows-no-department","kind":"design","title":"Patient knows no department"},{"id":"bus-routes-by-type","kind":"design","title":"EventBus delivers events by type"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Separate what happened from who cares. The patient can state the fact (\"discharged\") without knowing a single department. Someone else delivers that fact to whoever listens.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`Patient` appends a `PatientDischarged` to a list and hands it out in `pullEvents()`. `EventBus` keeps handlers per event class. `Ward` registers one handler per department in its constructor and publishes after `patient.discharge()`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The registration in `Ward`:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["bus.on(PatientDischarged.class,","    e -> billing.invoice(e.patientId()));","bus.on(PatientDischarged.class,","    e -> housekeeping.cleanBed(e.bedId()));","bus.on(PatientDischarged.class,","    e -> pharmacy.handOff(e.patientId()));"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"domain-event","kind":"refactor","minutes":25,"readOnly":["Ports.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Ports.java","source":"// What the other departments offer. Read-only.\ninterface Billing { void invoice(String patientId); }\n\ninterface Housekeeping { void cleanBed(String bedId); }\n\ninterface Pharmacy { void handOff(String patientId); }\n"},{"name":"Events.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.function.Consumer;\n\nrecord PatientDischarged(String patientId, String bedId) { }\n\nfinal class EventBus {\n    private final Map<Class<?>, List<Consumer<Object>>> handlers =\n        new HashMap<>();\n\n    <E> void on(Class<E> type, Consumer<E> handler) {\n        handlers.computeIfAbsent(type, t -> new ArrayList<>())\n            .add(e -> handler.accept(type.cast(e)));\n    }\n\n    void publish(List<?> events) {\n        for (Object e : events) {\n            handlers.getOrDefault(e.getClass(), List.of())\n                .forEach(h -> h.accept(e));\n        }\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Patient.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nfinal class Patient {\n    private final String id;\n    private final String bedId;\n    private final List<PatientDischarged> events = new ArrayList<>();\n    private boolean discharged;\n\n    Patient(String id, String bedId) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.bedId = bedId;\n    }\n\n    void discharge() {\n        if (discharged) throw new IllegalStateException(\"already discharged\");\n        discharged = true;\n        events.add(new PatientDischarged(id, bedId));\n    }\n\n    List<PatientDischarged> pullEvents() {\n        var out = List.copyOf(events);\n        events.clear();\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    boolean isDischarged() { return discharged; }\n}\n"},{"name":"Ward.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nfinal class Ward {\n    private final Map<String, Patient> patients = new HashMap<>();\n    private final EventBus bus = new EventBus();\n\n    Ward(Billing billing, Housekeeping housekeeping, Pharmacy pharmacy) {\n        bus.on(PatientDischarged.class, e -> billing.invoice(e.patientId()));\n        bus.on(PatientDischarged.class, e -> housekeeping.cleanBed(e.bedId()));\n        bus.on(PatientDischarged.class, e -> pharmacy.handOff(e.patientId()));\n    }\n\n    Patient admit(String id, String bedId) {\n        var patient = new Patient(id, bedId);\n        patients.put(id, patient);\n        return patient;\n    }\n\n    void discharge(String id) {\n        Patient patient = patients.get(id);\n        if (patient == null) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown patient: \" + id);\n        }\n        patient.discharge();\n        bus.publish(patient.pullEvents());\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Ports.java","source":"// What the other departments offer. Read-only.\ninterface Billing { void invoice(String patientId); }\n\ninterface Housekeeping { void cleanBed(String bedId); }\n\ninterface Pharmacy { void handOff(String patientId); }\n"},{"name":"Patient.java","source":"// The aggregate calls every department itself.\nfinal class Patient {\n    private final String id;\n    private final String bedId;\n    private final Billing billing;\n    private final Housekeeping housekeeping;\n    private final Pharmacy pharmacy;\n    private boolean discharged;\n\n    Patient(String id, String bedId, Billing billing,\n            Housekeeping housekeeping, Pharmacy pharmacy) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.bedId = bedId;\n        this.billing = billing;\n        this.housekeeping = housekeeping;\n        this.pharmacy = pharmacy;\n    }\n\n    void discharge() {\n        if (discharged) throw new IllegalStateException(\"already discharged\");\n        discharged = true;\n        billing.invoice(id);\n        housekeeping.cleanBed(bedId);\n        pharmacy.handOff(id);\n    }\n\n    boolean isDischarged() { return discharged; }\n}\n"},{"name":"Ward.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nfinal class Ward {\n    private final Map<String, Patient> patients = new HashMap<>();\n    private final Billing billing;\n    private final Housekeeping housekeeping;\n    private final Pharmacy pharmacy;\n\n    Ward(Billing billing, Housekeeping housekeeping, Pharmacy pharmacy) {\n        this.billing = billing;\n        this.housekeeping = housekeeping;\n        this.pharmacy = pharmacy;\n    }\n\n    Patient admit(String id, String bedId) {\n        var patient = new Patient(id, bedId, billing, housekeeping, pharmacy);\n        patients.put(id, patient);\n        return patient;\n    }\n\n    void discharge(String id) {\n        Patient patient = patients.get(id);\n        if (patient == null) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown patient: \" + id);\n        }\n        patient.discharge();\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Patient.discharge()` calls billing, housekeeping and the pharmacy itself.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Make the patient record a fact and let the departments react. `Ward(Billing, Housekeeping, Pharmacy)`, `admit(id, bed)` and `discharge(id)` keep working exactly as before.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `record PatientDischarged(String patientId, String bedId)`.","`Patient(String id, String bedId)` keeps `discharge()` and `isDischarged()` and gains `pullEvents()`, which returns the recorded events once and then clears them.","Add `EventBus` with `<E> void on(Class<E>, Consumer<E>)` and `void publish(List<?>)`, routing by the event's class.","`Ward` subscribes the three departments in the order billing, housekeeping, pharmacy, and publishes what the patient recorded.","`Ports.java` is read-only."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"DomainEventKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.function.Consumer;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass DomainEventKataTest {\n    final List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    Ward ward() {\n        return new Ward(\n            id -> log.add(\"bill \" + id),\n            bed -> log.add(\"clean \" + bed),\n            id -> log.add(\"pharmacy \" + id));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"discharge-reaches-everyone\")\n    void dischargeReachesEveryone() {\n        Ward ward = ward();\n        ward.admit(\"p-1\", \"bed-7\");\n        ward.discharge(\"p-1\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"bill p-1\", \"clean bed-7\", \"pharmacy p-1\"), log,\n            \"reactions to a discharge, in order\");\n        Expect.isTrue(ward.admit(\"p-2\", \"bed-8\") != null, \"admit still returns the patient\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"double-discharge-rejected\")\n    void doubleDischargeRejected() {\n        Ward ward = ward();\n        ward.admit(\"p-1\", \"bed-7\");\n        ward.discharge(\"p-1\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> ward.discharge(\"p-1\"),\n            \"discharging the same patient twice\");\n        Expect.equal(3, log.size(), \"reactions after a rejected second discharge\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-patient\")\n    void unknownPatient() {\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> ward().discharge(\"ghost\"),\n            \"discharging an unknown patient\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), log, \"reactions to an unknown patient\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"patients-are-independent\")\n    void patientsAreIndependent() {\n        Ward ward = ward();\n        Patient a = ward.admit(\"p-1\", \"bed-1\");\n        Patient b = ward.admit(\"p-2\", \"bed-2\");\n        ward.discharge(\"p-2\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"bill p-2\", \"clean bed-2\", \"pharmacy p-2\"), log, \"reactions\");\n        Expect.isTrue(b.isDischarged() && !a.isDischarged(), \"only p-2 is discharged\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"event-names-what-happened\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void eventNamesWhatHappened() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> event = Types.named(\"PatientDischarged\");\n        Expect.isTrue(event.isRecord(), \"PatientDischarged should be a record\");\n        Object e = Types.create(Types.constructor(event, String.class, String.class), \"p-1\", \"bed-7\");\n        Expect.equal(\"p-1\", Types.call(Types.method(event, \"patientId\"), e), \"patientId()\");\n        Expect.equal(\"bed-7\", Types.call(Types.method(event, \"bedId\"), e), \"bedId()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"patient-records-the-event\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void patientRecordsTheEvent() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> event = Types.named(\"PatientDischarged\");\n        Patient patient = ward().admit(\"p-1\", \"bed-7\");\n        Method pull = Types.method(Patient.class, \"pullEvents\");\n        Expect.equal(0, ((List<?>) Types.call(pull, patient)).size(), \"events before discharge\");\n        patient.discharge();\n        List<?> events = (List<?>) Types.call(pull, patient);\n        Expect.equal(1, events.size(), \"events after discharge\");\n        Expect.isTrue(event.isInstance(events.get(0)), \"the event should be a PatientDischarged\");\n        Expect.equal(0, ((List<?>) Types.call(pull, patient)).size(), \"events after pulling them\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), log, \"Patient.discharge should not call a department\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"patient-knows-no-department\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void patientKnowsNoDepartment() {\n        Class<?> patient = Types.named(\"Patient\");\n        for (String port : List.of(\"Billing\", \"Housekeeping\", \"Pharmacy\")) {\n            Class<?> p = Types.named(port);\n            Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(patient, p).isEmpty(), \"Patient still holds a \" + port);\n            for (Constructor<?> c : patient.getDeclaredConstructors()) {\n                Expect.isTrue(!List.of(c.getParameterTypes()).contains(p),\n                    \"A Patient constructor still takes a \" + port);\n            }\n            Expect.none(Source.type(\"Patient\").mentions(port), \"Patient still mentions \" + port);\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bus-routes-by-type\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void busRoutesByType() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> bus = Types.named(\"EventBus\");\n        Class<?> event = Types.named(\"PatientDischarged\");\n        Object b = Types.create(Types.constructor(bus));\n        List<Object> seen = new ArrayList<>();\n        Consumer<Object> handler = seen::add;\n        Types.call(Types.method(bus, \"on\", Class.class, Consumer.class), b, event, handler);\n        Object e = Types.create(Types.constructor(event, String.class, String.class), \"p\", \"b\");\n        Types.call(Types.method(bus, \"publish\", List.class), b, List.of(\"noise\", e));\n        Expect.equal(List.of(e), seen, \"events delivered to a handler for PatientDischarged\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Let a discharge announce itself"},{"checks":[{"id":"revenue-per-customer","kind":"behaviour","title":"Revenue adds up per customer"},{"id":"top-ranking","kind":"behaviour","title":"top ranks by revenue, ties by name"},{"id":"duplicate-order-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"A duplicate order id is rejected"},{"id":"bad-amount-rejected","kind":"behaviour","title":"A non-positive amount is rejected"},{"id":"write-side-exists","kind":"design","title":"OrderCommands handles commands and publishes a feed"},{"id":"write-side-answers-no-queries","kind":"design","title":"The write side answers no queries"},{"id":"view-needs-only-events","kind":"design","title":"RevenueView is built from the feed alone"},{"id":"view-does-not-reach-the-write-side","kind":"design","title":"RevenueView never touches OrderCommands"},{"id":"shop-only-wires","kind":"design","title":"Shop keeps no data of its own"}],"hints":[[{"text":"There are two different jobs: deciding whether an order is allowed, and answering questions about totals. They want different shapes of data, so give each its own model.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`OrderCommands` keeps what it needs to reject duplicates plus the feed of `OrderPlaced` facts. `RevenueView` keeps `Map<String, Integer>` totals and a count of events already applied. `Shop` calls `handle`, then `catchUp(commands.feed())`.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The projection only moves forward through the feed:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["void catchUp(List<OrderPlaced> feed) {","    for (; applied < feed.size(); applied++) {","        var e = feed.get(applied);","        byCustomer.merge(e.customer(), e.cents(), Integer::sum);","    }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"cqrs","kind":"refactor","minutes":25,"readOnly":["Messages.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Messages.java","source":"// The command and the fact it produces. Read-only.\nrecord PlaceOrder(String orderId, String customer, int cents) { }\n\nrecord OrderPlaced(String orderId, String customer, int cents) { }\n"},{"name":"OrderCommands.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\n// Write side: validates, keeps current state, announces facts.\nfinal class OrderCommands {\n    private final Set<String> placed = new HashSet<>();\n    private final List<OrderPlaced> feed = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    void handle(PlaceOrder cmd) {\n        if (cmd.cents() <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"amount\");\n        if (!placed.add(cmd.orderId())) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"duplicate \" + cmd.orderId());\n        }\n        feed.add(new OrderPlaced(cmd.orderId(), cmd.customer(), cmd.cents()));\n    }\n\n    List<OrderPlaced> feed() { return List.copyOf(feed); }\n}\n"},{"name":"RevenueView.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\n// Read side: a projection built only from the feed.\nfinal class RevenueView {\n    private final Map<String, Integer> byCustomer = new HashMap<>();\n    private int applied;\n\n    void catchUp(List<OrderPlaced> feed) {\n        for (; applied < feed.size(); applied++) {\n            var e = feed.get(applied);\n            byCustomer.merge(e.customer(), e.cents(), Integer::sum);\n        }\n    }\n\n    int revenue(String customer) {\n        return byCustomer.getOrDefault(customer, 0);\n    }\n\n    List<String> top(int n) {\n        return byCustomer.entrySet().stream()\n            .sorted(Map.Entry.<String, Integer>comparingByValue().reversed()\n                .thenComparing(Map.Entry.comparingByKey()))\n            .limit(n).map(e -> e.getKey() + \"=\" + e.getValue()).toList();\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Shop.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\nfinal class Shop {\n    private final OrderCommands commands = new OrderCommands();\n    private final RevenueView view = new RevenueView();\n\n    void place(String orderId, String customer, int cents) {\n        commands.handle(new PlaceOrder(orderId, customer, cents));\n        view.catchUp(commands.feed());\n    }\n\n    int revenue(String customer) { return view.revenue(customer); }\n\n    List<String> top(int n) { return view.top(n); }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Messages.java","source":"// The command and the fact it produces. Read-only.\nrecord PlaceOrder(String orderId, String customer, int cents) { }\n\nrecord OrderPlaced(String orderId, String customer, int cents) { }\n"},{"name":"Shop.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\n// Writes and reads share one model: every query rescans the orders.\nfinal class Shop {\n    private record Order(String customer, int cents) { }\n\n    private final Map<String, Order> orders = new HashMap<>();\n\n    void place(String orderId, String customer, int cents) {\n        if (cents <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"amount\");\n        if (orders.containsKey(orderId)) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"duplicate \" + orderId);\n        }\n        orders.put(orderId, new Order(customer, cents));\n    }\n\n    int revenue(String customer) {\n        return orders.values().stream()\n            .filter(o -> o.customer().equals(customer))\n            .mapToInt(Order::cents).sum();\n    }\n\n    java.util.List<String> top(int n) {\n        var totals = new HashMap<String, Integer>();\n        orders.values().forEach(o ->\n            totals.merge(o.customer(), o.cents(), Integer::sum));\n        return totals.entrySet().stream()\n            .sorted(Map.Entry.<String, Integer>comparingByValue().reversed()\n                .thenComparing(Map.Entry.comparingByKey()))\n            .limit(n).map(e -> e.getKey() + \"=\" + e.getValue()).toList();\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Shop` accepts orders and answers revenue questions from the same data.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Split it in two and keep `Shop.place`, `revenue` and `top` behaving exactly as now (`top` ranks by revenue, ties by name).","type":"p"},{"items":["`OrderCommands` is the write side: `void handle(PlaceOrder)` validates (`IllegalArgumentException(\"amount\")`, `IllegalStateException(\"duplicate <id>\")`) and appends an `OrderPlaced` to `List<OrderPlaced> feed()`. It answers no queries.","`RevenueView` is the read side: `void catchUp(List<OrderPlaced> feed)` applies only events it has not seen, then `int revenue(String)` and `List<String> top(int)` answer from its own totals.","`Shop` only wires the two. `Messages.java` is read-only."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"CqrsKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass CqrsKataTest {\n    static Shop shop() {\n        Shop s = new Shop();\n        s.place(\"o1\", \"ada\", 1500);\n        s.place(\"o2\", \"bob\", 700);\n        s.place(\"o3\", \"ada\", 1000);\n        return s;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"revenue-per-customer\")\n    void revenuePerCustomer() {\n        Shop s = shop();\n        Expect.equal(2500, s.revenue(\"ada\"), \"ada's revenue\");\n        Expect.equal(700, s.revenue(\"bob\"), \"bob's revenue\");\n        Expect.equal(0, s.revenue(\"nobody\"), \"an unknown customer's revenue\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"top-ranking\")\n    void topRanking() {\n        Shop s = shop();\n        s.place(\"o4\", \"cy\", 700);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ada=2500\", \"bob=700\"), s.top(2), \"top 2, ties by name\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"ada=2500\", \"bob=700\", \"cy=700\"), s.top(10), \"top 10\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"duplicate-order-rejected\")\n    void duplicateOrderRejected() {\n        Shop s = shop();\n        var e = Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n            () -> s.place(\"o1\", \"eve\", 100), \"placing order o1 twice\");\n        Expect.isTrue(String.valueOf(e.getMessage()).contains(\"o1\"), \"the message should name o1\");\n        Expect.equal(0, s.revenue(\"eve\"), \"revenue of the rejected order\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bad-amount-rejected\")\n    void badAmountRejected() {\n        Shop s = shop();\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> s.place(\"o9\", \"eve\", 0), \"amount 0\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> s.place(\"o9\", \"eve\", -5), \"amount -5\");\n        s.place(\"o9\", \"eve\", 100);\n        Expect.equal(100, s.revenue(\"eve\"), \"o9 can be placed once it is valid\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"write-side-exists\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void writeSideExists() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> commands = Types.named(\"OrderCommands\");\n        Object c = Types.create(Types.constructor(commands));\n        Types.call(Types.method(commands, \"handle\", PlaceOrder.class), c, new PlaceOrder(\"a\", \"ada\", 5));\n        List<?> feed = (List<?>) Types.call(Types.method(commands, \"feed\"), c);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new OrderPlaced(\"a\", \"ada\", 5)), feed, \"the feed after one command\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"write-side-answers-no-queries\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void writeSideAnswersNoQueries() {\n        Class<?> commands = Types.named(\"OrderCommands\");\n        for (Method m : commands.getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            if (Modifier.isPrivate(m.getModifiers()) || m.isSynthetic()) continue;\n            boolean feed = m.getName().equals(\"feed\");\n            Expect.isTrue(feed || m.getReturnType() == void.class,\n                \"OrderCommands.\" + m.getName() + \" returns data; queries belong on the read side\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"view-needs-only-events\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void viewNeedsOnlyEvents() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> view = Types.named(\"RevenueView\");\n        Object v = Types.create(Types.constructor(view));\n        Method catchUp = Types.method(view, \"catchUp\", List.class);\n        var feed = new ArrayList<OrderPlaced>();\n        feed.add(new OrderPlaced(\"a\", \"ada\", 5));\n        Types.call(catchUp, v, feed);\n        Types.call(catchUp, v, feed);\n        feed.add(new OrderPlaced(\"b\", \"ada\", 7));\n        Types.call(catchUp, v, feed);\n        Expect.equal(12, Types.call(Types.method(view, \"revenue\", String.class), v, \"ada\"),\n            \"revenue after catching up three times over a growing feed\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"view-does-not-reach-the-write-side\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void viewDoesNotReachTheWriteSide() {\n        var view = Source.type(\"RevenueView\");\n        Expect.none(view.mentions(\"OrderCommands\"), \"RevenueView reaches into OrderCommands\");\n        Expect.none(view.mentions(\"PlaceOrder\"), \"RevenueView depends on commands\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(Types.named(\"RevenueView\"), Types.named(\"OrderCommands\")).isEmpty(),\n            \"RevenueView holds the write side\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shop-only-wires\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void shopOnlyWires() {\n        Class<?> shop = Types.named(\"Shop\");\n        for (var f : shop.getDeclaredFields()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(!java.util.Map.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType())\n                    && !java.util.Collection.class.isAssignableFrom(f.getType()),\n                \"Shop.\" + f.getName() + \" keeps data itself; it should only wire the two sides\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Split Shop into commands and a read view"},{"checks":[{"id":"replay-rebuilds-state","kind":"behaviour","title":"Replaying events rebuilds the state"},{"id":"replay-any-prefix","kind":"behaviour","title":"Any prefix of history is a past state"},{"id":"commands-record-events","kind":"behaviour","title":"Commands record events and apply them"},{"id":"rules-reject-without-events","kind":"behaviour","title":"Rejected commands leave no event"},{"id":"save-appends-pending","kind":"behaviour","title":"saveTo appends pending events once"},{"id":"stale-save-conflicts","kind":"behaviour","title":"A stale save is a VersionConflict"},{"id":"history-is-protected","kind":"behaviour","title":"Stored history cannot be edited from outside"},{"id":"events-are-immutable-records","kind":"design","title":"Events are records"},{"id":"store-keeps-events-not-state","kind":"design","title":"The store holds events, not state"},{"id":"rebuild-is-a-static-replay","kind":"design","title":"State is rebuilt by StockItem.replay"}],"hints":[[{"text":"State is never assigned directly. It is a fold over the events, and the same fold runs when you replay history and when a new command succeeds.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Write one private method that applies a single event to `onHand` and bumps `version`. `replay` calls it for each historical event. A command validates, builds the event, then calls a `record` helper that applies it and adds it to a pending list.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The save uses optimistic concurrency:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["void saveTo(EventStore store, String streamId) {","    store.append(streamId, version - pending.size(), pending);","    pending.clear();","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"event-sourcing","kind":"implement","minutes":30,"readOnly":["Events.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Events.java","source":"// The facts of a stock ledger. Read-only.\nsealed interface StockEvent permits Received, Picked, Adjusted { }\n\nrecord Received(int units) implements StockEvent { }\n\nrecord Picked(int units) implements StockEvent { }\n\nrecord Adjusted(int delta) implements StockEvent { }\n\nfinal class VersionConflict extends RuntimeException {\n    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;\n\n    VersionConflict(String message) { super(message); }\n}\n"},{"name":"EventStore.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\n\nfinal class EventStore {\n    private final Map<String, List<StockEvent>> streams = new HashMap<>();\n\n    List<StockEvent> load(String streamId) {\n        return List.copyOf(streams.getOrDefault(streamId, List.of()));\n    }\n\n    void append(String streamId, int expectedVersion, List<StockEvent> events) {\n        var stream = streams.computeIfAbsent(streamId, k -> new ArrayList<>());\n        if (stream.size() != expectedVersion) {\n            throw new VersionConflict(\"expected v\" + expectedVersion\n                + \" but found v\" + stream.size());\n        }\n        stream.addAll(events);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"StockItem.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nfinal class StockItem {\n    private final List<StockEvent> pending = new ArrayList<>();\n    private int onHand;\n    private int version;\n\n    static StockItem replay(List<StockEvent> history) {\n        var item = new StockItem();\n        history.forEach(item::apply);\n        return item;\n    }\n\n    private void apply(StockEvent event) {\n        switch (event) {\n            case Received r -> onHand += r.units();\n            case Picked p -> onHand -= p.units();\n            case Adjusted a -> onHand += a.delta();\n        }\n        version++;\n    }\n\n    private void record(StockEvent event) {\n        apply(event);\n        pending.add(event);\n    }\n\n    void receive(int units) {\n        if (units <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"units\");\n        record(new Received(units));\n    }\n\n    void pick(int units) {\n        if (units <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"units\");\n        if (units > onHand) {\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"insufficient stock\");\n        }\n        record(new Picked(units));\n    }\n\n    void adjust(int delta) {\n        if (onHand + delta < 0) throw new IllegalStateException(\"below zero\");\n        record(new Adjusted(delta));\n    }\n\n    List<StockEvent> pendingEvents() { return List.copyOf(pending); }\n\n    void saveTo(EventStore store, String streamId) {\n        store.append(streamId, version - pending.size(), pending);\n        pending.clear();\n    }\n\n    int onHand() { return onHand; }\n    int version() { return version; }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Events.java","source":"// The facts of a stock ledger. Read-only.\nsealed interface StockEvent permits Received, Picked, Adjusted { }\n\nrecord Received(int units) implements StockEvent { }\n\nrecord Picked(int units) implements StockEvent { }\n\nrecord Adjusted(int delta) implements StockEvent { }\n\nfinal class VersionConflict extends RuntimeException {\n    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;\n\n    VersionConflict(String message) { super(message); }\n}\n"},{"name":"EventStore.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\nfinal class EventStore {\n    /** Every event of a stream, oldest first. Unknown streams are empty. */\n    List<StockEvent> load(String streamId) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Appends only if the stream has exactly expectedVersion events. */\n    void append(String streamId, int expectedVersion, List<StockEvent> events) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"StockItem.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\n// One SKU. Its state is whatever the events add up to.\nfinal class StockItem {\n    private int onHand;\n    private int version;\n\n    static StockItem replay(List<StockEvent> history) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void receive(int units) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void pick(int units) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void adjust(int delta) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    List<StockEvent> pendingEvents() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void saveTo(EventStore store, String streamId) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    int onHand() { return onHand; }\n    int version() { return version; }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A warehouse ledger keeps what happened, and derives how many units are on the shelf.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`StockEvent`s and `VersionConflict` are given. Implement `EventStore` and `StockItem`.","type":"p"},{"items":["`EventStore.load(id)` returns an unmodifiable copy of the stream (empty if unknown). `append(id, expectedVersion, events)` copies the events in only if the stream has exactly `expectedVersion` events, else throws `VersionConflict`.","`StockItem.replay(history)` applies each event: `Received` adds, `Picked` subtracts, `Adjusted` adds its `delta`. `version()` is the number of events applied.","`receive`, `pick` and `adjust` check the rules, then record an event and apply it. `units` must be positive (`IllegalArgumentException`); picking more than on hand, or adjusting below zero, is an `IllegalStateException` and records nothing.","`pendingEvents()` returns what is not saved yet. `saveTo(store, id)` appends it using the version it was loaded at, then clears it."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"EventSourcingKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass EventSourcingKataTest {\n    static final List<StockEvent> HISTORY =\n        List.of(new Received(10), new Picked(3), new Adjusted(-2));\n\n    @Check(id = \"replay-rebuilds-state\")\n    void replayRebuildsState() {\n        StockItem item = StockItem.replay(HISTORY);\n        Expect.equal(5, item.onHand(), \"on hand after replay\");\n        Expect.equal(3, item.version(), \"version after replay\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), item.pendingEvents(), \"replayed events are not pending\");\n        Expect.equal(0, StockItem.replay(List.of()).version(), \"version of an empty history\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"replay-any-prefix\")\n    void replayAnyPrefix() {\n        StockItem then = StockItem.replay(HISTORY.subList(0, 2));\n        Expect.equal(7, then.onHand(), \"on hand at version 2\");\n        Expect.equal(2, then.version(), \"version at version 2\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"commands-record-events\")\n    void commandsRecordEvents() {\n        StockItem item = StockItem.replay(List.of());\n        item.receive(8);\n        item.pick(3);\n        item.adjust(1);\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new Received(8), new Picked(3), new Adjusted(1)),\n            item.pendingEvents(), \"pending events\");\n        Expect.equal(6, item.onHand(), \"on hand\");\n        Expect.equal(3, item.version(), \"version\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rules-reject-without-events\")\n    void rulesRejectWithoutEvents() {\n        StockItem item = StockItem.replay(List.of(new Received(2)));\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> item.pick(3), \"picking more than on hand\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> item.adjust(-3), \"adjusting below zero\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> item.receive(0), \"receiving 0 units\");\n        Expect.raises(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> item.pick(-1), \"picking -1 units\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), item.pendingEvents(), \"events after rejected commands\");\n        Expect.equal(1, item.version(), \"version after rejected commands\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"save-appends-pending\")\n    void saveAppendsPending() {\n        var store = new EventStore();\n        StockItem item = StockItem.replay(store.load(\"sku-42\"));\n        item.receive(10);\n        item.pick(4);\n        item.saveTo(store, \"sku-42\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new Received(10), new Picked(4)), store.load(\"sku-42\"), \"stored events\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), item.pendingEvents(), \"pending after save\");\n        item.saveTo(store, \"sku-42\");\n        item.adjust(-1);\n        item.saveTo(store, \"sku-42\");\n        Expect.equal(3, store.load(\"sku-42\").size(), \"events after a no-op save and one more\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), store.load(\"other\"), \"an unknown stream\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"stale-save-conflicts\")\n    void staleSaveConflicts() {\n        var store = new EventStore();\n        StockItem seed = StockItem.replay(List.of());\n        seed.receive(10);\n        seed.saveTo(store, \"sku-42\");\n\n        StockItem mine = StockItem.replay(store.load(\"sku-42\"));\n        StockItem rival = StockItem.replay(store.load(\"sku-42\"));\n        rival.pick(1);\n        rival.saveTo(store, \"sku-42\");\n        mine.pick(2);\n        Expect.raises(VersionConflict.class, () -> mine.saveTo(store, \"sku-42\"),\n            \"saving on top of a stream that moved on\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(new Received(10), new Picked(1)), store.load(\"sku-42\"),\n            \"the stream after a rejected save\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"history-is-protected\")\n    void historyIsProtected() {\n        var store = new EventStore();\n        var batch = new ArrayList<StockEvent>(List.of(new Received(1)));\n        store.append(\"s\", 0, batch);\n        batch.add(new Picked(1));\n        Expect.equal(1, store.load(\"s\").size(), \"a caller's list must not stay linked to the stream\");\n        Expect.raises(UnsupportedOperationException.class,\n            () -> store.load(\"s\").add(new Picked(1)), \"adding to a loaded history\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"events-are-immutable-records\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void eventsAreImmutableRecords() {\n        for (String name : List.of(\"Received\", \"Picked\", \"Adjusted\")) {\n            Expect.isTrue(Types.named(name).isRecord(), name + \" should be a record\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"store-keeps-events-not-state\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void storeKeepsEventsNotState() {\n        Class<?> store = Types.named(\"EventStore\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(store, Types.named(\"StockItem\")).isEmpty(),\n            \"EventStore holds StockItem state; it should hold events only\");\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"EventStore\").mentions(\"onHand\"), \"EventStore knows about stock levels\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rebuild-is-a-static-replay\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void rebuildIsAStaticReplay() {\n        Method replay = Types.staticMethod(Types.named(\"StockItem\"), \"replay\", List.class);\n        Expect.equal(Types.named(\"StockItem\"), replay.getReturnType(), \"replay's return type\");\n        for (Method m : Types.named(\"StockItem\").getDeclaredMethods()) {\n            boolean setterLike = !Modifier.isPrivate(m.getModifiers()) && m.getName().startsWith(\"set\");\n            Expect.isTrue(!setterLike, \"StockItem.\" + m.getName() + \" lets callers set state directly\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Rebuild a stock item from its events"},{"checks":[{"id":"fast-call-returns","kind":"behaviour","title":"A fast call returns its value"},{"id":"slow-call-times-out","kind":"behaviour","title":"A hanging call ends in TimeoutException"},{"id":"timeout-cancels-worker","kind":"behaviour","title":"The timed-out work is interrupted"},{"id":"remote-failure-propagates","kind":"behaviour","title":"Remote failures keep their cause"},{"id":"caller-interrupt-cancels","kind":"behaviour","title":"An interrupted caller cancels the work"},{"id":"no-unbounded-wait","kind":"design","title":"fetch never waits without a bound"},{"id":"cancel-on-timeout","kind":"design","title":"fetch cancels abandoned work"}],"hints":[[{"text":"`Future.get()` waits as long as the work does. A timeout has two halves: stop *waiting*, and stop the *work*.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Use the `Future.get(long, TimeUnit)` overload. When it throws, call `cancel(true)` on the `Future` so the worker thread is interrupted, then let the exception continue.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Wrap the wait:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["try {","    return result.get(timeoutMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);","} catch (TimeoutException | InterruptedException e) {","    result.cancel(true);","    throw e;","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"timeout","kind":"fix","minutes":15,"solution":[{"name":"Gateway.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Future;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException;\n\ninterface Remote {\n    String call() throws Exception;\n}\n\n// Checkout asks the price service through this gateway. When the\n// service hangs, so does every request thread that reaches it.\nfinal class Gateway {\n    private final ExecutorService pool;\n\n    Gateway(ExecutorService pool) { this.pool = pool; }\n\n    String fetch(Remote remote, long timeoutMs)\n            throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException,\n                   TimeoutException {\n        Future<String> result = pool.submit(remote::call);\n        try {\n            return result.get(timeoutMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);\n        } catch (TimeoutException | InterruptedException e) {\n            result.cancel(true);\n            throw e;\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Gateway.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Future;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException;\n\ninterface Remote {\n    String call() throws Exception;\n}\n\n// Checkout asks the price service through this gateway. When the\n// service hangs, so does every request thread that reaches it.\nfinal class Gateway {\n    private final ExecutorService pool;\n\n    Gateway(ExecutorService pool) { this.pool = pool; }\n\n    String fetch(Remote remote, long timeoutMs)\n            throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException,\n                   TimeoutException {\n        Future<String> result = pool.submit(remote::call);\n        return result.get();\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"When the price service hangs, every checkout request hangs with it.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Fix `Gateway.fetch(Remote, long timeoutMs)` so that a call which does not finish in time is **bounded and cancelled**.","type":"p"},{"items":["After `timeoutMs` the caller gets a `TimeoutException`, never an endless wait.","The abandoned work is cancelled with an interrupt, so it stops using its pool thread.","If the caller is interrupted while waiting, the work is cancelled too and `InterruptedException` propagates.","A remote that throws still surfaces as `ExecutionException` with the original cause.","Signatures and the `Remote` interface stay as they are."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"TimeoutKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Executors;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass TimeoutKataTest {\n    static ExecutorService daemonPool() {\n        return Executors.newCachedThreadPool(r -> {\n            Thread t = new Thread(r, \"kata-worker\");\n            t.setDaemon(true);\n            return t;\n        });\n    }\n\n    /** Blocks until interrupted; records the interruption. */\n    static final class Hang implements Remote {\n        final CountDownLatch started = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        final CountDownLatch interrupted = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        final CountDownLatch never = new CountDownLatch(1);\n\n        public String call() throws Exception {\n            started.countDown();\n            try {\n                never.await();\n            } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                interrupted.countDown();\n                throw e;\n            }\n            return \"late\";\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fast-call-returns\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void fastCallReturns() throws Exception {\n        Gateway gateway = new Gateway(daemonPool());\n        Expect.equal(\"42.00\", gateway.fetch(() -> \"42.00\", 1000), \"a fast call\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"slow-call-times-out\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void slowCallTimesOut() {\n        Gateway gateway = new Gateway(daemonPool());\n        Hang hang = new Hang();\n        Expect.completesWithin(1500, () -> {\n            Expect.raises(TimeoutException.class,\n                () -> gateway.fetch(hang, 30), \"a call that never returns\");\n            return null;\n        }, \"Gateway.fetch with a 30 ms timeout\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"timeout-cancels-worker\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void timeoutCancelsWorker() throws Exception {\n        Gateway gateway = new Gateway(daemonPool());\n        Hang hang = new Hang();\n        Expect.completesWithin(1500, () -> {\n            Expect.raises(TimeoutException.class,\n                () -> gateway.fetch(hang, 30), \"a call that never returns\");\n            return null;\n        }, \"Gateway.fetch with a 30 ms timeout\");\n        Expect.isTrue(hang.interrupted.await(1500, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS),\n            \"After the timeout the abandoned call should be cancelled \"\n                + \"(interrupted), not left running\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"remote-failure-propagates\", timeoutMs = 3000)\n    void remoteFailurePropagates() {\n        Gateway gateway = new Gateway(daemonPool());\n        ExecutionException e = Expect.raises(ExecutionException.class,\n            () -> gateway.fetch(() -> {\n                throw new IllegalStateException(\"boom\");\n            }, 1000), \"a remote that throws\");\n        Expect.isTrue(e.getCause() instanceof IllegalStateException,\n            \"ExecutionException should carry the remote's own exception\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"caller-interrupt-cancels\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void callerInterruptCancels() throws Exception {\n        Gateway gateway = new Gateway(daemonPool());\n        Hang hang = new Hang();\n        AtomicInteger outcome = new AtomicInteger();\n        Thread caller = new Thread(() -> {\n            try {\n                gateway.fetch(hang, 10_000);\n            } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                outcome.set(1);\n            } catch (Exception e) {\n                outcome.set(2);\n            }\n        }, \"kata-caller\");\n        caller.setDaemon(true);\n        caller.start();\n        Expect.isTrue(hang.started.await(1500, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS),\n            \"the remote call never started\");\n        caller.interrupt();\n        caller.join(1500);\n        Expect.equal(1, outcome.get(),\n            \"an interrupted caller should get InterruptedException\");\n        Expect.isTrue(hang.interrupted.await(1500, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS),\n            \"Interrupting the caller should cancel the remote call too\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-unbounded-wait\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noUnboundedWait() {\n        var fetch = Source.type(\"Gateway\").method(\"fetch\");\n        boolean bounded = !fetch.mentions(\"TimeUnit\").isEmpty()\n            || !fetch.mentions(\"Duration\").isEmpty()\n            || !fetch.calls(\"orTimeout\").isEmpty();\n        Expect.isTrue(bounded,\n            \"Gateway.fetch does not pass timeoutMs to a timed wait \"\n                + \"(use the Future.get overload that takes a unit)\");\n        Expect.none(fetch.calls(\"join\"),\n            \"Gateway.fetch must not join without a bound\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"cancel-on-timeout\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void cancelOnTimeout() {\n        var fetch = Source.type(\"Gateway\").method(\"fetch\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!fetch.calls(\"cancel\").isEmpty(),\n            \"Gateway.fetch never cancels the abandoned work\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Stop the price call from hanging forever"},{"checks":[{"id":"ceiling-doubles-then-caps","kind":"behaviour","title":"Ceilings double and stop at the cap"},{"id":"success-first-try","kind":"behaviour","title":"A first-try success never sleeps"},{"id":"recovers-after-transient","kind":"behaviour","title":"Transient failures are retried with backoff"},{"id":"sleeps-what-jitter-returns","kind":"behaviour","title":"Each sleep is the jittered delay"},{"id":"gives-up-after-max-attempts","kind":"behaviour","title":"The last TransientException is rethrown"},{"id":"permanent-is-not-retried","kind":"behaviour","title":"Permanent failures are not retried"},{"id":"single-attempt-never-sleeps","kind":"behaviour","title":"maxAttempts of 1 never sleeps"},{"id":"no-real-time-or-randomness","kind":"design","title":"Time and randomness are injected"},{"id":"retries-only-transient","kind":"design","title":"Only TransientException is caught"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Two separate ideas: the *ceiling* grows deterministically, the *delay* is whatever the injected jitter picks below it. Keep them in two steps.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`call` is a loop over attempts. Catch `TransientException` only; if it is the last attempt rethrow, otherwise ask `jitter` for a delay and hand it to `sleeper`. Cap the shift so `<<` cannot overflow.","type":"p"}],[{"language":"java","lines":["for (int attempt = 1; ; attempt++) {","    try {","        return op.get();","    } catch (TransientException e) {","        if (attempt >= maxAttempts) throw e;","        long ms = jitter.applyAsLong(ceilingMs(attempt));","        sleeper.sleep(Duration.ofMillis(ms));","    }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"retry-backoff","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Support.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Support.java","source":"import java.time.Duration;\n\n@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nclass TransientException extends RuntimeException {\n    TransientException(String message) { super(message); }\n}\n\n@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nclass PermanentException extends RuntimeException {\n    PermanentException(String message) { super(message); }\n}\n\ninterface Sleeper {\n    void sleep(Duration d);\n}\n"},{"name":"Retry.java","source":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.function.LongUnaryOperator;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\n\n// Retries transient failures with capped exponential backoff.\nfinal class Retry {\n    private final int maxAttempts;\n    private final long baseMs;\n    private final long capMs;\n    private final LongUnaryOperator jitter;\n    private final Sleeper sleeper;\n\n    Retry(int maxAttempts, long baseMs, long capMs,\n          LongUnaryOperator jitter, Sleeper sleeper) {\n        this.maxAttempts = maxAttempts;\n        this.baseMs = baseMs;\n        this.capMs = capMs;\n        this.jitter = jitter;\n        this.sleeper = sleeper;\n    }\n\n    /** The ceiling for a 1-based attempt, before jitter is applied. */\n    long ceilingMs(int attempt) {\n        int shift = Math.min(attempt - 1, 20);\n        return Math.min(capMs, baseMs << shift);\n    }\n\n    <T> T call(Supplier<T> op) {\n        for (int attempt = 1; ; attempt++) {\n            try {\n                return op.get();\n            } catch (TransientException e) {\n                if (attempt >= maxAttempts) {\n                    throw e;\n                }\n                long wait = jitter.applyAsLong(ceilingMs(attempt));\n                sleeper.sleep(Duration.ofMillis(wait));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Support.java","source":"import java.time.Duration;\n\n@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nclass TransientException extends RuntimeException {\n    TransientException(String message) { super(message); }\n}\n\n@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nclass PermanentException extends RuntimeException {\n    PermanentException(String message) { super(message); }\n}\n\ninterface Sleeper {\n    void sleep(Duration d);\n}\n"},{"name":"Retry.java","source":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.function.LongUnaryOperator;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\n\n// Retries transient failures with capped exponential backoff.\nfinal class Retry {\n    private final int maxAttempts;\n    private final long baseMs;\n    private final long capMs;\n    private final LongUnaryOperator jitter;\n    private final Sleeper sleeper;\n\n    Retry(int maxAttempts, long baseMs, long capMs,\n          LongUnaryOperator jitter, Sleeper sleeper) {\n        this.maxAttempts = maxAttempts;\n        this.baseMs = baseMs;\n        this.capMs = capMs;\n        this.jitter = jitter;\n        this.sleeper = sleeper;\n    }\n\n    /** The ceiling for a 1-based attempt, before jitter is applied. */\n    long ceilingMs(int attempt) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    <T> T call(Supplier<T> op) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Make flaky calls recover on their own, without hammering the dependency.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `Retry` (constructor given). Time and randomness are injected: it sleeps through a `Sleeper` and picks each delay with the `LongUnaryOperator jitter`, which maps a ceiling in ms to the delay in ms.","type":"p"},{"items":["`long ceilingMs(int attempt)`: for a 1-based attempt, `min(capMs, baseMs * 2^(attempt-1))`. It must not overflow for large attempts.","`<T> T call(Supplier<T> op)` runs `op`, retrying only on `TransientException`, up to `maxAttempts` calls in total.","Between attempts sleep `jitter.applyAsLong(ceilingMs(attempt))` ms. Never sleep after the last attempt.","When attempts run out, rethrow the last `TransientException`. Any other exception, including `PermanentException`, propagates at once."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"RetryKataTest.java","source":"import java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Random;\nimport java.util.function.LongUnaryOperator;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass RetryKataTest {\n    static final class Waits implements Sleeper {\n        final List<Long> ms = new ArrayList<>();\n        public void sleep(Duration d) { ms.add(d.toMillis()); }\n    }\n\n    static final class Flaky implements Supplier<String> {\n        final int failures;\n        final RuntimeException error;\n        int calls;\n        Flaky(int failures, RuntimeException error) {\n            this.failures = failures;\n            this.error = error;\n        }\n        public String get() {\n            if (calls++ < failures) throw error;\n            return \"ok\";\n        }\n    }\n\n    static Retry retry(int attempts, LongUnaryOperator jitter, Sleeper s) {\n        return new Retry(attempts, 100, 1000, jitter, s);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"ceiling-doubles-then-caps\")\n    void ceilingDoublesThenCaps() {\n        Retry r = retry(5, c -> c, new Waits());\n        List<Long> got = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int a = 1; a <= 6; a++) got.add(r.ceilingMs(a));\n        Expect.equal(List.of(100L, 200L, 400L, 800L, 1000L, 1000L), got,\n            \"ceilings for attempts 1 to 6 (base 100, cap 1000)\");\n        Expect.equal(1000L, r.ceilingMs(200),\n            \"the ceiling for attempt 200 (no overflow)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"success-first-try\")\n    void successFirstTry() {\n        Waits waits = new Waits();\n        Flaky op = new Flaky(0, new TransientException(\"x\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"ok\", retry(3, c -> c, waits).call(op), \"the result\");\n        Expect.equal(1, op.calls, \"calls to the operation\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), waits.ms, \"sleeps before a first-try success\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"recovers-after-transient\")\n    void recoversAfterTransient() {\n        Waits waits = new Waits();\n        Flaky op = new Flaky(2, new TransientException(\"503\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"ok\", retry(5, c -> c, waits).call(op), \"the result\");\n        Expect.equal(3, op.calls, \"calls to the operation\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(100L, 200L), waits.ms, \"sleeps between attempts\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sleeps-what-jitter-returns\")\n    void sleepsWhatJitterReturns() {\n        Random seeded = new Random(7);\n        List<Long> ceilings = new ArrayList<>();\n        List<Long> picked = new ArrayList<>();\n        LongUnaryOperator jitter = c -> {\n            ceilings.add(c);\n            long v = (long) (seeded.nextDouble() * (c + 1));\n            picked.add(v);\n            return v;\n        };\n        Waits waits = new Waits();\n        Flaky op = new Flaky(99, new TransientException(\"503\"));\n        Expect.raises(TransientException.class,\n            () -> retry(4, jitter, waits).call(op), \"an exhausted retry\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(100L, 200L, 400L), ceilings,\n            \"ceilings handed to the jitter function\");\n        Expect.equal(picked, waits.ms, \"sleeps should equal the jittered delays\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"gives-up-after-max-attempts\")\n    void givesUpAfterMaxAttempts() {\n        Waits waits = new Waits();\n        TransientException boom = new TransientException(\"503\");\n        Flaky op = new Flaky(99, boom);\n        TransientException e = Expect.raises(TransientException.class,\n            () -> retry(3, c -> c, waits).call(op), \"an exhausted retry\");\n        Expect.isTrue(e == boom, \"the last TransientException should be rethrown as is\");\n        Expect.equal(3, op.calls, \"calls to the operation\");\n        Expect.equal(2, waits.ms.size(), \"sleeps (none after the last attempt)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"permanent-is-not-retried\")\n    void permanentIsNotRetried() {\n        Waits waits = new Waits();\n        Flaky op = new Flaky(99, new PermanentException(\"400\"));\n        Expect.raises(PermanentException.class,\n            () -> retry(5, c -> c, waits).call(op), \"a permanent failure\");\n        Expect.equal(1, op.calls, \"calls to the operation\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), waits.ms, \"sleeps before a permanent failure\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"single-attempt-never-sleeps\")\n    void singleAttemptNeverSleeps() {\n        Waits waits = new Waits();\n        Flaky op = new Flaky(99, new TransientException(\"503\"));\n        Expect.raises(TransientException.class,\n            () -> retry(1, c -> c, waits).call(op), \"maxAttempts = 1\");\n        Expect.equal(1, op.calls, \"calls to the operation\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), waits.ms, \"sleeps\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-real-time-or-randomness\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noRealTimeOrRandomness() {\n        var retry = Source.type(\"Retry\");\n        Expect.none(retry.news(\"Random\"), \"Retry creates its own Random\");\n        Expect.none(retry.calls(\"random\"), \"Retry draws its own randomness\");\n        Expect.none(retry.calls(\"nextLong\"), \"Retry draws its own randomness\");\n        Expect.none(retry.calls(\"nextDouble\"), \"Retry draws its own randomness\");\n        Expect.none(retry.mentions(\"Thread\"), \"Retry sleeps on a Thread instead of the Sleeper\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"retries-only-transient\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void retriesOnlyTransient() {\n        var call = Source.type(\"Retry\").method(\"call\");\n        for (String broad : List.of(\"Exception\", \"RuntimeException\", \"Throwable\")) {\n            Expect.none(call.mentions(broad),\n                \"Retry.call catches \" + broad + \"; retry only TransientException\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Retry with capped exponential backoff"},{"checks":[{"id":"closed-passes-through","kind":"behaviour","title":"A closed breaker passes calls through"},{"id":"opens-after-threshold","kind":"behaviour","title":"It opens after threshold failures"},{"id":"open-rejects-without-calling","kind":"behaviour","title":"Open rejects without calling the operation"},{"id":"success-resets-failure-count","kind":"behaviour","title":"Only consecutive failures count"},{"id":"half-open-after-cooldown","kind":"behaviour","title":"After the cool-down one call probes"},{"id":"probe-failure-reopens","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failed probe reopens and restarts the timer"},{"id":"only-one-probe-at-a-time","kind":"behaviour","title":"Other callers are rejected during the probe"},{"id":"racing-callers-share-one-probe","kind":"behaviour","title":"Racing callers cause exactly one probe"},{"id":"slow-call-does-not-block-others","kind":"behaviour","title":"A slow call does not hold a lock"},{"id":"injected-clock-only","kind":"design","title":"Only the injected clock is used"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Three states and two counters: consecutive failures, and when it opened. The hard part is the transition OPEN to HALF_OPEN: exactly one caller may take it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Split `call` into `permit()` and `record(boolean ok)`, both `synchronized`, with `op.get()` between them, outside the lock. `permit()` flips OPEN to HALF_OPEN and returns true for that one caller only.","type":"p"}],[{"language":"java","lines":["private synchronized boolean permit() {","    if (state == State.OPEN","            && clock.getAsLong() - openedAt >= openMs) {","        state = State.HALF_OPEN;","        return true;","    }","    return state == State.CLOSED;","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"circuit-breaker","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"readOnly":["State.java"],"solution":[{"name":"State.java","source":"enum State { CLOSED, OPEN, HALF_OPEN }\n"},{"name":"CircuitBreaker.java","source":"import java.util.function.LongSupplier;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\n\n// Protects a shaky dependency: stop calling it while it is down.\nfinal class CircuitBreaker {\n    private final int threshold;\n    private final long openMs;\n    private final LongSupplier clock;\n    private State state = State.CLOSED;\n    private int failures;\n    private long openedAt;\n\n    CircuitBreaker(int threshold, long openMs, LongSupplier clock) {\n        this.threshold = threshold;\n        this.openMs = openMs;\n        this.clock = clock;\n    }\n\n    synchronized State state() { return state; }\n\n    <T> T call(Supplier<T> op, Supplier<T> fallback) {\n        if (!permit()) {\n            return fallback.get();\n        }\n        try {\n            T result = op.get();\n            record(true);\n            return result;\n        } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n            record(false);\n            return fallback.get();\n        }\n    }\n\n    // The caller that flips OPEN to HALF_OPEN is the single probe.\n    private synchronized boolean permit() {\n        if (state == State.OPEN && clock.getAsLong() - openedAt >= openMs) {\n            state = State.HALF_OPEN;\n            return true;\n        }\n        return state == State.CLOSED;\n    }\n\n    private synchronized void record(boolean ok) {\n        if (ok) {\n            state = State.CLOSED;\n            failures = 0;\n        } else if (state == State.HALF_OPEN || ++failures >= threshold) {\n            state = State.OPEN;\n            openedAt = clock.getAsLong();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"State.java","source":"enum State { CLOSED, OPEN, HALF_OPEN }\n"},{"name":"CircuitBreaker.java","source":"import java.util.function.LongSupplier;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\n\n// Protects a shaky dependency: stop calling it while it is down.\nfinal class CircuitBreaker {\n    private final int threshold;\n    private final long openMs;\n    private final LongSupplier clock;\n\n    CircuitBreaker(int threshold, long openMs, LongSupplier clock) {\n        this.threshold = threshold;\n        this.openMs = openMs;\n        this.clock = clock;\n    }\n\n    State state() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    <T> T call(Supplier<T> op, Supplier<T> fallback) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Stop calling a dependency that keeps failing, then probe it to see if it recovered.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `CircuitBreaker(int threshold, long openMs, LongSupplier clock)` with `State state()` and `<T> T call(Supplier<T> op, Supplier<T> fallback)`. `State` is given. Time comes only from `clock` (ms).","type":"p"},{"items":["**CLOSED:** run `op`. A `RuntimeException` counts as a failure and returns `fallback.get()`. A success resets the count of consecutive failures.","`threshold` consecutive failures make it **OPEN**: `op` is not called, callers get `fallback.get()`.","Once `openMs` have passed, one caller becomes the probe and the state is **HALF_OPEN**; everyone else still gets the fallback.","A successful probe closes the breaker; a failed probe reopens it and restarts the cool-down.","Never hold a lock while `op` runs."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"BreakerKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass BreakerKataTest {\n    final AtomicLong now = new AtomicLong();\n    final AtomicInteger calls = new AtomicInteger();\n    final CircuitBreaker breaker = new CircuitBreaker(3, 1000, now::get);\n\n    Supplier<String> failing() {\n        return () -> {\n            calls.incrementAndGet();\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"down\");\n        };\n    }\n\n    Supplier<String> working() {\n        return () -> {\n            calls.incrementAndGet();\n            return \"live\";\n        };\n    }\n\n    String fail() { return breaker.call(failing(), () -> \"cached\"); }\n\n    void trip() {\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) fail();\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"closed-passes-through\")\n    void closedPassesThrough() {\n        Expect.equal(\"live\", breaker.call(working(), () -> \"cached\"), \"a healthy call\");\n        Expect.equal(State.CLOSED, breaker.state(), \"state after success\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"opens-after-threshold\")\n    void opensAfterThreshold() {\n        Expect.equal(\"cached\", fail(), \"a failing call returns the fallback\");\n        fail();\n        Expect.equal(State.CLOSED, breaker.state(), \"state after 2 failures\");\n        fail();\n        Expect.equal(State.OPEN, breaker.state(), \"state after 3 failures\");\n        Expect.equal(3, calls.get(), \"calls to the operation\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"open-rejects-without-calling\")\n    void openRejectsWithoutCalling() {\n        trip();\n        now.set(999);\n        Expect.equal(\"cached\", breaker.call(working(), () -> \"cached\"),\n            \"a call while open\");\n        Expect.equal(3, calls.get(), \"the operation must not run while open\");\n        Expect.equal(State.OPEN, breaker.state(), \"state just before the cool-down ends\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"success-resets-failure-count\")\n    void successResetsFailureCount() {\n        fail();\n        fail();\n        breaker.call(working(), () -> \"cached\");\n        fail();\n        fail();\n        Expect.equal(State.CLOSED, breaker.state(),\n            \"state after fail, fail, success, fail, fail (only consecutive failures count)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"half-open-after-cooldown\")\n    void halfOpenAfterCooldown() {\n        trip();\n        now.set(1000);\n        State[] seen = new State[1];\n        breaker.call(() -> {\n            seen[0] = breaker.state();\n            return \"live\";\n        }, () -> \"cached\");\n        Expect.equal(State.HALF_OPEN, seen[0], \"state while the probe runs\");\n        Expect.equal(State.CLOSED, breaker.state(), \"state after a successful probe\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"probe-failure-reopens\")\n    void probeFailureReopens() {\n        trip();\n        now.set(1000);\n        Expect.equal(\"cached\", fail(), \"a failing probe returns the fallback\");\n        Expect.equal(State.OPEN, breaker.state(), \"state after a failed probe\");\n        int before = calls.get();\n        now.set(1999);\n        breaker.call(working(), () -> \"cached\");\n        Expect.equal(before, calls.get(),\n            \"the cool-down restarts from the failed probe\");\n        now.set(2000);\n        Expect.equal(\"live\", breaker.call(working(), () -> \"cached\"),\n            \"the next probe after a second cool-down\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"only-one-probe-at-a-time\")\n    void onlyOneProbeAtATime() {\n        trip();\n        now.set(1000);\n        AtomicInteger inner = new AtomicInteger();\n        String outer = breaker.call(() -> {\n            breaker.call(() -> {\n                inner.incrementAndGet();\n                return \"live\";\n            }, () -> \"cached\");\n            return \"live\";\n        }, () -> \"cached\");\n        Expect.equal(\"live\", outer, \"the probe\");\n        Expect.equal(0, inner.get(),\n            \"a call made while the probe is in flight must get the fallback\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"racing-callers-share-one-probe\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void racingCallersShareOneProbe() {\n        trip();\n        int before = calls.get();\n        now.set(1000);\n        Stress.race(8, () -> breaker.call(failing(), () -> \"cached\"));\n        Expect.equal(before + 1, calls.get(),\n            \"operation calls after the cool-down (exactly one probe)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"slow-call-does-not-block-others\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void slowCallDoesNotBlockOthers() throws Exception {\n        CountDownLatch entered = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        CountDownLatch release = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        Thread slow = new Thread(() -> breaker.call(() -> {\n            entered.countDown();\n            try {\n                release.await();\n            } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n            }\n            return \"live\";\n        }, () -> \"cached\"));\n        slow.setDaemon(true);\n        slow.start();\n        try {\n            Expect.isTrue(entered.await(2, TimeUnit.SECONDS), \"the slow call never started\");\n            Expect.equal(State.CLOSED,\n                Expect.completesWithin(1000, breaker::state, \"state() during a slow call\"),\n                \"state during a slow call\");\n        } finally {\n            release.countDown();\n            slow.join(1000);\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"injected-clock-only\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void injectedClockOnly() {\n        var breaker = Source.type(\"CircuitBreaker\");\n        Expect.none(breaker.calls(\"currentTimeMillis\"), \"CircuitBreaker reads the system clock\");\n        Expect.none(breaker.calls(\"nanoTime\"), \"CircuitBreaker reads the system clock\");\n        Expect.none(breaker.calls(\"now\"), \"CircuitBreaker reads the system clock\");\n        Expect.none(breaker.calls(\"sleep\"), \"CircuitBreaker must never sleep\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"A circuit breaker with a half-open probe"},{"checks":[{"id":"runs-under-the-limit","kind":"behaviour","title":"A call under the limit runs"},{"id":"rejects-when-full","kind":"behaviour","title":"A full bulkhead rejects by name"},{"id":"rejection-does-not-wait","kind":"behaviour","title":"Rejection is immediate, not queued"},{"id":"permit-returned-after-success","kind":"behaviour","title":"Permits return after success"},{"id":"permit-returned-after-failure","kind":"behaviour","title":"Permits return after a failure"},{"id":"bulkheads-are-independent","kind":"behaviour","title":"A full bulkhead does not affect another"},{"id":"never-exceeds-the-limit","kind":"behaviour","title":"Racing callers never exceed the limit"},{"id":"limit-is-per-instance","kind":"design","title":"No shared static state"},{"id":"operation-runs-outside-a-monitor","kind":"design","title":"The operation runs outside synchronized"}],"hints":[[{"text":"A bulkhead is a counter of free slots plus the discipline to give each slot back. Which `java.util.concurrent` type counts permits and can refuse without blocking?","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Hold a `Semaphore` created with `maxConcurrent`. Use the non-blocking `tryAcquire()`; reject if it says no. Run `op` in a `try` and release the permit in `finally`.","type":"p"}],[{"language":"java","lines":["if (!permits.tryAcquire()) {","    throw new BulkheadFullException(name);","}","try {","    return op.get();","} finally {","    permits.release();","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"bulkhead","kind":"implement","minutes":15,"readOnly":["Support.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Support.java","source":"@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nclass BulkheadFullException extends RuntimeException {\n    BulkheadFullException(String name) { super(name + \" is full\"); }\n}\n"},{"name":"Bulkhead.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.Semaphore;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\n\n// One compartment per dependency: at most maxConcurrent calls inside.\nfinal class Bulkhead {\n    private final String name;\n    private final Semaphore permits;\n\n    Bulkhead(String name, int maxConcurrent) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.permits = new Semaphore(maxConcurrent);\n    }\n\n    <T> T call(Supplier<T> op) {\n        if (!permits.tryAcquire()) {\n            throw new BulkheadFullException(name);\n        }\n        try {\n            return op.get();\n        } finally {\n            permits.release();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Support.java","source":"@SuppressWarnings(\"serial\")\nclass BulkheadFullException extends RuntimeException {\n    BulkheadFullException(String name) { super(name + \" is full\"); }\n}\n"},{"name":"Bulkhead.java","source":"import java.util.function.Supplier;\n\n// One compartment per dependency: at most maxConcurrent calls inside.\nfinal class Bulkhead {\n    private final String name;\n    private final int maxConcurrent;\n\n    Bulkhead(String name, int maxConcurrent) {\n        this.name = name;\n        this.maxConcurrent = maxConcurrent;\n    }\n\n    <T> T call(Supplier<T> op) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Cap how many calls one dependency may have in flight, so a stall cannot eat every thread.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `Bulkhead(String name, int maxConcurrent)` and `<T> T call(Supplier<T> op)`. `BulkheadFullException` is given.","type":"p"},{"items":["Up to `maxConcurrent` calls run `op` at the same time, each on its own caller's thread.","When the bulkhead is full, `call` throws `new BulkheadFullException(name)` **immediately**; it must not block or queue, and `op` must not run.","A permit is returned when `op` finishes, whether it returns or throws; the exception reaches the caller unchanged.","Two `Bulkhead` instances share nothing."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"BulkheadKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport java.util.function.Supplier;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass BulkheadKataTest {\n    final CountDownLatch release = new CountDownLatch(1);\n    final List<Thread> holders = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    /** Starts calls that stay inside the bulkhead until release is counted down. */\n    void occupy(Bulkhead b, int n) throws InterruptedException {\n        CountDownLatch entered = new CountDownLatch(n);\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            Thread t = new Thread(() -> b.call(() -> {\n                entered.countDown();\n                try {\n                    release.await();\n                } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n                }\n                return \"done\";\n            }), \"kata-holder\");\n            t.setDaemon(true);\n            holders.add(t);\n            t.start();\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(entered.await(1, TimeUnit.SECONDS),\n            \"calls within the limit should be admitted\");\n    }\n\n    void drain() throws InterruptedException {\n        release.countDown();\n        for (Thread t : holders) t.join(1000);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"runs-under-the-limit\")\n    void runsUnderTheLimit() {\n        Bulkhead b = new Bulkhead(\"inventory\", 2);\n        Expect.equal(\"ok\", b.call(() -> \"ok\"), \"a call under the limit\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rejects-when-full\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void rejectsWhenFull() throws Exception {\n        Bulkhead b = new Bulkhead(\"inventory\", 2);\n        occupy(b, 2);\n        try {\n            AtomicInteger ran = new AtomicInteger();\n            BulkheadFullException e = Expect.raises(BulkheadFullException.class,\n                () -> b.call(() -> ran.incrementAndGet()), \"a third concurrent call\");\n            Expect.isTrue(e.getMessage().contains(\"inventory\"),\n                \"the rejection should name the bulkhead\");\n            Expect.equal(0, ran.get(), \"a rejected operation must not run\");\n        } finally {\n            drain();\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rejection-does-not-wait\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void rejectionDoesNotWait() throws Exception {\n        Bulkhead b = new Bulkhead(\"inventory\", 1);\n        occupy(b, 1);\n        try {\n            Expect.completesWithin(1000, () -> {\n                Expect.raises(BulkheadFullException.class,\n                    () -> b.call(() -> \"x\"), \"a call to a full bulkhead\");\n                return null;\n            }, \"a call to a full bulkhead (it must reject, not queue)\");\n        } finally {\n            drain();\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"permit-returned-after-success\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void permitReturnedAfterSuccess() throws Exception {\n        Bulkhead b = new Bulkhead(\"inventory\", 2);\n        occupy(b, 2);\n        drain();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n            Expect.equal(\"ok\", b.call(() -> \"ok\"), \"call \" + (i + 1) + \" after the holders finished\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"permit-returned-after-failure\")\n    void permitReturnedAfterFailure() {\n        Bulkhead b = new Bulkhead(\"payments\", 1);\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n            IllegalStateException e = Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class,\n                () -> b.call(() -> {\n                    throw new IllegalStateException(\"boom\");\n                }), \"a failing operation\");\n            Expect.equal(\"boom\", e.getMessage(), \"the original exception\");\n        }\n        Expect.equal(\"ok\", b.call(() -> \"ok\"), \"a call after the failures\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bulkheads-are-independent\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void bulkheadsAreIndependent() throws Exception {\n        Bulkhead inventory = new Bulkhead(\"inventory\", 1);\n        Bulkhead payments = new Bulkhead(\"payments\", 1);\n        occupy(inventory, 1);\n        try {\n            Expect.equal(\"paid\", payments.call(() -> \"paid\"),\n                \"a call to payments while inventory is full\");\n        } finally {\n            drain();\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"never-exceeds-the-limit\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void neverExceedsTheLimit() {\n        Bulkhead b = new Bulkhead(\"inventory\", 3);\n        AtomicInteger inside = new AtomicInteger();\n        AtomicInteger peak = new AtomicInteger();\n        List<Boolean> admitted = Stress.race(12, () -> {\n            try {\n                b.call(() -> {\n                    peak.accumulateAndGet(inside.incrementAndGet(), Math::max);\n                    Stress.pause(10);\n                    inside.decrementAndGet();\n                    return \"x\";\n                });\n                return true;\n            } catch (BulkheadFullException e) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        });\n        Expect.isTrue(peak.get() <= 3,\n            \"at most 3 calls may be inside at once, saw \" + peak.get());\n        Expect.isTrue(admitted.stream().anyMatch(a -> a),\n            \"some of the racing calls should be admitted\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"limit-is-per-instance\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void limitIsPerInstance() {\n        for (Field f : Types.named(\"Bulkhead\").getDeclaredFields()) {\n            int m = f.getModifiers();\n            Expect.isTrue(!Modifier.isStatic(m) || Modifier.isFinal(m),\n                \"Bulkhead.\" + f.getName() + \" is shared mutable static state; \"\n                    + \"each bulkhead needs its own permits\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"operation-runs-outside-a-monitor\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void operationRunsOutsideAMonitor() {\n        var call = Source.type(\"Bulkhead\").method(\"call\");\n        List<Hit> inside = call.calls(\"get\").stream().filter(Hit::insideSynchronized).toList();\n        Expect.none(inside, \"Bulkhead runs the operation inside synchronized\");\n        Expect.none(call.calls(\"sleep\"), \"Bulkhead must not sleep\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"A bulkhead for the inventory service"},{"checks":[{"id":"burst-up-to-capacity","kind":"behaviour","title":"A full bucket admits a burst"},{"id":"retry-after-in-ms","kind":"behaviour","title":"Rejections return milliseconds to wait"},{"id":"refills-with-time","kind":"behaviour","title":"Tokens refill with elapsed time"},{"id":"never-above-capacity","kind":"behaviour","title":"Idle time never banks past capacity"},{"id":"rejections-cost-nothing","kind":"behaviour","title":"Rejected requests take no tokens"},{"id":"retry-after-is-honest","kind":"behaviour","title":"Waiting the advertised time succeeds"},{"id":"clients-have-separate-buckets","kind":"behaviour","title":"Each client has its own bucket"},{"id":"racing-callers-share-the-burst","kind":"behaviour","title":"Racing callers cannot overspend"},{"id":"time-is-injected","kind":"design","title":"Only the injected clock is read"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Do not run a timer. Remember how many tokens you had and when you last looked; on each call, add what the elapsed time earned, capped at capacity.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`TokenBucket` keeps `double tokens` and `long last`. `acquire` is `synchronized`: refill, then either spend 1 or compute the wait from the missing fraction. `Limiter` maps client to bucket with `computeIfAbsent`.","type":"p"}],[{"language":"java","lines":["long now = nanos.getAsLong();","tokens = Math.min(capacity,","    tokens + (now - last) * perSecond / 1e9);","last = now;","if (tokens >= 1) { tokens -= 1; return 0; }","return (long) Math.ceil((1 - tokens) / perSecond * 1000);"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"rate-limiter","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"solution":[{"name":"TokenBucket.java","source":"import java.util.function.LongSupplier;\n\n// Starts full. Refills perSecond tokens per second, up to capacity.\nfinal class TokenBucket {\n    private final double capacity;\n    private final double perSecond;\n    private final LongSupplier nanos;\n    private double tokens;\n    private long last;\n\n    TokenBucket(int capacity, double perSecond, LongSupplier nanos) {\n        this.capacity = capacity;\n        this.perSecond = perSecond;\n        this.nanos = nanos;\n        this.tokens = capacity;\n        this.last = nanos.getAsLong();\n    }\n\n    /** Returns 0 if admitted, else the milliseconds until a token exists. */\n    synchronized long acquire() {\n        long now = nanos.getAsLong();\n        tokens = Math.min(capacity, tokens + (now - last) * perSecond / 1e9);\n        last = now;\n        if (tokens >= 1) {\n            tokens -= 1;\n            return 0;\n        }\n        return (long) Math.ceil((1 - tokens) / perSecond * 1000);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Limiter.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.function.LongSupplier;\n\n// One bucket per client, all with the same capacity and rate.\nfinal class Limiter {\n    private final int capacity;\n    private final double perSecond;\n    private final LongSupplier nanos;\n    private final Map<String, TokenBucket> buckets = new HashMap<>();\n\n    Limiter(int capacity, double perSecond, LongSupplier nanos) {\n        this.capacity = capacity;\n        this.perSecond = perSecond;\n        this.nanos = nanos;\n    }\n\n    /** 0 if the client may proceed, else the retry-after in ms. */\n    synchronized long acquire(String client) {\n        return buckets\n            .computeIfAbsent(client,\n                c -> new TokenBucket(capacity, perSecond, nanos))\n            .acquire();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"TokenBucket.java","source":"import java.util.function.LongSupplier;\n\n// Starts full. Refills perSecond tokens per second, up to capacity.\nfinal class TokenBucket {\n    private final double capacity;\n    private final double perSecond;\n    private final LongSupplier nanos;\n\n    TokenBucket(int capacity, double perSecond, LongSupplier nanos) {\n        this.capacity = capacity;\n        this.perSecond = perSecond;\n        this.nanos = nanos;\n    }\n\n    /** Returns 0 if admitted, else the milliseconds until a token exists. */\n    long acquire() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Limiter.java","source":"import java.util.function.LongSupplier;\n\n// One bucket per client, all with the same capacity and rate.\nfinal class Limiter {\n    private final int capacity;\n    private final double perSecond;\n    private final LongSupplier nanos;\n\n    Limiter(int capacity, double perSecond, LongSupplier nanos) {\n        this.capacity = capacity;\n        this.perSecond = perSecond;\n        this.nanos = nanos;\n    }\n\n    /** 0 if the client may proceed, else the retry-after in ms. */\n    long acquire(String client) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Admit a burst, then a steady rate, and tell rejected callers when to come back.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `TokenBucket(int capacity, double perSecond, LongSupplier nanos)` and `Limiter(int capacity, double perSecond, LongSupplier nanos)`. Time comes only from the `nanos` supplier.","type":"p"},{"items":["A `TokenBucket` starts full. `long acquire()` returns `0` if a token was taken, otherwise the **milliseconds, rounded up,** until one exists.","Tokens refill lazily from elapsed time (no timer thread) and never exceed `capacity`. A rejection takes nothing.","`Limiter.acquire(String client)` gives every client its own bucket and returns the same convention.","Both must be safe to call from many threads."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"RateKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass RateKataTest {\n    final AtomicLong clock = new AtomicLong();\n\n    void atMs(long ms) { clock.set(ms * 1_000_000); }\n\n    TokenBucket bucket() { return new TokenBucket(3, 2, clock::get); }\n\n    @Check(id = \"burst-up-to-capacity\")\n    void burstUpToCapacity() {\n        TokenBucket b = bucket();\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {\n            Expect.equal(0L, b.acquire(), \"request \" + i + \" of the initial burst\");\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(b.acquire() > 0, \"the 4th request should be rejected\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"retry-after-in-ms\")\n    void retryAfterInMs() {\n        TokenBucket b = bucket();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) b.acquire();\n        Expect.equal(500L, b.acquire(), \"retry-after right after the burst (2 tokens/s)\");\n        atMs(100);\n        Expect.equal(400L, b.acquire(), \"retry-after 100 ms later\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"refills-with-time\")\n    void refillsWithTime() {\n        TokenBucket b = bucket();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) b.acquire();\n        atMs(499);\n        Expect.isTrue(b.acquire() > 0, \"no token after 499 ms\");\n        atMs(500);\n        Expect.equal(0L, b.acquire(), \"one token after 500 ms\");\n        Expect.isTrue(b.acquire() > 0, \"only one token was earned\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"never-above-capacity\")\n    void neverAboveCapacity() {\n        TokenBucket b = bucket();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) b.acquire();\n        atMs(60_000);\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {\n            Expect.equal(0L, b.acquire(), \"request \" + i + \" after a long idle\");\n        }\n        Expect.isTrue(b.acquire() > 0, \"idle time must not bank more than capacity\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rejections-cost-nothing\")\n    void rejectionsCostNothing() {\n        TokenBucket b = bucket();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) b.acquire();\n        for (int i = 0; i < 20; i++) b.acquire();\n        atMs(500);\n        Expect.equal(0L, b.acquire(), \"rejected requests must not delay the refill\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"retry-after-is-honest\")\n    void retryAfterIsHonest() {\n        TokenBucket b = new TokenBucket(1, 3, clock::get);\n        Expect.equal(0L, b.acquire(), \"the only token\");\n        long wait = b.acquire();\n        Expect.equal(334L, wait, \"retry-after at 3 tokens/s, rounded up\");\n        atMs(wait);\n        Expect.equal(0L, b.acquire(), \"a request after waiting the advertised time\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"clients-have-separate-buckets\")\n    void clientsHaveSeparateBuckets() {\n        Limiter limiter = new Limiter(3, 2, clock::get);\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n            Expect.equal(0L, limiter.acquire(\"a\"), \"client a, request \" + (i + 1));\n        }\n        Expect.equal(500L, limiter.acquire(\"a\"), \"client a past its burst\");\n        Expect.equal(0L, limiter.acquire(\"b\"), \"client b is unaffected by a\");\n        atMs(500);\n        Expect.equal(0L, limiter.acquire(\"a\"), \"client a after refill\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"racing-callers-share-the-burst\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void racingCallersShareTheBurst() {\n        Limiter limiter = new Limiter(5, 1, clock::get);\n        List<Long> results = Stress.race(16, () -> limiter.acquire(\"shared\"));\n        long admitted = results.stream().filter(r -> r == 0).count();\n        Expect.equal(5L, admitted, \"requests admitted from a capacity-5 bucket\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"time-is-injected\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void timeIsInjected() {\n        for (String type : List.of(\"TokenBucket\", \"Limiter\")) {\n            var shape = Source.type(type);\n            Expect.none(shape.calls(\"nanoTime\"), type + \" reads the system clock\");\n            Expect.none(shape.calls(\"currentTimeMillis\"), type + \" reads the system clock\");\n            Expect.none(shape.calls(\"now\"), type + \" reads the system clock\");\n            Expect.none(shape.calls(\"sleep\"), type + \" must reject, never sleep\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"A token-bucket rate limiter"},{"checks":[{"id":"first-delivery-applied","kind":"behaviour","title":"A first delivery is applied"},{"id":"duplicate-is-skipped","kind":"behaviour","title":"An immediate duplicate is skipped"},{"id":"late-duplicate-is-skipped","kind":"behaviour","title":"A late duplicate is skipped"},{"id":"identity-is-the-message-id","kind":"behaviour","title":"Same content, different id, is new"},{"id":"failed-effect-can-be-redelivered","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failed effect can be retried"},{"id":"concurrent-duplicates-apply-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"Concurrent duplicates apply once"},{"id":"concurrent-distinct-messages-all-apply","kind":"behaviour","title":"Concurrent distinct messages all apply"}],"hints":[[{"text":"At-least-once delivery means the consumer must remember which message ids it has handled. Check, apply and mark are one step: nothing may come between them.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep a `Set<String>` of processed ids. Look the id up, call `ledger.credit`, and only then add the id, all inside one critical section. If `credit` throws, the id is never added.","type":"p"}],[{"language":"java","lines":["synchronized boolean handle(Deposit m) {","    if (processed.contains(m.messageId())) return false;","    ledger.credit(m.account(), m.cents());","    processed.add(m.messageId());","    return true;","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"idempotent-consumer","kind":"fix","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Support.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Support.java","source":"record Deposit(String messageId, String account, long cents) { }\n\ninterface Ledger {\n    void credit(String account, long cents);\n}\n"},{"name":"AccountConsumer.java","source":"import java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\n// The broker delivers at least once: acks get lost, producers publish\n// twice. Today every delivery credits the account again.\nfinal class AccountConsumer {\n    private final Ledger ledger;\n    private final Set<String> processed = new HashSet<>();\n\n    AccountConsumer(Ledger ledger) { this.ledger = ledger; }\n\n    /** True if the deposit was applied, false if it was a duplicate. */\n    synchronized boolean handle(Deposit m) {\n        if (processed.contains(m.messageId())) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        ledger.credit(m.account(), m.cents());\n        processed.add(m.messageId());\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Support.java","source":"record Deposit(String messageId, String account, long cents) { }\n\ninterface Ledger {\n    void credit(String account, long cents);\n}\n"},{"name":"AccountConsumer.java","source":"// The broker delivers at least once: acks get lost, producers publish\n// twice. Today every delivery credits the account again.\nfinal class AccountConsumer {\n    private final Ledger ledger;\n\n    AccountConsumer(Ledger ledger) { this.ledger = ledger; }\n\n    /** True if the deposit was applied, false if it was a duplicate. */\n    boolean handle(Deposit m) {\n        ledger.credit(m.account(), m.cents());\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"The broker redelivers messages, and each redelivery credits the account again.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Fix `AccountConsumer.handle(Deposit)` so handling a message twice has the effect of handling it once. `Deposit` and `Ledger` are given; the constructor stays.","type":"p"},{"items":["Return `true` when the deposit was applied, `false` for a message id already processed.","Identify a message by `messageId`, not by its content.","If `ledger.credit` throws, the id must **not** count as processed: the redelivery has to be applied.","The same message arriving on several threads at once is applied exactly once; different messages must not be lost."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"IdempotentKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass IdempotentKataTest {\n    static final class Books implements Ledger {\n        final Map<String, Long> balances = new TreeMap<>();\n        boolean failNext;\n        long pauseMs;\n        int credits;\n\n        public void credit(String account, long cents) {\n            if (pauseMs > 0) Stress.pause(pauseMs);   // widens the race window\n            synchronized (this) {\n                if (failNext) {\n                    failNext = false;\n                    throw new IllegalStateException(\"db down\");\n                }\n                credits++;\n                balances.merge(account, cents, Long::sum);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    final Books books = new Books();\n    final AccountConsumer consumer = new AccountConsumer(books);\n\n    @Check(id = \"first-delivery-applied\")\n    void firstDeliveryApplied() {\n        Expect.isTrue(consumer.handle(new Deposit(\"m1\", \"alice\", 500)),\n            \"a first delivery should be applied\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"alice\", 500L), books.balances, \"balances\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"duplicate-is-skipped\")\n    void duplicateIsSkipped() {\n        Deposit m1 = new Deposit(\"m1\", \"alice\", 500);\n        consumer.handle(m1);\n        Expect.isTrue(!consumer.handle(m1), \"a redelivered message should report false\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"alice\", 500L), books.balances, \"balances after a duplicate\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"late-duplicate-is-skipped\")\n    void lateDuplicateIsSkipped() {\n        consumer.handle(new Deposit(\"m1\", \"alice\", 500));\n        consumer.handle(new Deposit(\"m2\", \"bob\", 300));\n        consumer.handle(new Deposit(\"m3\", \"alice\", 250));\n        Expect.isTrue(!consumer.handle(new Deposit(\"m1\", \"alice\", 500)),\n            \"m1 redelivered after other messages\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"alice\", 750L, \"bob\", 300L), books.balances, \"balances\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"identity-is-the-message-id\")\n    void identityIsTheMessageId() {\n        Expect.isTrue(consumer.handle(new Deposit(\"m1\", \"alice\", 500)), \"m1\");\n        Expect.isTrue(consumer.handle(new Deposit(\"m2\", \"alice\", 500)),\n            \"a different message with identical content is a different deposit\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"alice\", 1000L), books.balances, \"balances\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"failed-effect-can-be-redelivered\")\n    void failedEffectCanBeRedelivered() {\n        Deposit m1 = new Deposit(\"m1\", \"alice\", 500);\n        books.failNext = true;\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> consumer.handle(m1),\n            \"a delivery whose effect fails\");\n        Expect.isTrue(consumer.handle(m1),\n            \"the redelivery after a failure must be applied, not skipped\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"alice\", 500L), books.balances, \"balances\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"concurrent-duplicates-apply-once\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void concurrentDuplicatesApplyOnce() {\n        books.pauseMs = 30;\n        Deposit m1 = new Deposit(\"m1\", \"alice\", 500);\n        List<Boolean> applied = Stress.race(6, () -> consumer.handle(m1));\n        long wins = applied.stream().filter(a -> a).count();\n        Expect.equal(1L, wins, \"deliveries reported as applied\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"alice\", 500L), books.balances,\n            \"balances after the same message arrived on 6 threads at once\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"concurrent-distinct-messages-all-apply\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void concurrentDistinctMessagesAllApply() {\n        java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger n =\n            new java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger();\n        List<Boolean> applied = Stress.race(6, () ->\n            consumer.handle(new Deposit(\"m\" + n.incrementAndGet(), \"alice\", 100)));\n        Expect.isTrue(applied.stream().allMatch(a -> a),\n            \"six different messages should all be applied\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(\"alice\", 600L), books.balances, \"balances\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Stop crediting duplicate deposits twice"},{"checks":[{"id":"order-is-saved-and-announced","kind":"behaviour","title":"A placed order is saved and announced"},{"id":"rollback-announces-nothing","kind":"behaviour","title":"A rejected order announces nothing"},{"id":"messages-keep-order","kind":"behaviour","title":"Messages arrive in order"},{"id":"delivered-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"Nothing is delivered twice"},{"id":"service-does-not-publish","kind":"design","title":"OrderService no longer talks to the broker"},{"id":"order-and-row-commit-together","kind":"design","title":"Order and outbox row share one transaction"},{"id":"relay-retries-until-acked","kind":"design","title":"The relay keeps rows until acknowledged"},{"id":"relay-stops-at-first-failure","kind":"design","title":"The relay preserves order across failures"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Two systems cannot commit together, but one database can. What if the \"message to send\" becomes a row written in the same transaction as the order? Who then sends it?","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`OrderService` calls `tx.saveOrder` and `tx.enqueue` inside one `inTransaction`. A new `Relay` reads `db.pending()`, publishes each row, and only afterwards calls `db.markPublished`. `Shop` connects them.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The relay loop:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["for (Message row : db.pending()) {","    try { broker.publish(row); }","    catch (IOException e) { return sent; }","    db.markPublished(row.id());","    sent++;","}","return sent;"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"transactional-outbox","kind":"refactor","minutes":25,"readOnly":["Db.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Db.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.function.Consumer;\n\nrecord Message(long id, String type, String payload) { }\n\ninterface Broker {\n    void publish(Message message) throws IOException;\n}\n\n// A tiny database: one transaction commits orders and outbox rows together.\nfinal class Db {\n    final class Tx {\n        private final List<String> orders = new ArrayList<>();\n        private final List<Message> rows = new ArrayList<>();\n\n        void saveOrder(String id) {\n            if (Db.this.orders.contains(id) || orders.contains(id)) {\n                throw new IllegalStateException(\"duplicate order \" + id);\n            }\n            orders.add(id);\n        }\n\n        void enqueue(String type, String payload) {\n            rows.add(new Message(++seq, type, payload));\n        }\n    }\n\n    final List<String> orders = new ArrayList<>();\n    final List<Message> outbox = new ArrayList<>();\n    private final Set<Long> published = new HashSet<>();\n    private long seq;\n\n    /** Commits on return, rolls everything back if work throws. */\n    boolean inTransaction(Consumer<Tx> work) {\n        Tx tx = new Tx();\n        try {\n            work.accept(tx);\n        } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        orders.addAll(tx.orders);\n        outbox.addAll(tx.rows);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /** Outbox rows not yet acknowledged by the broker, oldest first. */\n    List<Message> pending() {\n        return outbox.stream()\n            .filter(m -> !published.contains(m.id())).toList();\n    }\n\n    void markPublished(long id) {\n        published.add(id);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"OrderService.java","source":"final class OrderService {\n    private final Db db;\n\n    OrderService(Db db) {\n        this.db = db;\n    }\n\n    boolean place(String id) {\n        return db.inTransaction(tx -> {\n            tx.saveOrder(id);\n            tx.enqueue(\"OrderPlaced\", id);\n        });\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Relay.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\n\nfinal class Relay {\n    private final Db db;\n    private final Broker broker;\n\n    Relay(Db db, Broker broker) {\n        this.db = db;\n        this.broker = broker;\n    }\n\n    /** Publishes pending rows oldest first; stops at the first failure. */\n    int pump() {\n        int sent = 0;\n        for (Message row : db.pending()) {\n            try {\n                broker.publish(row);\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                return sent;\n            }\n            db.markPublished(row.id());\n            sent++;\n        }\n        return sent;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Shop.java","source":"final class Shop {\n    private final OrderService orders;\n    private final Relay relay;\n\n    Shop(Db db, Broker broker) {\n        this.orders = new OrderService(db);\n        this.relay = new Relay(db, broker);\n    }\n\n    boolean place(String id) {\n        return orders.place(id);\n    }\n\n    int deliver() {\n        return relay.pump();\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Db.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.function.Consumer;\n\nrecord Message(long id, String type, String payload) { }\n\ninterface Broker {\n    void publish(Message message) throws IOException;\n}\n\n// A tiny database: one transaction commits orders and outbox rows together.\nfinal class Db {\n    final class Tx {\n        private final List<String> orders = new ArrayList<>();\n        private final List<Message> rows = new ArrayList<>();\n\n        void saveOrder(String id) {\n            if (Db.this.orders.contains(id) || orders.contains(id)) {\n                throw new IllegalStateException(\"duplicate order \" + id);\n            }\n            orders.add(id);\n        }\n\n        void enqueue(String type, String payload) {\n            rows.add(new Message(++seq, type, payload));\n        }\n    }\n\n    final List<String> orders = new ArrayList<>();\n    final List<Message> outbox = new ArrayList<>();\n    private final Set<Long> published = new HashSet<>();\n    private long seq;\n\n    /** Commits on return, rolls everything back if work throws. */\n    boolean inTransaction(Consumer<Tx> work) {\n        Tx tx = new Tx();\n        try {\n            work.accept(tx);\n        } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        orders.addAll(tx.orders);\n        outbox.addAll(tx.rows);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /** Outbox rows not yet acknowledged by the broker, oldest first. */\n    List<Message> pending() {\n        return outbox.stream()\n            .filter(m -> !published.contains(m.id())).toList();\n    }\n\n    void markPublished(long id) {\n        published.add(id);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"OrderService.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\n\n// Places orders and tells the world about them: two writes, no shared fate.\nfinal class OrderService {\n    private final Db db;\n    private final Broker broker;\n\n    OrderService(Db db, Broker broker) {\n        this.db = db;\n        this.broker = broker;\n    }\n\n    boolean place(String id) {\n        boolean saved = db.inTransaction(tx -> tx.saveOrder(id));\n        if (!saved) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        try {\n            broker.publish(new Message(0, \"OrderPlaced\", id));\n        } catch (IOException e) {\n            // swallowed: the order exists but nobody hears about it\n        }\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers use this entry point. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Shop {\n    private final OrderService orders;\n\n    Shop(Db db, Broker broker) {\n        this.orders = new OrderService(db, broker);\n    }\n\n    boolean place(String id) {\n        return orders.place(id);\n    }\n\n    /** Delivers whatever is waiting to the broker; returns how many. */\n    int deliver() {\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`OrderService` saves the order, then publishes; if publishing fails, the event is lost.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Write the message into the **outbox** in the same transaction as the order, and let a **relay** publish it later. `Shop.place` and `Shop.deliver` must keep working for callers. `Db`, `Message` and `Broker` are given.","type":"p"},{"items":["`OrderService(Db db)`: `place(id)` saves the order and calls `tx.enqueue(\"OrderPlaced\", id)` in one `inTransaction`. It must not know the broker.","`Relay(Db db, Broker broker)`: `int pump()` publishes `db.pending()` oldest first and calls `markPublished(id)` only after the broker accepted it. Stop at the first `IOException`; return the number sent.","`Shop(db, broker)` wires both; `deliver()` calls `pump()`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"TransactionalOutboxKataTest.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass TransactionalOutboxKataTest {\n    static final class Recorder implements Broker {\n        final List<String> seen = new ArrayList<>();\n        int failFrom = -1;     // calls with index >= failFrom fail while 'down'\n        boolean down;\n        int calls;\n\n        public void publish(Message m) throws IOException {\n            calls++;\n            if (down && calls >= failFrom) throw new IOException(\"broker down\");\n            seen.add(m.type() + \":\" + m.payload());\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"order-is-saved-and-announced\")\n    void savedAndAnnounced() {\n        Db db = new Db();\n        Recorder broker = new Recorder();\n        Shop shop = new Shop(db, broker);\n        Expect.isTrue(shop.place(\"o-1\"), \"place(o-1) should succeed\");\n        shop.deliver();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"o-1\"), db.orders, \"saved orders\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"OrderPlaced:o-1\"), broker.seen, \"messages the broker received\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rollback-announces-nothing\")\n    void rollbackAnnouncesNothing() {\n        Db db = new Db();\n        Recorder broker = new Recorder();\n        Shop shop = new Shop(db, broker);\n        shop.place(\"o-1\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!shop.place(\"o-1\"), \"a duplicate order is rejected\");\n        shop.deliver();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"OrderPlaced:o-1\"), broker.seen, \"messages the broker received\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"o-1\"), db.orders, \"saved orders\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"messages-keep-order\")\n    void messagesKeepOrder() {\n        Db db = new Db();\n        Recorder broker = new Recorder();\n        Shop shop = new Shop(db, broker);\n        shop.place(\"a\");\n        shop.place(\"b\");\n        shop.place(\"c\");\n        shop.deliver();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"OrderPlaced:a\", \"OrderPlaced:b\", \"OrderPlaced:c\"), broker.seen, \"delivery order\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"delivered-once\")\n    void deliveredOnce() {\n        Db db = new Db();\n        Recorder broker = new Recorder();\n        Shop shop = new Shop(db, broker);\n        shop.place(\"a\");\n        shop.deliver();\n        Expect.equal(0, shop.deliver(), \"messages delivered by a second call\");\n        Expect.equal(1, broker.seen.size(), \"messages the broker received\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-does-not-publish\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void serviceDoesNotPublish() {\n        var svc = Source.type(\"OrderService\");\n        Expect.none(svc.mentions(\"Broker\"), \"OrderService still talks to the Broker\");\n        Expect.none(svc.calls(\"publish\"), \"OrderService still publishes directly\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(Types.named(\"OrderService\"), Broker.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"OrderService still holds a Broker\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"order-and-row-commit-together\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void commitTogether() throws Throwable {\n        Db db = new Db();\n        Class<?> cls = Types.named(\"OrderService\");\n        Object svc = Types.create(Types.constructor(cls, Db.class), db);\n        Method place = Types.method(cls, \"place\", String.class);\n        Expect.equal(true, Types.call(place, svc, \"o-1\"), \"place(o-1)\");\n        Expect.equal(1, db.orders.size(), \"orders saved\");\n        Expect.equal(1, db.outbox.size(), \"outbox rows written in the same transaction\");\n        Expect.equal(\"OrderPlaced\", db.outbox.get(0).type(), \"the row's type\");\n        Expect.equal(\"o-1\", db.outbox.get(0).payload(), \"the row's payload\");\n        Expect.equal(false, Types.call(place, svc, \"o-1\"), \"a duplicate place(o-1)\");\n        Expect.equal(1, db.outbox.size(), \"A rolled-back order must leave no outbox row\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"relay-retries-until-acked\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void relayRetries() throws Throwable {\n        Db db = new Db();\n        Recorder broker = new Recorder();\n        Class<?> svcType = Types.named(\"OrderService\");\n        Object svc = Types.create(Types.constructor(svcType, Db.class), db);\n        Types.call(Types.method(svcType, \"place\", String.class), svc, \"o-1\");\n        Class<?> relayType = Types.named(\"Relay\");\n        Object relay = Types.create(Types.constructor(relayType, Db.class, Broker.class), db, broker);\n        Method pump = Types.method(relayType, \"pump\");\n        broker.down = true;\n        broker.failFrom = 1;\n        Expect.equal(0, Types.call(pump, relay), \"rows sent while the broker is down\");\n        Expect.equal(1, db.pending().size(), \"A row that was not acknowledged must stay pending\");\n        broker.down = false;\n        Expect.equal(1, Types.call(pump, relay), \"rows sent once the broker is back\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"OrderPlaced:o-1\"), broker.seen, \"messages received\");\n        Expect.equal(0, Types.call(pump, relay), \"rows sent by a third pump (no duplicates)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"relay-stops-at-first-failure\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void relayKeepsOrder() throws Throwable {\n        Db db = new Db();\n        Recorder broker = new Recorder();\n        Class<?> svcType = Types.named(\"OrderService\");\n        Object svc = Types.create(Types.constructor(svcType, Db.class), db);\n        Method place = Types.method(svcType, \"place\", String.class);\n        for (String id : List.of(\"a\", \"b\", \"c\")) Types.call(place, svc, id);\n        Class<?> relayType = Types.named(\"Relay\");\n        Object relay = Types.create(Types.constructor(relayType, Db.class, Broker.class), db, broker);\n        Method pump = Types.method(relayType, \"pump\");\n        broker.down = true;\n        broker.failFrom = 2;      // the second publish fails\n        Expect.equal(1, Types.call(pump, relay), \"rows sent before the failure\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"OrderPlaced:a\"), broker.seen, \"messages received\");\n        broker.down = false;\n        Expect.equal(2, Types.call(pump, relay), \"rows sent by the next pump\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"OrderPlaced:a\", \"OrderPlaced:b\", \"OrderPlaced:c\"), broker.seen,\n            \"Order must be preserved across a failure\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Replace the dual write with an outbox"},{"checks":[{"id":"happy-path","kind":"behaviour","title":"All steps succeed, nothing is undone"},{"id":"undo-in-reverse","kind":"behaviour","title":"Compensations run newest first"},{"id":"failed-step-not-undone","kind":"behaviour","title":"The failed step is not compensated"},{"id":"stops-at-failure","kind":"behaviour","title":"Later steps never run after a failure"},{"id":"undo-continues-after-failure","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failing compensation does not stop the rest"},{"id":"empty-saga","kind":"behaviour","title":"An empty saga succeeds"},{"id":"saga-uses-compensation","kind":"design","title":"Saga drives each step's action and compensation"},{"id":"saga-knows-no-step-names","kind":"design","title":"The workflow is data, not branches"},{"id":"saga-takes-step-list","kind":"design","title":"Saga is built from a list of steps"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Which steps need undoing when step N fails? Only the ones that already succeeded, and the most recent one first. What data structure hands things back newest first?","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep a `Deque<Step>` of completed steps and `push` after each success. On failure, `pop` until empty, running `compensation()` inside its own try/catch so one bad undo cannot stop the others.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Compensation loop:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["while (!done.isEmpty()) {","    Step step = done.pop();","    try {","        step.compensation().run();","        log.add(\"undo \" + step.name());","    } catch (RuntimeException e) {","        log.add(\"stuck \" + step.name());","    }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"saga","kind":"implement","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Step.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Step.java","source":"// One local transaction and the semantic undo that pairs with it.\nrecord Step(String name, Runnable action, Runnable compensation) { }\n"},{"name":"Saga.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayDeque;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Deque;\nimport java.util.List;\n\nfinal class Saga {\n    private final List<Step> steps;\n    private final List<String> log = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    Saga(List<Step> steps) {\n        this.steps = List.copyOf(steps);\n    }\n\n    boolean run() {\n        Deque<Step> done = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        for (Step step : steps) {\n            try {\n                step.action().run();\n            } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n                log.add(\"fail \" + step.name());\n                compensate(done);\n                return false;\n            }\n            log.add(\"do \" + step.name());\n            done.push(step);\n        }\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    private void compensate(Deque<Step> done) {\n        while (!done.isEmpty()) {\n            Step step = done.pop();\n            try {\n                step.compensation().run();\n                log.add(\"undo \" + step.name());\n            } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n                log.add(\"stuck \" + step.name());\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    List<String> log() {\n        return List.copyOf(log);\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Step.java","source":"// One local transaction and the semantic undo that pairs with it.\nrecord Step(String name, Runnable action, Runnable compensation) { }\n"},{"name":"Saga.java","source":"import java.util.List;\n\n// Orchestrates a checkout across services that share no transaction.\nfinal class Saga {\n    Saga(List<Step> steps) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Runs the steps in order. Returns true when every step succeeded. */\n    boolean run() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** What happened, in order: \"do x\", \"fail x\", \"undo x\", \"stuck x\". */\n    List<String> log() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"A checkout touches services that share no transaction, so a failure must be undone by hand.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `Saga` in `Saga.java`. `Step` is given and must not change.","type":"p"},{"items":["`new Saga(List<Step>)`; `run()` executes each `action()` in order and returns `true` if all succeed.","When an action throws a `RuntimeException`, stop, then run the `compensation()` of the steps that **succeeded**, newest first. The failed step is not compensated. `run()` returns `false`.","If a compensation throws, keep going with the older ones.","`log()` lists events in order: `do x`, `fail x`, `undo x`, or `stuck x` (a compensation that threw)."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"SagaKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass SagaKataTest {\n    static final List<String> trace = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    static Step ok(String name) {\n        return new Step(name, () -> { }, () -> trace.add(\"comp \" + name));\n    }\n\n    static Step failing(String name) {\n        return new Step(name, () -> { throw new IllegalStateException(name); },\n            () -> trace.add(\"comp \" + name));\n    }\n\n    static Step brokenUndo(String name) {\n        return new Step(name, () -> { },\n            () -> { throw new IllegalStateException(\"undo \" + name); });\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"happy-path\")\n    void happyPath() {\n        trace.clear();\n        Saga saga = new Saga(List.of(ok(\"reserve\"), ok(\"charge\"), ok(\"ship\")));\n        Expect.isTrue(saga.run(), \"a saga whose steps all succeed returns true\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"do reserve\", \"do charge\", \"do ship\"), saga.log(), \"the log\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), trace, \"compensations that ran\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"undo-in-reverse\")\n    void undoInReverse() {\n        trace.clear();\n        Saga saga = new Saga(List.of(ok(\"reserve\"), ok(\"hold\"), failing(\"charge\"), ok(\"ship\")));\n        Expect.isTrue(!saga.run(), \"a failing step makes run() return false\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"comp hold\", \"comp reserve\"), trace,\n            \"compensations should run newest first\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"do reserve\", \"do hold\", \"fail charge\", \"undo hold\", \"undo reserve\"),\n            saga.log(), \"the log\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"failed-step-not-undone\")\n    void failedStepNotUndone() {\n        trace.clear();\n        new Saga(List.of(failing(\"charge\"), ok(\"ship\"))).run();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), trace, \"compensations: nothing succeeded, so nothing to undo\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"stops-at-failure\")\n    void stopsAtFailure() {\n        trace.clear();\n        int[] shipped = {0};\n        Step ship = new Step(\"ship\", () -> shipped[0]++, () -> { });\n        new Saga(List.of(failing(\"charge\"), ship)).run();\n        Expect.equal(0, shipped[0], \"steps after the failure that ran\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"undo-continues-after-failure\")\n    void undoContinues() {\n        trace.clear();\n        Saga saga = new Saga(List.of(ok(\"a\"), brokenUndo(\"b\"), ok(\"c\"), failing(\"d\")));\n        Expect.isTrue(!saga.run(), \"run() still reports failure\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"comp c\", \"comp a\"), trace,\n            \"a compensation that throws must not stop the older ones\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"do a\", \"do b\", \"do c\", \"fail d\", \"undo c\", \"stuck b\", \"undo a\"),\n            saga.log(), \"the log\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"empty-saga\")\n    void emptySaga() {\n        Saga saga = new Saga(List.of());\n        Expect.isTrue(saga.run(), \"an empty saga succeeds\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(), saga.log(), \"the log\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"saga-uses-compensation\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void usesCompensation() {\n        var saga = Source.type(\"Saga\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!saga.calls(\"compensation\").isEmpty(),\n            \"Saga never calls a step's compensation()\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!saga.calls(\"action\").isEmpty(), \"Saga never calls a step's action()\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"saga-knows-no-step-names\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void knowsNoNames() {\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"Saga\").comparedStrings(),\n            \"Saga compares step names; the workflow should be data, not code\");\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"Saga\").switches(), \"Saga switches on something\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"saga-takes-step-list\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void takesList() {\n        Constructor<?> c = Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Saga\"), List.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(c != null, \"Saga(List<Step>) is missing\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Orchestrate a saga with compensation"},{"checks":[{"id":"second-read-is-a-hit","kind":"behaviour","title":"A second read is served from the cache"},{"id":"rename-is-visible-at-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"A rename shows up on the next read"},{"id":"rename-writes-before-it-evicts","kind":"behaviour","title":"Write first, then evict"},{"id":"missing-rows-are-not-cached","kind":"behaviour","title":"Absence is not cached"},{"id":"ttl-bounds-staleness","kind":"behaviour","title":"The TTL still bounds staleness"},{"id":"rename-evicts-only-that-user","kind":"behaviour","title":"A rename evicts only its own entry"},{"id":"concurrent-readers-agree","kind":"behaviour","title":"Concurrent readers agree"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Two different bugs, one cause: the cache is trusted more than the store. One is about what happens *after a write*, the other about what a *miss* is allowed to store.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"In `rename`, after `store.save`, remove only that key from `cache`. In `get`, put an entry only when the store returned a row; an empty `Optional` must leave the cache untouched.","type":"p"}],[{"language":"java","lines":["row.ifPresent(n -> cache.put(id, new Entry(n, expiresAt)));","return row;","// ...","store.save(id, name);","cache.remove(id);"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"cache-aside","kind":"fix","minutes":15,"readOnly":["Store.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Store.java","source":"import java.util.Optional;\n\ninterface UserStore {\n    Optional<String> find(String id);\n    void save(String id, String name);\n}\n"},{"name":"UserService.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.function.LongSupplier;\n\n// Reads go through a cache with a TTL; the store is the truth.\n// Support wants a rename to show up at once, and a new user too.\nfinal class UserService {\n    private record Entry(String name, long expiresAt) { }\n\n    private final UserStore store;\n    private final LongSupplier clock;\n    private final long ttlMs;\n    private final Map<String, Entry> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n    UserService(UserStore store, LongSupplier clock, long ttlMs) {\n        this.store = store;\n        this.clock = clock;\n        this.ttlMs = ttlMs;\n    }\n\n    Optional<String> get(String id) {\n        Entry hit = cache.get(id);\n        if (hit != null && hit.expiresAt() > clock.getAsLong()) {\n            return Optional.of(hit.name());\n        }\n        Optional<String> row = store.find(id);\n        long expiresAt = clock.getAsLong() + ttlMs;\n        row.ifPresent(n -> cache.put(id, new Entry(n, expiresAt)));\n        return row;\n    }\n\n    void rename(String id, String name) {\n        store.save(id, name);\n        cache.remove(id);\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Store.java","source":"import java.util.Optional;\n\ninterface UserStore {\n    Optional<String> find(String id);\n    void save(String id, String name);\n}\n"},{"name":"UserService.java","source":"import java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.function.LongSupplier;\n\n// Reads go through a cache with a TTL; the store is the truth.\n// Support wants a rename to show up at once, and a new user too.\nfinal class UserService {\n    private record Entry(Optional<String> name, long expiresAt) { }\n\n    private final UserStore store;\n    private final LongSupplier clock;\n    private final long ttlMs;\n    private final Map<String, Entry> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n\n    UserService(UserStore store, LongSupplier clock, long ttlMs) {\n        this.store = store;\n        this.clock = clock;\n        this.ttlMs = ttlMs;\n    }\n\n    Optional<String> get(String id) {\n        Entry hit = cache.get(id);\n        if (hit != null && hit.expiresAt() > clock.getAsLong()) {\n            return hit.name();\n        }\n        Optional<String> row = store.find(id);\n        cache.put(id, new Entry(row, clock.getAsLong() + ttlMs));\n        return row;\n    }\n\n    void rename(String id, String name) {\n        store.save(id, name);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Support renames a user, reloads the page, and still sees the old name.","type":"lead"},{"text":"`UserService` is a cache-aside layer over a `UserStore` (given): read the cache first, fall back to the store on a miss, and keep the store as the source of truth. It has two bugs. Fix them without changing any signature.","type":"p"},{"items":["After `rename(id, name)` the next `get(id)` must return the new name. Write the store first, then evict that one entry.","A user that does not exist yet must not be remembered as absent: once it is created, `get` finds it.","The TTL and the injected clock stay as they are."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"CacheKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Optional;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass CacheKataTest {\n    static final class FakeStore implements UserStore {\n        final Map<String, String> rows = new HashMap<>();\n        int reads;\n        Runnable beforeSave = () -> { };\n\n        public synchronized Optional<String> find(String id) {\n            reads++;\n            return Optional.ofNullable(rows.get(id));\n        }\n\n        public void save(String id, String name) {\n            beforeSave.run();\n            synchronized (this) {\n                rows.put(id, name);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    final AtomicLong now = new AtomicLong();\n    final FakeStore db = new FakeStore();\n    final UserService users = new UserService(db, now::get, 60_000);\n\n    @Check(id = \"second-read-is-a-hit\")\n    void secondReadIsAHit() {\n        db.rows.put(\"u1\", \"Ada\");\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"Ada\"), users.get(\"u1\"), \"first read\");\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"Ada\"), users.get(\"u1\"), \"second read\");\n        Expect.equal(1, db.reads, \"store reads for two gets\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rename-is-visible-at-once\")\n    void renameIsVisibleAtOnce() {\n        db.rows.put(\"u1\", \"Ada\");\n        users.get(\"u1\");\n        users.rename(\"u1\", \"Grace\");\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"Grace\"), users.get(\"u1\"),\n            \"a read right after rename (the cache still holds the old name)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rename-writes-before-it-evicts\")\n    void renameWritesBeforeItEvicts() {\n        db.rows.put(\"u1\", \"Ada\");\n        users.get(\"u1\");\n        // A reader slips in while the write is in progress and re-fills the cache.\n        db.beforeSave = () -> users.get(\"u1\");\n        users.rename(\"u1\", \"Grace\");\n        db.beforeSave = () -> { };\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"Grace\"), users.get(\"u1\"),\n            \"a read after rename when a reader raced the write \"\n                + \"(write the store first, then evict)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"missing-rows-are-not-cached\")\n    void missingRowsAreNotCached() {\n        Expect.equal(Optional.empty(), users.get(\"u9\"), \"a user that does not exist yet\");\n        db.rows.put(\"u9\", \"Lin\");\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"Lin\"), users.get(\"u9\"),\n            \"the same user after it was created (do not cache absence)\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"ttl-bounds-staleness\")\n    void ttlBoundsStaleness() {\n        db.rows.put(\"u1\", \"Ada\");\n        users.get(\"u1\");\n        db.rows.put(\"u1\", \"Grace\");          // changed behind the cache's back\n        now.set(59_999);\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"Ada\"), users.get(\"u1\"), \"a read before the TTL ends\");\n        now.set(60_000);\n        Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"Grace\"), users.get(\"u1\"), \"a read once the TTL ended\");\n        Expect.equal(2, db.reads, \"store reads\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"rename-evicts-only-that-user\")\n    void renameEvictsOnlyThatUser() {\n        db.rows.put(\"u1\", \"Ada\");\n        db.rows.put(\"u2\", \"Bob\");\n        users.get(\"u1\");\n        users.get(\"u2\");\n        users.rename(\"u1\", \"Grace\");\n        int before = db.reads;\n        users.get(\"u2\");\n        Expect.equal(before, db.reads, \"reading u2 after renaming u1 should still be a hit\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"concurrent-readers-agree\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void concurrentReadersAgree() {\n        db.rows.put(\"u1\", \"Ada\");\n        List<Optional<String>> all = Stress.race(8, () -> users.get(\"u1\"));\n        for (Optional<String> r : all) {\n            Expect.equal(Optional.of(\"Ada\"), r, \"a concurrent read\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Fix the stale profile cache"},{"checks":[{"id":"worker-drains-until-stop","kind":"behaviour","title":"A worker stops at the poison pill"},{"id":"worker-survives-failing-job","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failing job does not kill the worker"},{"id":"worker-ends-on-interrupt","kind":"behaviour","title":"An interrupt ends an idle worker"},{"id":"each-job-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"Every job is handled exactly once"},{"id":"jobs-run-in-parallel","kind":"behaviour","title":"Workers really compete in parallel"},{"id":"shutdown-drains-queue","kind":"behaviour","title":"shutdown() waits for queued jobs"},{"id":"pool-shares-one-queue","kind":"design","title":"All workers share one queue"},{"id":"no-polling-or-locks","kind":"design","title":"Waiting is done by the queue, not by sleeping"},{"id":"worker-keeps-no-job-state","kind":"design","title":"Workers share nothing mutable but the queue"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The queue is the only thing the workers share, and `take()` already makes an idle worker wait. Which single worker gets a job is the queue's decision, not yours.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`Worker.run` loops on `queue.take()` and returns on `Job.STOP`. `WorkerPool` owns the `LinkedBlockingQueue`, starts N threads running `Worker`, and in `shutdown` adds one `STOP` per worker then joins.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Worker loop:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["try {","    while (true) {","        Job job = queue.take();","        if (job == Job.STOP) return;","        try { handler.handle(job); } catch (Exception e) { }","    }","} catch (InterruptedException e) {","    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"competing-consumers","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"readOnly":["Job.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Job.java","source":"// A unit of work. STOP is the poison pill that tells one worker to quit.\nrecord Job(int id, int cost) {\n    static final Job STOP = new Job(-1, 0);\n}\n\n// What a worker does with each job. It may throw.\ninterface JobHandler {\n    void handle(Job job) throws Exception;\n}\n"},{"name":"Worker.java","source":"import java.util.Objects;\nimport java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\n\nfinal class Worker implements Runnable {\n    private final BlockingQueue<Job> queue;\n    private final JobHandler handler;\n\n    Worker(BlockingQueue<Job> queue, JobHandler handler) {\n        this.queue = Objects.requireNonNull(queue, \"queue\");\n        this.handler = Objects.requireNonNull(handler, \"handler\");\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void run() {\n        try {\n            while (true) {\n                Job job = queue.take();\n                if (job == Job.STOP) {\n                    return;\n                }\n                try {\n                    handler.handle(job);\n                } catch (Exception e) {\n                    // one bad job must not kill the consumer\n                }\n            }\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"WorkerPool.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.LinkedBlockingQueue;\n\nfinal class WorkerPool {\n    private final BlockingQueue<Job> queue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();\n    private final List<Thread> threads = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    WorkerPool(int workers, JobHandler handler) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < workers; i++) {\n            Thread t = Thread.ofVirtual().unstarted(new Worker(queue, handler));\n            threads.add(t);\n            t.start();\n        }\n    }\n\n    void submit(Job job) {\n        queue.add(job);\n    }\n\n    void shutdown() throws InterruptedException {\n        for (int i = 0; i < threads.size(); i++) {\n            queue.add(Job.STOP);\n        }\n        for (Thread t : threads) {\n            t.join();\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Job.java","source":"// A unit of work. STOP is the poison pill that tells one worker to quit.\nrecord Job(int id, int cost) {\n    static final Job STOP = new Job(-1, 0);\n}\n\n// What a worker does with each job. It may throw.\ninterface JobHandler {\n    void handle(Job job) throws Exception;\n}\n"},{"name":"Worker.java","source":"import java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\n\n// One consumer: takes jobs from a queue it shares with its siblings.\nfinal class Worker implements Runnable {\n    Worker(BlockingQueue<Job> queue, JobHandler handler) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void run() {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"WorkerPool.java","source":"// N workers competing for one queue.\nfinal class WorkerPool {\n    WorkerPool(int workers, JobHandler handler) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    void submit(Job job) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Lets queued jobs finish, stops every worker, returns when all ended. */\n    void shutdown() throws InterruptedException {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"stressRuns":20,"task":[{"text":"Several workers pull from one queue; each job goes to exactly one of them.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `Worker` and `WorkerPool`. `Job`, `Job.STOP` and `JobHandler` are given and must not change.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Worker(BlockingQueue<Job>, JobHandler)` is a `Runnable`: it blocks on the queue, calls the handler for each job, and returns when it takes `Job.STOP`.","A handler exception skips that job only. An interrupt ends the worker and keeps the interrupt flag.","`WorkerPool(int workers, JobHandler)` starts that many workers on one shared queue. `submit(Job)` enqueues.","`shutdown()` lets queued jobs finish, stops every worker with one `Job.STOP` each, and returns once they have ended."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"CompetingConsumersKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;\nimport java.util.concurrent.LinkedBlockingQueue;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass CompetingConsumersKataTest {\n    @Check(id = \"worker-drains-until-stop\")\n    void workerDrainsUntilStop() {\n        BlockingQueue<Job> queue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();\n        List<Integer> seen = new java.util.ArrayList<>();\n        queue.add(new Job(1, 1));\n        queue.add(new Job(2, 1));\n        queue.add(Job.STOP);\n        queue.add(new Job(3, 1));\n        new Worker(queue, job -> seen.add(job.id())).run();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(1, 2), seen, \"jobs handled before the poison pill\");\n        Expect.equal(1, queue.size(), \"jobs left behind the poison pill\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"worker-survives-failing-job\")\n    void workerSurvivesFailure() {\n        BlockingQueue<Job> queue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();\n        List<Integer> seen = new java.util.ArrayList<>();\n        queue.add(new Job(1, 1));\n        queue.add(new Job(2, 1));\n        queue.add(new Job(3, 1));\n        queue.add(Job.STOP);\n        new Worker(queue, job -> {\n            if (job.id() == 2) throw new IllegalStateException(\"poison\");\n            seen.add(job.id());\n        }).run();\n        Expect.equal(List.of(1, 3), seen, \"jobs handled around a failing one\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"worker-ends-on-interrupt\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void workerEndsOnInterrupt() throws Exception {\n        BlockingQueue<Job> queue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();\n        Thread t = new Thread(new Worker(queue, job -> { }));\n        t.setDaemon(true);\n        t.start();\n        Stress.pause(20);\n        t.interrupt();\n        t.join(2000);\n        Expect.isTrue(!t.isAlive(), \"A worker blocked on an empty queue should stop when interrupted\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"each-job-once\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void eachJobOnce() throws Exception {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> handled = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n        WorkerPool pool = new WorkerPool(4, job -> handled.merge(job.id(), 1, Integer::sum));\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 300; i++) pool.submit(new Job(i, i));\n        pool.shutdown();\n        Expect.equal(300, handled.size(), \"distinct jobs handled\");\n        Expect.isTrue(handled.values().stream().allMatch(n -> n == 1),\n            \"Some job was handled more than once: \" + handled);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"jobs-run-in-parallel\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void jobsRunInParallel() throws Exception {\n        CountDownLatch bothInside = new CountDownLatch(2);\n        AtomicInteger finished = new AtomicInteger();\n        WorkerPool pool = new WorkerPool(2, job -> {\n            bothInside.countDown();\n            if (bothInside.await(3, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) finished.incrementAndGet();\n        });\n        pool.submit(new Job(1, 1));\n        pool.submit(new Job(2, 1));\n        pool.shutdown();\n        Expect.equal(2, finished.get(),\n            \"Two jobs should be in progress at the same time with two workers\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"shutdown-drains-queue\", timeoutMs = 4000)\n    void shutdownDrains() throws Exception {\n        AtomicInteger done = new AtomicInteger();\n        WorkerPool pool = new WorkerPool(3, job -> {\n            Stress.pause(1);\n            done.incrementAndGet();\n        });\n        for (int i = 0; i < 60; i++) pool.submit(new Job(i, 1));\n        pool.shutdown();\n        Expect.equal(60, done.get(), \"jobs finished when shutdown() returned\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"pool-shares-one-queue\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void poolSharesOneQueue() {\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(Types.named(\"WorkerPool\"), BlockingQueue.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()) && Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n            \"WorkerPool.\" + f.getName() + \" should be private final\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(Types.named(\"Worker\"), BlockingQueue.class).size() == 1,\n            \"Each Worker should hold the shared queue, not a copy per worker\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-polling-or-locks\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noPollingOrLocks() {\n        for (String type : List.of(\"Worker\", \"WorkerPool\")) {\n            var shape = Source.type(type);\n            Expect.none(shape.calls(\"sleep\"), type + \" sleeps to wait for work; block on the queue instead\");\n            Expect.none(shape.calls(\"isEmpty\"), type + \" polls isEmpty(); block on the queue instead\");\n        }\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"Worker\").calls(\"wait\"), \"Worker uses wait/notify; the queue already blocks\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"worker-keeps-no-job-state\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void workerKeepsNoJobState() {\n        for (Field f : Types.named(\"Worker\").getDeclaredFields()) {\n            Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()) && !Modifier.isStatic(f.getModifiers()),\n                \"Worker.\" + f.getName() + \" should be a final instance field; \"\n                + \"competing consumers share nothing mutable except the queue\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Build a pool of competing consumers"},{"checks":[{"id":"forwards-to-route","kind":"behaviour","title":"Requests reach the matching service"},{"id":"service-receives-request","kind":"behaviour","title":"The service sees the original request"},{"id":"longest-prefix-wins","kind":"behaviour","title":"The longest prefix wins in any order"},{"id":"unknown-path-is-404","kind":"behaviour","title":"Unrouted paths give 404"},{"id":"auth-first","kind":"behaviour","title":"Bad tokens never reach a service"},{"id":"aggregate-joins-in-order","kind":"behaviour","title":"An aggregate joins its parts in order"},{"id":"aggregate-degrades","kind":"behaviour","title":"A failing part degrades to n/a"},{"id":"aggregate-needs-auth","kind":"behaviour","title":"Aggregates are authenticated too"},{"id":"api-shape","kind":"design","title":"route and aggregate chain"},{"id":"routes-are-data","kind":"design","title":"Routes are data, not branches"},{"id":"gateway-names-no-service","kind":"design","title":"No fixed service fields"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Routes are data: a table from prefix to service. Authentication happens once, at the door, before any lookup. What decides between two prefixes that both match?","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Keep a `Map<String, Service>` for routes and a `Map<String, List<String>>` for aggregates. In `handle`: check the token, look for an aggregate by exact path, else scan prefixes keeping the longest match.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Longest match:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["String best = null;","for (String prefix : routes.keySet()) {","    if (path.startsWith(prefix)","            && (best == null || prefix.length() > best.length())) {","        best = prefix;","    }","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"api-gateway","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"readOnly":["Messages.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Messages.java","source":"record Request(String path, String token) { }\n\nrecord Response(int status, String body) { }\n\n// A backend the gateway forwards to.\ninterface Service {\n    Response handle(Request request);\n}\n"},{"name":"Gateway.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\nfinal class Gateway {\n    private final Set<String> tokens;\n    private final Map<String, Service> routes = new HashMap<>();\n    private final Map<String, List<String>> aggregates = new HashMap<>();\n\n    Gateway(Set<String> tokens) {\n        this.tokens = Set.copyOf(tokens);\n    }\n\n    Gateway route(String prefix, Service service) {\n        routes.put(prefix, service);\n        return this;\n    }\n\n    Gateway aggregate(String path, List<String> prefixes) {\n        aggregates.put(path, List.copyOf(prefixes));\n        return this;\n    }\n\n    Response handle(Request request) {\n        if (request.token() == null || !tokens.contains(request.token())) {\n            return new Response(401, \"unauthorized\");\n        }\n        List<String> parts = aggregates.get(request.path());\n        if (parts != null) {\n            return combine(request, parts);\n        }\n        String best = null;\n        for (String prefix : routes.keySet()) {\n            if (request.path().startsWith(prefix)\n                    && (best == null || prefix.length() > best.length())) {\n                best = prefix;\n            }\n        }\n        return best == null\n            ? new Response(404, \"no route\")\n            : routes.get(best).handle(request);\n    }\n\n    private Response combine(Request request, List<String> prefixes) {\n        List<String> bodies = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (String prefix : prefixes) {\n            bodies.add(call(prefix, request));\n        }\n        return new Response(200, String.join(\" | \", bodies));\n    }\n\n    private String call(String prefix, Request request) {\n        Service service = routes.get(prefix);\n        if (service == null) {\n            return prefix + \":n/a\";\n        }\n        try {\n            Response res = service.handle(request);\n            return res.status() >= 500 ? prefix + \":n/a\" : res.body();\n        } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n            return prefix + \":n/a\";\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Messages.java","source":"record Request(String path, String token) { }\n\nrecord Response(int status, String body) { }\n\n// A backend the gateway forwards to.\ninterface Service {\n    Response handle(Request request);\n}\n"},{"name":"Gateway.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\n// The single entry point in front of the backend services.\nfinal class Gateway {\n    Gateway(Set<String> tokens) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Sends every path that starts with prefix to service. */\n    Gateway route(String prefix, Service service) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    /** Answers path itself by calling the routes of these prefixes. */\n    Gateway aggregate(String path, List<String> prefixes) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    Response handle(Request request) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"Clients talk to one gateway; the gateway authenticates, routes and combines.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `Gateway` in `Gateway.java`. `Request`, `Response` and `Service` are given and must not change.","type":"p"},{"items":["`new Gateway(Set<String> tokens)`; `route(prefix, service)` and `aggregate(path, prefixes)` return the gateway so calls chain.","`handle(request)`: a token that is null or not allowed gives `401 \"unauthorized\"`, before anything else.","An aggregate path calls each listed route and joins the bodies with `\" | \"`, in order, as `200`. A route that throws, answers 5xx or does not exist contributes `<prefix>:n/a`.","Otherwise forward to the route with the **longest** matching prefix, whatever the order of registration. No match gives `404 \"no route\"`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"ApiGatewayKataTest.java","source":"import java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass ApiGatewayKataTest {\n    static Service says(String body) {\n        return r -> new Response(200, body);\n    }\n\n    static Gateway gateway() {\n        return new Gateway(Set.of(\"t-1\", \"t-2\"));\n    }\n\n    static String call(Gateway g, String path, String token) {\n        Response res = g.handle(new Request(path, token));\n        return res.status() + \" \" + res.body();\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"forwards-to-route\")\n    void forwards() {\n        Gateway g = gateway().route(\"/users\", says(\"user:7\")).route(\"/orders\", says(\"orders:2\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"200 user:7\", call(g, \"/users/7\", \"t-1\"), \"/users/7\");\n        Expect.equal(\"200 orders:2\", call(g, \"/orders\", \"t-2\"), \"/orders\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"service-receives-request\")\n    void serviceReceivesRequest() {\n        Gateway g = gateway().route(\"/echo\", r -> new Response(200, r.path() + \"@\" + r.token()));\n        Expect.equal(\"200 /echo/1@t-1\", call(g, \"/echo/1\", \"t-1\"), \"the request seen by the service\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"longest-prefix-wins\")\n    void longestPrefixWins() {\n        Gateway a = gateway().route(\"/users\", says(\"users\"))\n            .route(\"/users/admin\", says(\"admin\")).route(\"/\", says(\"root\"));\n        Gateway b = gateway().route(\"/\", says(\"root\"))\n            .route(\"/users/admin\", says(\"admin\")).route(\"/users\", says(\"users\"));\n        for (Gateway g : List.of(a, b)) {\n            Expect.equal(\"200 admin\", call(g, \"/users/admin/3\", \"t-1\"), \"/users/admin/3\");\n            Expect.equal(\"200 users\", call(g, \"/users/9\", \"t-1\"), \"/users/9\");\n            Expect.equal(\"200 root\", call(g, \"/health\", \"t-1\"), \"/health\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unknown-path-is-404\")\n    void unknownIs404() {\n        Gateway g = gateway().route(\"/users\", says(\"u\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"404 no route\", call(g, \"/billing\", \"t-1\"), \"an unrouted path\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"auth-first\")\n    void authFirst() {\n        AtomicInteger calls = new AtomicInteger();\n        Gateway g = gateway().route(\"/users\", r -> {\n            calls.incrementAndGet();\n            return new Response(200, \"u\");\n        });\n        Expect.equal(\"401 unauthorized\", call(g, \"/users/1\", \"bad\"), \"a wrong token\");\n        Expect.equal(\"401 unauthorized\", call(g, \"/users/1\", null), \"a missing token\");\n        Expect.equal(\"401 unauthorized\", call(g, \"/billing\", \"bad\"), \"a wrong token on an unrouted path\");\n        Expect.equal(0, calls.get(), \"calls that reached the service\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"aggregate-joins-in-order\")\n    void aggregateJoins() {\n        Gateway g = gateway().route(\"/users\", says(\"user:7\")).route(\"/orders\", says(\"orders:2\"))\n            .aggregate(\"/home\", List.of(\"/users\", \"/orders\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"200 user:7 | orders:2\", call(g, \"/home\", \"t-1\"), \"/home\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"aggregate-degrades\")\n    void aggregateDegrades() {\n        Gateway g = gateway().route(\"/users\", says(\"user:7\"))\n            .route(\"/orders\", r -> { throw new IllegalStateException(\"down\"); })\n            .route(\"/promos\", r -> new Response(503, \"busy\"))\n            .aggregate(\"/home\", List.of(\"/users\", \"/orders\", \"/promos\", \"/ghost\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"200 user:7 | /orders:n/a | /promos:n/a | /ghost:n/a\", call(g, \"/home\", \"t-1\"),\n            \"/home with failing backends\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"aggregate-needs-auth\")\n    void aggregateNeedsAuth() {\n        Gateway g = gateway().route(\"/users\", says(\"u\")).aggregate(\"/home\", List.of(\"/users\"));\n        Expect.equal(\"401 unauthorized\", call(g, \"/home\", \"bad\"), \"/home with a bad token\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"api-shape\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void apiShape() {\n        Class<?> gw = Types.named(\"Gateway\");\n        Types.constructor(gw, Set.class);\n        Expect.equal(gw, Types.method(gw, \"route\", String.class, Service.class).getReturnType(),\n            \"route(...) should return the Gateway so calls chain\");\n        Expect.equal(gw, Types.method(gw, \"aggregate\", String.class, List.class).getReturnType(),\n            \"aggregate(...) should return the Gateway so calls chain\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"routes-are-data\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void routesAreData() {\n        var gw = Source.type(\"Gateway\");\n        Expect.none(gw.comparedStrings(),\n            \"Gateway compares against string literals; routes belong in route(...) calls\");\n        Expect.none(gw.switches(), \"Gateway switches on the path\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"gateway-names-no-service\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void namesNoService() {\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(Types.named(\"Gateway\"), Service.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"Gateway keeps a fixed Service field; hold routes in a collection instead\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Build an API gateway"},{"checks":[{"id":"allowed-request-reaches-app","kind":"behaviour","title":"Authorised requests reach the app"},{"id":"bad-token-denied","kind":"behaviour","title":"Bad or missing tokens are denied"},{"id":"access-log","kind":"behaviour","title":"Every request is logged, denials too"},{"id":"metrics","kind":"behaviour","title":"Status codes are counted"},{"id":"app-holds-no-platform-concerns","kind":"design","title":"OrderApp holds only business logic"},{"id":"sidecar-wraps-a-handler","kind":"design","title":"Sidecar wraps a Handler"},{"id":"sidecar-fronts-any-app","kind":"design","title":"Sidecar works with an app it has never seen"},{"id":"pipeline-wires-the-sidecar","kind":"design","title":"Pipeline returns the sidecar"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Which lines of `handle` are about orders, and which would be identical in any other service? The second group wants to live next to the app, not inside it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`Sidecar` implements the same `Handler` interface as `OrderApp` and holds a `private final Handler app`. It does the token check and `telemetry.record`, and delegates in between.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"The wiring:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["static Handler build(Set<String> tokens, Telemetry t) {","    return new Sidecar(new OrderApp(), tokens, t);","}"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"sidecar","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"readOnly":["Handler.java"],"solution":[{"name":"Handler.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\n\nrecord Request(String path, Map<String, String> headers) { }\n\nrecord Response(int status, String body) { }\n\ninterface Handler {\n    Response handle(Request request);\n}\n\n// Where the platform collects what services report.\nfinal class Telemetry {\n    final List<String> accessLog = new ArrayList<>();\n    final Map<Integer, Integer> metrics = new TreeMap<>();\n\n    void record(String path, int status) {\n        accessLog.add(path + \" \" + status);\n        metrics.merge(status, 1, Integer::sum);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"OrderApp.java","source":"final class OrderApp implements Handler {\n    @Override\n    public Response handle(Request request) {\n        String id = request.path().substring(\"/orders/\".length());\n        return new Response(200, \"order:\" + id);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Sidecar.java","source":"import java.util.Set;\n\nfinal class Sidecar implements Handler {\n    private final Handler app;\n    private final Set<String> tokens;\n    private final Telemetry telemetry;\n\n    Sidecar(Handler app, Set<String> tokens, Telemetry telemetry) {\n        this.app = app;\n        this.tokens = tokens;\n        this.telemetry = telemetry;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public Response handle(Request request) {\n        String token = request.headers().getOrDefault(\"token\", \"\");\n        Response res = tokens.contains(token)\n            ? app.handle(request)\n            : new Response(401, \"denied\");\n        telemetry.record(request.path(), res.status());\n        return res;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Pipeline.java","source":"import java.util.Set;\n\nfinal class Pipeline {\n    private Pipeline() { }\n\n    static Handler build(Set<String> tokens, Telemetry telemetry) {\n        return new Sidecar(new OrderApp(), tokens, telemetry);\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Handler.java","source":"import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\n\nrecord Request(String path, Map<String, String> headers) { }\n\nrecord Response(int status, String body) { }\n\ninterface Handler {\n    Response handle(Request request);\n}\n\n// Where the platform collects what services report.\nfinal class Telemetry {\n    final List<String> accessLog = new ArrayList<>();\n    final Map<Integer, Integer> metrics = new TreeMap<>();\n\n    void record(String path, int status) {\n        accessLog.add(path + \" \" + status);\n        metrics.merge(status, 1, Integer::sum);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"OrderApp.java","source":"import java.util.Set;\n\n// Orders business logic, tangled with auth, access logs and metrics.\nfinal class OrderApp implements Handler {\n    private final Set<String> tokens;\n    private final Telemetry telemetry;\n\n    OrderApp(Set<String> tokens, Telemetry telemetry) {\n        this.tokens = tokens;\n        this.telemetry = telemetry;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public Response handle(Request request) {\n        String token = request.headers().getOrDefault(\"token\", \"\");\n        Response res;\n        if (!tokens.contains(token)) {\n            res = new Response(401, \"denied\");\n        } else {\n            String id = request.path().substring(\"/orders/\".length());\n            res = new Response(200, \"order:\" + id);\n        }\n        telemetry.record(request.path(), res.status());\n        return res;\n    }\n}\n\n// Callers build the service here. Keep its signature and behaviour.\nfinal class Pipeline {\n    private Pipeline() { }\n\n    static Handler build(Set<String> tokens, Telemetry telemetry) {\n        return new OrderApp(tokens, telemetry);\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`OrderApp` authenticates, logs and counts requests as well as handling orders.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Move the cross-cutting concerns into a **sidecar** that wraps the app. `Pipeline.build(tokens, telemetry)` must keep answering, logging and counting exactly as now.","type":"p"},{"items":["`OrderApp` keeps only the business logic: a no-argument constructor, no tokens, no `Telemetry`.","Add `Sidecar implements Handler` with constructor `Sidecar(Handler app, Set<String> tokens, Telemetry telemetry)`. It checks the `token` header, forwards to the app, then records the outcome.","`Pipeline.build` returns the `Sidecar` around a new `OrderApp`."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"SidecarKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Field;\nimport java.lang.reflect.Modifier;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Set;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass SidecarKataTest {\n    static Response call(Handler h, String path, String token) {\n        Map<String, String> headers = token == null ? Map.of() : Map.of(\"token\", token);\n        return h.handle(new Request(path, headers));\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"allowed-request-reaches-app\")\n    void allowed() {\n        Handler h = Pipeline.build(Set.of(\"s3cret\"), new Telemetry());\n        Response res = call(h, \"/orders/42\", \"s3cret\");\n        Expect.equal(new Response(200, \"order:42\"), res, \"an authorised request\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bad-token-denied\")\n    void denied() {\n        Handler h = Pipeline.build(Set.of(\"s3cret\"), new Telemetry());\n        Expect.equal(new Response(401, \"denied\"), call(h, \"/orders/9\", \"wrong\"), \"a wrong token\");\n        Expect.equal(new Response(401, \"denied\"), call(h, \"/orders/9\", null), \"a missing token\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"access-log\")\n    void accessLog() {\n        Telemetry t = new Telemetry();\n        Handler h = Pipeline.build(Set.of(\"s3cret\"), t);\n        call(h, \"/orders/42\", \"s3cret\");\n        call(h, \"/orders/9\", \"wrong\");\n        call(h, \"/orders/7\", \"s3cret\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"/orders/42 200\", \"/orders/9 401\", \"/orders/7 200\"), t.accessLog,\n            \"the access log, denied requests included\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"metrics\")\n    void metrics() {\n        Telemetry t = new Telemetry();\n        Handler h = Pipeline.build(Set.of(\"s3cret\"), t);\n        call(h, \"/orders/1\", \"s3cret\");\n        call(h, \"/orders/2\", \"x\");\n        call(h, \"/orders/3\", \"s3cret\");\n        Expect.equal(Map.of(200, 2, 401, 1), t.metrics, \"status counts\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"app-holds-no-platform-concerns\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void appIsPure() {\n        Class<?> app = Types.named(\"OrderApp\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(app, Telemetry.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"OrderApp still holds a Telemetry; reporting is a platform concern\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.fieldsOfType(app, Set.class).isEmpty(),\n            \"OrderApp still holds the allowed tokens; authentication is a platform concern\");\n        var src = Source.type(\"OrderApp\");\n        Expect.none(src.mentions(\"Telemetry\"), \"OrderApp still mentions Telemetry\");\n        Expect.none(src.calls(\"record\"), \"OrderApp still records access and metrics\");\n        Expect.none(src.calls(\"getOrDefault\"), \"OrderApp still reads the token header\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sidecar-wraps-a-handler\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void sidecarWraps() {\n        Class<?> sidecar = Types.named(\"Sidecar\");\n        Expect.isTrue(Handler.class.isAssignableFrom(sidecar),\n            \"Sidecar should implement Handler so callers cannot tell it from the app\");\n        Field f = Types.onlyFieldOfType(sidecar, Handler.class);\n        Expect.isTrue(Modifier.isPrivate(f.getModifiers()) && Modifier.isFinal(f.getModifiers()),\n            \"Sidecar.\" + f.getName() + \" should be a private final Handler\");\n        Types.constructor(sidecar, Handler.class, Set.class, Telemetry.class);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"sidecar-fronts-any-app\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void frontsAnyApp() throws Throwable {\n        AtomicInteger reached = new AtomicInteger();\n        Handler stub = r -> {\n            reached.incrementAndGet();\n            return new Response(200, \"stub\");\n        };\n        Telemetry t = new Telemetry();\n        var ctor = Types.constructor(Types.named(\"Sidecar\"), Handler.class, Set.class, Telemetry.class);\n        Handler h = (Handler) Types.create(ctor, stub, Set.of(\"k\"), t);\n        Expect.equal(\"stub\", call(h, \"/x\", \"k\").body(), \"an authorised call to any wrapped handler\");\n        Expect.equal(401, call(h, \"/x\", \"no\").status(), \"an unauthorised call\");\n        Expect.equal(1, reached.get(), \"calls that reached the wrapped handler\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"/x 200\", \"/x 401\"), t.accessLog, \"the sidecar's access log\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"pipeline-wires-the-sidecar\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void pipelineWires() {\n        Handler h = Pipeline.build(Set.of(\"k\"), new Telemetry());\n        Expect.isTrue(Types.named(\"Sidecar\").isInstance(h),\n            \"Pipeline.build should return the Sidecar that wraps the app\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Pull the platform concerns out of OrderApp"},{"checks":[{"id":"routes-by-key-hash","kind":"behaviour","title":"A key goes to its shard"},{"id":"success-calls-once","kind":"behaviour","title":"A healthy call is made once"},{"id":"retries-same-replica","kind":"behaviour","title":"Transient failures are retried"},{"id":"fails-over-after-attempts","kind":"behaviour","title":"Exhausted replicas fail over"},{"id":"gives-up-with-cause","kind":"behaviour","title":"A dead shard gives a clear IOException"},{"id":"bugs-are-not-retried","kind":"behaviour","title":"Runtime exceptions are not retried"},{"id":"timeout-fails-over","kind":"behaviour","title":"A hanging replica times out"},{"id":"profile-service-unchanged","kind":"behaviour","title":"ProfileService works through it"},{"id":"ambassador-is-a-keyvalue","kind":"design","title":"The ambassador implements the same port"},{"id":"application-stays-unaware","kind":"design","title":"The application knows nothing of it"},{"id":"no-sleeping-retry","kind":"design","title":"Retries do not sleep"}],"hints":[[{"text":"The ambassador is the same interface as the thing it fronts, so the app cannot tell the difference. Two nested loops: replicas outside, tries inside. Which failures deserve a retry?","type":"p"}],[{"text":"For the timeout, run each try on its own thread (a virtual thread is cheap) completing a `CompletableFuture`, and `get(timeoutMs, MILLISECONDS)`. Map `TimeoutException` to an `IOException` so the retry logic is one path.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Skeleton:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["for (KeyValue replica : shards.get(shard)) {","    for (int i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {","        try { return attempt(replica, key); }","        catch (IOException e) { last = e; }","    }","}","throw new IOException(\"shard \" + shard + \" unavailable\", last);"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"ambassador","kind":"implement","minutes":25,"readOnly":["KeyValue.java"],"solution":[{"name":"KeyValue.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\n\n// The port the application already talks to.\ninterface KeyValue {\n    String get(String key) throws IOException;\n}\n\n// The application. It must stay unaware of shards, retries and timeouts.\nfinal class ProfileService {\n    private final KeyValue store;\n\n    ProfileService(KeyValue store) { this.store = store; }\n\n    String load(String user) throws IOException {\n        return store.get(\"user:\" + user);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Ambassador.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutionException;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException;\n\nfinal class Ambassador implements KeyValue {\n    private final List<List<KeyValue>> shards;\n    private final int attempts;\n    private final long timeoutMs;\n\n    Ambassador(List<List<KeyValue>> shards, int attempts, long timeoutMs) {\n        this.shards = shards;\n        this.attempts = attempts;\n        this.timeoutMs = timeoutMs;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String get(String key) throws IOException {\n        int shard = Math.floorMod(key.hashCode(), shards.size());\n        IOException last = null;\n        for (KeyValue replica : shards.get(shard)) {\n            for (int i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {\n                try {\n                    return attempt(replica, key);\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    last = e;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        throw new IOException(\"shard \" + shard + \" unavailable\", last);\n    }\n\n    private String attempt(KeyValue replica, String key) throws IOException {\n        CompletableFuture<String> call = new CompletableFuture<>();\n        Thread.ofVirtual().start(() -> {\n            try {\n                call.complete(replica.get(key));\n            } catch (Throwable e) {\n                call.completeExceptionally(e);\n            }\n        });\n        try {\n            return call.get(timeoutMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);\n        } catch (TimeoutException e) {\n            call.cancel(true);\n            throw new IOException(\"timed out after \" + timeoutMs + \" ms\", e);\n        } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n            throw new IOException(\"interrupted\", e);\n        } catch (ExecutionException e) {\n            if (e.getCause() instanceof IOException io) {\n                throw io;\n            }\n            if (e.getCause() instanceof RuntimeException re) {\n                throw re;\n            }\n            throw new IOException(e.getCause());\n        }\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"KeyValue.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\n\n// The port the application already talks to.\ninterface KeyValue {\n    String get(String key) throws IOException;\n}\n\n// The application. It must stay unaware of shards, retries and timeouts.\nfinal class ProfileService {\n    private final KeyValue store;\n\n    ProfileService(KeyValue store) { this.store = store; }\n\n    String load(String user) throws IOException {\n        return store.get(\"user:\" + user);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Ambassador.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\nimport java.util.List;\n\n// A client-side proxy in front of a sharded, replicated store.\nfinal class Ambassador implements KeyValue {\n    /**\n     * shards: replicas per shard, preferred first.\n     * attempts: tries per replica. timeoutMs: limit for one try.\n     */\n    Ambassador(List<List<KeyValue>> shards, int attempts, long timeoutMs) {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String get(String key) throws IOException {\n        throw new UnsupportedOperationException(\"TODO\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"The app asks one `KeyValue`; the ambassador handles shards, retries and timeouts for it.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Implement `Ambassador implements KeyValue` in `Ambassador.java`. `KeyValue` and `ProfileService` are given and must not change.","type":"p"},{"items":["`Ambassador(List<List<KeyValue>> shards, int attempts, long timeoutMs)`: the shard of a key is `Math.floorMod(key.hashCode(), shards.size())`; replicas are tried in order.","Each replica gets up to `attempts` tries. An `IOException`, or a try that takes longer than `timeoutMs`, counts as a failure; then retry, then try the next replica.","When all are exhausted, throw `IOException` whose message starts `shard N unavailable` and whose cause is the last failure.","A `RuntimeException` from a replica is a bug: it propagates at once, with no retry."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"AmbassadorKataTest.java","source":"import java.io.IOException;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Collections;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass AmbassadorKataTest {\n    /** Fails the first {@code failures} calls, then answers name:key. */\n    static final class Node implements KeyValue {\n        final String name;\n        final int failures;\n        final List<String> trace;\n        final AtomicInteger calls = new AtomicInteger();\n\n        Node(String name, int failures, List<String> trace) {\n            this.name = name;\n            this.failures = failures;\n            this.trace = trace;\n        }\n\n        public String get(String key) throws IOException {\n            trace.add(name);\n            if (calls.incrementAndGet() <= failures) throw new IOException(name + \" is down\");\n            return name + \":\" + key;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static List<String> trace() {\n        return Collections.synchronizedList(new ArrayList<>());\n    }\n\n    static String keyForShard(int shard, int shards) {\n        for (int i = 0; ; i++) {\n            if (Math.floorMod((\"k\" + i).hashCode(), shards) == shard) return \"k\" + i;\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"routes-by-key-hash\")\n    void routesByHash() throws Exception {\n        List<String> t = trace();\n        var amb = new Ambassador(List.of(\n            List.of(new Node(\"a\", 0, t)), List.of(new Node(\"b\", 0, t))), 1, 500);\n        Expect.equal(\"a:\" + keyForShard(0, 2), amb.get(keyForShard(0, 2)), \"a key of shard 0\");\n        Expect.equal(\"b:\" + keyForShard(1, 2), amb.get(keyForShard(1, 2)), \"a key of shard 1\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"success-calls-once\")\n    void successCallsOnce() throws Exception {\n        List<String> t = trace();\n        var amb = new Ambassador(List.of(List.of(new Node(\"a\", 0, t), new Node(\"b\", 0, t))), 3, 500);\n        amb.get(\"x\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a\"), t, \"replicas called on a healthy store\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"retries-same-replica\")\n    void retriesSameReplica() throws Exception {\n        List<String> t = trace();\n        var amb = new Ambassador(List.of(List.of(new Node(\"a\", 2, t), new Node(\"b\", 0, t))), 3, 500);\n        Expect.equal(\"a:x\", amb.get(\"x\"), \"the answer after two transient failures\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a\", \"a\", \"a\"), t, \"calls made\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"fails-over-after-attempts\")\n    void failsOver() throws Exception {\n        List<String> t = trace();\n        var amb = new Ambassador(List.of(List.of(new Node(\"a\", 99, t), new Node(\"b\", 0, t))), 2, 500);\n        Expect.equal(\"b:x\", amb.get(\"x\"), \"the answer from the second replica\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a\", \"a\", \"b\"), t, \"calls made\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"gives-up-with-cause\")\n    void givesUp() {\n        List<String> t = trace();\n        String key = keyForShard(1, 2);\n        var amb = new Ambassador(List.of(List.of(new Node(\"z\", 0, t)),\n            List.of(new Node(\"a\", 99, t), new Node(\"b\", 99, t))), 2, 500);\n        IOException e = Expect.raises(IOException.class, () -> amb.get(key), \"a shard that is fully down\");\n        Expect.isTrue(e.getMessage() != null && e.getMessage().contains(\"shard 1 unavailable\"),\n            \"The message should name the shard: shard 1 unavailable, got \" + e.getMessage());\n        Expect.isTrue(e.getCause() instanceof IOException, \"The last failure should be the cause\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"a\", \"a\", \"b\", \"b\"), t, \"calls made\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"bugs-are-not-retried\")\n    void bugsNotRetried() {\n        List<String> t = trace();\n        KeyValue buggy = k -> {\n            t.add(\"bug\");\n            throw new IllegalStateException(\"npe-ish\");\n        };\n        var amb = new Ambassador(List.of(List.of(buggy, new Node(\"b\", 0, t))), 3, 500);\n        Expect.raises(IllegalStateException.class, () -> amb.get(\"x\"), \"a RuntimeException from a replica\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(\"bug\"), t, \"calls made\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"timeout-fails-over\", timeoutMs = 5000)\n    void timeoutFailsOver() throws Exception {\n        CountDownLatch never = new CountDownLatch(1);\n        List<String> t = trace();\n        KeyValue hung = k -> {\n            t.add(\"hung\");\n            try {\n                never.await();\n            } catch (InterruptedException e) {\n                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();\n            }\n            return \"late\";\n        };\n        var amb = new Ambassador(List.of(List.of(hung, new Node(\"b\", 0, t))), 1, 40);\n        try {\n            String answer = Expect.completesWithin(3000, () -> amb.get(\"x\"),\n                \"a call to a replica that hangs forever\");\n            Expect.equal(\"b:x\", answer, \"the answer from the healthy replica\");\n            Expect.equal(List.of(\"hung\", \"b\"), t, \"calls made\");\n        } finally {\n            never.countDown();\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"profile-service-unchanged\")\n    void profileServiceUnchanged() throws Exception {\n        List<String> t = trace();\n        var amb = new Ambassador(List.of(List.of(new Node(\"a\", 1, t), new Node(\"b\", 0, t))), 1, 500);\n        Expect.equal(\"b:user:7\", new ProfileService(amb).load(\"7\"), \"ProfileService.load through the ambassador\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"ambassador-is-a-keyvalue\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void isAKeyValue() {\n        Expect.isTrue(KeyValue.class.isAssignableFrom(Types.named(\"Ambassador\")),\n            \"Ambassador should implement KeyValue so the application cannot tell it apart\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"application-stays-unaware\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void appUnaware() {\n        var app = Source.type(\"ProfileService\");\n        Expect.none(app.mentions(\"Ambassador\"), \"ProfileService names the Ambassador\");\n        Expect.none(app.calls(\"sleep\"), \"ProfileService retries itself\");\n        Expect.none(app.news(\"Ambassador\"), \"ProfileService builds its own proxy\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"no-sleeping-retry\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void noSleep() {\n        Expect.none(Source.type(\"Ambassador\").calls(\"sleep\"),\n            \"Ambassador sleeps between tries; retry immediately, the tests have no time to waste\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Write a client-side ambassador"},{"checks":[{"id":"migrated-prefix-goes-modern","kind":"behaviour","title":"/customers is fully migrated"},{"id":"partial-rollout-by-user","kind":"behaviour","title":"/invoices is migrated for half the users"},{"id":"a-user-sticks-to-one-side","kind":"behaviour","title":"A user always sees the same system"},{"id":"unmigrated-stays-legacy","kind":"behaviour","title":"Other paths stay on legacy"},{"id":"backend-is-one-method","kind":"design","title":"Backend is a one-method interface"},{"id":"facade-holds-both-systems","kind":"design","title":"The facade is a Backend over two Backends"},{"id":"facade-routes-by-rule","kind":"design","title":"The facade routes any backends by rule"},{"id":"site-delegates-to-facade","kind":"design","title":"Site no longer routes by itself"}],"hints":[[{"text":"Callers must not notice which system answers. Give the old system and the new one the same interface, and put the choosing in one place that is also that interface.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"`StranglerFacade` keeps two `Backend` fields and an ordered `Map<String, Integer>` of prefix to percent. `migrate` adds a rule and returns `this`. `Site` builds one facade and forwards to it.","type":"p"}],[{"text":"Routing inside the facade:","type":"p"},{"language":"java","lines":["for (var rule : migrated.entrySet()) {","    if (path.startsWith(rule.getKey())) {","        int bucket = Math.floorMod(userId.hashCode(), 100);","        return (bucket < rule.getValue() ? modern : legacy)","            .handle(userId, path);","    }","}","return legacy.handle(userId, path);"],"type":"code"}]],"itemId":"strangler-fig","kind":"refactor","minutes":20,"solution":[{"name":"Site.java","source":"final class Site {\n    private final Backend entry =\n        new StranglerFacade(new LegacyBackend(), new ModernBackend())\n            .migrate(\"/customers\", 100)\n            .migrate(\"/invoices\", 50);\n\n    String handle(String userId, String path) {\n        return entry.handle(userId, path);\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"Backend.java","source":"interface Backend {\n    String handle(String userId, String path);\n}\n\nfinal class LegacyBackend implements Backend {\n    public String handle(String userId, String path) {\n        return \"legacy \" + path;\n    }\n}\n\nfinal class ModernBackend implements Backend {\n    public String handle(String userId, String path) {\n        return \"modern \" + path;\n    }\n}\n"},{"name":"StranglerFacade.java","source":"import java.util.LinkedHashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.Objects;\n\nfinal class StranglerFacade implements Backend {\n    private final Backend legacy;\n    private final Backend modern;\n    private final Map<String, Integer> migrated = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n\n    StranglerFacade(Backend legacy, Backend modern) {\n        this.legacy = Objects.requireNonNull(legacy, \"legacy\");\n        this.modern = Objects.requireNonNull(modern, \"modern\");\n    }\n\n    StranglerFacade migrate(String prefix, int percent) {\n        migrated.put(prefix, percent);\n        return this;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String handle(String userId, String path) {\n        for (var rule : migrated.entrySet()) {\n            if (path.startsWith(rule.getKey())) {\n                int bucket = Math.floorMod(userId.hashCode(), 100);\n                return bucket < rule.getValue()\n                    ? modern.handle(userId, path)\n                    : legacy.handle(userId, path);\n            }\n        }\n        return legacy.handle(userId, path);\n    }\n}\n"}],"starter":[{"name":"Site.java","source":"// Pages are moving from the old system to the new one, path by path.\nfinal class Site {\n    String handle(String userId, String path) {\n        int bucket = Math.floorMod(userId.hashCode(), 100);\n        if (path.startsWith(\"/customers\")) {\n            return modern(path);                  // fully migrated\n        }\n        if (path.startsWith(\"/invoices\")) {\n            return bucket < 50 ? modern(path) : legacy(path);   // half\n        }\n        return legacy(path);\n    }\n\n    private String legacy(String path) {\n        return \"legacy \" + path;\n    }\n\n    private String modern(String path) {\n        return \"modern \" + path;\n    }\n}\n"}],"task":[{"text":"`Site` mixes the routing rules with both systems; migrating one more path means editing it.","type":"lead"},{"text":"Put a **strangler facade** in front. `new Site().handle(userId, path)` must return exactly what it returns now.","type":"p"},{"items":["Add `interface Backend` with `String handle(String userId, String path)`; the old and new systems each implement it.","Add `StranglerFacade implements Backend` with `StranglerFacade(Backend legacy, Backend modern)` and a chainable `migrate(String prefix, int percent)`.","A path starting with a migrated prefix goes to `modern` when `Math.floorMod(userId.hashCode(), 100) < percent`, else `legacy`. The first matching rule wins; no rule means `legacy`.","`Site` just builds the facade with its two rules and delegates."],"type":"bullets"}],"tests":[{"name":"StranglerFigKataTest.java","source":"import java.lang.reflect.Method;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport kata.*;\n\nclass StranglerFigKataTest {\n    static final List<String> USERS = List.of(\"alice\", \"bob\", \"carol\", \"dave\", \"erin\", \"frank\", \"gina\", \"hank\");\n\n    static String half(String user, String path) {\n        return Math.floorMod(user.hashCode(), 100) < 50 ? \"modern \" + path : \"legacy \" + path;\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"migrated-prefix-goes-modern\")\n    void fullyMigrated() {\n        Site site = new Site();\n        for (String u : USERS) {\n            Expect.equal(\"modern /customers/9\", site.handle(u, \"/customers/9\"), \"/customers for \" + u);\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"partial-rollout-by-user\")\n    void partial() {\n        Site site = new Site();\n        for (String u : USERS) {\n            Expect.equal(half(u, \"/invoices/1\"), site.handle(u, \"/invoices/1\"), \"/invoices/1 for \" + u);\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"a-user-sticks-to-one-side\")\n    void sticky() {\n        Site site = new Site();\n        for (String u : USERS) {\n            String first = site.handle(u, \"/invoices/1\");\n            for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n                Expect.equal(first, site.handle(u, \"/invoices/1\"), \"repeat calls for \" + u);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"unmigrated-stays-legacy\")\n    void unmigrated() {\n        Site site = new Site();\n        for (String u : USERS) {\n            Expect.equal(\"legacy /reports/q3\", site.handle(u, \"/reports/q3\"), \"/reports for \" + u);\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"backend-is-one-method\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void backendInterface() {\n        Class<?> backend = Types.named(\"Backend\");\n        Expect.isTrue(backend.isInterface(), \"Backend should be an interface\");\n        var m = Types.singleAbstractMethod(backend);\n        Expect.equal(\"handle\", m.getName(), \"the method name\");\n        Expect.equal(List.of(String.class, String.class), List.of(m.getParameterTypes()), \"handle's parameters\");\n        Expect.equal(String.class, m.getReturnType(), \"handle's return type\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"facade-holds-both-systems\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void facadeHolds() {\n        Class<?> backend = Types.named(\"Backend\");\n        Class<?> facade = Types.named(\"StranglerFacade\");\n        Expect.isTrue(backend.isAssignableFrom(facade),\n            \"StranglerFacade should be a Backend, so callers cannot tell it apart\");\n        Expect.equal(2, Types.fieldsOfType(facade, backend).size(),\n            \"StranglerFacade should hold exactly two Backends (legacy and modern)\");\n        Types.constructor(facade, backend, backend);\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"facade-routes-by-rule\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void facadeRoutes() throws Throwable {\n        Class<?> backend = Types.named(\"Backend\");\n        Class<?> facade = Types.named(\"StranglerFacade\");\n        List<String> calls = new ArrayList<>();\n        Object old = Types.implement(backend, a -> { calls.add(\"old\"); return \"old\"; });\n        Object fresh = Types.implement(backend, a -> { calls.add(\"new\"); return \"new\"; });\n        Object f = Types.create(Types.constructor(facade, backend, backend), old, fresh);\n        Method migrate = Types.method(facade, \"migrate\", String.class, int.class);\n        Method handle = Types.method(facade, \"handle\", String.class, String.class);\n        Expect.equal(\"old\", Types.call(handle, f, \"u\", \"/x/1\"), \"before any rule\");\n        Object same = Types.call(migrate, f, \"/x\", 100);\n        Expect.isTrue(same == f, \"migrate(...) should return the facade so rules chain\");\n        Expect.equal(\"new\", Types.call(handle, f, \"u\", \"/x/1\"), \"a prefix migrated at 100\");\n        Expect.equal(\"old\", Types.call(handle, f, \"u\", \"/y/1\"), \"a prefix with no rule\");\n        Types.call(migrate, f, \"/z\", 0);\n        Expect.equal(\"old\", Types.call(handle, f, \"u\", \"/z/1\"), \"a prefix migrated at 0\");\n    }\n\n    @Check(id = \"site-delegates-to-facade\", kind = Kind.DESIGN)\n    void siteDelegates() {\n        var site = Source.type(\"Site\");\n        Expect.isTrue(!site.news(\"StranglerFacade\").isEmpty(), \"Site never builds a StranglerFacade\");\n        Expect.none(site.calls(\"startsWith\"), \"Site still routes by path itself\");\n        Expect.none(site.calls(\"floorMod\"), \"Site still buckets users itself\");\n    }\n}\n"}],"timeoutSeconds":10,"title":"Strangle the legacy pages behind a facade"}],"topicId":"design-patterns"}
